window.FLOCK={"points":[{"id":"p1","title":"Cameras went up before the Town said go","plain":"Flock promised to hold every install until permits were in. Four cameras went up anyway, before the Town issued a notice to proceed. That same day, the citizen advisory committee's agenda said the Town was still \"hoping\" to have cameras in place by the end of February.","why":"If the vendor and the department can't follow their own permit process, residents have no reason to trust them with the rules on data.","cites":[["e0867","We are holding ALL installs until all permits/permissions are received."],["e0877","Four cameras were already inadvertently installed"],["a2025-01-09","Hoping to have cameras in place by end of February"],["e0164","4 of your cameras were installed prematurely"],["e0877","provide us with an email to disregard"]]},{"id":"p2","title":"The State wouldn't allow it, so the plan was to \"be creative\"","plain":"In June 2024 the Chief wrote that SCDOT was not allowing license plate readers on its property because of a SLED complaint about how the data is stored. In September 2025, Town staff wrote that SCDOT had paused all new permits for Flock cameras because of ongoing litigation. Flock then told staff it could use Dominion Energy poles inside SCDOT's right-of-way anyway. The Town's own compliance director said Dominion can't grant that permission.","why":"A state agency raised a data-storage concern serious enough to block these cameras. The Town worked around it instead of answering it.","cites":[["e0114","SCDOT is not allowing any cameras or ALPR's to be put up on their property"],["e0114","(Due to the SLED Complaint on their storage of data) so we must be creative."],["e0201","SCDOT has paused all new Encroachment Permit approval for Flock cameras due to ongoing litigation"],["e0201","Flock that they have previously received permissions from Dominion"],["e0201","then Dominion cannot give us such authorization"]]},{"id":"p3","title":"Council voted before the Chief had the camera list","plain":"The day before Town Council voted on the first-phase contract, the Chief asked Flock's salesperson for the list of camera locations, writing that he didn't believe he had ever received it. Flock had been asking him to click \"Approve\" on each location so it could process the order.","why":"Council was asked to approve a surveillance network before the department in charge had the list of where the cameras would go.","cites":[["e1134","I don't believe I ever got that list."],["e1134","I am meeting with Council tomorrow night to get the contract for firs phase approved."],["e1134","clicking the \"Approve\" button once for each location"],["e1137","If you are approved, I will need the name and contact information of the town manager"]]},{"id":"p4","title":"Bought through an out-of-state side door, with a deadline discount","plain":"Flock sent a sole-source letter and suggested buying through a North Carolina sheriffs' co-op. When that fell through, the Town asked to \"piggyback\" on a Virginia Sheriffs' Association contract. In June 2024, months before Council voted, Flock routed the contract for signature with a $14,000 discount if it was signed that week. Weeks earlier the Chief had written that budget approval was still pending.","why":"Co-op piggybacking skips local competitive bidding, and a sign-this-week discount puts pressure on staff before elected officials have weighed in.","cites":[["e0097","I have also attached a copy of our sole source letter"],["e0097","please have her look into the NC Sheriff's Association, as we can do a co-op through them"],["e0090","are we able to piggyback off of the VA contract as a SC agency?"],["e0090","We are still waiting for budget approval"],["e0092","Please note the $14,000 discount offered if we can have this signed by the end of this week."],["e0092","we are pushing to have this wrapped up by EOD tomorrow."]]},{"id":"p5","title":"Citizen oversight came after the fact","plain":"Flock sent its first price quote in April 2023. The citizen advisory committee (LECAC) first heard the Chief's \"desire to obtain\" Flock in February 2024. The committee didn't review the Flock policy until November 14, 2024: two months after Council approved the contract, and the same day the Flock account went live and admins were trained that morning. The committee approved an audit only after cameras were already running.","why":"The committee meant to protect residents was shown the rules after the purchase, not before.","cites":[["e1101","Flock Safety Preliminary Quote"],["m2024-02-08","discussed the department's desire to obtain FLOCK camera systems"],["e1166","Your Flock Safety account is now active."],["e0140","This is an administrative class for the Flock Cameras."],["a2024-11-14","Review of New SOP for use of Flock Cameras."],["a2025-03-13","Approval of Flock Camera System Audit"]]},{"id":"p6","title":"Cameras on land the Town didn't control","plain":"Town staff warned that Town-run security cameras on private property would be \"a touchy issue,\" and that Flock's spec photos for property owners were blurred. One planned camera sat on heirs' property in litigation with no clear owner. The fallback spot was in a power-line easement and outside Town limits. Flock also asked which planned spots were outside the Town's jurisdiction, and one permit list gives a Hardeeville address.","why":"The network reaches past Town limits and onto property where ownership and consent were unsettled.","cites":[["e0865","Town operated security cameras on private property is going to be a touchy issue"],["e0865","The photos at the bottom of the Falcon Tech Specs are blurred"],["e0289","currently in litigation of heirs with no clear owner."],["e0877","is in the powerline easement (and also not in Town limits)"],["e1147","which locations are outside of your jurisdiction"],["e0236","31 Palmetto Pt, Hardeeville, SC 29927"],["e0867","The Town of Bluffton verbally approved the install on Town property."]]},{"id":"p7","title":"Far more than a license plate reader","plain":"The project wired about 98 of the Town's existing public safety cameras into Flock through a gateway installed on the Town network. It added 23 pan-tilt-zoom live video cameras, one more than the contracts called for. Flock loaded parcel, address and school map layers, and the Chief asked for school blueprints too. Flock's AI search finds things like \"biker wearing black sweatshirt.\" The Chief's own letter to property owners called it a tool for \"tracking vehicles entering and exiting our town.\"","why":"This is a town-wide live video and tracking system, not a few plate cameras on main roads.","cites":[["e0899","Wing Gateway - (1) 128-channel gateway to bring in Digital Watchdog IP cameras"],["e0234","I've successfully added 98 cameras from the list Bob provided."],["e0313","it appears an additional PTZ was added that was not included in the original contracts."],["e0027","Blueprints of the schools like we did with the GIS Map."],["e0696","biker wearing black sweatshirt"],["e0142","a crucial tool in tracking vehicles entering and exiting our town"]]},{"id":"p8","title":"Neighborhoods and big-box stores feed the system","plain":"Within weeks, Bluffton PD had more than 540 outside camera networks shared with it. HOAs like Pine Ridge, Palmetto Pointe and Coosaw Point shared their cameras, Home Depot gave statewide access, and Flock pushed Lowe's access again and again. The Chief asked for alerts on vehicles entering private communities, including Sun City. A Flock-built \"Bluffton Safe\" website and flyers recruit residents to register or connect their own cameras.","why":"Private cameras that residents never agreed to have watched by police are folded into one police search tool.","cites":[["e0164","you have over 540 networks shared with you so far"],["e0677","have all shared their cameras with you"],["e0682","state-wide access to The Home Depot owned Flock safety"],["e0698","setting alerts for vehicles that go into our private communities that have Flock"],["e0698","Sun City Hilton Head (SC)"],["e0925","members of the community can sign up if they want to register or integrate their cameras"]]},{"id":"p9","title":"Everyone gets access to everything","plain":"Asked how to set up access, the Chief said he had no issue giving every group access to all cameras, including School Resource Officers. The user roster lists over 50 officers, 14 of them SROs. Flock's own integration engineer was also given a login to Bluffton's system.","why":"The broader the access, the higher the risk of misuse, and the harder it is to audit.","cites":[["e0677","I don't have an issue of giving all groups access to all the cameras."],["e0677","(Admin, CID, Patrol, and SRO's)"],["e0681","R-14"],["e0915","Flock would like to set up your Integrations Manager to have access to your Flock system"]]},{"id":"p10","title":"Security shortcuts","plain":"One shared username and password for the Town's camera system was emailed to the vendor in plain text (we have blacked it out here). Flock asked for port-forwarding rules into the Town network. Flock suggested an SSO setting that lets anyone in the Town directory get a Flock account automatically. As of June 2026, Bluffton still didn't require two-factor login. Flock's live-video cameras, the model Bluffton uses, had debug pages exposed online without a password, and a Flock error sent alerts for plates that weren't actually on the national stolen and wanted (NCIC) list.","why":"A false alert can mean a wrongful traffic stop, and loose logins put everyone's location history at risk.","cites":[["e0232","A credential was added for viewing only for Flock."],["e0031","Do you have ability to create port forwarding rules for our gateway?"],["e0234","change User assignment required? to No"],["e0259","Our records show your organization does not yet have MFA required for login."],["e0264","temporarily accessible on the internet without password protection"],["e0253","Some alerts were generated for plates that were not actually on the NCIC list."]]},{"id":"p11","title":"The vendor treats public records as an attack","plain":"Flock's CEO wrote to the Chief that activists are trying to turn public records into a weapon. Flock then built redaction tools to limit what agencies release, removed officer names and searched plates from network audit logs, and told agencies to think about public-records exposure before turning on a new audit tool.","why":"The company is building its product to give the public less information, which is exactly what FOIA exists to prevent.","cites":[["e0667","They're also trying to turn a public records process into a weapon against you and against us."],["e1057","focusing on redaction capabilities and additional safeguards, to help agencies limit what is included in audit exports"],["e0262","will no longer include: Officer names Specific plates searched"],["e0857","we'd recommend evaluating how a data-aggregation view like Audit Assistance is treated under those laws."]]},{"id":"p12","title":"Scripted answers for Council","plain":"Flock emailed a ready-made Q&A for council members with a blank \"<Chief / Sheriff / Department Name>\" signature, to forward \"as-is.\" It offered to send a Flock representative to talk to elected leaders before votes. Flock's success manager asked for the data the department planned to show the advisory committee, and Flock collects \"impact\" numbers to use in council conversations and renewals.","why":"Oversight questions are being answered with vendor-written talking points.","cites":[["e0273","You can forward this email as-is"],["e0273","<Chief / Sheriff / Department Name>"],["e0270","would like a Flock representative to engage with your elected leaders ahead of a vote"],["e0847","Are you willing to share a copy of the data that will be presented at the meeting?"],["e0855","We use this data to support your success reporting, council conversations, and renewals."]]},{"id":"p13","title":"Federal and out-of-state sharing is a settings switch","plain":"Flock told agencies that turning on federal sharing could bring an FBI data request within days. It describes national sharing and lets agencies share with states that have \"similar laws\" on immigration enforcement. Whether Bluffton's data leaves South Carolina depends on settings the public can't see.","why":"Residents' movements could be searched by agencies far outside Bluffton, under rules set by a vendor's menu.","cites":[["e0272","may receive a data sharing request from the FBI in the coming days."],["e0249","Share with agencies with similar laws (for example, regarding immigration enforcement and data)"],["e0249","Opt into Flock's national sharing network."]]},{"id":"p14","title":"The price keeps growing","plain":"Phase 1 was quoted at $89,050 for the first year and $74,500 every year after. A September 2025 invoice billed $109,500 more. Phase 2 was signed as an \"additional services\" add-on under the original agreement, and the sales emails never stop: drones, trailers, $500-a-year video add-ons, paid AI search. Flock also offered two free conference tickets and free swag.","why":"Recurring costs are locked in and the scope expands through add-on orders.","cites":[["e0102","The first quote says 89,050 for \"subtotal year 1\""],["e0102","annual recurring subtotal of 74,500"],["e0348","Invoice Total: USD 109,500.00"],["e1098","we are simply adding products to your existing account"],["e1151","upgrade your existing LPRs for just $500 a year"],["e0724","We have two free tickets reserved for your department"]]}],"story":[{"id":"c1","title":"The sales pitch","span":"April 2023 – February 2024","intro":"Flock was selling to Bluffton PD almost a year before the public advisory committee heard about it.","entries":[["2023-04-12","Flock's salesperson sends the department a preliminary price quote after a demo. It assumes cameras on SCDOT property.",[["e1101","reflects all cameras being installed at SCDOT locations"]]],["2024-01-24","The Chief meets Flock and sends two years of crime heat maps. Flock sends a 15-camera starter map, a sole-source letter, and a tip to buy through a sheriffs' co-op.",[["e0097","Attached you will see two different heat maps"],["e0097","this is what Hilton Head Island did!"]]],["2024-01-30","The Chief sends Flock a list of every Town public safety camera. Flock quotes three phases, ending with 18 more live-video cameras.",[["e0101","See attached list of all Public Safety Cameras."],["e0102","encompasses the 18 remaining Condor live video cameras"]]],["2024-02-08","The citizen advisory committee first hears the Chief's wish to get Flock. A resident praises the Flock cameras already in her HOA.",[["m2024-02-08","discussed the department's desire to obtain FLOCK camera systems"],["m2024-02-08","FLOCK cameras that are currently being used in her neighborhood"]]]]},{"id":"c2","title":"Buying it","span":"May – September 2024","intro":"The purchase moved through out-of-state contracts and a signing deadline before Council voted.","entries":[["2024-05-14","Town contracts staff ask to piggyback on a Virginia sheriffs' contract. The Chief says budget approval is still pending.",[["e0090","are we able to piggyback off of the VA contract as a SC agency?"]]],["2024-06-12","The Chief tells staff SCDOT won't allow plate readers on its land because of a SLED complaint about data storage.",[["e0114","(Due to the SLED Complaint on their storage of data) so we must be creative."]]],["2024-06-27","Flock routes the contract for signature with a $14,000 sign-this-week discount, and sends the FlockOS statement of work.",[["e0092","Please note the $14,000 discount offered if we can have this signed by the end of this week."],["e1129","Please see the attached SOW for the FlockOS portion of the project."]]],["2024-09-09","The day before Council votes, the Chief asks Flock for the camera location list.",[["e1134","I don't believe I ever got that list."]]],["2024-09-16","The statement of work covers bridging 128 existing camera streams into Flock.",[["e1089","bridging 128 camera streams"]]],["2024-09-23","Flock asks which planned locations are outside Bluffton's jurisdiction.",[["e1147","which locations are outside of your jurisdiction"]]]]},{"id":"c3","title":"Rules after the purchase","span":"October 2024 – March 2025","intro":"The policy, the training, and the audit all arrived after the contract.","entries":[["2024-10-31","The Chief drafts the letter asking property owners to host cameras, describing them as a way of tracking vehicles in and out of town.",[["e0142","a crucial tool in tracking vehicles entering and exiting our town"]]],["2024-11-14","Morning: the Flock account goes live and admin training is held. Evening: the advisory committee is shown the new Flock policy for the first time.",[["e1166","Your Flock Safety account is now active."],["a2024-11-14","Review of New SOP for use of Flock Cameras."]]],["2024-11-18","HOAs share their cameras with the department. The Chief opens all cameras to every group.",[["e0677","I don't have an issue of giving all groups access to all the cameras."]]],["2025-01-09","The committee agenda says \"hoping\" for cameras by end of February. A Town project recap sent that same morning lists four cameras already installed.",[["a2025-01-09","Hoping to have cameras in place by end of February"],["e0877","Cameras Already Installed - #01, #06, #07, #12"]]],["2025-03-13","The committee is asked to approve a Flock audit, after cameras are running.",[["a2025-03-13","Approval of Flock Camera System Audit"]]]]},{"id":"c4","title":"Putting up poles","span":"October 2024 – March 2025","intro":"Siting the cameras ran into private land, heirs' property, and missing permits.","entries":[["2024-10-02","Flock's permit list shows sites on church, business, and homeowner land, plus a Hardeeville address.",[["e0236","31 Palmetto Pt, Hardeeville, SC 29927"]]],["2024-10-18","Town staff need easements from 11 private property owners.",[["e0142","lists the 11 private property owners"]]],["2024-11-19","Town staff call cameras on private property a touchy issue and ask Flock for clearer photos than its blurred specs.",[["e0865","Town operated security cameras on private property is going to be a touchy issue"]]],["2024-12-09","Camera #16 is found to be on heirs' property in litigation. The Chief still wants coverage there.",[["e0289","currently in litigation of heirs with no clear owner."],["e0867","I would really like something in that area"]]],["2024-12-23","Flock says all installs are on hold until permits are in. Town property approval is only verbal.",[["e0867","We are holding ALL installs until all permits/permissions are received."],["e0867","The Town of Bluffton verbally approved the install on Town property."]]],["2025-01-16","Flock admits four cameras went up prematurely, promises a credit, and agrees to send an email telling the Town to disregard any resulting payment request.",[["e0164","4 of your cameras were installed prematurely"],["e0877","provide us with an email to disregard"]]],["2025-03-19","Cameras are live. The department tests them by putting one of its own cars on a hot list.",[["e0176","We put one of our vehicles into a hit list and drove through each camera."]]]]},{"id":"c5","title":"Wiring in everything","span":"December 2024 – May 2025","intro":"FlockOS connected Town cameras, maps, private networks, and a public recruitment site.","entries":[["2024-12-13","Flock's integration project starts: single sign-on, map layers, a community website, and a 128-channel gateway for Town cameras.",[["e0899","Wing Gateway - (1) 128-channel gateway to bring in Digital Watchdog IP cameras"]]],["2025-01-07","The Chief approves a Flock employee login to Bluffton's system. Flock starts the community camera website.",[["e0915","Flock would like to set up your Integrations Manager to have access to your Flock system"],["e0925","members of the community can sign up if they want to register or integrate their cameras"]]],["2025-01-08","Home Depot offers statewide camera access.",[["e0682","state-wide access to The Home Depot owned Flock safety"]]],["2025-01-16","Bluffton has over 540 outside networks shared with it.",[["e0164","you have over 540 networks shared with you so far"]]],["2025-01-23","The Chief asks for school blueprints on the Flock map.",[["e0027","Blueprints of the schools like we did with the GIS Map."]]],["2025-02-07","Alerts are switched on for private communities and a Home Depot store.",[["e0698","Sun City Hilton Head (SC)"],["e0698","Home Depot #1115"]]],["2025-05-22","A shared camera login and password is emailed to Flock in plain text.",[["e0232","A credential was added for viewing only for Flock."]]],["2025-05-30","Flock adds 98 Town cameras to the system.",[["e0234","I've successfully added 98 cameras from the list Bob provided."]]]]},{"id":"c6","title":"Phase 2 and beyond","span":"July 2025 – July 2026","intro":"More cameras arrived as add-ons while the state permit fight continued.","entries":[["2025-07-11","Flock offers the department two free conference tickets.",[["e0724","We have two free tickets reserved for your department"]]],["2025-09-10","Town staff note SCDOT has paused Flock permits over litigation. Flock says Dominion poles can be used anyway; Town legal disagrees.",[["e0201","SCDOT has paused all new Encroachment Permit approval for Flock cameras due to ongoing litigation"],["e0201","then Dominion cannot give us such authorization"]]],["2025-09-11","Phase 2 is signed as an add-on to the original agreement.",[["e1098","we are simply adding products to your existing account"]]],["2025-09-18","Flock bills $109,500. Town staff tell Flock that Town property needs no extra paperwork.",[["e0348","Invoice Total: USD 109,500.00"],["e1096","need any additional paperwork for Bluffton."]]],["2026-06-03","Flock's count: 29 plate readers and 23 live-video cameras, one more than contracted.",[["e0313","Phase 2 shows 13 LPRs and 19 PTZs installed."],["e0313","it appears an additional PTZ was added that was not included in the original contracts."]]],["2026-07-06","FOIA 20363 lists 50 camera locations and says not all are active yet.",[["f20363","not all listed cameras are currently active"]]]]},{"id":"c7","title":"The vendor pushes back","span":"December 2025 – July 2026","intro":"As public scrutiny grew, Flock's messages to the Chief focused on limiting disclosure and managing Council.","entries":[["2025-12-08","Flock's CEO says public records are being turned into a weapon. Flock plans redaction tools for audit exports.",[["e0667","They're also trying to turn a public records process into a weapon against you and against us."],["e1057","focusing on redaction capabilities and additional safeguards"]]],["2025-12-11","Network audit logs stop showing officer names and plates searched.",[["e0262","will no longer include: Officer names Specific plates searched"]]],["2025-12-23","Flock discloses live-video camera debug pages were online without a password.",[["e0264","temporarily accessible on the internet without password protection"]]],["2026-01-08","Flock asks for the data the department will show the advisory committee.",[["e0847","Are you willing to share a copy of the data that will be presented at the meeting?"]]],["2026-03-23","Flock tells agencies that enable federal sharing to expect FBI requests.",[["e0272","may receive a data sharing request from the FBI in the coming days."]]],["2026-03-30","Flock sends a fill-in-the-blank Q&A for council members.",[["e0273","You can forward this email as-is"]]],["2026-04-03","A Flock error sends alerts for plates not on the NCIC list.",[["e0253","Some alerts were generated for plates that were not actually on the NCIC list."]]],["2026-06-29","Flock notes Bluffton still doesn't require two-factor login.",[["e0259","Our records show your organization does not yet have MFA required for login."]]]]}],"fair":[["The Chief declined Flock's steakhouse dinner during a 2024 police conference in Boston, and said he couldn't attend the SC Chiefs' conference when Flock asked.",[["e0137","I am not going to be able to make it"],["e0124","No unfortunately I will not be able to attend."]]],["Flock says federal agencies can't find an agency's data unless that agency switches federal sharing on. These records don't show Bluffton's actual sharing settings.",[["e0272","Our default setting is to make ALL local police agencies undiscoverable by federal law enforcement"]]],["The Chief refused to approve two Phase 2 cameras that would have needed SCDOT permission.",[["e0201","I will not approve the two on May River unless they are powered by solar"]]],["These records don't include search audit logs, Council minutes, the signed contract, or the LECAC audit results, so they can't show whether anyone misused the system.",[]]],"next":[["Town Council minutes, agenda packet, and vote for the Flock contract (around September 10, 2024), and any Council action approving Phase 2 (contract 2026-18).","p3"],["The signed Master Services Agreement, every order form, the Virginia Sheriffs' Association contract used, and the sole-source letter.","p4"],["The SLED complaint about SCDOT's data storage and the SCDOT litigation that paused Flock permits.","p2"],["The notice-to-proceed records, Beaufort County encroachment permit, and the Flock credit for the four early installs.","p1"],["LECAC minutes for November 14, 2024 and January 2026, the Flock SOP as adopted, and every audit report presented.","p5"],["Bluffton's Flock sharing settings, the list of agencies it shares with, and the organization and network audit logs.","p13"],["All signed easements and property permission letters, including any outside Town limits.","p6"],["The list of 98 Town cameras added to Flock, and who can view live video.","p7"]],"docs":{"e1101":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1101","title":"Flock Safety Preliminary Quote","frm":"Taylor Ellison","date":"2023-04-12","text":"From:\nTaylor Ellison\nSent:\nWednesday, April 12, 2023 11:59:08 AM\nTo:\nCharles, Robert; jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com; hburke@townofbluffton.com; Chandler, Donald\nSubject:\nFlock Safety Preliminary Quote\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:Quote_20230412_154809.pdf ;\n\nAll,\nI wanted to take a moment to say thank you once again for allowing me the opportunity to show you our demo.  I look forward\nto our next meeting on the 27th.\nIn the meantime, I wanted to make sure you had some preliminary numbers between now and then; in case you needed to submit\nsomething for the budget before our next meeting.  This is quoted high and reflects all cameras being installed at SCDOT\nlocations.  Once we meet and determine exactly where the cameras will be placed, I will be able to revise any install fees\naccordingly which could save you money.\nPlease let me know if you have any questions, and I look forward to meeting with you all again on the 27th.\nThanks,\nTaylor Ellison\nLE Territory Sales Manager - NC/SC\n704-942-6362","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item1101.pdf"},"e1102":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1102","title":"Flock Safety Mapping Call - Reschedule","frm":"Taylor Ellison","date":"2023-05-04","text":"From:\nTaylor Ellison\nSent:\nThursday, May 4, 2023 9:16:53 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nFlock Safety Mapping Call - Reschedule\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nJoseph,\nI wanted to touch base with you to see when we can reschedule our mapping call?\nPlease get back to me at your earliest convenience, and I look forward to hearing from you.\nThanks,\nTaylor Ellison\nLE Territory Sales Manager - NC/SC\n704-942-6362","pdf":null},"e0668":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0668","title":"Virtual Product Launch - Are you registered yet_","frm":"Garrett Langley, CEO, Flock Safety","date":"2023-05-16","text":"From:\nGarrett Langley, CEO, Flock Safety\nSent:\nTuesday, May 16, 2023 11:09:44 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nVirtual Product Launch - Are you registered yet?\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi Joe,\nI wanted to reach out because I see you haven't registered for our upcoming product launch tomorrow, May\n17th, at 2 p.m. ET / 11 a.m. PT.\nI'll be walking through two new products and a quick update on both Falcon and Raven. It should be a lot of fun\nand includes a live Q&A at the end.\nYou can register here .\nLet's eliminate crime together,\nGarrett Langley\nCEO & Founder","pdf":null},"e1106":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1106","title":"Flock Safety Deployment Plan Follow Up","frm":"Taylor Ellison","date":"2023-07-18","text":"From:\nTaylor Ellison\nSent:\nTuesday, July 18, 2023 1:11:52 PM\nTo:\nhburke@townofbluffton.com; Chandler, Donald; jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com; Charles, Robert\nSubject:\nRe: Flock Safety Deployment Plan Follow Up\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood afternoon,\nI am following up to see if you were able to identify any utility poles that we could utilize for the LPR cameras.  If so, we will\nneed to meet and update the map.  If not, I can go ahead and send a contract over so we can get the ball rolling.\nPlease let me know as soon as you are able to do so.\nThanks,\nTaylor Ellison\nLE Territory Sales Manager - NC/SC\n704-942-6362\nOn Wed, Jul 12, 2023 at 9:29 PM Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHey Captain Burke,\nFollowing back up on last week's mapping call.  Were you guys able to find some utility poles that we can utilize to save you\nsome money?\nUpdate me when you can so we can get another mapping call scheduled to review any potential poles.\nThanks,\nTaylor Ellison\nLE Territory Sales Manager - NC/SC\n704-942-6362\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\n flocksafety.com\n\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0831":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0831","title":"I don\\220t see you registered for tomorrow","frm":"Hayden at Flock Safety","date":"2023-10-31","text":"From:\nHayden at Flock Safety\nSent:\nTuesday, October 31, 2023 8:05:55 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nI don’t see you registered for tomorrow\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi there,\nI wanted to reach out as I haven’t seen your registration come through for our virtual product launch with Founder and\nCEO Garrett Langley tomorrow at 2pm ET / 11am PT.\nOur discussion will feature an exclusive preview of cutting-edge AI solutions and integrations designed to give you\ncomprehensive insights across LPR, video, audio, and third-party devices and systems, enabling more confident\nresponses and better outcomes.\nYou can save your spot here.\nSee you there!\nHayden\nP.S. Have a scheduling conflict? No problem! Register anyway and we'll forward you the event recording","pdf":null},"e1107":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1107","title":"Flock Safety Follow Up","frm":"Taylor Ellison","date":"2024-01-16","text":"From:\nTaylor Ellison\nSent:\nTuesday, January 16, 2024 5:03:55 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nFlock Safety Follow Up\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\nHope all is well in Bluffton.  I received your request for me to give you a call - I tried but got your voicemail\nPer my message, give me a call back when you are able.\nThanks,\nTaylor Ellison\nLE Territory Sales Manager - NC/SC\n704-942-6362\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0097":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0097","title":"Bluffton PD Heat Maps","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2024-01-25","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSent:\nThursday, January 25, 2024 8:36:49 AM\nTo:\nTaylor Ellison\nSubject:\nRE: Bluffton PD Heat Maps\nSensitivity:Normal\nThanks Taylor. Tuesday 1/30 in the afternoon work for us. Anytime after 1:00.\n\nThanks,\n\nChief Joe Babkiewicz\n\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Wednesday, January 24, 2024 8:49 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Bluffton PD Heat Maps\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\n\nIt was a pleasure meeting you today!  Thank you for sending over the crime maps - I have sent them over to Tyler,\nwho will work on building out a full city coverage solution for you.\n\nAs discussed, I have linked the original 15 camera deployment for your reference below.  Some of this may\nchange based on Tyler's professional recommendations, but I wanted to make sure you had a copy of it.\n\nhttps://planner.flocksafety.com/public/3c7f1548-002b-449d-8735-c2bb56e7c965\n\nI have also attached a copy of our sole source letter for your procurement director to review.  Should this not\nsuffice, please have her look into the NC Sheriff's Association, as we can do a co-op through them - this is what\nHilton Head Island did!\n\nLastly,  Tyler anticipates having a map built for you by Friday.  When would be a good time for us to meet over a\nZoom call to review, and go over the live video integrations with your IT director?  I have availability Monday 1/29\nin the morning, Tuesday 1/30 in the afternoon, or Wednesday 1/31 after 11am.  Should none of those times work\nfor you, let's look at the week of Feb 12th, as I will be on vacation from Feb 1-10th.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any additional questions, and I look forward to working with you further on this\nproject!\n\nTaylor Ellison\nLE Territory Sales Manager of the Carolinas\n704-942-6362\n\nOn Wed, Jan 24, 2024 at 2:11 PM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nTaylor,\n\nThank you for meeting with us today. Attached you will see two different heat maps for calls for service over the\npast two years. Please let me know if you need anything else. Thanks again for your time.\n\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nChief of Police\nOffice | 843-706-4537\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\n--\nTaylor Ellison\n\nTerritory Sales Manager\nflocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0097.pdf"},"e0099":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0099","title":"Bluffton PD Map Review_OS Demo and Integrations Review","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2024-01-30","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph on behalf of: Taylor Ellison\nSent:\nTuesday, January 30, 2024 8:06:18 AM\nTo:\nRoth, Felicia; Chandler, Donald\nSubject:\nFW: Bluffton PD Map Review/OS Demo and Integrations Review\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:attachment.ics ;invite.ics ;\n\n-----Original Appointment-----\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Friday, January 26, 2024 9:44 AM\nTo: Taylor Ellison; Babkiewicz, Joseph; Samantha Santucci; Chandler, Donald; Tyler Harris; Louie Rabenold\nSubject: Bluffton PD Map Review/OS Demo and Integrations Review\nWhen: Tuesday, January 30, 2024 2:00 PM-3:00 PM America/New_York.\nWhere:\n\n – 3 p m\n\nJoin Zoom Meeting\nflocksafety.zoom.us/j/83209495691\nID: 83209495691\nJoin by phone\n(US) +1 689-278-1000\nJoin using SIP\n83209495691@zoomcrc.com\nJoining instructions\nJoining notes\n------------\nZoom for G Suite Add-On Help\n------------\nMeeting host:\ntaylor.ellison@flocksafety.com\nWhen\nTuesday Jan 30, 2024 ⋅ 2pm – 3pm (Eastern Time - New York)\nGuests\nTaylor Ellison - organizer\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSamantha Santucci\ndchandler@townofbluffton.com\nTyler Harris\nLouie Rabenold\nView all guest info\nReply for jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\n\nJoin Zoom Meeting:\nhttps://flocksafety.zoom.us/j/83209495691\nYes\nNo\nMaybe\nMore options\nInvitation from Google Calendar\nYou are receiving this email because you are an attendee on the event. To stop receiving future updates for this event, decline this event.\nForwarding this invitation could allow any recipient to send a response to the organizer, be added to the guest list, invite others regardless of their\nown invitation status, or modify your RSVP. Learn more","pdf":null},"e0100":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0100","title":"Public Safety Cameras in Bluffton","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2024-01-30","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSent:\nTuesday, January 30, 2024 3:18:09 PM\nTo:\nTaylor Ellison\nSubject:\nPublic Safety Cameras in Bluffton\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:Public Safety Cameras Downtown.png ;Public Safety Cameras.png ;\nTaylor,\n\nHere is a screen shot for all the public safety cameras we have. I will send you a list in another email.\n\nThanks\n\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nChief of Police\nOffice | 843-706-4537\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov","pdf":null},"e0101":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0101","title":"Bluffton PD Public Safety Camera List","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2024-01-30","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSent:\nTuesday, January 30, 2024 3:24:56 PM\nTo:\nTaylor Ellison\nSubject:\nBluffton PD Public Safety Camera List\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:Public Safety Camera- List.docx ;\nSee attached list of all Public Safety Cameras.\n\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nChief of Police\nOffice | 843-706-4537\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0101.pdf"},"e0102":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0102","title":"Flock Safety Quotes and Total Deployment Map","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2024-02-01","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSent:\nThursday, February 1, 2024 12:40:08 PM\nTo:\nTaylor Ellison\nSubject:\nRE: Flock Safety Quotes and Total Deployment Map\nSensitivity:Normal\nTaylor,\n\nI have a question about the quotes. The first quote says 89,050 for “subtotal year 1”  and then annual recurring subtotal of\n74,500. For a total of 163,550. Does this mean that if this amount is paid in full then we are paid up for two years and then we\nstart the annual recurring total for FY27? Or can we pay year one (89,050) and pay year 2 (74,500) at start of year 2? I need to\nknow this for my council presentation. So if this is correct for phase one it would look like this:\n\nFiscal Year\nBudget\nFY2025\n163,550\nFY2026\n0\nFY2027\n74,500\nFY2028\n74,500\nOr\n\nFiscal Year\nBudget\nFY2025\n89,050\nFY2026\n74,500\nFY2027\n74,500\nFY2028\n74,500\n\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, January 30, 2024 7:23 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Flock Safety Quotes and Total Deployment Map\n\nChief,\n\nThanks for sending over the list of current camera locations.  I got those over to Tyler who will update the map.\n\nIn the meantime, I have linked what Tyler has already put together so that you can take a further look:\nhttps://planner.flocksafety.com/public/siting/d65d0f34-6f11-4f07-b022-9c9df0718ab6\n\nAdditionally, your quotes are attached below.  The first encompasses the first 17 LPR cameras, 4 Condor live video cameras, as\nwell as the integration of your existing live video.  The second is for Phase 2, and encompasses the 12 remaining LPR\ncameras.  The 3rd is for Phase 3, and encompasses the 18 remaining Condor live video cameras.  The final quote reflects\neverything all on one quote for a full out the door price.  If you want the quantities and products redistributed between the\nquotes for phases 2 and 3 just let me know!\n\nI will send the updated map to you once Tyler has finished adding your current cameras in.\n\nLet me know if you have any questions, and I look forward to hearing from you soon!\n\nTaylor Ellison\n704-942-6362\n\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\nflocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0102.pdf"},"e0832":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0832","title":"I don\\220t see you on the registration list for tomorrow","frm":"Hayden at Flock Safety","date":"2024-02-12","text":"From:\nHayden at Flock Safety\nSent:\nMonday, February 12, 2024 10:14:27 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nI don’t see you on the registration list for tomorrow\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi there,\n\nI wanted to reach out as I haven’t seen your registration for our Quarterly Product Update with Founder\nand CEO Garrett Langley tomorrow at 1 p.m. ET / 10 a.m. PT.\nOur discussion will feature how your agency can reduce the uncertainty and risk officers face when walking\ninto high-stakes situations, a demo of new features inspired by you, and new solutions to help you grow your\nnetwork with ease.\nYou won’t want to miss this. You can save your spot here.\nSee you there,\nHayden\nP.S. Have a scheduling conflict? Go ahead and register, and we'll send you the recording after the event.","pdf":null},"e0833":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0833","title":"Last Chance to Register -- Webinar Today at 1pm ET","frm":"Hayden at Flock Safety","date":"2024-02-13","text":"From:\nHayden at Flock Safety\nSent:\nTuesday, February 13, 2024 11:21:05 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nLast Chance to Register -- Webinar Today at 1pm ET\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi there,\n\nJust a final reminder that our Flock Safety Quarterly Product Update is taking place today at 1 p.m. ET / 10\na.m. PT. If you are unable to make the product launch today but are still interested in watching the recording,\nplease register so I can make sure you're on the distribution list to receive the recorded version.\nDuring this quarterly product update, we will discuss the release of new products, highly requested features,\nand what they mean for you.\nThanks,\nHayden","pdf":null},"e0662":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0662","title":"Personal Invitation_ Join me at Flock Forward 2024","frm":"Garrett Langley","date":"2024-03-06","text":"From:\nGarrett Langley\nSent:\nWednesday, March 6, 2024 10:07:52 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nPersonal Invitation: Join me at Flock Forward 2024\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi there,\nWe're gearing up for an incredible event at Flock Forward in Atlanta from June 12th - 14th, and we'd love to have you\njoin us. We expect hundreds of police chiefs and command staff, and we're set to dive into the latest innovations in public\nsafety and explore the future of policing together.\nOur lineup of speakers promises to be exciting, ranging from topics about AI and policing to real-time crime centers to\ngaining buy-in from your city council. Our product team will even have hands-on stations to show off the newest hardware\nand software innovations. This is an event I wouldn't want to miss.\nSpots are limited, so please RSVP soon to secure your spot.\nI look forward to seeing you there,\nGarrett","pdf":null},"e0663":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0663","title":"I don't see your RSVP for Flock Forward 2024 \\204 save your spot today","frm":"Garrett Langley","date":"2024-03-29","text":"From:\nGarrett Langley\nSent:\nFriday, March 29, 2024 10:01:28 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nI don't see your RSVP for Flock Forward 2024 — save your spot today\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi there,\nFlock Forward 2024 is right around the corner, and I hope you’ll join us in Atlanta for what will be an unforgettable event.\nWe’re inviting law enforcement leaders – including you – from across the country to gather for 3 days of collaboration,\nnetworking and learning as we discuss the role of technology in the future of policing.\nYou’ll have the opportunity to spend time connecting with peers, Flock product experts, and industry leaders to gain\nvaluable insights to bring back to your department.\nSpots are limited, so please RSVP soon to save your seat.\nI look forward to seeing you there,\nGarrett","pdf":null},"e0664":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0664","title":"Flock Forward - Will I see you there_","frm":"Garrett Langley","date":"2024-04-10","text":"From:\nGarrett Langley\nSent:\nWednesday, April 10, 2024 10:25:52 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nFlock Forward - Will I see you there?\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi there,\nFlock Forward is a couple of months away, and I want to make sure you have a chance to save your seat before early bird\npricing ends on April 14th.\nIf you haven’t already, check out the conference agenda. We have a compelling lineup of speakers planned featuring\nchiefs, public officials, and product experts from across the country.\nI look forward to seeing you there,\nGarrett","pdf":null},"e0322":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0322","title":"Join us at Flock Forward to elevate your real-time policing strategies","frm":"Dalton Webb","date":"2024-04-24","text":"From:\nDalton Webb\nSent:\nWednesday, April 24, 2024 10:03:57 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nJoin us at Flock Forward to elevate your real-time policing strategies\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi there,\nI'm reaching out to personally invite you to Flock Forward, our first-ever customer conference.\nFrom engaging discussions on safety at large-scale sporting events – to fostering trust within communities – and exploring\nthe future of real-time policing, the agenda for this conference has been carefully crafted with law enforcement leaders like\nyourself in mind.\nI’m looking forward to taking the stage myself, joined by my colleagues Jamie Hudson and Caity Peak who bring experience\nworking together in Elk Grove PD’s Real Time Information Center. We’ll share invaluable insights into real-time policing\nstrategies applicable to agencies of any size or stage of development.\nI would be thrilled if you could join us in Atlanta from June 12-14. It's set to be an amazing experience where police chiefs\nand sheriffs from across the nation will come together to share their expertise and strategies on adapting to the evolving\nlandscape of real-time policing. Your insights would be incredibly valuable to us, and we'd be honored to have you attend.\nPlease take a moment to review the full agenda and purchase your ticket today.\nI look forward to the opportunity to connect with you in Georgia!\nDalton","pdf":null},"e0834":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0834","title":"I don't see you on the registration list for Thursday's webinar","frm":"Hayden at Flock Safety","date":"2024-05-14","text":"From:\nHayden at Flock Safety\nSent:\nTuesday, May 14, 2024 10:13:17 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nI don't see you on the registration list for Thursday's webinar\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi,\nI wanted to reach out as I haven’t seen your registration for our upcoming live webinar with Founder and\nCEO Garrett Langley on Thursday 5/16 at 1 p.m. ET / 10 a.m. PT.\nWe will be introducing our latest hardware and highly anticipated features, designed to broaden your\ncapabilities, maximize your resources, and enhance crime-solving efficiency.\nYou won’t want to miss this. You can save your spot here.\nSee you there,\nHayden\nP.S. Have a scheduling conflict? Go ahead and register, and we'll send you the recording after the event.","pdf":null},"e0090":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0090","title":"Bluffton PD_Virginia Sheriff's Association","frm":"Anna Martin","date":"2024-05-14","text":"Anna Martin\nSenior Coordinator – Business Development\nNorth Carolina Sheriffs’ Association, Inc.\nPost Office Box 20049\nRaleigh, North Carolina 27619-0049\nTelephone:  (919) 459-1072          Fax:  (919) 783-5272\nEmail: amartin@ncsheriffs.net      Webpage: www.ncsheriffs.org\nFrom:\nAnna Martin\nSent:\nTuesday, May 14, 2024 4:05:58 PM\nTo:\nRoth, Felicia; Babkiewicz, Joseph; Taylor Ellison\nSubject:\nRE: Bluffton PD/Virginia Sheriff's Association\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon All,\n\nYou will be able to use the contract when it is Awarded.  The Awards won’t be announced until June 20 and the PO will need\nto be submitted after that date.  I know Flock Safety is working on their bid.\n\nThanks!\nAnna\n\nNorth Carolina Sheriffs’ Association\nProudly Serving the Sheriffs and Citizens of North Carolina since 1922\n\nFrom: Roth, Felicia <froth@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Tuesday, May 14, 2024 2:32 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>; Anna Martin\n<amartin@ncsheriffs.net>\nSubject: RE: Bluffton PD/Virginia Sheriff's Association\n\nThanks for the introduction, Chief.  Anna, are we able to piggyback off of the VA contract as a SC agency?\n\nFelicia L. Roth, JD\nDirector of Compliance and Contracts\n\nTown of Bluffton\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nOffice: 843-7 06-7 816\nNEW mobile: 843-540-57 12\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Tuesday, May 14, 2024 2:31 PM\nTo: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>; Anna Martin <amartin@ncsheriffs.net>\nCc: Roth, Felicia <froth@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: RE: Bluffton PD/Virginia Sheriff's Association\n\nThank you Taylor. We are still waiting for budget approval before we can move forward with anything. I am hopeful that it\nwill get approved. I am also including Felicia Roth on this email who is our procurement specialist. Any communications\nplease include her on the email so that we can all stay updated and ensure we do things in accordance with\nprocurement requirements.\n\nChief Joe Babkiewicz\n\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, May 14, 2024 2:26 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Anna Martin <amartin@ncsheriffs.net>\nSubject: Bluffton PD/Virginia Sheriff's Association\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\n\nAllow me to introduce Anna Martin.  Anna oversees the NC and VA Sheriff's Associations contracts with us.  As I\nmentioned in last week's conversation, we were unable to secure a contract with NCSA this year, but are on the\nVirginia Sheriff's Association contract.  She will be able to help you with the co-op portion of the contract with\nFlock.\n\nAnna - Chief Babkiewicz is planning to purchase Flock in this coming budget year.  I wanted to go ahead and\nconnect to two of you so that you can get everything in place.\n\nThanks,\nTaylor Ellison\n\n--\n\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\nflocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0090.pdf"},"e1058":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1058","title":"I don\\220t see you on the registration list for Flock Forward 2024","frm":"Meg Heusel","date":"2024-05-22","text":"From:\nMeg Heusel\nSent:\nWednesday, May 22, 2024 10:07:23 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nI don’t see you on the registration list for Flock Forward 2024\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi there,\nI wanted to reach out as I haven’t seen your registration for Flock Forward, our conference for law enforcement leadership,\nwhich is taking place from June 12-14 in Atlanta.\nThe three-day event will offer invaluable opportunities to collaborate with other law enforcement leaders, gain insights from\nexperts, and discover innovative strategies to solve more crime in your community.\nYou won’t want to miss this event.\nYou can view the full agenda and purchase your ticket here.\nSee you there,\nMeg","pdf":null},"e1059":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1059","title":"Exclusive Offer - Flock\\220s Conference for LEOs in ATL","frm":"Meg Heusel","date":"2024-05-30","text":"From:\nMeg Heusel\nSent:\nThursday, May 30, 2024 9:07:28 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nExclusive Offer - Flock’s Conference for LEOs in ATL\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi there,\nI wanted to reach out with an exclusive discount code for Flock Forward, our conference for law enforcement leadership,\nwhich is taking place from June 12-14 in Atlanta.\nSimply use the code FLOCK50 at checkout to receive 50% off your registration at flocksafety.com/flock-forward-2024. But\nyou'll need to act fast because this special code is only valid until June 5th.\nWatch the full video\nHope to see you in Atlanta!\nMeg","pdf":null},"e1114":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1114","title":"Flock Sample Permission Letter","frm":"Taylor Ellison","date":"2024-06-12","text":"From:\nTaylor Ellison\nSent:\nWednesday, June 12, 2024 2:53:35 PM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nFlock Sample Permission Letter\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:Flock Safety Property License Agreement .docx (11).pdf ;\n\nChief,\nPlease see attached.\nTaylor Ellison\n704-942-6362\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0114":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0114","title":"Flock_Bluffton PD Integrations Call - OS Advanced","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2024-06-13","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSent:\nThursday, June 13, 2024 11:04:27 AM\nTo:\nTaylor Ellison\nSubject:\nRE: Flock/Bluffton PD Integrations Call - OS Advanced\nSensitivity:Normal\nYes sir I have. Thank you\n\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, June 13, 2024 10:01 AM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock/Bluffton PD Integrations Call - OS Advanced\n\nGood morning Chief Babkiewicz,\n\nI just adjusted the calendar invite for Thursday the 27th at 10am.  Please confirm that you received the updated\ncalendar invite.\n\nThanks,\nTaylor Ellison\nLE Territory Sales Manager - nc/sc\n704-942-6362\n\nOn Wed, Jun 12, 2024 at 3:45 PM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nDisregard. I have spoken with Taylor and asked that we look at the following week 24th or 27th for the meeting. He will\nsend out invite once he returns to office.\n\n-----Original Appointment-----\nFrom: Babkiewicz, Joseph On Behalf Of Taylor Ellison\nSent: Wednesday, June 12, 2024 3:30 PM\nTo: Roth, Felicia; Charles, Robert; Stormer, Tracye\nSubject: FW: Flock/Bluffton PD Integrations Call - OS Advanced\nWhen: Thursday, June 20, 2024 3:00 PM-4:00 PM America/New_York.\nWhere:\n\nGood afternoon,\n\nPlease see invite below reference a meeting with Flock Cameras. I would like each of you (Tracye is out that day so\nsomeone from IT) to sit in on that meeting so that we can get moving on the project come July 1.\n\nToday, I went over the camera placement for each camera in Phase 1 and it went well. However, there are some\nareas where we will need to get permission from the property owners to put a 12ft pole up or from utility company to\nput on existing pole. As of this time, SCDOT is not allowing any cameras or ALPR’s to be put up on their property\n\n(Due to the SLED Complaint on their storage of data) so we must be creative. Once that matter is resolved, Flock will\nmove the cameras on SCDOT property at no cost.  I can discuss more about this later.\n\nChief\n\n-----Original Appointment-----\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Wednesday, June 12, 2024 3:10 PM\nTo: Taylor Ellison; Louie Rabenold; Babkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject: Flock/Bluffton PD Integrations Call - OS Advanced\nWhen: Thursday, June 20, 2024 3:00 PM-4:00 PM America/New_York.\nWhere:\n\n – 4 p m\n\nJoin Zoom Meeting\nflocksafety.zoom.us/j/88683009022\nID: 88683009022\nJoin by phone\n(US) +1 386-347-5053\nJoin using SIP\n88683009022@zoomcrc.com\nJoining instructions\nJoining notes\n------------\nZoom for G Suite Add-On Help\n------------\nMeeting host:\ntaylor.ellison@flocksafety.com\nJoin Zoom Meeting:\nhttps://flocksafety.zoom.us/j/88683009022\nWhen\nThursday Jun 20, 2024 ⋅ 3pm – 4pm (Eastern Time - New York)\nGuests\nTaylor Ellison - organizer\nLouie Rabenold\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nView all guest info\nReply for jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nYes\nNo\nMaybe\n\nMore options\n\nInvitation from Google Calendar\nYou are receiving this email because you are an attendee on the event. To stop receiving future updates for this event, decline this event.\nForwarding this invitation could allow any recipient to send a response to the organizer, be added to the guest list, invite others regardless of their\nown invitation status, or modify your RSVP. Learn more\n\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\nflocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0114.pdf"},"e1129":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1129","title":"ToB IT Contacts","frm":"Taylor Ellison","date":"2024-06-27","text":"From:\nTaylor Ellison\nSent:\nThursday, June 27, 2024 3:58:22 PM\nTo:\nStormer, Tracye\nCc:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph; Roth, Felicia; Charles, Robert; Ocasio, Peter; Coleman, Ryan\nSubject:\nRe: ToB IT Contacts\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:Complete_with_Docusign_SC_-_Bluffton_PD_Floc.pdf ;\n\nPlease see the attached SOW for the FlockOS portion of the project.  Please sign and return as soon as you are able.\nThanks,\nTaylor Ellison\nLE Territory Sales Manager - NC/SC\n704-942-6362\nOn Thu, Jun 27, 2024 at 10:20 AM Stormer, Tracye <tstormer@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood morning Taylor,\n\nTown of Bluffton IT contacts for Flock system:\n\nCamera system Admin – Robert (Bob) Charles (rcharles@townofbluffton.com)\nGIS – Ryan Coleman (rcoleman@townofbluffton.com)\nSystem Administrator – Peter Ocasio (pocasio@townofbluffton.com)\n\nTracye F. Stormer\nChief Technology Officer\n\nTown of Bluffton\n\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\n(Office) 843-706-4580\n(Cell) 843-816-9953\nhttps://dot.cards/tracyestormer\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item1129.pdf"},"e0092":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0092","title":"Flock Safety Contract and Deployment Map","frm":"Anna Martin","date":"2024-06-27","text":"Anna Martin\nSenior Coordinator – Business Development\nNorth Carolina Sheriffs’ Association, Inc.\nPost Office Box 20049\nRaleigh, North Carolina 27619-0049\nTelephone:  (919) 459-1072          Fax:  (919) 783-5272\nEmail: amartin@ncsheriffs.net      Webpage: www.ncsheriffs.org\nFrom:\nAnna Martin\nSent:\nThursday, June 27, 2024 12:08:23 PM\nTo:\nTaylor Ellison; froth@townofbluffton.com; Babkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nRE: Flock Safety Contract and Deployment Map\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Morning All,\n\nThank you for considering the Virginia Sheriffs’ Association’s First Responder Supplies and Equipment program for your Flock\nSafety purchases!  Felicia, what information can I help you with?  Membership or registration is not required to purchase from\nthis contract.\n\nHave a great day!\nAnna\n\nNorth Carolina Sheriffs’ Association\nProudly Serving the Sheriffs and Citizens of North Carolina since 1922\n\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, June 27, 2024 11:36 AM\nTo: froth@townofbluffton.com; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Anna Martin <amartin@ncsheriffs.net>\nSubject: Flock Safety Contract and Deployment Map\n\nChief Babkiewicz and Felicia,\n\nThanks for your time this morning!\n\nFirst and foremost, I have routed the contract via DocuSign to Felicia at the Chief's request - it is ready for review and\nsignature.  Please note the $14,000 discount offered if we can have this signed by the end of this week.\n\nSecondly, I have included a link to the deployment map below.  Chief - you will need to go in, enter your name in the\ndesignated box, and click the \"Approve\" button for EACH location - I will need the contract signed and this completed before I\nam able to process the order.\n\nhttps://planner.flocksafety.com/public/bebd2eeb-ed81-4102-b497-ba3018cf39c7?cat=72c5ec157343\n\nLastly,  I have copied Anna Martin to this email and listed her contact information below.\n\nAnna Martin\nSenior Coordinator – Business Development\nNorth Carolina Sheriffs’ Association, Inc.\nPost Office Box 20049\nRaleigh, North Carolina 27619-0049\nTelephone:  (919) 459-1072          Fax:  (919) 783-5272\nEmail: amartin@ncsheriffs.net      Webpage: www.ncsheriffs.org\n\nIf you need anything else from me, please give me a call.\n\nThanks,\nTaylor Ellison\nLE Territory Sales Manager - NC/SC\n704-942-6362\nAnna - please connect with Felicia Roth at Bluffton PD so we can get this rolling - we are pushing to have this wrapped up by\nEOD tomorrow.\n\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\nflocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0092.pdf"},"e0835":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0835","title":"Have you registered for next weeks webinar_","frm":"Hayden at Flock Safety","date":"2024-08-14","text":"From:\nHayden at Flock Safety\nSent:\nWednesday, August 14, 2024 10:14:24 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nHave you registered for next weeks webinar?\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi,\nI wanted to reach out as I haven’t seen your registration for our upcoming webinar next Tuesday. We will be\nannouncing our newest product updates and features based on feedback from law enforcement agencies like\nyours.\nI hope you’re able to make it. You can save your spot here.\nSee you there,\nHayden\nP.S. Have a scheduling conflict? Go ahead and register, and we'll send you the recording after the event.","pdf":null},"e1134":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1134","title":"Flock Safety Contract for Council","frm":"Taylor Ellison","date":"2024-09-09","text":"From:\nTaylor Ellison\nSent:\nMonday, September 9, 2024 1:21:48 PM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph; Stormer, Tracye\nSubject:\nRe: Flock Safety Contract for Council\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nPlease see your new link below.  Let me know if you run into any issues again.\nhttps://planner.flocksafety.com/public/bebd2eeb-ed81-4102-b497-ba3018cf39c7?cat=d9701bcdf517\nTaylor\n704-942-6362\nOn Mon, Sep 9, 2024 at 1:13 PM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nTaylor this site has crashed and I cannot access it. Also could you include our CTO Tracye Stormer in on all correspondence\nmoving forward. He email is tstormer@townofbluffton.com\n\nThanks,\n\nJoe Babkiewicz\n\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, September 9, 2024 12:02 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock Safety Contract for Council\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\n\nPlease see the link below to your locations.  They will ultimately need your approval as well.\n\nOnce your review is complete, please approve the locations by entering your name in the designated box, and clicking the\n\"Approve\" button once for each location.\n\nOnce this is done and the contract has been signed, I will be able to process your order.\n\nhttps://planner.flocksafety.com/public/bebd2eeb-ed81-4102-b497-ba3018cf39c7?cat=99d8f5dca3c7\n\nGive me a call if you have any questions.\n\nThanks,\nTaylor Ellison\nLE Territory Sales Manager - NC/SC\n704-942-6362\n\nOn Mon, Sep 9, 2024 at 11:44 AM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood morning Taylor,\n\nCan you send me the locations that we picked out for the cameras. I don’t believe I ever got that list. I am meeting with\nsomeone a 1:00 to go over these locations. Also, I am meeting with Council tomorrow night to get the contract for firs phase\napproved.\n\nChief Joe Babkiewicz\n\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Friday, August 30, 2024 12:16 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Roth, Felicia <froth@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Flock Safety Contract for Council\n\nChief Babkiewicz and Felicia,\n\nI wanted to touch base since we are nearing the council date to approve Flock.  When would you like me to route the\ncontract over to the town manager for signature?\n\nIf there is anything else needed from me to prepare for council please let me know.\n\nThanks and have a great weekend,\n\nTaylor Ellison\nLE Territory Sales Manager - NC/SC\n704-942-6362\n\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\n flocksafety.com\n\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\n flocksafety.com\n\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item1134.pdf"},"e1137":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1137","title":"Flock - Council Follow Up","frm":"Taylor Ellison","date":"2024-09-11","text":"From:\nTaylor Ellison\nSent:\nWednesday, September 11, 2024 10:55:38 AM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph; Stormer, Tracye; Roth, Felicia\nSubject:\nFlock - Council Follow Up\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood morning All,\nI am following up on the council meeting last night.\nIf you are approved, I will need the name and contact information of the town manager so I can route the contract over for\nsignature.\nChief Babkiewicz will need to approve the locations on the deployment plan as well - I have linked it again in this email for\nconvenience.\nhttps://planner.flocksafety.com/public/bebd2eeb-ed81-4102-b497-ba3018cf39c7?cat=a30beb3d5e5d\nIf any of you have questions or need anything additional from Flock just let me know!\nTaylor Ellison\nLE Territory Sales Manager - NC/SC\n704-942-6362\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item1137.pdf"},"e0119":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0119","title":"Updated Flock Approval Link","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2024-09-13","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSent:\nFriday, September 13, 2024 12:26:40 PM\nTo:\nTaylor Ellison\nSubject:\nRE: Updated Flock Approval Link\nSensitivity:Normal\nDone. Thank you\n\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Friday, September 13, 2024 12:23 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Updated Flock Approval Link\n\nChief,\n\nPlease see the new link below\nhttps://planner.flocksafety.com/public/bebd2eeb-ed81-4102-b497-ba3018cf39c7?cat=ad1a26604ceb\n\nEnter your name in the designated box, and click the \"Approve\" button for EACH location.\n\nGive me a call if you have any more issues.\n\nTaylor\n704-942-6362\n\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e1089":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1089","title":"Needs Signature - Flock Safety Statement of Work","frm":"Roth, Felicia","date":"2024-09-16","text":"From:\nRoth, Felicia\nSent:\nMonday, September 16, 2024 4:15:30 PM\nTo:\nTaylor Ellison; Babkiewicz, Joseph\nCc:\nStormer, Tracye\nSubject:\nRE: Needs Signature - Flock Safety Statement of Work\nSensitivity:Normal\nHi Taylor,\n\nCan you please provide me a w9 for Flock so I can get y’all entered into our Financial system?  Many thanks!\n\nFelicia L. Roth, JD\nDirector of Compliance and Contracts\n\nTown of Bluffton\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nOffice: 843-7 06-7 816\nNEW mobile: 843-540-57 12\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, September 16, 2024 11:37 AM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Roth, Felicia <froth@townofbluffton.com>; Stormer, Tracye <tstormer@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Needs Signature - Flock Safety Statement of Work\n\nChief - understood!\n\nWhen we did our integrations call months ago, I believe we had already confirmed this, but by all means please\ndouble check.\n\nLet me know if there are any questions.\n\nThanks,\nTaylor\n704-942-6362\n\nOn Mon, Sep 16, 2024 at 11:32 AM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood morning Taylor,\n\nI am going to ask Felicia and Tracye (I have copied her on this email) to review this before signing. I am not sure if I\nneed to be the one signing this or someone else from the town. Once she looks it over and is good with it then we will\nreturn a signed copy.\n\nTracye my big questions for you in bridging 128 camera streams is to make sure our current cameras have the\nrequirements listed in this agreement. (able to support RTSP or ONVIF). I do not know the answer to that.\n\nChief Joe Babkiewicz\n\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Friday, September 13, 2024 12:52 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Needs Signature - Flock Safety Statement of Work\n\nChief,\n\nPlease see our statement of work for the FlockOS portion of the project.  We will need you to sign and return\nthis to us.\n\nLet me know if you have any questions.\n\nThanks,\nTaylor Ellison\nLE Territory Sales Manager - NC/SC\n704-942-6362\n\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\n flocksafety.com\n\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item1089.pdf"},"e0123":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0123","title":"Statement of Work","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2024-09-18","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSent:\nWednesday, September 18, 2024 8:34:40 AM\nTo:\nTaylor Ellison\nCc:\nRoth, Felicia\nSubject:\nStatement of Work\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:BlufftonPD_20240918_074019.pdf ;\nGood morning,\n\nPlease see attached. Thanks Taylor.\n\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nChief of Police\nOffice | 843-706-4537\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov","pdf":null},"e0124":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0124","title":"SC Chief's Conference","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2024-09-18","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSent:\nWednesday, September 18, 2024 12:14:05 PM\nTo:\nTaylor Ellison\nSubject:\nRE: SC Chief's Conference\nSensitivity:Normal\nNo unfortunately I will not be able to attend.\n\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Wednesday, September 18, 2024 12:08 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: SC Chief's Conference\n\nHey Chief,\n\nForgot to ask you on the phone this morning - will you be attending the SC Chief's conference next week in Myrtle\nBeach?\n\nTaylor\n704-942-6362\n\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0124.pdf"},"e1145":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1145","title":"Kickoff meeting","frm":"Taylor Ellison","date":"2024-09-23","text":"From:\nTaylor Ellison\nSent:\nMonday, September 23, 2024 8:24:04 AM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nRe: Kickoff meeting\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood morning Chief - I just sent you a calendar invite for 2:30pm this afternoon.  Look forward to seeing you then.\nTaylor\n704-942-6362\nOn Thu, Sep 19, 2024 at 7:34 AM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood morning Taylor,\nI spoke with our Team and it appears that Monday around 2:30-3:00 would be best for a kickoff meeting. Can we set\nsomething up for that date and time?\nChief Joe Babkiewicz\nSent from my iPhone\n\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0127":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0127","title":"Flock_Bluffton PD Kickoff Call","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2024-09-23","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph on behalf of: Taylor Ellison\nSent:\nMonday, September 23, 2024 8:40:49 AM\nTo:\nClarkson, Constance; James, Megan; Stormer, Tracye; Jones, Kim; Rooney, Pat; DuBose, Amanda; Charles,\nRobert; Ocasio, Peter\nSubject:\nFW: Flock/Bluffton PD Kickoff Call\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:attachment.ics ;invite.ics ;\n\nPlease see the below information for a kickoff meeting with Flock Today. I am sorry for the last minute notice but just\nheard from Taylor this morning.\n\n-----Original Appointment-----\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, September 23, 2024 8:23 AM\nTo: Taylor Ellison; Georgia Abdallah; Babkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject: Flock/Bluffton PD Kickoff Call\nWhen: Monday, September 23, 2024 2:30 PM-3:00 PM America/New_York.\nWhere:\n\n – 3 p m\n\nJoin Zoom Meeting\nflocksafety.zoom.us/j/88939278565\nID: 88939278565\nJoin by phone\n(US) +1 386-347-5053\nJoin using SIP\n88939278565@zoomcrc.com\nJoining instructions\nJoining notes\n------------\nZoom for G Suite Add-On Help\n------------\nWhen\nMonday Sep 23, 2024 ⋅ 2:30pm – 3pm (Eastern Time - New York)\nGuests\nTaylor Ellison - organizer\nGeorgia Abdallah\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nView all guest info\nReply for jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\n\nMeeting host:\ntaylor.ellison@flocksafety.com\nJoin Zoom Meeting:\nhttps://flocksafety.zoom.us/j/88939278565\nYes\nNo\nMaybe\nMore options\nInvitation from Google Calendar\nYou are receiving this email because you are an attendee on the event. To stop receiving future updates for this event, decline this event.\nForwarding this invitation could allow any recipient to send a response to the organizer, be added to the guest list, invite others regardless of their\nown invitation status, or modify your RSVP. Learn more","pdf":null},"e0130":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0130","title":"LPR Policy","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2024-09-23","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSent:\nMonday, September 23, 2024 2:58:19 PM\nTo:\nTaylor Ellison\nSubject:\nRE: LPR Policy\nSensitivity:Normal\nThank you Taylor\n\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, September 23, 2024 2:55 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: LPR Policy\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\n\nI just received this from Captain Caldwell at Garner PD - this is a copy of their LPR policy.\nhttps://public.powerdms.com/GARPD/tree/documents/2604110\n\nLet me know if you have any other questions or need anything else!\n\nThanks,\nTaylor Ellison\nLE Territory Sales Manager - NC/SC\n704-942-6362\n\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0131":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0131","title":"Flock_Bluffton PD Map Adjustments","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2024-09-30","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph on behalf of: Taylor Ellison\nSent:\nMonday, September 30, 2024 10:27:37 AM\nTo:\nClarkson, Constance; James, Megan; Stormer, Tracye; Rooney, Pat; DuBose, Amanda; Ocasio, Peter; Charles,\nRobert\nSubject:\nFW: Flock/Bluffton PD Map Adjustments\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:attachment.ics ;invite.ics ;\n\nTaylor from flock sent me this invite last week for the placement of the cameras. I became a little occupied with the\nHurricane and I forgot to send this out. Is anyone able to attend this meeting? If not I can reschedule. Please let me\nknow as soon as you can so I can let them know one way or the other. Thank you.\n\nChief\n\n-----Original Appointment-----\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, September 23, 2024 2:53 PM\nTo: Taylor Ellison; Babkiewicz, Joseph; Shelby Smith\nSubject: Flock/Bluffton PD Map Adjustments\nWhen: Monday, September 30, 2024 4:00 PM-5:00 PM America/New_York.\nWhere:\n\ne n t s\n – 5 p m\n\nJoin Zoom Meeting\nflocksafety.zoom.us/j/82249239463\nID: 82249239463\nJoin by phone\n(US) +1 346-248-7799\nJoin using SIP\n82249239463@zoomcrc.com\nJoining instructions\nJoining notes\n------------\nWhen\nMonday Sep 30, 2024 ⋅ 4pm – 5pm (Eastern Time - New York)\nGuests\nTaylor Ellison - organizer\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nShelby Smith\nView all guest info\nReply for jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\n\nZoom for G Suite Add-On Help\n------------\nMeeting host:\ntaylor.ellison@flocksafety.com\nJoin Zoom Meeting:\nhttps://flocksafety.zoom.us/j/82249239463\nYes\nNo\nMaybe\nMore options\nInvitation from Google Calendar\nYou are receiving this email because you are an attendee on the event. To stop receiving future updates for this event, decline this event.\nForwarding this invitation could allow any recipient to send a response to the organizer, be added to the guest list, invite others regardless of their\nown invitation status, or modify your RSVP. Learn more","pdf":null},"e1147":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1147","title":"Flock Camera Adjustments","frm":"Taylor Ellison","date":"2024-09-23","text":"From:\nTaylor Ellison\nSent:\nMonday, September 23, 2024 2:59:27 PM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nFlock Camera Adjustments\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHey Chief,\nPer my deployment specialists request, if you could let us know which locations are outside of your jurisdiction, Shelby can go\nahead and start looking for alternate locations between now and next week - just to have some ideas in place.\nLet me know your thoughts.\nTaylor\n704-942-6362\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item1147.pdf"},"e0673":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0673","title":"Kickoff Call Follow Up - Flock Safety + Bluffton PD","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2024-10-24","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nThursday, October 24, 2024 3:45:54 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nRe: Kickoff Call Follow Up - Flock Safety + Bluffton PD\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nI hope all is well. Following up to see if we can get our admin training scheduled for this week or next. If you have some time,\nplease click here to schedule that call.\nThanks,\nGeorgia\nOn Wed, Oct 2, 2024 at 1:01 PM Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nGood Afternoon,\nI hope all is well. Following up to see if we can get our admin training scheduled for this week or next. If you have some time,\nplease click here to schedule that call.\nThanks,\nGeorgia\nOn Mon, Sep 23, 2024 at 3:00 PM Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nGood Afternoon,\nThanks for your time earlier today. I attached the deck from our call here for reference.\nPlease click here to schedule our admin training call. In the meantime, you can access our Admin Training Guide to begin\nexploring the system.\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n--\n\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSenior Customer Success Manager\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSenior Customer Success Manager\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSenior Customer Success Manager\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0206":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0206","title":"Flock Safety INV-47807","frm":"Billing Team","date":"2024-09-27","text":"From:\nBilling Team\nSent:\nFriday, September 27, 2024 1:15:13 AM\nTo:\nDonald Chandler; Joseph Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nFlock Safety INV-47807\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:invoice-INV-47807.pdf ;Flock_Payment_Info.pdf ;W-9_Flock_Safety.pdf ;2024_COI_Flock_Safety.pdf ;\n\nFlock Safety Customer,\nThank you for choosing Flock Safety. You recently should have received an invoice. If you have not received an invoice\nplease email\nbilling@flocksafety.com.\nAttached you will find our W-9, payment options, and Flocks general COI. If you require further documentation please\ncontact us before the invoice is due.\nPlease visit http://help.flocksafety.com/\n for self-help articles and FAQ.\nYour business is greatly appreciated.\nFlock Safety\n[CM015c1-6ed0]\n--\nPowered by Tesorio","pdf":null},"e1081":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1081","title":"Meeting for placement_locations of cameras","frm":"Ocasio, Peter","date":"2024-09-30","text":"From:\nOcasio, Peter\nSent:\nMonday, September 30, 2024 3:08:59 PM\nTo:\nRooney, Pat; Charles, Robert; Babkiewicz, Joseph\nCc:\nClarkson, Constance; James, Megan; Stormer, Tracye; Jones, Kim; DuBose, Amanda; Taylor Ellison\nSubject:\nRE: Meeting for placement/locations of cameras\nSensitivity:Normal\nThat works for me also.\n\nPeter Ocasio\nNetwork Administrator\n\nOffice | 843-706-4565\nCell | 843-540-3782\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Rooney, Pat <prooney@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Monday, September 30, 2024 2:52 PM\nTo: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>; James, Megan <mjames@townofbluffton.com>; Stormer, Tracye\n<tstormer@townofbluffton.com>; Jones, Kim <kjones@townofbluffton.com>; DuBose, Amanda\n<adubose@townofbluffton.com>; Ocasio, Peter <pocasio@townofbluffton.com>; Taylor Ellison\n<taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: RE: Meeting for placement/locations of cameras\n\nWorks for me also.\n\nFrom: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Monday, September 30, 2024 1:30 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>; James, Megan <mjames@townofbluffton.com>; Stormer, Tracye\n<tstormer@townofbluffton.com>; Jones, Kim <kjones@townofbluffton.com>; Rooney, Pat <prooney@townofbluffton.com>;\nDuBose, Amanda <adubose@townofbluffton.com>; Ocasio, Peter <pocasio@townofbluffton.com>; Taylor Ellison\n<taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: Meeting for placement/locations of cameras\n\nThis will work for me Chief.\n\nBob\n\nRobert Charles\nLaw Enforcement Technical Analyst\n\nOffice | 843-706-7814\n\nTown of Bluffton | Police Department\nPO Box 386\n101 Progressive Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nOn Sep 30, 2024, at 1:19 PM, Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood morning,\n\nThere was a meeting invite I sent out for today at 4:00. Taylor is unavailable at this time and asked if we\ncould reschedule this meeting. I would like to reschedule the meeting for this Thursday, October 3, 2024 at\n3:00. Please let me know if that works for everyone. Thank you.\n\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nChief of Police\nOffice | 843-706-4537\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\n<image001.png>\n<image002.png>","pdf":null},"e0277":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0277","title":"Flock Meeting for Placement_Locations of Cameras","frm":"Clarkson, Constance","date":"2024-09-30","text":"From:\nClarkson, Constance\nSent:\nMonday, September 30, 2024 2:21:03 PM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph; James, Megan; Stormer, Tracye; Jones, Kim; Rooney, Pat; DuBose, Amanda; Ocasio,\nPeter; Charles, Robert; Taylor Ellison\nSubject:\nFlock Meeting for Placement/Locations of Cameras\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:attachment.ics ;\n_____________________________________________\nFrom: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Monday, September 30, 2024 2:06 PM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>; James, Megan <mjames@townofbluffton.com>; Stormer, Tracye\n<tstormer@townofbluffton.com>; Jones, Kim <kjones@townofbluffton.com>; Rooney, Pat <prooney@townofbluffton.com>;\nDuBose, Amanda <adubose@townofbluffton.com>; Ocasio, Peter <pocasio@townofbluffton.com>; Charles, Robert\n<rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: RE: Meeting for placement/locations of cameras\n\nTaylor,\n\ncan you please schedule a 3:00 this Thursday for all of us to attend. Thank you\n\nChief\n\nFrom: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Monday, September 30, 2024 1:39 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; James, Megan <mjames@townofbluffton.com>; Stormer, Tracye\n<tstormer@townofbluffton.com>; Jones, Kim <kjones@townofbluffton.com>; Rooney, Pat <prooney@townofbluffton.com>;\nDuBose, Amanda <adubose@townofbluffton.com>; Ocasio, Peter <pocasio@townofbluffton.com>; Charles, Robert\n<rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: Meeting for placement/locations of cameras\n\nWorks for my schedule Chief. Thank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Monday, September 30, 2024 1:19:48 PM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>; James, Megan <mjames@townofbluffton.com>; Stormer, Tracye\n<tstormer@townofbluffton.com>; Jones, Kim <kjones@townofbluffton.com>; Rooney, Pat <prooney@townofbluffton.com>;\nDuBose, Amanda <adubose@townofbluffton.com>; Ocasio, Peter <pocasio@townofbluffton.com>; Charles, Robert\n<rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Meeting for placement/locations of cameras\n\nGood morning,\n\nThere was a meeting invite I sent out for today at 4:00. Taylor is unavailable at this time and asked if we could\nreschedule this meeting. I would like to reschedule the meeting for this Thursday, October 3, 2024 at 3:00. Please let\nme know if that works for everyone. Thank you.\n\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nChief of Police\nOffice | 843-706-4537\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov","pdf":null},"e0896":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0896","title":"Flock Camera Placement_Locations","frm":"James, Megan","date":"2024-10-01","text":"From:\nJames, Megan\nSent:\nTuesday, October 1, 2024 11:00:31 AM\nTo:\nClarkson, Constance; Rooney, Pat; DuBose, Amanda; Ocasio, Peter; Charles, Robert; Babkiewicz, Joseph;\ntaylor.ellison@flocksafety.com\nSubject:\nFlock Camera Placement/Locations\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:attachment.ics ;\n\nJoin Zoom Meeting\nflocksafety.zoom.us/j/82249239463\nID: 82249239463\nJoin by phone\n(US) +1 346-248-7799\nJoin using SIP\n82249239463@zoomcrc.com\nJoining instructions\nJoining notes\nMeeting host: taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com\nJoin Zoom Meeting:\nhttps://flocksafety.zoom.us/j/82249239463\nWhen\nThursday Oct 3, 2024 ⋅ 3pm – 4pm (Eastern Time - New York)\nGuests\nTaylor Ellison - organizer\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nShelby Smith\nJessica Khokhlan\nmjames@townofbluffton.com\nView all guest info\nReply for mjames@townofbluffton.com\nYes\nNo\nMaybe\nMore options","pdf":null},"e0236":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0236","title":"Flock Safety - SC - Bluffton PD Phase 1 - Project Update","frm":"Charmissha Hamlin","date":"2024-10-14","text":"From:\nCharmissha Hamlin\nSent:\nMonday, October 14, 2024 3:11:14 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nCc:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSubject:\nRe: Flock Safety - SC - Bluffton PD Phase 1 - Project Update\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood afternoon,\nI am following up on the progress obtaining permission letters.  Please let me know if you have any questions.\nThank you,\nCharmissha Hamlin\nProject Manager\n 404.549.5545\n flocksafety.com\nOn Wed, Oct 2, 2024 at 4:26 PM Charmissha Hamlin <charmissha.hamlin@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nGood afternoon,\nSorry I missed the kick-off call while on PTO last week.  My name is Charmissha, a project manager here at Flock, I will be your\nprimary point of contact moving forward throughout the installation process to ensure you are set up for success!  I'm so excited to\nwork with you to get your community up and running with Flock Safety.\nCurrently locations are pending permission letters from Private Property owners, City or County permits, or attachment approval\nfrom the power company.  I have listed below each location and whom I would need a permission letter from.  I have attached an\nexample of a private property permission letter for locations installing on private property.  The City or County locations, if you\nhave someone who would give approval stating no permit is required, I can move forward with those locations.  If not, we would\napply for a permit with the jurisdiction and wait on approval.  I have attached an example of a No Permit Required letter.  Lasty,\n\nwe would need approval from Palmetto Electric to install on their poles to move forward with those locations.  Please let me know\nif you have any questions.\nI have attached the AC power handout you can share with your electrician for all locations using AC power.\nName\nAddress\nPermit Jurisdiction\n#01 Buckwalter Pkwy @ Fording Island Rd SB\n790 Buckwalter Pkwy, Bluffton, SC 29910, United States\nBluffton (City of)\n#02 Simmonsville Rd @ Hwy 278 SB\n10 Simmonsville Rd, Bluffton, SC 29910, United States\nLOWCOUNTRY PRESBYTERIAN CHURCH\n#03 Buck Island @ Jennifer Ct NB\n391 Buck Island Rd, Bluffton, SC 29910-5947, United States\nMICHAEL BRADLEY HOLDINGS LLC\n#04 S Okatie Hwy @ Palmetto Pt EB\n31 Palmetto Pt, Hardeeville, SC 29927, United States\nSCOTT CLYDE F\n#05 Route 170 E @ May River Crossing\n3521 Okatie Hwy, Bluffton, SC 29910, United States\nPR II MAY RIVER CROSSING LLC\n#06 Bluffton Pkwy EB @ Route 170\n4324 Bluffton Pkwy, Bluffton, SC 29910, United States\nBluffton (City of)\n#07 170 WB @ Sun City\n22 Saint Andrews Ln, Bluffton, SC 29909-4584, United States\nSUN CITY HILTON HEAD COMMUNITY ASSOCIATION GENNY\nSCRIVNE\n#08 Buckwalter Pkwy NB @ May River\n876 May River Rd, Bluffton, SC 29910-7024, United States\nBeaufort County (County of)\n#09 Bluffton Pkwy WB @ Bluffton Rd\n100 Bluffton Rd, Bluffton, SC 29910, United States\nBeaufort County (County of)\n#10 Bluffton Rd SB @ Bluffton Pkwy\n102 Bluffton Rd, Bluffton, SC 29910, United States\nBEAUFORT COUNTY\n#11May River Rd EB @ Dubois Rd\n1276 May River Rd, Bluffton, SC 29910, United States\nPalmetto Electric\n#12 Bluffton Pkwy WB @ Buckwalter Pkwy\n410 Buckwalter Pkwy, Bluffton, SC 29910, United States\nBluffton (City of)\n#13 Buckwalter Pkwy NB @ Bluffton Pkwy\n365 Buckwalter Pkwy, Bluffton, SC 29910, United States\nBluffton (City of)\n#14 Buck Island Rd SB @ Old Carolina\n117 Buck Island Rd, Bluffton, SC 29910-5927, United States\nHILTON HEAD SPORTS SERVICES LLC\n#15 Bluffton Rd SB @ Kitty's Crossing\n164 Bluffton Rd, Bluffton, SC 29910, United States\nPalmetto Electric\n#16 Simmonsville Rd SB @ Bluffton Pkwy\n2 Billy Simmons Dr, Bluffton, SC 29910, United States\nBOLDEN FRED A\n#17 Buck Island Rd SB @ Bluffton Pkwy\n134 Buck Island Rd, Bluffton, SC 29910, United States\nBluffton (City of)\nC#01 Bluffton Pkwy @ Buckwalter Pkwy\n410 Bluffton Pkwy, Bluffton, SC 29910, United States\nBeaufort County (County of)\nC#02 Buckwalter Pkwy @ Hwy 278\n790 Buckwalter Pkwy, Bluffton, SC 29910, United States\nBEAUFORT COUNTY\nC#03 Bluffton Pkwy @ Route 170\n106 Okatie Hwy, Bluffton, SC 29910, United States\nBEAUFORT COUNTY\nC#04 Route 46 @ Route 170\n3600 Okatie Hwy, Bluffton, SC 29910, United States\nPalmetto Electric\nCharmissha Hamlin\nProject Manager\n 404.549.5545\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0236.pdf"},"e0669":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0669","title":"Introducing Flock's Next Chapter in Public Safety Innovation","frm":"Garrett at Flock Safety","date":"2024-10-16","text":"From:\nGarrett at Flock Safety\nSent:\nWednesday, October 16, 2024 9:07:38 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nIntroducing Flock's Next Chapter in Public Safety Innovation\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nView in Browser  |  Forward to a Friend\nDear Joseph,\nYou’ve told our team time and time again that you need cutting-edge tools that help you\nstop crime and keep communities safe. Today, we’re excited to share the next chapter in\nthat mission.\nWe’re All In on Drones as a First Responder (DFR).\nWe’ve acquired Aerodome, a pioneer in Drones as a First Responder technology. They\nhave by far the most intuitive and powerful DFR software on the planet. And with Flock’s\nexpertise in hardware, computer vision, and commitment to launch new features based\non your input, the future of real-time policing just became real.\n\nImagine, you receive a gunshot alert from your fleet of Raven devices and you’re not\nsure if patrol can get there in time. With DFR, you’ll get eyes on the scene in seconds,\nsaving lives and making arrests. Or you pull over a vehicle associated with a hot list hit\nfrom your Flock LPR, and the suspect decides to run, but a chase gets called off for\nbeing too dangerous. DFR will keep eyes on the suspect vehicle until you find a safer\nplace to intercept. And just like today, your entire team will be able to see that info\nwherever you need it - from a computer screen in Dispatch to the officer’s MDT or mobile\ndevice. Flock drones will integrate seamlessly with all of Flock’s existing tools, so your\nofficers and deputies will know exactly the risks and challenges of the scene ahead.\nWe are building the future of public safety, together—where rapid response becomes the\nstandard, and incidents can be addressed in real-time.\nWhat does this mean for you?\nYou already know about FlockOS, the most powerful real-time policing software that\nsupports thousands of agencies across the country. And starting in 2025, we’ll be\nlaunching a fleet of American-made, NDAA compliant drones designed specifically for\nlaw enforcement needs. The best part? We're growing our team.\nWith this acquisition, we’re not only expanding our product lineup, but also investing\nheavily in your future. We’re hiring over a hundred world-class engineers — experts who\nwill help us refine and enhance every aspect of our technology. This means more\ninnovation, better service, and faster response times to your needs.\nWhat’s next?\nOver the coming months, we’ll be sharing more details about the launch of our drone\nprogram, how it integrates with your current Flock systems, and what you can expect in\n2025. We’re excited for the future, and we can’t wait to bring these innovations to your\ndepartment.\nWant to learn more? Head to our booth at IACP or sign up for our DFR webinar on\nNovember 13.\nThank you for your continued trust in Flock Safety. Together, we’re not just solving\ncrimes—we’re preventing them.\nOnward,\nGarrett Langley\nCEO, Flock Safety\nFlock Safety\n1170 Howell Mill Rd NW, Suite 210\nAtlanta, Georgia 30318, United States","pdf":null},"e0142":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0142","title":"I0001 Flock Camera - Information Request","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2024-10-31","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSent:\nThursday, October 31, 2024 1:49:57 PM\nTo:\nClarkson, Constance\nCc:\nTaylor Ellison\nSubject:\nRe: I0001 Flock Camera - Information Request\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:image001.png ;image002.png ;\nConstance,\nWill this statement from me work?\n“We are reaching out to request your permission to install Flock Safety cameras on your property. These cameras are a\ncrucial tool in tracking vehicles entering and exiting our town, allowing us to identify vehicles that may have been\ninvolved in criminal activities.\nBy allowing us to place these cameras on your property, you will be supporting an initiative designed to enhance the\nsafety and security of our entire community. This proactive approach helps deter crime and ensures a safer\nenvironment for residents, businesses, and visitors alike.\nWe are happy to answer any questions you may have about the cameras, their placement, or how the data is utilized to\nprotect our town. Thank you for considering this important partnership to make our community safer.”\nThanks,\nChief\nSent from my iPhone\nOn Oct 31, 2024, at 1:29 PM, Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood afternoon Chief and Taylor.\n\nThis is just a follow up to the below email.  We are still in need of the brief summary that Amanda can use\nin her communications to the property owners requesting they meet with you to discuss the needed\neasement.\n\nPlease advise if you can forward the summary by next Tuesday, November 5.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\n\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\n<image001.png>\n<image002.png>\n\nFrom: Clarkson, Constance\nSent: Friday, October 18, 2024 12:27 PM\nTo: Roth, Felicia <froth@townofbluffton.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Taylor\nEllison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>; charmissha.hamlin@flocksafety.com\nCc: Stormer, Tracye <tstormer@townofbluffton.com>; Jones, Kim <kjones@townofbluffton.com>; Rooney, Pat\n<prooney@townofbluffton.com>; DuBose, Amanda <adubose@townofbluffton.com>; Ocasio, Peter\n<pocasio@townofbluffton.com>; Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: I0001 Flock Camera - Information Request\n\nGood morning.\n\nFelicia – Attached is the draft Easement Agreement to the private property owners for this project.\nAmanda has revised our standard lighting easement agreement to accommodate the camera scope.\nPlease add this to the 10/22/24 legal meeting on Tuesday for review and approval by Richardson.\n\nChief and Taylor – The Easement List tab of the attached spreadsheet lists the 11 private property\nowners.  Please reply by Wednesday, 10/30/24 with a brief summary that Amanda can use in her\ncommunications to the property owners requesting they meet with you.  To help with scheduling, please\nalso include any dates you definitely cannot meet.\n\nCharmissha – The Easement List has three locations (highlighted in yellow) which need clarification, it is\nuncertain if the pole is located in the ROW or on private property.  We prefer to have it in the ROW.\nPlease adjust the pin on the GIS map and advise by Wednesday, 10/30/24, if possible.\n\nThank you all for your time.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\n<image001.png>\n<image002.png>","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0142.pdf"},"e0137":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0137","title":"Flock Safety Dinner 10_19","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2024-10-19","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSent:\nSaturday, October 19, 2024 12:02:30 PM\nTo:\nTaylor Ellison\nSubject:\nRe: Flock Safety Dinner 10/19\nSensitivity:Normal\nTaylor,\nI am not going to be able to make it, my son is flying into the city today and we are going to take him out. Thank you for the offer\nand I will hopefully see you tomorrow at the exhibit hall.\n Chief Joe Babkiewicz\nSent from my iPhone\nOn Oct 19, 2024, at 10:30 AM, Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com> wrote:\n\nGood morning Everyone,\nI just wanted to write you all a quick reminder for our dinner this evening at Davio's Northern Italian Steakhouse.\nThe address is 26 Fan Pier Boulevard, Boston MA, 02210\nI look forward to seeing you all there!\nTaylor Ellison\nLE Territory Sales Manager - NC/SC\n704-942-6362\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nTerritory Sales Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0137.pdf"},"e0283":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0283","title":"(no subject)","frm":"Clarkson, Constance","date":"2024-10-22","text":"From:\nClarkson, Constance on behalf of: Charmissha Hamlin\nSent:\nTuesday, October 22, 2024 9:04:16 AM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nFW: ✨SC - Bluffton PD - Charmissha/Shelby Mapping Call\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:attachment.ics ;invite.ics ;\n\n-----Original Appointment-----\nFrom: Charmissha Hamlin <charmissha.hamlin@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, October 21, 2024 1:31 PM\nTo: Charmissha Hamlin; Clarkson, Constance; Shelby Smith; Heather Phillips\nCc: DuBose, Amanda\nSubject: ✨SC - Bluffton PD - Charmissha/Shelby Mapping Call\nWhen: Thursday, October 31, 2024 10:30 AM-11:30 AM America/New_York.\nWhere:\n\n✨\nm\n\nThis event has been updated\nChanged: title\n\nEvent name: Charmissha/Shelby Mapping Call\nhttps://us-5372.join.gong.io/flock-safety/charmissha.hamlin?tkn=gM-U7q-EQO2NLmmR39XD4g\nNeed to make changes to this event?\nReschedule: https://www.getclockwise.com/booking/d5f82ef410a3454da49a0a423e514da1/reschedule\nCancel: https://www.getclockwise.com/booking/d5f82ef410a3454da49a0a423e514da1/cancel\n…\n✨This meeting was scheduled with Clockwise, which finds the best time to meet, based on your Focus Time\n\nneeds and calendar preferences.\nWhen\nThursday Oct 31, 2024 ⋅ 10:30am – 11:30am (Eastern Time - New York)\nGuests\nCharmissha Hamlin - organizer\ncclarkson@townofbluffton.com\nShelby Smith\nHeather Phillips\nadubose@townofbluffton.com - optional\nView all guest info\nReply for cclarkson@townofbluffton.com\nYes\nNo\nMaybe\nMore options\nInvitation from Google Calendar\nYou are receiving this email because you are an attendee on the event. To stop receiving future updates for this event, decline this event.\nForwarding this invitation could allow any recipient to send a response to the organizer, be added to the guest list, invite others regardless of their\nown invitation status, or modify your RSVP. Learn more","pdf":null},"e0140":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0140","title":"Flock Safety + Bluffton PD - Admin Training","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2024-10-29","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph on behalf of: Georgia Abdallah\nSent:\nTuesday, October 29, 2024 12:36:19 PM\nTo:\nBPD_Commandstaff\nSubject:\nFW: Flock Safety + Bluffton PD - Admin Training\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:attachment.ics ;invite.ics ;\n\nThis is an administrative class for the Flock Cameras.\n\n-----Original Appointment-----\nFrom: Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, October 29, 2024 11:54 AM\nTo: Georgia Abdallah; Babkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject: Flock Safety + Bluffton PD - Admin Training\nWhen: Thursday, November 14, 2024 9:15 AM-10:00 AM America/New_York.\nWhere:\n\n – 1 0 a m\n\nJoin Gong Meeting\n//us-5372.join.gong.io/flock-safet...\nID: 2391866234342538594\nJoining notes\nClick the link to enter the meeting or view\ndial-in options\nWhen\nThursday Nov 14, 2024 ⋅ 9:15am – 10am (Eastern Time - New\nYork)\nGuests\nGeorgia Abdallah - organizer\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nView all guest info\nReply for jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nYes\nNo\nMaybe\nMore options\n\nInvitation from Google Calendar\nYou are receiving this email because you are an attendee on the event. To stop receiving future updates for this event, decline this event.\nForwarding this invitation could allow any recipient to send a response to the organizer, be added to the guest list, invite others regardless of their\nown invitation status, or modify your RSVP. Learn more","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0140.pdf"},"e0248":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0248","title":"I0001 Flock Camera - Information Request - Bluffton BPD","frm":"Charmissha Hamlin","date":"2024-11-04","text":"From:\nCharmissha Hamlin\nSent:\nMonday, November 4, 2024 9:32:44 PM\nTo:\nClarkson, Constance\nCc:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph; DuBose, Amanda; Georgia Abdallah; heather.phillips@flocksafety.com\nSubject:\nRe: I0001 Flock Camera - Information Request - Bluffton BPD\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood evening,\nYes, Lat and Long will update based on new locations.  I will sit tight until I hear back from you.\nThank you,\nCharmissha Hamlin\nProject Manager\n 404.549.5545\n flocksafety.com\nOn Mon, Nov 4, 2024 at 5:15 PM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood afternoon Charmissha.\n\nThank you for the specifications and below.\n\nFollow up:\n\n1. As we moved cameras slightly to different locations on the deployment map, please confirm the latitudes and\nlongitudes automatically updated as well.\n2. I understand with C#02 being changed to solar, we now only have three locations which will require new wiring, C#01,\nC#03, and C#04.\n3. For the list provided below, Amanda is confirming the actual property owners as we will still need to obtain easements\nfrom them before Dominion or Palmetto will consider our application for a pole attachment.  To that point, please wait\nuntil the confirmation is complete as there may be more to add to the encroachment permit packages.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Charmissha Hamlin <charmissha.hamlin@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Friday, November 1, 2024 1:44 PM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: I0001 Flock Camera - Information Request - Bluffton BPD\n\nGood afternoon,\n\nBelow is the breakdown from our call yesterday.  Please let me know if you have any questions.\n\nNext Steps:\nYour team will work on obtaining private property permission letters for all locations on private property (example letter\nattached)\nYou will submit the request to Dominion to attach to their poles (specs attached)\nYou will reach out to Palmetto Electric to inquire about attaching to their poles and submit request (if applicable)\nIf they deny attachment we will review other locations (private property)\nMy team will submit permit applications for all Town and County locations\nBelow are all locations and the property owners.  Please review and approve the updated Deployment Plan.\n\nLocation Name\nPole Type Property Owner\n#01 Buckwalter Pkwy @ Fording Island Rd SB Flock Pole Beaufort County\n#02 Simmonsville Rd @ Hwy 278 SB\nFlock Pole LOWCOUNTRY PRESBYTERIAN CHURCH\n#03 Buck Island @ Jennifer Ct NB\nFlock Pole MICHAEL BRADLEY HOLDINGS LLC\n#04 S Okatie Hwy @ Palmetto Pt EB\nUtility Pole Dominion Power\n#05 Route 170 E @ May River Crossing\nFlock Pole PR II MAY RIVER CROSSING LLC\n#06 Bluffton Pkwy EB @ Route 170\nFlock Pole Beaufort County\n#07 170 WB @ Cypres Ridge\nFlock Pole Town of Bluffton\n#08 Buckwalter Pkwy NB @ May River\nFlock Pole Beaufort County\n#08 May River @ Red Cedar WB\nFlock Pole Beaufort County\n#09 Bluffton Pkwy WB @ Goethe Rd\nFlock Pole Beaufort County\n#10 Bluffton Rd SB @ Burnt Church Distillery\nFlock Pole BC DISTILLERY HOLDINGS LLC\n#11 May River Rd EB @ Dubois Rd\nUtility Pole Palmetto Electric\n#12 Bluffton Pkwy WB @ Buckwalter Pkwy\nFlock Pole Beaufort County\n#13 Buckwalter Pkwy NB @ Bluffton Pkwy\nFlock Pole Beaufort County\n#14 Buck Island Rd SB @ Old Carolina\nFlock Pole HILTON HEAD SPORTS SERVICES LLC\n#15 Bluffton Rd SB @ Sea Smiles\nUtility Pole Palmetto Electric\n#16 Simmonsville Rd SB @ Bluffton Pkwy\nFlock Pole BOLDEN FRED A\n#17 Buck Island Rd SB @ Bluffton Pkwy\nFlock Pole Beaufort County\nC#01 Bluffton Pkwy @ Buckwalter Pkwy\nUtility Pole Need to verify pole owner\nC#02 Buckwalter Pkwy @ Hwy 278\nC#03 Bluffton Pkwy @ Route 170\nC#04 Route 46 @ Route 170\nUtility Pole Palmetto Electric\n\nCharmissha Hamlin\nProject Manager\n 404.549.5545\n flocksafety.com\n\nOn Thu, Oct 31, 2024 at 1:59 PM Charmissha Hamlin <charmissha.hamlin@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nThank you for the understanding. I will send in the morning.\n\nThank you,\nCharmissha Hamlin\nProject Manager\n 404.549.5545\n flocksafety.com\n\nOn Thu, Oct 31, 2024 at 12:48 PM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nCharmissha, no worries at all really.  And the recap can wait until your back, no need to work on it tonight.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Charmissha Hamlin <charmissha.hamlin@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, October 31, 2024 12:18 PM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>; Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: FW: I0001 Flock Camera - Information Request - Bluffton BPD\n\nGood afternoon,\n\nThanks for meeting with us this morning.  I will be sending the recap this evening.  I actually have time off this afternoon and will\n\nsend my full follow up this evening.\n\nThank you,\nCharmissha Hamlin\nProject Manager\n 404.549.5545\n flocksafety.com\n\nOn Wed, Oct 23, 2024 at 12:56 PM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nThan you Charmissha.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Charmissha Hamlin <charmissha.hamlin@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Wednesday, October 23, 2024 12:52 PM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>; Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: FW: I0001 Flock Camera - Information Request - Bluffton BPD\n\nGood afternoon,\n\nPlease see below.  Let me know if you have any questions.\n\n1. Since the Falcon’s are solar, do they require any electrical or wiring from the Town’s electrician? - Solar does\nnot require any electrical work/wiring\n2. Does Flock install the poles and camera equipment at the same time? - Yes, we install typically install pole and\ncamera at the same time unless there are circumstances preventing\nThank you,\nCharmissha Hamlin\nProject Manager\n\n 404.549.5545\n flocksafety.com\n\nOn Wed, Oct 23, 2024 at 9:49 AM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood morning Charmissha.\n\nThank you for the attachments.\n\n1. Since the Falcon’s are solar, do they require any electrical or wiring from the Town’s electrician?\n2. Does Flock install the poles and camera equipment at the same time?\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Charmissha Hamlin <charmissha.hamlin@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, October 22, 2024 1:28 PM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: FW: I0001 Flock Camera - Information Request - Bluffton BPD\n\nGood afternoon,\n\nSorry for the delay.  It's been a day of back to back meetings.  Please see attached.  Let me know if you have any questions.\n\nThank you,\nCharmissha Hamlin\nProject Manager\n 404.549.5545\n flocksafety.com\n\nOn Tue, Oct 22, 2024 at 9:23 AM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood afternoon.\n\nI’m meeting with our electrical engineer and need to know the power requirements for the condor equipment.  Do\nthe falcon’s need any electrical or wiring at all?\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\n\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Clarkson, Constance\nSent: Friday, October 18, 2024 12:27 PM\nTo: Roth, Felicia <froth@townofbluffton.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Taylor\nEllison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>; charmissha.hamlin@flocksafety.com\nCc: Stormer, Tracye <tstormer@townofbluffton.com>; Jones, Kim <kjones@townofbluffton.com>; Rooney, Pat\n<prooney@townofbluffton.com>; DuBose, Amanda <adubose@townofbluffton.com>; Ocasio, Peter\n<pocasio@townofbluffton.com>; Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: I0001 Flock Camera - Information Request\n\nGood morning.\n\nFelicia – Attached is the draft Easement Agreement to the private property owners for this project.  Amanda has\nrevised our standard lighting easement agreement to accommodate the camera scope.  Please add this to the\n10/22/24 legal meeting on Tuesday for review and approval by Richardson.\n\nChief and Taylor – The Easement List tab of the attached spreadsheet lists the 11 private property owners.\nPlease reply by Wednesday, 10/30/24 with a brief summary that Amanda can use in her communications to the\nproperty owners requesting they meet with you.  To help with scheduling, please also include any dates you\ndefinitely cannot meet.\n\nCharmissha – The Easement List has three locations (highlighted in yellow) which need clarification, it is\nuncertain if the pole is located in the ROW or on private property.  We prefer to have it in the ROW.  Please\nadjust the pin on the GIS map and advise by Wednesday, 10/30/24, if possible.\n\nThank you all for your time.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov","pdf":null},"e1166":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1166","title":"Action Required_ Complete Your Flock Safety Account Activation","frm":"hello=flocksafety.com@mail.flocksafety.com","date":"2024-11-14","text":"From:\nhello=flocksafety.com@mail.flocksafety.com on behalf of: hello@flocksafety.com\nSent:\nThursday, November 14, 2024 9:15:58 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nAction Required: Complete Your Flock Safety Account Activation\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nWelcome to the Flock.\nYour Flock Safety account is now active. Please click the box below within the next 96\nhours to create your account.\n\nCREATE YOUR ACCOUNT\n\nAfter 96 hours, this link will expire. If 96 hours have passed, please click here.\nBe sure to save the website to your bookmarks or favorites for easy future access. If\nyou ever have any questions, our Customer Support team is always here for you.\n\nProblems or questions?\n\nsupport@flocksafety.com\n+1 (866) 901-1781","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item1166.pdf"},"e0677":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0677","title":"Admin Training Follow Up - Flock Safety + Bluffton PD","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2024-11-18","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nMonday, November 18, 2024 10:00:41 AM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nRe: Admin Training Follow Up - Flock Safety + Bluffton PD\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nYes, typically Admins and CID have access too all available networks but a lot of the time, departments will limit patrol access to\nonly the surrounding area. I went ahead and updated the admin and CID role - let me know if you'd like me to update the other\ntwo as well.\nOn Mon, Nov 18, 2024 at 8:54 AM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nI wasn’t sure what other departments have done. I don’t have an issue of giving all groups access to all the cameras. Is that what\nmost other agencies do? If so then I would be good with giving everyone the same access to all the cameras.\n\nFrom: Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, November 18, 2024 8:45 AM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Admin Training Follow Up - Flock Safety + Bluffton PD\n\nGood Morning,\n\nI hope you had a great weekend. As an update, Pine Ridge Property Owners association, Villages at Palmetto\nPointe, and Coosaw Point POA have all shared their cameras with you. I'm still waiting to hear back on a few\nother private cameras in the area.\n\nBased on your current setup, Admins has access to 201 networks and then CID, Patrol and School Resource\n\nOfficers only have access to 5 networks. You'll need to add any new networks to all the roles that should be able\nto access them at least once a week to keep it updated. I can do a bulk update for you if you let me know which\nroles should have access to all available networks.\n\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n\nOn Thu, Nov 14, 2024 at 2:01 PM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood afternoon Georgia,\n\nA quick question that I have as  I a setting up roles. Do ost agencies allow access to all networks for everyone or just the local\nones. I have it broken down into 4 groups (Admin, CID, Patrol, and SRO’s) and I wasn’t sure if all roles would have access to\nall networks that share with us. Thoughts?\n\nChief Joe Babkiewicz\n\nFrom: Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, November 14, 2024 10:52 AM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Burke, Helen <hburke@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Admin Training Follow Up - Flock Safety + Bluffton PD\n\nGood Morning,\n\nThanks for your time this morning. I requested access to Pine Ridge Property Owners association, Villages at Palmetto\nPointe, Habersham Neighborhood Association, Coosaw Point POA, and Fripp Island POA on your behalf. You'll get\nnotified as they share with you.\n\nIn order for me to bulk add your users, please format your CSV file with the headers in the following order: First Name, Last\n\nName, Email, Phone (Not required), Title, Role.\n\nPlease see below for links to our training resources.\nAdmin Training Guide\nUser Training Guide\n\nLowe's Next Steps\nAlso, if you would like to request access to Lowe’s cameras, please have your Head of Agency complete\nthe template below. Once completed and sent over to the email address below, Lowe’s will review the\ntemplate to make sure that the information has been completed appropriately and will usually grant access to\nall of the Lowe's cameras in the region within a week or two.\n\nEmail Template to be completed by the head of the agency BELOW\n—\nEmail Subject Line- Lowe’s Camera Share; Name of the Agency\nEmail Template sent to: todd.a.isenhour@lowes.com and CC emma.jensen@flocksafety.com\n\nAs TITLE for CITY/ COUNTY, I would like to formally request regional access to Lowe’s owned Flock safety\nsystems and/ or LiveView. This technology will assist in preventing or investigating criminal activity in the local\ncommunity we both serve. Lowe’s technology and my department’s access to such will only be used for bona\nfide investigations, which are documented within our department and via audit trail within the Flock Safety\nplatform. These investigative tools and technology will not be permitted for personal use, for use on\nunauthorized devices or by unauthorized users within our department.  I understand if the technology is not\nused correctly, Lowe's reserves the right to terminate the department’s access to Lowe's owned Flock safety\nsystems and/or LiveView.\n\nName\nSignature of Head of Agency, Chief of Police or Sheriff\nTitle\n\nLet me know if you have any questions or if you get stuck.\n\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSenior Customer Success Manager\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSenior Customer Success Manager\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSenior Customer Success Manager\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0677.pdf"},"e0865":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0865","title":"Flock Cameras for Bluffton Police Dept - Information Request","frm":"Heather Phillips","date":"2024-11-19","text":"From:\nHeather Phillips\nSent:\nTuesday, November 19, 2024 11:40:39 AM\nTo:\nClarkson, Constance\nCc:\nGeorgia Abdallah; DuBose, Amanda; Babkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nRe: Flock Cameras for Bluffton Police Dept - Information Request\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nI completely understand. Here are 2 photos from recent installs with the same equipment. Do you think this would suffice? Looks\nlike one was too large and is being sent via google drive. Let me know if you have any issues accessing it, or if you need more\ndetails.\n image.png\n\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 412-512-0563\n flocksafety.com\nOn Tue, Nov 19, 2024 at 11:05 AM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nMorning Heather.\n\nThank you for your quick response.  The photos at the bottom of the Falcon Tech Specs are blurred and doesn’t convey\n‘transparency’ in our communications to the property owners.  Town operated security cameras on private property is\ngoing to be a touchy issue, so we want the property owners to know we are providing all the information possible.\nCan we get a clearer image of the solar and flock pole?  It can even be an existing mockup or model so long as the\ncolors and configuration will be the same.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, November 19, 2024 10:34 AM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; DuBose, Amanda <adubose@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock Cameras for Bluffton Police Dept - Information Request\n\nGood Morning,\n\nI attached specs for both the camera and pole.\n\nPlease let me know if you need anything else.\n\nThank you,\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 412-512-0563\n flocksafety.com\n\nOn Tue, Nov 19, 2024 at 9:31 AM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood morning Heather.\n\nWe’re drafting the package to be sent to the private property owners requesting we place a pole and camera on\ntheir property.\n\nFor the purposes of full disclosure to the owner, please provide the below at your earliest convenience.\n\n1. Images of the pole and camera equipment, the same pole color and equipment that will be used for the BPD\nproject.\n2. Either on the image or as a separate sketch, the height of the pole and dimensions of the equipment on the\npole.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0865.pdf"},"e0679":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0679","title":"Flock Roster","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2024-12-06","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nFriday, December 6, 2024 1:35:55 PM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nRe: Flock Roster\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nUnfortunately, I'm still seeing the same N/A. It's because the data in the sheet is using a filter and that data isn't copying over\nwhen you send it to me. If you can copy and paste the values only from the sheet into a new sheet, I think that would do the\ntrick.\nOn Thu, Dec 5, 2024 at 1:23 PM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nThat’s Weird. Lets try it again. When I click on it, it shows the correct information. If it doesn’t work this time I will manually\nenter the names into Flock myself when I have time.\n\nFrom: Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, December 5, 2024 1:16 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock Roster\n\nGood Afternoon,\n\nHmm it doesn't look like the data in the sheet came through correctly. Here's what I see\n\nCan you please resend it?\n\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n\nOn Thu, Dec 5, 2024 at 9:40 AM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood morning Georgia,\n\nI hope you had a great thanksgiving. Please see the attached roster for Flock users for our department. If you have any\nquestions please let me know. We have a few new staff members who do not have work phones yet, once we get those we\nwill add those to the list.\n\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nChief of Police\nOffice | 843-706-4537\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSenior Customer Success Manager\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSenior Customer Success Manager\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0289":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0289","title":"Determination of Camera #16","frm":"Clarkson, Constance","date":"2024-12-09","text":"From:\nClarkson, Constance\nSent:\nMonday, December 9, 2024 1:48:05 PM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nCc:\nHeather Phillips; Georgia Abdallah; Taylor Ellison; DuBose, Amanda\nSubject:\nDetermination of Camera #16\nSensitivity:Normal\nGood afternoon Chief.\n\nCamera #16 was located on Simmonsville Road SB at Bluffton Parkway.  Amanda’s research found the property\ncurrently in litigation of heirs with no clear owner.\nPer our prior emails, I requested Flock reposition the camera further north on County property due to the pending legal\nissues.\nFlock advised this will be too far from the roadway.\nThe property between the roadway and County property is SCDOT.\n\nPlease advise if you want to locate the camera elsewhere or remove it from the plan.\n\nFlock Deployment Plan can be found here https://planner.flocksafety.com/public/bebd2eeb-ed81-4102-b497-\nba3018cf39c7?cat=d9701bcdf517\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0289.pdf"},"e0899":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0899","title":"Bluffton PD - FlockOS Advanced - Project Documents & Intro Call","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2024-12-17","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nTuesday, December 17, 2024 3:32:37 PM\nTo:\n'Babkiewicz, Joseph'\nSubject:\nRE: Bluffton PD - FlockOS Advanced - Project Documents & Intro Call\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nInvite sent! Please let me know if there are other folks I should add to the call.\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com\n\nFrom: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Tuesday, December 17, 2024 7:04 AM\nTo: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: RE: Bluffton PD - FlockOS Advanced - Project Documents & Intro Call\n\nGood morning Kelly,\n\nThis month is extremely busy for us. Let’s schedule the meeting for 1/7 if that works for you.\n\nThank you,\n\nChief Joe Babkiewicz\n\nFrom: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Friday, December 13, 2024 2:55 PM\nTo: georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com; alex.menke@flocksafety.com; latonia.oyeniran@flocksafety.com;\ncourtney.wilson@flocksafety.com; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: 'Taylor Ellison' <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Bluffton PD - FlockOS Advanced - Project Documents & Intro Call\n\nGood afternoon, Chief Babkiewicz,\n\nI wanted to reach out and introduce myself and the FlockOS team. I will be managing the Bluffton PD FlockOS\nimplementation, along with Alex Menke, the Integrations Manager, and your Customer Success Manager, Georgia Abdallah.\nThe goal of this project is to integrate multiple systems into the FlockOS platform so your agency can access these systems in\none place.\n\nPlease see below for information regarding the project materials:\nProject Tasks: high level overview and status of the project tasks\nGoogle Drive: meeting notes and project documents saved here (you should have received a link to access the shared\ndrive)\n\nI would like to schedule a 30-minute call with the team to discuss your priorities and action items for this project, which\nincludes the following integrations:\n\nSSO\nMap Attachments\nESRI layers\nCommunity Website\nWing Gateway - (1) 128-channel gateway to bring in Digital Watchdog IP cameras\n\nBelow are some day/time options over the next couple of weeks, please let me know which option works best and I will send\nout an invite.\n\nWednesday, 12/18: 11:30am-1pm EST\nThursday, 12/19: 2:30-4:30pm EST\nThursday, 1/2: 11am-4pm\nTuesday, 1/7: 1-3:30pm\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions I can answer before our initial meeting.\n\nThanks!\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0899.pdf"},"e0681":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0681","title":"Flock Roster BPD","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2024-12-17","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nTuesday, December 17, 2024 11:55:56 AM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph; Flock Safety Support\nSubject:\nRe: Flock Roster BPD\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi team,\nI'm having trouble adding the below users to Bluffton PD's account. Can you please assist?\nReinl\nJosef\njreinl@townofb [phone] Officer\nPatrol\nNass\nAdam\nanass@townof843-540-0681 Sergeant\nPatrol\nThanks,\nGeorgia\nOn Tue, Dec 17, 2024 at 11:45 AM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nBoth of those email addresses are correct.\n\nFrom: Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, December 17, 2024 9:42 AM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock Roster BPD\n\nGood Morning,\n\nI was able to add everyone except the two users below. I keep getting an error. Can you double check the email addresses for me?\n\nReinl Josef jreinl@townofbluffton.com\n[phone] Officer\nPatrol\nNass Adam anass@townofbluffton.com [phone] Sergeant Patrol\n\nOn Mon, Dec 16, 2024 at 7:12 AM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGeorgia,\n\nI hope all is well. Lets see if this will work:\n\n500\nBabkiewicz\n Joseph\n jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\n Chief\n Admin\n [phone]\n SWORN\n501\nBurke\n Helen\n hburke@townofbluffton.com\n Captain\n Admin\n [phone]\n SWORN\n502\nKarafa\n Craig\n ckarafa@townofbluffton.com\n Captain\n Admin\n [phone]\n SWORN\n503\nDeStasio\n John\n jdestasio@townofbluffton.com\n Lieutenant\n Admin\n [phone]\n SWORN\n504\nMayers\n Michelle\n mmayers@townofbluffton.com\n Lieutenant\n Admin\n [phone]\n SWORN\n505\nFazekas\n Ryan\n rfazekas@townofbluffton.com\n Lieutenant\n Admin\n [phone]\n SWORN\n506\nFerrelli\n William\n wferrelli@townofbluffton.com\n Lieutenant\n Admin\n [phone]\n SWORN\n507\nMarciano\n Daniel\n dmarciano@townofbluffton.com\n Lieutenant\n Admin\n [phone]\n SWORN\n508\nCooler\n Brandon\n bcooler@townofbluffton.com\n Lieutenant\n Admin\n [phone]\n SWORN\n510\nRickett\n Daniel\n drickett@townofbluffton.com\n Sergeant\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n512\nLindiakos\n Alexa\n alindiakos@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n513\nReinl\n Josef\n jreinl@townofblufftoncom\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n514\nKing\n Edward\n eking@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n515\nYoung\n Azahel\n ayoung@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n521\nLaccesaglia\n Michael\n mlaccesaglia@townofbluffton.com\n Corporal\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n522\nMoore\n Christian\n cmoore@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n523\nOtsubo\n Stephanie\n spasquale@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n\n525\nBrown\n Athen\n athen.brown@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n530\nNass\n Adam\n anass@townofbluffton.com\n Sergeant\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n531\nSchaefer\n Sarah\n sschaefer@townofbluffton.com\n Corporal\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n532\nCorlett\n Taylor\n tcorlett@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n533\nNelson\n Brian\n bnelson@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n534\nRamirez\n Richard\n rramirez@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n535\nLopez\n Christopher\n clopez@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n540\nRodriguez\n Jason\n jrodriguez@townofbluffton.com\n Sergeant\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n541\nAnthony\n Lilia\n lmontero@townofbluffton.com\n Corporal\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n542\nGinn\n Frank\n fginn@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n543\nPagano\n Gabrielle\n gpagano@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n544\nLamm\n Alexander\n alamm@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n545\nQuarti\n Joel\n jquarti@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n580\nFerrelli\n Matthew\n mferrelli@townofbluffton.com\n Sergeant\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n581\nHopper\n Daniel\n dhopper@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n582\nAyler\n William\n wayler@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n583\nCollins\n Matthew\n mcollins@townofbluffton.com\n Recruit\n Patrol\n#REF!\nSWORN\n586\nBoyd\n Danielle\n dboyd@townofbluffton.com\n Recruit\n Patrol\n#REF!\nSWORN\n587\nDorta\n Oscar\n odorta@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n589\nCash\n Christopher\n ccash@townofbluffton.com\n Officer\n Patrol\n#REF!\nSWORN\nI-1\nPouchprom\n Zatch\n zpouchprom@townofbluffton.com\n Sergeant\n CID\n [phone]\n SWORN\nI-2\nLuechtefeld\n Amanda\n abilbrey@townofbluffton.com\n Detective\n CID\n [phone]\n SWORN\nI-3\nEisenmenger\n Matthew\n meisenmenger@townofbluffton.com\n Detective\n CID\n [phone]\n SWORN\n I-4\n Cooler\n Kate\n kcooler@townofbluffton.com\n Detective\n CID\n [phone]\n SWORN\nR-1\nLancaster\n Cecil\n clancaster@townofbluffton.com\n Sergeant\n SRO\n [phone]\n SWORN\n R-10\n Mullenix\n Brian\n bmullenix@townofbluffton.com\n SRO\n SRO\n [phone]\n SWORN\n R-11\n Brown\n Jarvis\n jbrown@townofbluffton.com\n SRO\n SRO\n [phone]\n SWORN\nR-12\nChrjapin\n Jason\n jchrjapin@townofbluffton.com\n SRO\n SRO\n [phone]\n SWORN\nR-13\nMielcarek\n Craig\n cmielcarek@townofbluffton.com\n SRO\n SRO\n [phone]\n SWORN\nR-14\nMcCallum\n Nathan\n nmccallum@townofbluffton.com\n SRO\n SRO\n [phone]\n SWORN\nR-2\nWilson\n Christopher\n cwilson@townofbluffton.com\n Sergeant\n SRO\n [phone]\n SWORN\n R-3\n Grant\n Brian\n bgrant@townofbluffton.com\n SRO\n SRO\n [phone]\n SWORN\n R-4\n Thompson\n Charles\n cthompson@townofbluffton.com\n SRO\n SRO\n [phone]\n SWORN\nR-5\nLambert\n Jeremy\n olambert@townofbluffton.com\n SRO\n SRO\n [phone]\n SWORN\n R-6\n Brown\n Akil\n abrown@townofbluffton.com\n Corporal\n SRO\n [phone]\n SWORN\nR-7\nFrazier\n Oscar\n ofrazier@townofbluffton.com\n Corporal\n SRO\n [phone]\n SWORN\n R-8\n Hendrickson\n Denise\n dhendrickson@townofbluffton.com\n SRO\n SRO\n [phone]\n SWORN\nR-9\nHarden\n Terry\n tharden@townofbluffton.com\n SRO\n SRO\n [phone]\n SWORN\nW-1\nPerkins\n James\n jperkins@townofbluffton.com\n Sergeant\n Patrol\n [phone]\n SWORN\n\nFrom: Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Friday, December 6, 2024 1:36 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock Roster\n\nUnfortunately, I'm still seeing the same N/A. It's because the data in the sheet is using a filter and that data isn't copying over when you send it to me. If you can copy and paste the values only from the sheet into a new sheet, I think that would do the trick.\n\nOn Thu, Dec 5, 2024 at 1:23 PM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nThat’s Weird. Lets try it again. When I click on it, it shows the correct information. If it doesn’t work this time I will manually enter the names into Flock myself when I have time.\n\nFrom: Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, December 5, 2024 1:16 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock Roster\n\nGood Afternoon,\n\nHmm it doesn't look like the data in the sheet came through correctly. Here's what I see\n\nCan you please resend it?\n\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n\nOn Thu, Dec 5, 2024 at 9:40 AM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood morning Georgia,\n\nI hope you had a great thanksgiving. Please see the attached roster for Flock users for our department. If you have any questions please let me know. We have a few new staff members who do not have work phones yet, once we get those we will add those to the list.\n\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nChief of Police\nOffice | [phone]\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSenior Customer Success Manager\n [phone]\n flocksafety.com\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSenior Customer Success Manager\n [phone]\n flocksafety.com\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSenior Customer Success Manager\n [phone]\n flocksafety.com\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSenior Customer Success Manager\n [phone]\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0681.pdf"},"e0867":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0867","title":"Flock Update Request","frm":"Heather Phillips","date":"2024-12-30","text":"From:\nHeather Phillips\nSent:\nMonday, December 30, 2024 12:45:22 PM\nTo:\nClarkson, Constance\nCc:\nTaylor Ellison; Georgia Abdallah; Babkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nRe: Flock Update Request\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nAfternoon!\nI know you're OOO but wanted to get a response to you. I'm still pending answers on system limitations to see if we\ncan get the deployment plan updated to reflect both the pole owner and the property information.\nOne question, please clarify what it means by Felicia “will NOT engage on pole attachments”?  Though the Town of\nBluffton will apply for the pole attachments, I wanted to ensure we’re all on the same page as to the prerequisites for\nsame.  The utility companies won’t approve a pole attachment application unless the property owner has approved\nfirst, which means the Town will need verification the encroachment permits were issued for any location where we’re\nrequesting pole attachments. *** I just wanted to note the fact we are not engaging the utility company. It's\nunderstood that we need to know who owns the actual property.\n\nLast item, from my email of 12/9/24 (copied below for your convenience, has a determination be made as to the\nrelocations of #16.  We had it on private property but due to it being heirs property, we wanted to move it to County\nproperty.  Flock had mentioned the new location was too far from the road and would provide options for us as to a\nbetter location.  Do we have an update on this camera location? ** I've nudged Shelby for an update.\n\nThank you!\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 412-512-0563\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com\n\nOn Mon, Dec 23, 2024 at 1:03 PM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood afternoon Heather.\n\nThank you for the below.\n\nOne question, please clarify what it means by Felicia “will NOT engage on pole attachments”?  Though the Town of\nBluffton will apply for the pole attachments, I wanted to ensure we’re all on the same page as to the prerequisites for\nsame.  The utility companies won’t approve a pole attachment application unless the property owner has approved\nfirst, which means the Town will need verification the encroachment permits were issued for any location where\nwe’re requesting pole attachments.\n\nLast item, from my email of 12/9/24 (copied below for your convenience, has a determination be made as to the\nrelocations of #16.  We had it on private property but due to it being heirs property, we wanted to move it to County\nproperty.  Flock had mentioned the new location was too far from the road and would provide options for us as to a\nbetter location.  Do we have an update on this camera location?\n\nThank you again for time on this project.  It’s greatly appreciated.\n\nI hope everyone has a great Holiday!!\n\nTown of Bluffton offices are closed as of 1pm today in observance of Christmas and will reopen on Thursday at 8am.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, December 23, 2024 12:37 PM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>; Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock Update Request\n\nGood Afternoon,\n\nSending a quick e-mail to follow up on what we discussed today:\n\nLocations #04, #11, #15, C#04: Requested Shelby update the \"Permitting\" section to indicate BOTH the Power Company\n(pole) as well as the actual property owner.\n\nLocations pending CX (Chiefs) approval: #04, #10, #17, C#02.\n\nFelicia will provide updates soon on County permits. She will NOT engage on pole attachments. The Town of Bluffton verbally\napproved the install on Town property.\nWe are holding ALL installs until all permits/permissions are received. Forecasting end of Feb / beginning of March install\ndates.\n\nI think this sums it all up. I'll be in touch with updates!\n\n-Heather\n\nOn Mon, Dec 16, 2024 at 1:25 PM Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nThank you! I changed the invite to Wednesday at 11A. We will make sure everything is on track!\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com\n OOO ALERT: 12/10-12/14\n\nFrom: Clarkson, Constance\nSent: Monday, December 9, 2024 2:19 PM\nTo: Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>; Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; Taylor\nEllison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: FW: Determination of Camera #16\n\nGood afternoon Heather.\n\nPlease see the Chief’s comments below.  If his next requested location is also not feasible, please provide your\nrecommendation of a better location.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\n\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Monday, December 9, 2024 2:16 PM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: RE: Determination of Camera #16\n\nThank you, Constance. I would really like something in that area as it is a busier roadway/intersection for calls. Can we put it on\nthe other side of the roadway and catch northbound traffic? I guess that would be better than not having one there. Thanks\n\nFrom: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Monday, December 9, 2024 1:48 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>; Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; Taylor\nEllison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>; DuBose, Amanda <adubose@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Determination of Camera #16\n\nGood afternoon Chief.\n\nCamera #16 was located on Simmonsville Road SB at Bluffton Parkway.  Amanda’s research found the property\n\ncurrently in litigation of heirs with no clear owner.\nPer our prior emails, I requested Flock reposition the camera further north on County property due to the pending\nlegal issues.\nFlock advised this will be too far from the roadway.\nThe property between the roadway and County property is SCDOT.\n\nPlease advise if you want to locate the camera elsewhere or remove it from the plan.\n\nFlock Deployment Plan can be found here https://planner.flocksafety.com/public/bebd2eeb-ed81-4102-b497-\nba3018cf39c7?cat=d9701bcdf517\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\n\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nOn Mon, Dec 16, 2024 at 1:23 PM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nMorning Heather.\n\nThank you for the quick response.  I know how you feel with the meetings schedule.\n\nI listed my availability below for the remainder of this week as I am already booked for tomorrow.  Please pick\nwhichever works best for you and Erin.\n\nThank you.\n\nWednesday - between 10am and noon\nThursday - anytime but noon to 1pm\nFriday – 8am to 1pm\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, December 16, 2024 1:18 PM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Erin Crouse <erin.crouse@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock Update Request\n\nGood Afternoon,\n\nApologies I missed your call. I've been in back to back meetings most of the day. I'd like to get time set up together with\nmy Permitting Manager. Unfortunately, she is out sick today. I set a time for tomorrow at 1:30PM. Please let me know if\nthat does not work for you.\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com\n OOO ALERT: 12/10-12/14\n\nOn Mon, Dec 16, 2024 at 12:00 PM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nMorning Heather.\n\nThere has been some disconnect between the start up and now as none of the locations owned by the Town of\nBluffton will need an encroachment permit.   This was relayed in the initial meeting when the Flock and Town\nstaff first met.\n\nI tried to call, but got your voice mail.  Please call me with Erin so we can sort throw these.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, December 16, 2024 11:01 AM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>; Erin Crouse <erin.crouse@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock Update Request\n\nGood Morning,\n\nI'm looping in my Permitting Associate @Erin Crouse to assist and answer any further questions. My understanding is\nthat as of last week, our Permitting Manager followed up with the County for a status update. Robin Primus the Public\nService Coordinator is going to provide her feedback after she reviews the pending locations. She left a message for\nLarry Beckler, the Public Service Director.\n\nLocations #1,6,8,9,12,13,17 are submitted to Beaufort County.\n\nLocation #7 is submitted as well to the County, but it's City.\n\nCan you elaborate on what specific information you might need?\n\nThank you,\n\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com\n OOO ALERT: 12/10-12/14\n\nOn Mon, Dec 16, 2024 at 10:11 AM Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nGood Morning,\n\nI have an urgent message out to my permitting team to provide us with an update. I will let you know as soon as I get\na response.\n\nThank you,\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com\n OOO ALERT: 12/10-12/14\n\nOn Mon, Dec 16, 2024 at 8:59 AM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood morning Heather.\n\nI’d like to provide an update to the Chief at a 10:30 meeting this morning but the Flock database doesn’t\nhave the information needed.\n\nCan you please reply with a quick update on the encroachment easements?  How many in total, how\nmany have been issued and if there are any issues with any of the locations.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0867.pdf"},"e0151":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0151","title":"Bluffton SC PD _ FlockOS - Implementation Intro Call","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2025-01-06","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph on behalf of: Kelly Baeza\nSent:\nMonday, January 6, 2025 2:20:40 PM\nTo:\nBPD_Commandstaff\nSubject:\nFW: Bluffton SC PD / FlockOS - Implementation Intro Call\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:attachment.ics ;invite.ics ;\n\nFlock use on Cell Phones. I would like for Command Staff to be a part of this meeting for review and application\npurposes.\n\n-----Original Appointment-----\nFrom: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, December 17, 2024 3:30 PM\nTo: Kelly Baeza; Georgia Abdallah; Babkiewicz, Joseph; LaTonia Oyeniran; Courtney Wilson; Alex Menke\nSubject: Bluffton SC PD / FlockOS - Implementation Intro Call\nWhen: Tuesday, January 7, 2025 1:00 PM-1:30 PM America/New_York.\nWhere:\n\np l e m\nm\ne r a s\n\nJoin with Google Meet\nMeeting link\nmeet.google.com/jbo-zfsj-jmq\nJoin by phone\n(US) +1 513-970-0827\nPIN: 449004438\nMore phone numbers\nIntegrations:\nSSO\nMap Attachments\nESRI layers\nCommunity Website\nWing Gateway - (1) 128-channel gateway to bring in Digital\nWatchdog IP cameras\nWhen\nTuesday Jan 7, 2025 ⋅ 1pm – 1:30pm (Eastern Time - New York)\nGuests\nKelly Baeza - organizer\nGeorgia Abdallah\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nLaTonia Oyeniran\nCourtney Wilson\nAlex Menke\nView all guest info\nReply for jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nYes\nNo\nMaybe\nMore options\nInvitation from Google Calendar\nYou are receiving this email because you are an attendee on the event.\nForwarding this invitation could allow any recipient to send a response to the organizer, be added to the guest list, invite others regardless of their\nown invitation status, or modify your RSVP. Learn more","pdf":null},"e0906":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0906","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Implementation Intro Call Agenda - 1_7_25","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-01-07","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nTuesday, January 7, 2025 9:05:47 AM\nTo:\n'Alex Menke'; 'Courtney Wilson'; 'LaTonia Oyeniran'; 'Georgia Abdallah'; 'Joe Babkiewicz';\nrfazekas@townofbluffton.com; 'Craig Karafa'; emoody@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nRE: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Implementation Intro Call Agenda - 1/7/25\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nUpdating the meeting attendees, please let me know if any titles are incorrect!\n\nMeeting\nAttendees\nAttendees - Flock Safety\n Kelly Baeza, Technical Project Manager\n Alex Menke, Integrations Manager\n Georgia Abdallah, Customer Success Manager\n [Shadowing] Courtney Wilson, Technical Project Manager\n [Shadowing] LaTonia Oyeniran, Technical Project Manager\n\nAttendees - Bluffton PD - EST\n Chief Joe Babkiewicz\n Lieutenant Ryan Fazekas\n Lieutenant Craig Karafa\n Edith Moody, Community Relations Manager\nProject\nMaterials\nProject Tasks: high level overview and status of the project tasks\nGoogle Drive: meeting notes and project documents saved here\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com\n\nFrom: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, January 7, 2025 9:00 AM\nTo: 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; 'Courtney Wilson' <courtney.wilson@flocksafety.com>; 'LaTonia Oyeniran'\n<latonia.oyeniran@flocksafety.com>; 'Georgia Abdallah' <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; 'Joe Babkiewicz'\n<jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; rfazekas@townofbluffton.com; 'Craig Karafa' <ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>\n\nSubject: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Implementation Intro Call Agenda - 1/7/25\n\nGood morning,\n\nBelow are the agenda items and project contacts for today’s call, please let me know if you have any questions!\n\nMeeting\nAttendees\nAttendees - Flock Safety\n Kelly Baeza, Technical Project Manager\n Alex Menke, Integrations Manager\n Georgia Abdallah, Customer Success Manager\n [Shadowing] Courtney Wilson, Technical Project Manager\n [Shadowing] LaTonia Oyeniran, Technical Project Manager\n\nAttendees - Bluffton PD - EST\n Chief Joe Babkiewicz\nProject\nMaterials\nProject Tasks: high level overview and status of the project tasks\nGoogle Drive: meeting notes and project documents saved here\n\nAgenda:\nIntroductions\nAny initial questions/important items to note about the FlockOS implementation\nProject materials shared with the team\nReview project plan and initial steps\nIdentify resources for the integrations\nSchedule bi-weekly meetings beginning the week of January 20th:\nTuesdays, 12-3pm EST\nWednesdays, 10:30am-1pm EST\nThursdays, 11:30am-12:30pm, 1:30-3pm EST\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0915":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0915","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Approval for Flock User","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-01-07","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nTuesday, January 7, 2025 3:44:14 PM\nTo:\n'Babkiewicz, Joseph'; 'Fazekas, Ryan'\nCc:\nalex.menke@flocksafety.com; courtney.wilson@flocksafety.com; latonia.oyeniran@flocksafety.com\nSubject:\nRE: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Approval for Flock User\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nThanks!\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com\n\nFrom: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Tuesday, January 7, 2025 2:28 PM\nTo: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: alex.menke@flocksafety.com; courtney.wilson@flocksafety.com; latonia.oyeniran@flocksafety.com\nSubject: RE: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Approval for Flock User\n\nYes I am good with this. Thank you.\n\nChief Joe Babkiewicz\n\nFrom: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, January 7, 2025 2:24 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: alex.menke@flocksafety.com; courtney.wilson@flocksafety.com; latonia.oyeniran@flocksafety.com\nSubject: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Approval for Flock User\n\nGood afternoon,\n\nAs we discussed in our call, Flock would like to set up your Integrations Manager to have access to your Flock system during\nthe implementation period so they can review how different integrations are appearing on the map.\n\nJust so that we have confirmation in writing, would you please respond in the affirmative that we are okay to proceed with\ncreating the user?\n\nThanks!\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0915.pdf"},"e0925":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0925","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Implementation Intro Call Notes - 1_7_25","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-01-14","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nTuesday, January 14, 2025 9:41:39 AM\nTo:\n'Moody, Edith'; 'Alex Menke'; 'Courtney Wilson'; 'LaTonia Oyeniran'; 'Georgia Abdallah'; 'Babkiewicz, Joseph';\n'Fazekas, Ryan'; 'Karafa, Craig'; 'Destasio, John'\nSubject:\nRE: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Implementation Intro Call Notes - 1/7/25\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nThese are great! I’ll get them to Marketing to build out the website and materials.\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com\n\nFrom: Moody, Edith <emoody@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Tuesday, January 14, 2025 9:22 AM\nTo: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>; 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; 'Courtney Wilson'\n<courtney.wilson@flocksafety.com>; 'LaTonia Oyeniran' <latonia.oyeniran@flocksafety.com>; 'Georgia Abdallah'\n<georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas, Ryan\n<rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig <ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Destasio, John\n<jdestasio@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: RE: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Implementation Intro Call Notes - 1/7/25\n\nHey Kelly,\n\nThank you for the attachments and direction. Please see that attached photos and let me know if they will work.\nThank you, again.\n\nEydie J. Moody,\nCommunity Relations Manager\n\nBluffton Police Department\n101 Progressive Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\n(843) 738-4622 (Office)\n(843) 505-3306 (Cell)\n\nFrom: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, January 13, 2025 4:33 PM\nTo: Moody, Edith <emoody@townofbluffton.com>; 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; 'Courtney Wilson'\n<courtney.wilson@flocksafety.com>; 'LaTonia Oyeniran' <latonia.oyeniran@flocksafety.com>; 'Georgia Abdallah'\n<georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas, Ryan\n<rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig <ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Destasio, John\n<jdestasio@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: RE: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Implementation Intro Call Notes - 1/7/25\n\nHi Eydie!\n\nTypically, we have the badge at the top left of the website, then the large image at the top (I included the examples below\n\nfor reference). Do you want them to be separate? Or keep them together? If separate, please send me new photos.\n\nExamples:\nhttps://refer.flocksafety.com/operation-plugged-in/\nhttps://refer.flocksafety.com/scottsdale-safe/\nhttps://refer.flocksafety.com/prosper-catch/\nhttps://refer.flocksafety.com/bloomington-psc-integration/\n\nThanks!\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com\n\nFrom: Moody, Edith <emoody@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Monday, January 13, 2025 2:37 PM\nTo: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>; 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; 'Courtney Wilson'\n<courtney.wilson@flocksafety.com>; 'LaTonia Oyeniran' <latonia.oyeniran@flocksafety.com>; 'Georgia Abdallah'\n<georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas, Ryan\n<rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig <ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Destasio, John\n<jdestasio@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: RE: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Implementation Intro Call Notes - 1/7/25\n\nGood afternoon Kelly,\n\nPlease let me know if this will work. One has the shield/badge faded and one does not. Thank you in advance.\n\nEydie J. Moody,\nCommunity Relations Manager\n\nBluffton Police Department\n101 Progressive Street\n\nBluffton, SC 29910\n(843) 738-4622 (Office)\n(843) 505-3306 (Cell)\n\nFrom: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, January 7, 2025 3:40 PM\nTo: 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; 'Courtney Wilson' <courtney.wilson@flocksafety.com>; 'LaTonia Oyeniran'\n<latonia.oyeniran@flocksafety.com>; 'Georgia Abdallah' <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph\n<jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig\n<ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Moody, Edith <emoody@townofbluffton.com>; Destasio, John\n<jdestasio@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Implementation Intro Call Notes - 1/7/25\n\nGood afternoon,\n\nAction items and notes from today’s call are below, please let me know if you have any questions!\n\nOwner\nAction Item\nStatus\nDue Date\nAlex\nReach out to Bob Charles for the SSO setup & Gateway install\nIn Progress\n1/10/2025\nChief\nIdentify resource to send ESRI layers\nIn Progress\n1/14/2025\nEdie\nSend images to use for the community website & materials\nIn Progress\n1/14/2024\nKelly\nSend email to create users in FlockOS\nCompleted\n1/7/2025\n\nIntegration\nNotes\nStatus\nMap\nAttachments\n1/7 - Your agency can add map attachments at any time (no need to send files to Flock); we\nsupport PDFs, Word docs, images (jpg, png), or website links as locations that show as pins\non the map. Examples include floor plans, links directly to a VMS, a link to instructions for a\nCompleted\n\nspecial event in the area, primary contacts for a school, etc. This link has the step-by-step\ninstructions to add attachments: https://help.flocksafety.com/s/article/Map-\nAttachments.\n\nNote: A Flock Admin user will need to add the Floor Plans permission for other Roles\nSSO\n1/7 - First step is to identify the SSO admin for Flock engineers to work with and also decide\nwhether OIDC and SAML is preferred. Alex will reach out to Bob Charles\n(rcharles@townofbluffton.com) to get this started (CC the Chief & Lt. Fazekas)\n\nWhat Single Sign On (SSO) options do we offer at Flock?\nOIDC based Azure AD /Active Directory/ Entra/ M365\nOIDC based Okta (can be any Identity Provider (IdP))\nSAML based using Auth0 (can be any Identity Provider (IdP))\n\nPlanned\nESRI Layers\n1/7 - We can bring in your ESRI layers to give you more detail on your FlockOS map. We\ntypically upload beats, city limits, and parcel layers for addresses, though we can upload\nmore (ex: hunting zones, horse trails, etc). Two ways we can load your ESRI layers: you can\nsend us a link to a publicly hosted ESRI feature server, or you can send us zipped shape files\nthat we can host for you. The Chief will identify the resource to send the layers (this can\noften be someone from the GIS team)\nPlanned\nCommunity\nWebsite &\nMarketing\nMaterials\n1/7 - A website where members of the community can sign up if they want to register or\nintegrate their cameras. We have a template for the website, but you can provide images\nand/or logos to customize the website, add quotes, or we can use stock images. We can also\nprovide marketing materials to help promote the website to the community like flyers,\nbusiness cards, window decals, and digital materials (a virtual post you can put on\nFacebook/Twitter/Instagram). I will work with Edie to get the images (& quote, if desired)\nfor the website\n\nTo get started on setting up the website and marketing materials to promote the website,\nwe will need the following information from your agency:\n\nWhat would you like the website/program name to be? The default will be Bluffton\nPD Safe\nWhat large image would you like to be utilized at the top of the website?\nWhat badge/logo/patch you would like us to use in the top corner of the website and\non the marketing materials?\nDo you want to have registration, integration, and purchase options on the website?\nOr do you want to remove one or two of these options?\nIs there a quote from your agency that you would like to include at the bottom of the\nwebsite?\n\nExamples:\nhttps://refer.flocksafety.com/operation-plugged-in/\nhttps://refer.flocksafety.com/scottsdale-safe/\nhttps://refer.flocksafety.com/prosper-catch/\nhttps://refer.flocksafety.com/bloomington-psc-integration/\n\nPlanned\nWing VMS w/\nGateway: (1)\n128-Channel\nBox\n1/7 - We will use a gateway to make the Digital Watchdog camera streams available in Flock\nsince we do not directly integrate with the VMS system. Bob Charles is the IT contact, Alex\nwill reach out to Bob Charles to get the camera info and the address to ship the gateway (CC\nthe Chief & Lt. Fazekas)\nPlanned\nEnable Flock\nUser Logins\n1/7 - Flock would like to have your Integrations Engineer have access to your Flock system\nduring the period of your FlockOS implementation so that they can review how different\nintegrations are appearing on the map. I sent an email for written confirmation, Chief\nCompleted\n\napproved\n\nMeeting\nAttendees\nTuesday, January 7th\n\nAttendees - Flock Safety\n Kelly Baeza, Technical Project Manager\n Alex Menke, Integrations Manager\n Georgia Abdallah, Customer Success Manager\n [Shadowing] Courtney Wilson, Technical Project Manager\n [Shadowing] LaTonia Oyeniran, Technical Project Manager\n\nAttendees - Bluffton PD - EST\n Chief Joe Babkiewicz\n Lieutenant Ryan Fazekas\n Lieutenant Craig Karafa\n Edith Moody, Community Relations Manager\n Michelle\n John Destasio\nProject\nMaterials\nProject Tasks: high level overview and status of the project tasks\nGoogle Drive: meeting notes and project documents saved here\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0925.pdf"},"e0682":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0682","title":"The Home Depot Camera Share - Bluffton PD","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2025-01-08","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nWednesday, January 8, 2025 5:23:52 PM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nThe Home Depot Camera Share - Bluffton PD\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nIn coordination with The Home Depot (THD), we are working to provide agencies with state access to THD cameras for both\nsearch and hotlist capabilities as a part of their rollout.\nThe only requirement is for the below template to be sent to the head of the agency. No further action is required from you.\nYou should expect to receive access to The Home Depot's statewide cameras within 1-2 weeks.\n—\nThe Home Depot would like to provide your agency with state-wide access to The Home Depot owned Flock safety\nsystems. This technology will assist in preventing or investigating criminal activity in the local community we both serve.\nThe Home Depot technology and your department’s access to such should only be used for bona fide investigations,\nwhich are documented within your department and via audit trail within the Flock Safety platform. These investigative\ntools and technology will not be permitted for personal use, for use on unauthorized devices or by unauthorized users\nwithin your department.  I understand if the technology is not used correctly, The Home Depot reserves the right to\nterminate the department’s access to The Home Depot owned Flock safety systems.\nIf your agency has any questions or concerns, please let me know.\n\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSenior Customer Success Manager\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0682.pdf"},"e0877":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0877","title":"Flock Update and Request for Approval","frm":"Heather Phillips","date":"2025-01-17","text":"From:\nHeather Phillips\nSent:\nFriday, January 17, 2025 2:04:16 PM\nTo:\nClarkson, Constance; Georgia Abdallah; Taylor Ellison\nCc:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nRe: Flock Update and Request for Approval\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nPlease see my notes below highlighted in yellow. Constance, we can talk more in detail Tuesday. Hope everyone has a great,\nlong weekend!\n1. Chief to approve below deployment plan locations with newly identified owners\n#11 – Legacy Plaza 1276 May River Road\n#16 – Regina Brown – 126 Simmonsville Road, this will be approved only if the Chief likes the new recommended location per\nthe email from Amanda on 1/10/25 11:01\n2. If the Chief still wants to wait on SCDOT for #16, Georgia to advise what impact it will have on the contract terms since the\ncamera cannot be installed in the most optimal location per the original deployment plan. @Taylor Ellison  - Can you please\nadvise?\n\n3. Heather to forward the exact locations approved on the Beaufort County Encroachment Permit.  These are needed for the\npole attachment applications.\nLocations on APPROVED Beaufort County Encroachment Permit: #01, #02, #06, #07, #09, #12, #13, P#003.\n - #01, #06, #12 (#07 City) were all installed.\n - #02 shows PPP: Low Country Presby Church - Co. Permit not required.\n - #07 shows Town of Bluffton - Co. Permit not required.\nPending approval for additional locations on Beaufort County Encroachment Permit: #08, #17, P#001 and P#002\nPole attachment locations for your reference:\n - #04: Town of Bluffton / Dominion\n - #11: PPP Legacy Plaza Owners Assoc. / Palmetto (Solar powered)\n - P#001: Beaufort County / Existing light pole. Pending permit.\n - C#04: SCDOT / Palmetto Electric (under review due to SCDOT restrictions)\n\n4. Heather to request Colby change #15 to Waff LLC 162 Bluffton Road with a flock pole.  The prior location was Sea Smiles\nat 164 Bluffton Road with an existing pole but they are not on Town property. This is now updated within the deployment\nplan.\n\n5. Team to revisit #C04 as SCDOT has been identified as the property owner.  There is already a County traffic camera on a\nPalmetto pole at this location. Chief, if this pole is not an option, we can move the camera approximately 50’ west and work with\nthe New Riverside association if the tree coverage is not an issue.  See attached and provide your comments. Engineer will need\nto rework the electrical plan requested for the prior location.\n\n6. Heather to advise of any follow up needed regarding the encroachment permit for the few cameras that were inadvertently\ninstalled without notice to proceed from the Town. Pending response from County - in the meantime, the application was\nsent for the 4 noted above.\n\n7. If the Town receives anything from Flock activating a term of the contract to include any payment request due to 5. above,\nConstance to advise Heather and she will work with Georgia to provide us with an email to disregard. @Clarkson, Constance  -\nbased on our chat today, let's revisit this one. #09, #13 (needs Chiefs approval), and P#003 can be moved to install,\nalong with any locations that you have received private property permission for.\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 412-512-0563\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com\nOn Thu, Jan 16, 2025 at 2:25 PM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood afternoon Heather – Thank you again for meeting with me this morning.  Below is a recap of our discussion and\none outstanding item (6.) from our last meeting.  Please let me know if you need to add anything.\n\nChief - there are a few action items for you.  Please let me know if you have any questions.\n\n1. Chief to approve below deployment plan locations with newly identified owners\n#11 – Legacy Plaza 1276 May River Road\n#16 – Regina Brown – 126 Simmonsville Road, this will be approved only if the Chief likes the new\nrecommended location per the email from Amanda on 1/10/25 11:01.\n\n2. If the Chief still wants to wait on SCDOT for #16, Georgia to advise what impact it will have on the contract\nterms since the camera cannot be installed in the most optimal location per the original deployment plan .\n\n3. Heather to forward the exact locations approved on the Beaufort County Encroachment Permit.  These are\nneeded for the pole attachment applications.\n\n4. Heather to request Colby change #15 to Waff LLC 162 Bluffton Road with a flock pole.  The prior location was\nSea Smiles at 164 Bluffton Road with an existing pole but they are not on Town property.\n\n5. Team to revisit #C04 as SCDOT has been identified as the property owner.  There is already a County traffic\ncamera on a Palmetto pole at this location. Chief, if this pole is not an option, we can move the camera\napproximately 50’ west and work with the New Riverside association if the tree coverage is not an issue.  See\nattached and provide your comments.  Engineer will need to rework the electrical plan requested for the prior\nlocation.\n\n6. Heather to advise of any follow up needed regarding the encroachment permit for the few cameras that were\ninadvertently installed without notice to proceed from the Town.\n\n7. If the Town receives anything from Flock activating a term of the contract to include any payment request due\nto 5. above, Constance to advise Heather and she will work with Georgia to provide us with an email to\ndisregard.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\n\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, January 16, 2025 10:33 AM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock Update and Request for Approval\n\nI'm joining now - but take your time!\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 412-512-0563\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com\n\nOn Thu, Jan 16, 2025 at 8:46 AM Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nWill do!\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 412-512-0563\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com\n\nOn Thu, Jan 16, 2025 at 8:40 AM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nMorning Heather.\n\nThank you for letting me know.  Please just call me when you can get on the call and we’ll meet up about 5\nminutes later as I’ll need to move to a conference room.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, January 16, 2025 8:37 AM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock Update and Request for Approval\n\nGood Morning,\nJust wanted to drop you a quick message that I have a mapping call at 10A that might run a bit over. Apologies in advance\nif I'm a few minutes late, but I will be there!\nAlso, our permitting manager Felicia has been OOO, so I don't have a solid response on permitting items just yet, but I've\nnudged for an update again.\n\nLook forward to talking soon!\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 412-512-0563\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com\n\nOn Fri, Jan 10, 2025 at 1:06 PM Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nGood Afternoon All,\n\nI hope everyone is staying warm! Just wanted to jump in and let you know what we've reviewed the proposed alternate\nlocation on our end and updated the Deployment Plan to reflect.\n\nThank you,\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 412-512-0563\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com\n\nOn Fri, Jan 10, 2025 at 11:01 AM DuBose, Amanda <adubose@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nThere may be another option further down Simmonsville.  See the attached snapshot.  Property owner is Regina\nBrown.  Appears to be clear title.   Not a lot of tree coverage on the road frontage.   Thoughts?\n\nAmanda DuBose\nEasement Acquisition Administrator\n\nCell | 843- 949-7783\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Thursday, January 9, 2025 1:10 PM\nTo: DuBose, Amanda <adubose@townofbluffton.com>; Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>;\nHeather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>\nCc: Rooney, Pat <prooney@townofbluffton.com>; Jones, Kim <kjones@townofbluffton.com>; Charles, Robert\n<rcharles@townofbluffton.com>; Ocasio, Peter <pocasio@townofbluffton.com>; Stormer, Tracye\n<tstormer@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: RE: Flock Update and Request for Approval\n\nThank you, Amanda. My concern is that if a vehicle turns onto Simmonsville road from Bluffton parkway we will not be\nable to capture it as it leaves a blind spot in that area.  if a crime occurs on Simmonsville Road we will have no data to\nreference. If we must wait (for an uncertain amount of time) for DOT to allow cameras on their property, then that is\nwhat we may have to do for now.\n\nChief\n\nFrom: DuBose, Amanda <adubose@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Thursday, January 9, 2025 12:24 PM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph\n<jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>\nCc: Rooney, Pat <prooney@townofbluffton.com>; Jones, Kim <kjones@townofbluffton.com>; Charles, Robert\n<rcharles@townofbluffton.com>; Ocasio, Peter <pocasio@townofbluffton.com>; Stormer, Tracye\n<tstormer@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: RE: Flock Update and Request for Approval\n\nHappy to respond.\n\nThe original location selected was on the property of Fred Bolden, who is deceased (see Yellow marker).  His estate is\n\nlocked in legal tie-ups so at this time there is not clear ownership of the property and therefore we cannot obtain an\neasement.  The adjacent property closer to the parkway is owned by Beaufort County (the convenience center)(see\nGreen marker).  However, Flock determined the property line is too far away from Simmonsville Rd. to work for the\ncameras.  The right of way of Simmonsville Rd is DOT owned, which we cannot place cameras in.\n\nThe subsequent property chosen by Flock for placement (see Red Marker)  is in the powerline easement (and also not\nin Town limits) so that won’t work.  The next closest property is Sauls Funeral (See Purple marker).\n\nThe Bluffton Parkway is county owned which may work but from the looks of the property lines, the placement would\nstill need to be on the North side of the Parkway and there may be too much tree coverage, but it is worth looking at.\n(See Blue marker.)\n\nPlease let me know if anyone has any further questions.\n\nAmanda DuBose\nEasement Acquisition Administrator\n\nCell | 843- 949-7783\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Thursday, January 9, 2025 11:56 AM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>\n\nCc: DuBose, Amanda <adubose@townofbluffton.com>; Rooney, Pat <prooney@townofbluffton.com>; Jones, Kim\n<kjones@townofbluffton.com>; Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>; Ocasio, Peter\n<pocasio@townofbluffton.com>; Stormer, Tracye <tstormer@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: RE: Flock Update and Request for Approval\n\nAmanda.\n\nPlease see below from Chief and see if we can accommodate based on our location criteria.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Thursday, January 9, 2025 11:54 AM\n\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>; Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>\nCc: DuBose, Amanda <adubose@townofbluffton.com>; Rooney, Pat <prooney@townofbluffton.com>; Jones, Kim\n<kjones@townofbluffton.com>; Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>; Ocasio, Peter\n<pocasio@townofbluffton.com>; Stormer, Tracye <tstormer@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: RE: Flock Update and Request for Approval\n\nThank you Constance. These have all been approved on the Flock Safety Website. As far as Camera Location #16 is\nthere a way we can get it down south of Bluffton parkway somewhere instead of Sauls funeral home? If not we can\nwork with having there but figured I would ask. Thank you again for all your help.\n\nChief\n\nFrom: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Thursday, January 9, 2025 11:42 AM\nTo: Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>\nCc: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; DuBose, Amanda <adubose@townofbluffton.com>;\nRooney, Pat <prooney@townofbluffton.com>; Jones, Kim <kjones@townofbluffton.com>; Charles, Robert\n<rcharles@townofbluffton.com>; Ocasio, Peter <pocasio@townofbluffton.com>; Stormer, Tracye\n<tstormer@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Flock Update and Request for Approval\n\nGood morning Heather.\n\nBelow is a recap of our meeting this morning.  I believe I captured everything, but please add anything I may\nhave missed.  Thank you.\n\n1. Chief, please pull up the website and approve the below camera locations which have been adjusted\ndue to various reasons - ownership, distance from road, etc.\na. #04, #10, #13, #17, C#02\n2. Scheduling\na. First installation of locations without easements – February 28\n                                                              i.      Lead time for Flock pole locations is 3 to 4 weeks from notice to\nproceed\n                                                             ii.      Lead time for existing pole locations is 2 to 3 weeks from\nnotice to proceed\n\n                                                           iii.      Target notice to proceed is 2/1/25\nb. Second installation of locations with easements – March 31\n                                                              i.      Target notice to proceed is 3/1/25\n3. Cameras Already Installed - #01, #06, #07, #12\na. Four cameras were already inadvertently installed upon Flock’s receipt of the Beaufort County\nEncroachment Easement for eight locations.\nb. Heather has confirmed that this unapproved installation will not trigger any terms to include\npayments due pursuant to the Agreement.\nc. Heather is reaching out to the Flock team to ensure the permit requirements were met prior to\ninstallation.\n4. Prior to other installations, Flock will initiate a site survey of each location.  If the site survey findings\nare not favorable for installation, the camera location will need to be relocated. Possible negative site\nsurvey results may include:\na. Limited or no solar coverage\nb. Utility line interference\nc. Private property owner issues\n5. Heather, Camera Location #16 has been relocated as it was in the power line easement.  Please\nreview the attached image and advise if Flock agrees with the new location at Saul’s Funeral Home.  If\nso, please update the database for the Chief’s approval.\n6. A recurring meeting with Flock will take place every Thursday at 10:30 am until the first approved\ninstallation.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0877.pdf"},"e0930":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0930","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Community Website and Marketing Materials","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-01-15","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nWednesday, January 15, 2025 5:03:13 PM\nTo:\n'Courtney Wilson'; 'LaTonia Oyeniran'; 'Georgia Abdallah'; 'Joe Babkiewicz'; 'Ryan Fazekas'; 'Craig Karafa';\n'Edith Moody'; jdestasio@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nBluffton PD / FlockOS - Community Website and Marketing Materials\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:CollateralMarketingMaterials-BlufftonPD-Proof1.pdf ;\n\nGood afternoon,\n\nAttached is the PDF with the marketing materials draft and below is the community website link for your review. If\neverything looks good, please send me the address to ship the materials and to whom they should be addressed. Thanks!\n\nhttps://refer.flocksafety.com/bluffton-safe/\n\nMarketing Materials:\nPg 2: flyer-front\nPg 3: flyer-back\nPg 4: window decal\nPg 5: front/back business card\nPg 6: digital marketing images\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0164":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0164","title":"Quick Updates - Bluffton PD + Flock Safety","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2025-01-29","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSent:\nWednesday, January 29, 2025 4:32:13 PM\nTo:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSubject:\nRE: Quick Updates - Bluffton PD + Flock Safety\nSensitivity:Normal\nThank you\n\nFrom: Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Wednesday, January 29, 2025 4:28 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Karafa, Craig <ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Lambert, Jeremy <jlambert@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Quick Updates - Bluffton PD + Flock Safety\n\nGood Afternoon,\n\nI am sorry for the delay - I've been at a conference this week. Unfortunately, you can't update an email address\nonce it's been saved so I just deactivated the old user and added jlambert@townofbluffton.com as a new user.\nYou weren't doing anything wrong, it's just a limitation of our platform.\n\nLet me know if I can help with anything else!\n\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n\nOn Mon, Jan 27, 2025 at 10:00 AM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood morning Georgia,\n\nI am having a problem with resetting on of my officers information in flock. I click on his name and change his email\naddress and click save. However, when I go back into it, it is still the same one before making the change. Am I doing\nsomething wrong?\n\nThe name of the officer is Jeremy lambert\nRight now flock has his email address as olambert@townofbluffton.com however it should be\njlambert@townofbluffton.com\n\nPlease let me know what I need to do to fix this. Thank you\n\nChief Joe Babkiewicz\n\nFrom: Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, January 16, 2025 11:00 AM\n\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Burke, Helen <hburke@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig <ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas, Ryan\n<rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Quick Updates - Bluffton PD + Flock Safety\n\nGood Morning,\n\nI hope all is well. Heather let me know that 4 of your cameras were installed prematurely. I want to assure you\nthat once we get all your cameras in the ground, we will issue a credit to make up for the time between your\nfirst camera getting installed and your final one. I apologize for the mistake on our end.\n\nI also checked in on your account and noticed your Admin and CID roles are set up to access 312 networks\nbut you have over 540 networks shared with you so far. I want to make sure you are aware that every time a\nnew network gets shared with you, you then have to add it to each role in order for those users to have the\nability to search across those cameras. I can do a mass update for both of those roles for you if you'd like.\n\nI also noticed your roles don't have the VMS permission turned on yet. The VMS permissions allow users to\nview, edit, download the footage from your live video cameras as well as control the Condor PTZ camera. This\nisn't super urgent because you don't have the live cameras installed yet but while you're in the roles area to\nupdate the networks, you may want to go ahead and add those permissions in as well.\n\nLastly, you have a Lowe's nearby but I don't see that you've requested access to it yet. If you'd like to request\naccess to Lowe’s cameras, please have your Head of Agency complete the template below. Once\ncompleted and sent over to the email address below, Lowe’s will review the template to make sure that the\ninformation has been completed appropriately and will usually grant access to all of the Lowe's cameras in the\nregion within a week or two.\n\nEmail Template to be completed by the head of the agency BELOW\n—\nEmail Subject Line- Lowe’s Camera Share; Name of the Agency\nEmail Template sent to: todd.a.isenhour@lowes.com and CC emma.jensen@flocksafety.com\n\nAs TITLE for CITY/ COUNTY, I would like to formally request regional access to Lowe’s owned Flock safety\nsystems and/ or LiveView. This technology will assist in preventing or investigating criminal activity in the local\ncommunity we both serve. Lowe’s technology and my department’s access to such will only be used for bona\nfide investigations, which are documented within our department and via audit trail within the Flock Safety\nplatform. These investigative tools and technology will not be permitted for personal use, for use on\nunauthorized devices or by unauthorized users within our department.  I understand if the technology is not\nused correctly, Lowe's reserves the right to terminate the department’s access to Lowe's owned Flock safety\nsystems and/or LiveView.\n\nName\nSignature of Head of Agency, Chief of Police or Sheriff\nTitle\n\nI'm sorry for the super long email - feel free to give me a call if you have any questions on the above or if there's\nanything else I can help you with in the meantime.\n\nBest,\nGeorgia\n--\n\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSenior Customer Success Manager\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0164.pdf"},"e0935":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0935","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Project Call Agenda - 1_23_25","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-01-23","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nThursday, January 23, 2025 8:11:00 AM\nTo:\n'Alex Menke'; 'Courtney Wilson'; 'LaTonia Oyeniran'; 'Georgia Abdallah'; 'Joe Babkiewicz'; 'Ryan Fazekas'; 'Craig\nKarafa'; 'Edith Moody'; jdestasio@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nBluffton PD / FlockOS - Project Call Agenda - 1/23/25\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood morning,\n\nBelow are the agenda items and project contacts for today’s call, please let me know if you have any questions!\n\nAgenda:\nAny questions on adding map attachments?\nSSO setup\nESRI layers\nResource identified?\nCommunity Website\nWebsite & materials reviewed?\nWing VMS with Gateway\nGateway ordered?\n\nMeeting\nAttendees\nAttendees - Flock Safety\n Kelly Baeza, Technical Project Manager\n Alex Menke, Integrations Manager\n Georgia Abdallah, Customer Success Manager\n [Shadowing] Courtney Wilson, Technical Project Manager\n [Shadowing] LaTonia Oyeniran, Technical Project Manager\n\nAttendees - Bluffton PD - EST\n Chief Joe Babkiewicz\n Lieutenant Ryan Fazekas\n Lieutenant Craig Karafa\n Edith Moody, Community Relations Manager\n Michelle\n John Destasio\nProject\nMaterials\nProject Tasks: high level overview and status of the project tasks\nGoogle Drive: meeting notes and project documents saved here\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0165":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0165","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Project Call Notes - 1_23_25","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2025-02-03","text":"<image004.png> <image005.png> <image006.png> <image007.png>\nFrom:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSent:\nMonday, February 3, 2025 7:47:41 PM\nTo:\nKelly Baeza\nSubject:\nRe: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Project Call Notes - 1/23/25\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:image003.png ;image004.png ;image005.png ;image006.png ;image007.png ;image008.png ;image009.png\n;image010.png ;image011.png ;\nI did not see him today. I will check with him tomorrow\nSent from my iPhone\nOn Feb 3, 2025, at 7:29 PM, Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com> wrote:\n\nGood evening,\n\nWe’ve reached out to Bob regarding the SSO setup but have not heard back. Was the PD able to touch base with\nhim about SSO?\n\nThanks,\n\n<image003.png>\nKelly\nBaeza\nTechnical\nProject\nManager\n<image008.png>\n flocksafety.com\n<image009.png>\n\nFrom: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, January 23, 2025 11:41 AM\nTo: 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; 'Courtney Wilson' <courtney.wilson@flocksafety.com>; 'LaTonia\n\nOyeniran' <latonia.oyeniran@flocksafety.com>; 'Georgia Abdallah' <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; 'Joe\nBabkiewicz' <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; 'Ryan Fazekas' <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; 'Craig Karafa'\n<ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; 'Edith Moody' <emoody@townofbluffton.com>; jdestasio@townofbluffton.com\nSubject: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Project Call Notes - 1/23/25\n\nGood morning,\n\nAction items and notes from today’s call are below, please let me know if you have any questions!\n\nOwner\nAction Item\nStatus\nDue Date\nKelly\nRequest to Marketing to print and ship materials\nIn Progress\n1/23/2025\nKelly\nReach out to Ryan Coleman for ESRI layers\nIn Progress\n1/23/2025\nBPD\nReach out to Bob Charles for SSO setup & Gateway install response\nIn Progress\n1/24/2025\n\nIntegration\nNotes\nStatus\nMap\nAttachments\n1/7 - Your agency can add map attachments at any time (no need to send files to\nFlock); we support PDFs, Word docs, images (jpg, png), or website links as\nlocations that show as pins on the map. Examples include floor plans, links\ndirectly to a VMS, a link to instructions for a special event in the area, primary\ncontacts for a school, etc. This link has the step-by-step instructions to add\nattachments: https://help.flocksafety.com/s/article/Map-Attachments.\n\nNote: A Flock Admin user will need to add the Floor Plans permission for other\nRoles\nCompleted\nSSO\n1/23 - Alex has reached out to Bob a few times w/ no response; the PD will follow\nup with Bob\n1/7 - First step is to identify the SSO admin for Flock engineers to work with and\nalso decide whether OIDC and SAML is preferred. Alex will reach out to Bob\nCharles (rcharles@townofbluffton.com) to get this started (CC the Chief & Lt.\nFazekas)\nIn Progress\nESRI Layers\n1/23 - I will reach out to Ryan Coleman - GIS resource for the town -\nrcoleman@townofbluffton.com\n1/7 - We can bring in your ESRI layers to give you more detail on your FlockOS\nmap. We typically upload beats, city limits, and parcel layers for addresses,\nthough we can upload more (ex: hunting zones, horse trails, etc). Two ways we\ncan load your ESRI layers: you can send us a link to a publicly hosted ESRI feature\nserver, or you can send us zipped shape files that we can host for you.\nIn Progress\nCommunity\nWebsite &\nMarketing\nMaterials\n1/23 - Website and materials approved! Attn: Eydie Moody, ship to:\n101 Progressive Street, Bluffton, SC 29910\n1/15 - I sent the website & marketing materials for review:\nhttps://refer.flocksafety.com/bluffton-safe/\nIn Progress\nWing VMS w/\nGateway: (1)\n128-Channel Box\n1/23 - Alex has reached out to Bob a few times w/ no response; the PD will follow\nup with Bob\n1/7 - We will use a gateway to make the Digital Watchdog camera streams\navailable in Flock since we do not directly integrate with the VMS system. Bob\nCharles is the IT contact, Alex will reach out to Bob Charles to get the camera info\nand the address to ship the gateway (CC the Chief & Lt. Fazekas)\nIn Progress\n\nMeeting\nAttendees\nAttendees - Flock Safety\n<image010.png>\n Kelly Baeza, Technical Project Manager\n\n<image004.png> <image005.png> <image006.png> <image007.png>\n<image010.png>\n Alex Menke, Integrations Manager\n<image010.png>\n Georgia Abdallah, Customer Success Manager\n<image010.png>\n [Shadowing] Courtney Wilson, Technical Project Manager\n<image010.png>\n [Shadowing] LaTonia Oyeniran, Technical Project Manager\n\nAttendees - Bluffton PD - EST\n<image010.png>\n Chief Joe Babkiewicz\n<image011.png>\n Lieutenant Ryan Fazekas\n<image010.png>\n Captain Craig Karafa\n<image010.png>\n Edith Moody, Community Relations Manager\n<image011.png>\n Michelle\n<image011.png>\n John Destasio\nProject\nMaterials\nProject Tasks: high level overview and status of the project tasks\nGoogle Drive: meeting notes and project documents saved here\n\nThanks,\n\n<image003.png>\nKelly\nBaeza\nTechnical\nProject\nManager\n\n<image008.png>\n flocksafety.com\n<image009.png>","pdf":null},"e0027":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0027","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - ESRI Layers","frm":"Alex Menke","date":"2025-02-18","text":"From:\nAlex Menke\nSent:\nTuesday, February 18, 2025 3:07:11 PM\nTo:\nColeman, Ryan\nCc:\nKelly Baeza; Babkiewicz, Joseph; Fazekas, Ryan; Karafa, Craig; courtney.wilson@flocksafety.com;\nlatonia.oyeniran@flocksafety.com\nSubject:\nRe: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - ESRI Layers\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nTeam,\nShapefiles have been uploaded and configured. Thanks for sending those.\nAddress Points\nParcels\nMunicipal Boundary\nSchools\nI can modify the viewing of any of those (colors, transparency, viewing height, labels, etc.) but not the actual content.\nLet me know what you think.\nThanks,\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nOn Tue, Feb 18, 2025 at 12:18 PM Coleman, Ryan <rcoleman@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\n\nAlex,\n\nPlease see attached\n\nThanks,\n\nRyan J. Coleman, GISP\nGIS Manager & DBA\nO: 843.706.4570\nM: 843.368.8114\nBluffton Map Gallery\n\nFrom: Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, February 17, 2025 3:48 PM\nTo: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nCc: Coleman, Ryan <rcoleman@townofbluffton.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas,\nRyan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig <ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; courtney.wilson@flocksafety.com;\nlatonia.oyeniran@flocksafety.com\nSubject: Re: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - ESRI Layers\n\nHi Ryan,\n\nWhat's your availability this week to sync over this and get the shapefiles?\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Thu, Feb 6, 2025 at 10:42 AM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nRyan,\n\nDo you have availability tomorrow or next week to meet on this?\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Tue, Jan 28, 2025 at 8:48 PM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nRyan,\n\nI have these layers loaded.\n\nLet's sync over the address/parcel layer. It might benefit from getting this in a shape file as I'm having some info being\nstripped out of Flock versus when I look at it on the feature server map viewer.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Tue, Jan 28, 2025 at 9:26 AM Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nThanks, Ryan!\n\nWe’ll work on getting these added to Flock.\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com\n\nFrom: Coleman, Ryan <rcoleman@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Friday, January 24, 2025 11:34 AM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nCc: Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig <ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>;\nalex.menke@flocksafety.com; courtney.wilson@flocksafety.com; latonia.oyeniran@flocksafety.com\nSubject: Re: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - ESRI Layers\n\nKelly,\n\nAddresses, Parcels (with school districts, other info), and Jurisdiction boundary:\nhttps://services2.arcgis.com/emqdvAOVfTSmahz0/arcgis/rest/services/AddressParcels/FeatureServer\n\nSchools and blueprint popups:\nhttps://services2.arcgis.com/emqdvAOVfTSmahz0/arcgis/rest/services/School/FeatureServer\n\nPlease let me know if that works or if you need anything else\nThanks\nRyan\n\nGet Outlook for iOS\nFrom: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Thursday, January 23, 2025 11:53:59 AM\nTo: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>; Coleman, Ryan <rcoleman@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig <ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>;\nalex.menke@flocksafety.com <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; courtney.wilson@flocksafety.com\n<courtney.wilson@flocksafety.com>; latonia.oyeniran@flocksafety.com <latonia.oyeniran@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: RE: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - ESRI Layers\n\nRyan I would like to see a couple things with this:\n\n1. See if we can add a layer of the current district zone assignments that we have\n2. Due to the pocket holes perhaps another layer of what is within our jurisdiction and what is not\n3. Blueprints of the schools like we did with the GIS Map.\n\nThank you\n\nChief Joe Babkiewicz\n\nFrom: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, January 23, 2025 11:46 AM\nTo: Coleman, Ryan <rcoleman@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa,\nCraig <ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; alex.menke@flocksafety.com; courtney.wilson@flocksafety.com;\nlatonia.oyeniran@flocksafety.com\nSubject: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - ESRI Layers\n\nGood morning, Ryan,\n\nI’m working with Bluffton PD to get ESRI layers added to their Flock Safety map. We typically upload beats, city\nlimits, and parcel layers for addresses, though we can upload more (ex: hunting zones, school districts, etc). Two\nways we can load the ESRI layers: you can send us a link to a publicly hosted ESRI feature server, or you can send\nzipped shape files that we can host for you.\n\nPlease send the layers at your earliest convenience.\n\nThanks!\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0027.pdf"},"e0069":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0069","title":"Flock _ Bluffton - SSO","frm":"Alex Menke","date":"2025-04-28","text":"From:\nAlex Menke\nSent:\nMonday, April 28, 2025 9:58:06 AM\nTo:\nCharles, Robert\nCc:\nKelly Baeza; Babkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nRe: Flock / Bluffton - SSO\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nBob,\nConfirming we have binded the SSO to your org. Any currently logged in users will be prompted for SSO login once their\ncurrent session expires.\nPlease let me know if you have any questions or concerns.\nThanks,\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\nC. 618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nText for Immediate Response\nOn Fri, Apr 25, 2025 at 10:23 PM Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nI will send out a notice to the group Sunday-\n\nFrom: Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\n\nSent: Friday, April 25, 2025 11:22 PM\nTo: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock / Bluffton - SSO\n\nPerfect! I will get that binded to your entire organization on Monday.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\nC. 618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nText for Immediate Response\n\nOn Fri, Apr 25, 2025 at 10:16 PM Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nWorked like a charm!\n\nFrom: Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Friday, April 25, 2025 5:09 PM\nTo: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock / Bluffton - SSO\n\nBob,\n\nYour SSO should be ready to test. If someone from your org can attempt to sign-in using the sign-in URL.\n\nhttps://users.flocksafety.com/sso-login/bluffton-sc-pd-saml\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\nC. 618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nText for Immediate Response\n\nOn Mon, Feb 17, 2025 at 2:50 PM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHi Bob,\n\nChecking on your availability for this? I haven't heard anything besides our brief sync on the weekly status call.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Thu, Feb 6, 2025 at 10:45 AM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nPreview attachment Bluffton PD SAML Setup with Flock.pdf\nBluffton PD SAML Setup with Flock.pdf\n129 KB\nAlex Menke\n\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\nDate: Fri, Jan 17, 2025 at 2:46 PM\nSubject: Flock / Bluffton - SSO\nTo: <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\n\nBob,\n\nFor your single sign-on to Flock Safety, do you have SAML or OIDC? If you can use SAML, please see the attached\ndocument in step 2 of the instructions.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0031":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0031","title":"Flock _ Bluffton - Watchdog IP Cameras","frm":"Alex Menke","date":"2025-02-27","text":"From:\nAlex Menke\nSent:\nThursday, February 27, 2025 9:06:10 PM\nTo:\nrcharles@townofbluffton.com\nCc:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph; Kelly Baeza\nSubject:\nRe: Flock / Bluffton - Watchdog IP Cameras\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nBob,\nDo you have any availability tomorrow? I am OOO next week returning 3/10.\nThanks,\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nOn Thu, Feb 20, 2025 at 10:43 AM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHi Bob,\nWhat's your availability this upcoming week to sync on your VMS connection? My availability\nCan you provide a mailing address for me to ship a Flock Gateway?\nSOW states 99 connections, are all of these cameras currently up and running?\nDo you have the ability to setup Flock with a username/password to login to these cameras via IP?\nOur Gateway needs to be installed into your network and connect to your camera's IP addresses\nDo you have ability to create port forwarding rules for our gateway?\n\nThanks,\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nOn Mon, Feb 17, 2025 at 2:50 PM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHi Bob,\nChecking on your availability for this? I haven't heard anything besides our brief sync on the weekly status call.\nThanks,\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nOn Mon, Feb 3, 2025 at 8:47 AM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHi Bob,\nChecking in on this.\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nOn Tue, Jan 28, 2025 at 9:04 PM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHi Bob,\nChecking in on this.\nThanks,\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nOn Wed, Jan 22, 2025 at 2:55 PM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHi Bob,\nPinging the below.\nThanks,\nAlex Menke\n\nIntegration Manager\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nOn Fri, Jan 17, 2025 at 2:55 PM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nBob,\nWhat's your availability this upcoming week to sync on your VMS connection?\nCan you provide a mailing address for me to ship a Flock Gateway?\nSOW states 99 connections, are all of these cameras currently up and running?\nDo you have the ability to setup Flock with a username/password to login to these cameras via IP?\nOur Gateway needs to be installed into your network and connect to your camera's IP addresses\nDo you have ability to create port forwarding rules for our gateway?\nThanks\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0031.pdf"},"e0665":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0665","title":"Axon plans to sever APIs with Flock","frm":"Garrett Langley","date":"2025-01-31","text":"From:\nGarrett Langley\nSent:\nFriday, January 31, 2025 3:02:17 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nAxon plans to sever APIs with Flock\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nView in Browser  |  Forward to a Friend\nI am disappointed to share that Axon made a surprise decision to end our partnership\nand cut off the API access that law enforcement depends upon. Axon decided that being\nopen and collaborative is “no longer in Axon’s best interests,” and no additional reason\nwas given to us.\nSo what does this mean for you?\nWe are not one-hundred percent sure. Axon executives have not returned our calls, so\nit's unclear their intention or plans.\nWhat we do know is:\n1. We will continue to invest in our own API program (including sending Flock data to\nAxon). As you already know, we work with a vast array of public safety technology\ncompanies (see below) and expect to continue growing our ecosystem of partners\nto help you solve more crime.\n2. Axon will no longer support new mutual customers starting July 24, 2025. They may\ncontinue to support existing customers, but it's unclear to what degree.\n3. We will continue to try to get Axon back to supporting an open ecosystem.\nHistory of the Flock and Axon Partnership\nAxon was actually an early investor in Flock Safety. Our patented Vehicle Fingerprint\ntechnology was integrated into their Fleet 3 devices upon launch 4 years ago. This\nintegration allowed for the automatic transfer of Flock-derived evidence into\nEvidence.com, streamlining the process for law enforcement.\nLast summer, we spent a couple of months with Axon to broaden our partnership. We\nproposed an expansive relationship but wanted to be mindful of keeping the majority of\nour engineering resources focused on building products for you. Axon chose a smaller,\nbut still increased integration across Fusus and Flock devices. We agreed to it on\nAugust 28, 2024, and we have not spoken to Axon about it since signing that new\npartnership agreement.\n\nFrom our onset, and given our name, Flock believes that we are better together. To this\neffect, hundreds of agencies leverage our APIs across dozens of products, including but\nnot limited to:\nCAD\nMark43\nTyler Technologies\nEvidence and Data\nForcemetrics\nLiveEarth\nThinkLP\nLocation Services\nCradlepoint\nGetac\nSafeFleet\nMapping\nESRI\nCritical Response Group\nGeoComm\nReal-time software\nCommand Central Aware by Motorola\nCitigraf by Genetec\nPrepared 911\nStraxx by Utility Inc.\nFusus by Axon\nVMS\nAvigilon\nGenetec\nMilestone\nAs you can see, many of these companies offer directly competitive products and\nservices to what Flock offers. You can see a more exhaustive list here:\nhttps://www.flocksafety.com/use-cases/real-time-crime-center\nMany companies in the industry are aligned that the world is safer when we all work\ntogether. We hope that Axon comes to the same conclusion over time.\nGarrett Langley\nFounder and CEO\nFlock Safety\nFlock Safety\n1170 Howell Mill Rd NW, Suite 210\nAtlanta, Georgia 30318, United States","pdf":null},"e0879":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0879","title":"Tracker Flock Cameras","frm":"Heather Phillips","date":"2025-02-06","text":"From:\nHeather Phillips\nSent:\nThursday, February 6, 2025 10:47:42 AM\nTo:\nClarkson, Constance; Babkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nRe: Tracker Flock Cameras\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Morning Chief,\nFollowing up to provide a link for approval (below) in case you need it. Also wanted to add that location #16 needs approval, in\naddition to 11, 13, 15 and C04.\nDeployment Plan\nThank you!\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 412-512-0563\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com\n\nOn Tue, Feb 4, 2025 at 5:28 PM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nAfternoon Heather.\n\nThank you for coordinating the Google sheet with me.  I’ve added a few columns, updated the Town’s status and\nsaved to your share drive.  For the rest of the team, I converted it to Excel and saved it to the project folder at\n I0001 Flock Data Spreadsheet.xlsx.\n\nHeather – please see Column C for the next approved installation of camera #s 8, 9, 17, C02, and C03.\nChief – Camera locations 11, 13, 15 and C04 were adjusted.  If you don’t have any questions or concerns, please\napprove these locations in the Flock Deployment Plan.\nAmanda – for the property owners who have not yet replied to emails for the easement requests, please start calling\nthem if you a have a good phone number.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, February 3, 2025 9:18 AM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Tracker\n\nGood Morning!!\n\nJust wanted to let you know that I am still working on our tracker. I should have it completed by COB. I got pulled into\nmeetings this morning so I'm delayed. I'll keep you posted!\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 412-512-0563\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0958":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0958","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Project Call Agenda - 2_6_25","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-02-06","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nThursday, February 6, 2025 8:57:50 AM\nTo:\n'Alex Menke'; 'Courtney Wilson'; 'Georgia Abdallah'; 'Joe Babkiewicz'; 'Ryan Fazekas'; 'Craig Karafa'; 'Edith\nMoody'; jdestasio@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nBluffton PD / FlockOS - Project Call Agenda - 2/6/25\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood morning,\n\nBelow are the agenda items and project contacts for today’s call, please let me know if you have any questions!\n\nAgenda:\nSSO setup\nBob responded to get started?\nESRI layers\nReview ESRI layers\nCommunity Website\nReview rollout options for the website\nWing VMS with Gateway\nBob responded with camera info?\nGateway ordered?\n\nMeeting\nAttendees\nAttendees - Flock Safety\n Kelly Baeza, Technical Project Manager\n Alex Menke, Integrations Manager\n Georgia Abdallah, Customer Success Manager\n [Shadowing] Courtney Wilson, Technical Project Manager\n\nAttendees - Bluffton PD - EST\n Chief Joe Babkiewicz\n Lieutenant Ryan Fazekas\n Captain Craig Karafa\n Edith Moody, Community Relations Manager\n Michelle\n John Destasio\nProject\nMaterials\nProject Tasks: high level overview and status of the project tasks\nGoogle Drive: meeting notes and project documents saved here\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0963":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0963","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Project Call Notes - 2_6_25","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-02-06","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nThursday, February 6, 2025 1:34:33 PM\nTo:\n'Alex Menke'; 'Courtney Wilson'; 'Georgia Abdallah'; 'Joe Babkiewicz'; 'Ryan Fazekas'; 'Craig Karafa'; 'Edith\nMoody'; jdestasio@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nBluffton PD / FlockOS - Project Call Notes - 2/6/25\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:2.6.25 - Bluffton PD FlockOS - Project Call Notes.pdf ;\n\nGood afternoon,\n\nAction items and notes from today’s call are below, please let me know if you have any questions!\n\nOwner\nAction Item\nStatus\nDue Date\nBob\nSchedule time w/ Alex to review gateway integration\nIn Progress\n2/10/2025\nAlex/PD\nRequest the shapefiles from the GIS contact (Ryan)\nIn Progress\n2/14/2025\nBob\nSSO setup on the PD side\nIn Progress\n2/14/2025\n\nIntegration\nNotes\nStatus\nSSO\n2/6 - Bob confirmed they use SAML for SSO, Alex sent him the information to set this up on\ntheir end\n1/23 - Alex has reached out to Bob a few times w/ no response; the PD will follow up with\nBob\n1/7 - First step is to identify the SSO admin for Flock engineers to work with and also decide\nwhether OIDC and SAML is preferred. Alex will reach out to Bob Charles\n(rcharles@townofbluffton.com) to get this started (CC the Chief & Lt. Fazekas)\nIn Progress\nESRI Layers\n2/6 - We reviewed the layers, there are some changes we'd like to make. The PD will help\nAlex sync with GIS to get shapefiles vs the REST endpoint (Alex sent an email to the GIS\ncontact after the call)\n1/30 - Alex loaded the ESRI layers\n1/23 - Email from the Chief: Ryan I would like to see a couple things with this:\n\n1. See if we can add a layer of the current district zone assignments that we have\n2. Due to the pocket holes perhaps another layer of what is within our jurisdiction and\nwhat is not\n3. Blueprints of the schools like we did with the GIS Map.\nIn Progress\nCommunity\nWebsite &\nMarketing\nMaterials\n2/6 - Materials were sent to the printer, they will be shipped to Eydie. Community website\nrollout plan: however you want to approach this is up to your agency, but some options\nwe've seen other agencies do:\nOption 1: Press release and public roll out\nHighest level is option 1, publish on social media and distribute marketing\nmaterials, \"here is what we're doing and we want to tell everyone about it\",\nCompleted\n\nsend out a press release\nOption 2: Social media posts and community outreach\nPost on social media, have officers hand out flyers, business cards, etc\nOption 3: just community outreach\nOfficer outreach, handing out the marketing materials\nOption 4: Website communication as needed\nThis is a targeted approach; target specific locations, just reach out to them\ndirectly and point them to the website\n1/23 - Website and materials approved! Attn: Eydie Moody, ship to: 101 Progressive Street,\nBluffton, SC 29910\n1/15 - I sent the website & marketing materials for review:\nhttps://refer.flocksafety.com/bluffton-safe/\nWing VMS w/\nGateway: (1) 128-\nChannel Box\n2/6 - Bob has the info we need for the gateway/VMS, he and Alex will schedule a separate\ncall to get this started (hopefully next week)\n1/23 - Alex has reached out to Bob a few times w/ no response; the PD will follow up with\nBob\n1/7 - We will use a gateway to make the Digital Watchdog camera streams available in Flock\nsince we do not directly integrate with the VMS system. Bob Charles is the IT contact, Alex\nwill reach out to Bob Charles to get the camera info and the address to ship the gateway\n(CC the Chief & Lt. Fazekas)\nIn Progress\n\nMeeting\nAttendees\nAttendees - Flock Safety\n Kelly Baeza, Technical Project Manager\n Alex Menke, Integrations Manager\n Georgia Abdallah, Customer Success Manager\n [Shadowing] Courtney Wilson, Technical Project Manager\n\nAttendees - Bluffton PD - EST\n Chief Joe Babkiewicz\n Lieutenant Ryan Fazekas\n Captain Craig Karafa\n Edith Moody, Community Relations Manager\n Michelle\n John Destasio\nProject\nMaterials\nProject Tasks: high level overview and status of the project tasks\nGoogle Drive: meeting notes and project documents saved here\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0698":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0698","title":"Private Divisions Alert","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2025-02-07","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nFriday, February 7, 2025 11:23:16 AM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nRe: Private Divisions Alert\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nWe're slowly rolling out the new roles page to Admins so soon your page will look like mine. In the meantime, I turned Alerts on for:\nBluffton PD\nSun City Hilton Head (SC)\nPine Ridge- Bluffton (SC)\nThe Villages at Palmetto Pointe (SC)\nHome Depot #1115\nWe've requested access to The Townes at Buckwalter so once they accept, I'll add them to the list.\nOther departments that have some cameras near your jurisdiction are Hardeeville PD, Jasper County SO, and Town of Hilton Head. If you decide you want me to turn this on for you later, just let me know.\nThanks,\nGeorgia\nOn Fri, Feb 7, 2025 at 11:01 AM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nThank you Georgia. I am trying to follow the video but I do not have the same thing as you. This is what I get when I go to edit a specific role. It does not allow me to change anything with the shared networks.  I think it would be easiest if I just told you the places we would like to receive alerts on.\n\nI would say everything within the town of Bluffton. This includes\n\nPalmetto point, Townes at Buckwalter, Pine Ridge, and I think there may be a few others. Anything out of town we do not want to receive alerts on at this time.\n\nThank you for your help in this.\n\nFrom: Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Friday, February 7, 2025 10:02 AM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Private Divisions Alert\n\nGood Morning,\n\nWatch this video and then give me a call if you have any questions.\n\nInstructions for Admins\n1. Go to each role > ensure the hot list is turned on for the agencies and networks that are nearby and that you actually want to receive alerts from. If you provide me with a list of agencies, I can make sure they are all selected along with the private cameras in your area.\n\nInstructions for your users\n\n1. Go to Alerts > Select All Cameras from the left hand side\n\nOn Thu, Feb 6, 2025 at 3:06 PM Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nYes, I'll record a quick video and send it over to you soon so that you can share with your department.\n\nOn Thu, Feb 6, 2025 at 3:03 PM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood afternoon Georgia,\n\nIn our meeting today you mentioned setting alerts for vehicles that go into our private communities that have Flock. Palmetto Point, Pineridge, and The Townes at Buckwalter were three locations that you mentioned. I tried to figure out how to set up those notification but could not figure it out.\nDo you have step by step on how to do this. Thank you.\n\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nChief of Police\nOffice | 843-706-4537\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0698.pdf"},"e0694":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0694","title":"Mobile App Guide - Flock Safety + Bluffton PD","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2025-02-06","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nThursday, February 6, 2025 3:05:31 PM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nMobile App Guide - Flock Safety + Bluffton PD\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:Flock Safety Mobile App Guide.PDF ;\n\nGood Afternoon,\nThanks for your time earlier today. Please see the attached Mobile App guide. Let me know if you have any questions.\nAlso, if you want to request access to Lowe's cameras, please complete the template below.\n—\nEmail Subject Line- Lowe’s Camera Share; Name of the Agency\nEmail Template sent to: todd.a.isenhour@lowes.com and CC emma.jensen@flocksafety.com\nAs TITLE for CITY/ COUNTY, I would like to formally request regional access to Lowe’s owned Flock safety\nsystems and/ or LiveView. This technology will assist in preventing or investigating criminal activity in the local\ncommunity we both serve. Lowe’s technology and my department’s access to such will only be used for bona fide\ninvestigations, which are documented within our department and via audit trail within the Flock Safety platform.\nThese investigative tools and technology will not be permitted for personal use, for use on unauthorized devices\nor by unauthorized users within our department.  I understand if the technology is not used correctly, Lowe's\nreserves the right to terminate the department’s access to Lowe's owned Flock safety systems and/or LiveView.\n\nName\nSignature of Head of Agency, Chief of Police or Sheriff\nTitle\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\n\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0696":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0696","title":"Flock Safety_ New AI Feature Coming Soon + API Update","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2025-02-07","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nFriday, February 7, 2025 9:28:28 AM\nTo:\nBcc:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nFlock Safety: New AI Feature Coming Soon + API Update\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nI'm reaching out to share some exciting news. We will be launching Freeform Search soon. This has been our #1 most requested\nfeature and will allow you to write exactly what you're searching for. For example, \"car with damage\", \"van with ladder on top\",\n\"biker wearing black sweatshirt\", \"car with stripes\".\nIf you are interested in getting early access to the feature, please let me know so that I can alert you when we launch the sign up\nsheet. We'll also share pricing details once we have it.\nIn the meantime, click here to register for Flock Safety's 2025 product launch to learn more about Freeform Search, our free\nAPI's and everything else we're working on in 2025.\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0696.pdf"},"e1067":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1067","title":"Flock Safety Product Update _ February 2025","frm":"Myron Maret","date":"2025-02-07","text":"From:\nMyron Maret\nSent:\nFriday, February 7, 2025 3:54:58 PM\nTo:\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nFlock Safety Product Update | February 2025\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nHello,\nHere's our monthly snapshot of our latest product releases. We've included videos and articles to help you\nmake the most of your Flock Safety system. Click here to see what's new.\nTopics in this month’s newsletter include:\nNo-Cost API Access\nAudio Analytics\nNew Search & Alerts Experiences\nSharing Permission Updates\nFor a deeper dive, we'd encourage you to check out the Help Center to access knowledge articles, create\nand track the status of your cases, and take advantage of trainings and certifications. Access the\nupdated help center here.\nIf you have any questions about how any of our latest enhancements might help your agency solve crime\nor you want to learn more about any other feature, please always feel free to reach out to me!\nThanks and be safe,\nMyron Maret\nCustomer Success\n\n flocksafety.com\nClick here to unsubscribe from this list or manage your preferences here.","pdf":null},"e0699":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0699","title":"Flock Safety New Trailer Options","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2025-02-17","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nMonday, February 17, 2025 11:39:53 AM\nTo:\nBcc:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nFlock Safety New Trailer Options\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:LPR Trailers One Sheet.PDF ;LE-Flock Mobile Security Trailer One Pager (2).PDF ;\n\nGood Afternoon,\nI hope all is well. We launched a few new products last week including two new trailer options featuring LPR's and Live Video\nCameras. Attached you'll find more information on these products. If you're interested in learning more, please let me know.\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0968":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0968","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Project Call Agenda - 2_19_25","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-02-19","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nWednesday, February 19, 2025 3:06:14 PM\nTo:\n'Alex Menke'; 'Georgia Abdallah'; 'Joe Babkiewicz'; 'Ryan Fazekas'; 'Craig Karafa'; 'Edith Moody';\njdestasio@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nBluffton PD / FlockOS - Project Call Agenda - 2/19/25\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood afternoon,\n\nBelow are the agenda items and project contacts for tomorrow’s call, please let me know if you have any questions!\n\nAgenda:\nSSO setup\nAwaiting response from Bob to start the setup\nWing VMS with Gateway\nAwaiting camera info from Bob\n\nMeeting\nAttendees\nAttendees - Flock Safety\n Kelly Baeza, Technical Project Manager\n Alex Menke, Integrations Manager\n Georgia Abdallah, Customer Success Manager\n\nAttendees - Bluffton PD - EST\n Chief Joe Babkiewicz\n Lieutenant Ryan Fazekas\n Captain Craig Karafa\n Edith Moody, Community Relations Manager\n Michelle\n John Destasio\nProject\nMaterials\nProject Tasks: high level overview and status of the project tasks\nGoogle Drive: meeting notes and project documents saved here\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0700":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0700","title":"Flock FreeForm and Nova Early Access","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2025-02-19","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nWednesday, February 19, 2025 6:21:24 PM\nTo:\nBcc:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nFlock FreeForm and Nova Early Access\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nReaching out to provide the sign up forms for paid early access to FreeForm Search and Flock Nova. If you have\nany interest in learning more about these new products, please sign up below. Early access is slated to begin at\nthe end of February.\nFreeForm Early Access - the ability to tell Flock exactly what you’re looking for in your own words. Example:\n\"black car with damage on the side\". Want to be a part of the paid early access period? Apply here.\nFlock Nova Early Access - consolidates CAD, RMS, Flock Data & external sources into a single platform,\nsaving hours for investigators and helping them connect the dots. Want to be a part of the paid early access\nperiod? Apply here.\nLet me know if you have any questions.\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0881":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0881","title":"Location #14 Approval","frm":"Heather Phillips","date":"2025-02-26","text":"From:\nHeather Phillips\nSent:\nWednesday, February 26, 2025 1:03:27 PM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nCc:\nClarkson, Constance\nSubject:\nLocation #14 Approval\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon Chief,\nWhen you have the time, could you please review and approve location #14? This was recently remapped down Buck Island\ntoward parkway. Please let me know if you have any questions.\nThank you!\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 412-512-0563\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e1068":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1068","title":"Flock Safety _ System updates coming next week","frm":"Myron Maret","date":"2025-02-28","text":"From:\nMyron Maret\nSent:\nFriday, February 28, 2025 2:53:00 PM\nTo:\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nFlock Safety | System updates coming next week\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nHello,\nWe’re excited to let you know that we’ll be updating your Flock Safety organization with enhanced\nversions of the Search, Alerts, and Roles pages. These updates are significant improvements based on\nyour feedback, and we’re confident they’ll make a big difference for your organization. If your agency\ncurrently uses these features, they will automatically be updated to the new experience. This email has\nonly been sent to your Flock Safety Administrator users - please forward the following as appropriate to\nyour general users.\n---------------------------------------\nOn 03/06, you will notice three changes to your Flock Safety system. Your Search and Alerts pages will\nbe updated to newly designed experiences that allow you to access the search results and hotlist alerts\nin a more organized and efficient way. If you are an Administrator, the Roles page in Admin will also be\ngetting a refresh to allow you to add and edit roles faster. Please review the following videos to familiarize\nyourself with the features ahead of their release.\nWhat to expect:\nSearch: Simplify investigations with easy-to-use filters, advanced mapping tools, multiple data\nviews, and efficient options to refine search criteria for faster and more accurate results. Watch\nvideo\nAlerts: Enhance alert management with grouped views, hotlist search capabilities, user-specific\npreferences, collaborative incident feed comments, and streamlined access to detailed alert\ninformation and actions. Watch video\nRoles (Admin-only): Streamline user permission and network management with bulk actions,\nimproved navigation, and greater flexibility in assigning specific permissions to networks and\nfeatures. Watch video\nIf you prefer, you can switch back to the legacy versions of the Search and Alert pages at any time by\nclicking the respective banners at the top of your screen. If you need assistance, please reach out to\nsupport@flocksafety.com.\nThank you and be safe,\n\nMyron Maret\nFlock Safety\nCustomer Success Technologist\n myron.maret@flocksafety.com\n 404.631.6599\n flocksafety.com\nClick here to unsubscribe from this list or manage your preferences here.","pdf":null},"e0234":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0234","title":"Flock _ Bluffton PD - Watchdog IP Cameras","frm":"Charles, Robert","date":"2025-05-30","text":"From:\nCharles, Robert\nSent:\nFriday, May 30, 2025 10:41:35 AM\nTo:\nAlex Menke; Babkiewicz, Joseph; Kelly Baeza\nCc:\nClay Lucas; Fazekas, Ryan\nSubject:\nRE: Flock / Bluffton PD - Watchdog IP Cameras\nSensitivity:Normal\nAlex, I will see if we have a list currently with the lat/long- They are all on our GIS maps and I’m not sure how he records them. May be a quick dump, or not!\n\nRegards,\n\nBob\n\nFrom: Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Friday, May 30, 2025 10:34 AM\nTo: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nCc: Clay Lucas <clay@carolinalowvoltage.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock / Bluffton PD - Watchdog IP Cameras\n\nHi Team,\n\nI've successfully added 98 cameras from the list Bob provided. There is a new network only available to admins currently. While most cameras are loading correctly, a few are not working as expected. Some of these were noted on Bob's list as potentially non-functional, and I've\nalready followed up with Bob regarding the other cameras that are not connecting. I'll continue to collaborate with him to resolve these issues.\n\nFor now, I've placed all camera locations at the police department. I'll do my best to update these locations based on the camera names. If you have a list of camera names with their corresponding latitude and longitude, please send it my way, and I can update the locations in bulk.\n\nThanks to Bob and Clay for all their assistance with this!\n\nHave a great weekend.\n\nBest,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\nC. 618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nText for Immediate Response\n\nOn Tue, May 6, 2025 at 8:09 PM Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nI literally just got it back from the Chief this afternoon! I’ll be on the road all day tomorrow and I don’t trust trying to run that from the car so I’m afraid it will be Thursday/Friday depending on the help I get!!!\n\nI will be in touch soon now, promise!\n\nBob\n\nFrom: Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, May 6, 2025 8:30 PM\nTo: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock / Bluffton PD - Watchdog IP Cameras\n\nHey Bob,\n\nAny status update on this list?\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\nC. 618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nText for Immediate Response\n\nOn Tue, Apr 29, 2025 at 11:12 AM Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nI handed it off to the Chief to validate one final time… You will have it as soon as I get it back. (OK, a little after!)\n\nFrom: Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, April 29, 2025 12:10 PM\nTo: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock / Bluffton PD - Watchdog IP Cameras\n\nAwesome, glad all is well then! Let me know if any other questions come up.\n\nAlso, please get me the camera list and I can configure it and you won't have to hear me pinging you again :)\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\nC. 618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nText for Immediate Response\n\nOn Tue, Apr 29, 2025 at 12:08 PM Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood news, we determined this after I added a new user to the group. I’ll let Command know that they default to Patrol, which is a good thing!\n\nAppreciate your help Alex.\n\nBob\n\nFrom: Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, April 29, 2025 11:31 AM\nTo: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock / Bluffton PD - Watchdog IP Cameras\n\nYou don't have to have a user account in Flock already for it to work, if you login using SSO for your first time then it will create you a new account in Flock. The new users will default to a \"patrol\" role in Flock.\n\nCheck the following:\n\n1. “User assignment required?” = No\nIf enabled, only users explicitly assigned can access the app — which blocks JIT provisioning for unassigned users.\nTo check:\nAzure AD → Enterprise Applications → [Flock App] → Properties\nSet User assignment required? to No\n\n2. SAML Attributes Must Include Email\nFlock needs to match or create users using a unique identifier — usually the email address in the SAML assertion.\nEnsure Azure is sending:\nNameID = user email (or user principal name, if that’s how Flock matches accounts)\nOR a custom claim like email = user.email\nTo verify:\nAzure AD → Enterprise Applications → [Flock App] → Single sign-on → Attributes & Claims\nEnsure at least one claim contains a valid email address for the user\n3. Claims Are Sent Even for New Users\nSometimes, custom claims are scoped only to assigned users or groups. Ensure that your claims (especially the email) aren’t conditional on group membership or a dynamic rule.\n4. The User’s Azure AD Profile Is Properly Populated\nIf user.mail is blank (which can happen with service accounts or synced accounts from on-prem AD), the email claim may not be populated, and Flock won’t create the user.\nTo check: Go to Azure AD → Users → [select user] → Ensure Email or UserPrincipalName is correctly filled out\n\nTest with a brand-new AD user\nIf you have a test user who is not assigned to the app but exists in AD and has the correct email fields, try signing in via the SSO login URL. If they’re blocked, the sign-in logs should tell you exactly why.\nLet me know if you have any questions or concerns.\nThanks,\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\nC. 618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nText for Immediate Response\n\nOn Tue, Apr 29, 2025 at 11:24 AM Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nI created a Flock security group and applied it to the Flock SAML. Initial results are fine of course, just trying to put together the pieces of how Flock will act with a new user. I’m assuming they still have to be entered into Flock as a user and then they will mate up.\n\nBob\n\nFrom: Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, April 29, 2025 10:03 AM\nTo: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock / Bluffton PD - Watchdog IP Cameras\n\nTry this: Azure AD only allows access to users that have been explicitly assigned to the SAML application, unless the setting “User assignment required?” is set to No.\n\nWhat to check:\nIn Azure AD → Enterprise Applications → Flock App → Users and groups\nMake sure the affected user is listed here.\nIf not, either:\nAdd the user, or\nGo to Properties and change User assignment required? to No (if appropriate for the org’s security posture).\nLet me know if that works.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\nC. 618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nText for Immediate Response\n\nOn Tue, Apr 29, 2025 at 9:59 AM Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nThis is what I get after the SSO:\n\nFrom: Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, April 29, 2025 9:43 AM\nTo: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock / Bluffton PD - Watchdog IP Cameras\n\nBob,\n\nCan you check the Active Directory permissions for Chief? If it worked for you then I would assume he doesn’t have access via AD.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex\n\nOn Apr 28, 2025, at 6:57 PM, Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nChief, I was able to log in without a problem. Keeping in mind I don’t have the access you do by any stretch. Alex or Kelly, can you look into the back end and see anything?\n\nRegards,\n\nBob\n\n<image002.png>\n\n<image003.png>\n\n<image004.png>\n\n<image005.png>\n\nFrom: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Monday, April 28, 2025 4:27 PM\nTo: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>; Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>; 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\nCc: Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Clay Lucas <clay@carolinalowvoltage.com>\nSubject: RE: Flock / Bluffton PD - Watchdog IP Cameras\n\nGood afternoon,\n\nI just went to sign into Flock and it is now giving me an error. It has been doing it all day. I am trying to input information into a case from last night. The message I received is that I need permission from administration to go into Flock. Can someone tell me what is going on and\nhow do we fix this????\n\nChief Joe Babkiewicz\n\nFrom: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, April 28, 2025 10:45 AM\nTo: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>; 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\nCc: Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Clay Lucas <clay@carolinalowvoltage.com>\nSubject: RE: Flock / Bluffton PD - Watchdog IP Cameras\n\nThanks, Bob!\n\nAre folks logging in to Flock via SSO? If so, I’ll go ahead and mark this integration complete. Please send the list of cameras at your earliest convenience today.\n\nThanks,\n\n<image001.png>\n\nKelly Baeza\nSr. Technical Project Manager\n<image006.png>\n flocksafety.com\n<image007.png>\n\nFrom: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Friday, April 25, 2025 11:21 PM\nTo: Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\nCc: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Clay Lucas <clay@carolinalowvoltage.com>\nSubject: RE: Flock / Bluffton PD - Watchdog IP Cameras\n\nExcellent, thank you for sending the rails.\n\nI spent the afternoon working on the camera sites that were down when you were here and have most of them running again. Need a little tree trimming next week to get the remaining three back up. That said, I will be able to configure those cameras now for\nFlock. List will be as complete as possible and to you by Monday.\n\nAgain, the SSO tested out so another win!\n\nI’ll be in touch, hope you have a good weekend.\n\nBob\n\nFrom: Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Friday, April 25, 2025 5:13 PM\nTo: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Clay Lucas <clay@carolinalowvoltage.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock / Bluffton PD - Watchdog IP Cameras\n\nBob,\n\nPlease keep me posted on the camera list and user/pass, once that is to me I can then configure the streams.\n\nI mailed you rails for the NVR to go into the server rack.\n\nSSO is ready to test.\n\nThanks for all the help so far.\n\nEnjoy your weekend.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\nC. 618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nText for Immediate Response\n\nOn Thu, Apr 24, 2025 at 8:35 AM Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nWilco.\n\nGot partially done last night and will finish as soon as I get some clear space this afternoon. Thank you for being here yesterday and working through the SSO. I will look for testing emails as well.\n\nRegards,\n\nBob\n\nFrom: Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, April 24, 2025 9:22 AM\nTo: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock / Bluffton PD - Watchdog IP Cameras\n\nBob,\n\nPlease follow up with the remaining camera list when you can.\n\nThank you very much for getting the hard parts completed with me yesterday, should be downhill from here with adding the remaining cameras.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex\n\nOn Apr 23, 2025, at 10:31 AM, Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nBob,\n\nWrapping up at Beaufort now. Will be heading your way soon from downtown Beaufort.\n\nI can take you to lunch too if needed.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\nC. 618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nText for Immediate Response\n\nOn Wed, Apr 23, 2025 at 8:03 AM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nBob,\n\nHeading to Beaufort and then I will reach out this afternoon when I’m headed your way.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex\n\nOn Apr 15, 2025, at 4:40 PM, Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHi Team,\n\nI wanted to send a quick reminder about my visit next week on Wednesday, April 23rd. I'll be in Beaufort during the morning and will head to your location that afternoon. I've also set aside a full day on Thursday 4/24 to dedicate to\nyour agency.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\nC. 618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\nText for Immediate Response\n\nOn Mon, Apr 7, 2025 at 4:07 PM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nBob,\n\nPlease use this link to see my schedule availability and to schedule time on my calendar.\n\nClockwise Scheduler\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Mon, Apr 7, 2025 at 3:46 PM Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood afternoon Alex. I would like to have a touch base this week to discuss the IT side specifically with DWS and our routing for your gateway.\n\nHow does your schedule look? I need to coordinate two other people for the call-\n\nThank you, in advance.\n\nBob\n\nRobert Charles\nLaw Enforcement Technical Analyst\nAgency ARSO/LASO\n\nOffice  | 843-706-7814\nMobile| 843-505-6836\n\nTown of Bluffton | Police Department\nPO Box 386\n101 Progressive Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, April 7, 2025 4:42 PM\nTo: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock / Bluffton PD - Watchdog IP Cameras\n\nBluffton Team,\n\nJust checking in — would you have some time this week for a quick sync to ensure we're aligned ahead of the onsite in two weeks? I want to make sure everything’s on track for a successful visit.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Wed, Apr 2, 2025 at 1:46 PM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nBob,\n\nDo you have availability next week that we could sync before my on site to ensure we are effective? 30-60 mins and used somewhat as a small working session: check out your SSO configurations, look into VMS setup and\npreplan static IP and port forwarding rules.\n\nI also realized I didn't CC everyone on my last response stating: \"Let's plan that I would come to your site on the second half of 4/23 at 1pm and would be available all day on 4/24 if needed.\"\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Mon, Mar 31, 2025 at 12:37 PM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nLet's plan that I would come to your site on the second half of 4/23 at 1pm and would be available all day on 4/24 if needed.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Mon, Mar 31, 2025 at 10:39 AM Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nI am good with this block except Tuesday morning (and this can be potentially changed). I would also want to have our camera vendor on standby as well in case there are any deeper questions that he could answer\nbetter.\n\nRegards,\n\nBob\n\nFrom: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Monday, March 31, 2025 10:08 AM\nTo: Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: RE: Flock / Bluffton PD - Watchdog IP Cameras\n\nI will be around. However, I think many things you will need to address will be with IT. I would want to hear from them about their availability.\n\nBob will you be around during this time?\n\nChief Joe Babkiewicz\n\nFrom: Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, March 31, 2025 10:05 AM\nTo: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock / Bluffton PD - Watchdog IP Cameras\n\nHi Team,\n\nI am following up on my previous email.\n\nWould coming on-site during the week of April 22-24 work for you? I'll already be in a neighboring city then.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Wed, Mar 19, 2025 at 7:23 PM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\n\n<image002.png> <image003.png> <image004.png> <image005.png>\nTeam,\n\nDoes me coming on site the week of 4/22-4/24 work for you? I will already be visiting a neighbor city of yours.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex\n\nOn Mar 10, 2025, at 9:46 PM, Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nTeam,\n\nWhat's your availability this week to sync on this?\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Tue, Mar 4, 2025 at 7:17 PM Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHi Bob!\n\nPlease choose a time next week to meet with Alex and me to discuss the Watchdog IP cameras.\n\nhttps://www.getclockwise.com/c/kelly-baeza-flocksafety-com/bluffton-pd-watchdog-ip-cameras-call\n\n1. Can you provide a mailing address for me to ship a Flock Gateway?\n2. SOW states 99 connections, are all of these cameras currently up and running?\n3. Do you have the ability to setup Flock with a username/password to login to these cameras via IP?\n4. Our Gateway needs to be installed into your network and connect to your camera's IP addresses\n1. Do you have ability to create port forwarding rules for our gateway?\n\nThanks!\n\n<image001.png>\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n<image006.png>\n flocksafety.com\n<image007.png>\n\nFrom: Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, February 27, 2025 9:05 PM\nTo: rcharles@townofbluffton.com\nCc: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock / Bluffton - Watchdog IP Cameras\n\nBob,\n\nDo you have any availability tomorrow? I am OOO next week returning 3/10.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Thu, Feb 20, 2025 at 10:43 AM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHi Bob,\n\nWhat's your availability this upcoming week to sync on your VMS connection? My availability\n·        Can you provide a mailing address for me to ship a Flock Gateway?\n·        SOW states 99 connections, are all of these cameras currently up and running?\n·        Do you have the ability to setup Flock with a username/password to login to these cameras via IP?\n·        Our Gateway needs to be installed into your network and connect to your camera's IP addresses\no   Do you have ability to create port forwarding rules for our gateway?\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Mon, Feb 17, 2025 at 2:50 PM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHi Bob,\n\nChecking on your availability for this? I haven't heard anything besides our brief sync on the weekly status call.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Mon, Feb 3, 2025 at 8:47 AM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHi Bob,\nChecking in on this.\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\n\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Tue, Jan 28, 2025 at 9:04 PM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHi Bob,\n\nChecking in on this.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Wed, Jan 22, 2025 at 2:55 PM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHi Bob,\n\nPinging the below.\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Fri, Jan 17, 2025 at 2:55 PM Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nBob,\n\nWhat's your availability this upcoming week to sync on your VMS connection?\n1. Can you provide a mailing address for me to ship a Flock Gateway?\n2. SOW states 99 connections, are all of these cameras currently up and running?\n3. Do you have the ability to setup Flock with a username/password to login to these cameras via IP?\n4. Our Gateway needs to be installed into your network and connect to your camera's IP addresses\n1. Do you have ability to create port forwarding rules for our gateway?\n\nThanks\n\nAlex Menke\nIntegration Manager\n\n618.210.0755 | Alex.Menke@flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0234.pdf"},"e0982":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0982","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Today's Project Call - 3_6_25","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-03-06","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nThursday, March 6, 2025 9:34:19 AM\nTo:\n'Babkiewicz, Joseph'; 'Alex Menke'; 'Georgia Abdallah'; 'Fazekas, Ryan'; 'Karafa, Craig'; 'Moody, Edith';\n'Destasio, John'; 'Charles, Robert'\nSubject:\nRE: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Today's Project Call - 3/6/25\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi Bob!\n\nI sent an email on Tuesday to schedule time with Alex to review the VMS with Gateway process, and I believe he has an email\ngoing with you to discuss the SSO setup, though I’m sure both can be addressed in 1 call.\n\nPlease use the link I sent you on Tuesday to select a time that works with your calendar for a call.\n\nThanks!\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com\n\nFrom: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Thursday, March 6, 2025 9:31 AM\nTo: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>; 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; 'Georgia Abdallah'\n<georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig\n<ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Moody, Edith <emoody@townofbluffton.com>; Destasio, John\n<jdestasio@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: RE: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Today's Project Call - 3/6/25\n\nI am fine with cancelling if there is nothing else to cover. I will touch base with Bob. Could we add him to the email list?\nHis email is\n\nrcharles@townofbluffton.com\n\nBob please see email below from Kelly. Thank you\n\nChief Joe Babkiewicz\n\nFrom: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, March 6, 2025 9:26 AM\nTo: 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; 'Georgia Abdallah' <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; Babkiewicz,\nJoseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig\n<ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Moody, Edith <emoody@townofbluffton.com>; Destasio, John\n<jdestasio@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Today's Project Call - 3/6/25\n\nGood morning!\n\nThe only remaining integrations in progress are the SSO and Wing VMS w/ Gateway; we are waiting for a response from Bob\non both items. Would someone from the PD please touch base with Bob so we can get these moving?\n\nI have nothing else to cover today, please let me know if you’d like to cancel, or if there are items/questions the PD would\nlike to review.\n\nThanks!\n\nKelly Baeza\nTechnical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e1069":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1069","title":"Flock Safety _ Monthly Product Update _ March 2025","frm":"Myron Maret","date":"2025-03-07","text":"From:\nMyron Maret\nSent:\nFriday, March 7, 2025 4:29:30 PM\nTo:\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nFlock Safety | Monthly Product Update | March 2025\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nHello,\nHere's our monthly snapshot of our latest updates and product releases. We've included videos and\narticles to help you make the most of your Flock Safety system. Click here to see what's new.\nTopics in this month’s newsletter include:\nNOVA\nAdding Networks to Roles\nFlock Forward 2025\nNew Zones feature\nMobile App Search by Date/Time\nFor a deeper dive, we'd encourage you to check out the Help Center to access knowledge articles, create\nand track the status of your cases, and take advantage of trainings and certifications. Access the\nupdated help center here.\nIf you have any questions about how any of our latest enhancements might help your agency solve crime\nor you want to learn more about any other feature, please always feel free to reach out to your Customer\nSuccess Manager or support@flocksafety.com\nThank you and be safe,\nMyron Maret\nFlock Safety\nCustomer Success\n myron.maret@flocksafety.com\n 404.631.6599\n flocksafety.com\nClick here to unsubscribe from this list or manage your preferences here.","pdf":null},"e0176":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0176","title":"Flock Cameras","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2025-03-19","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSent:\nWednesday, March 19, 2025 1:02:08 PM\nTo:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nCc:\nClarkson, Constance\nSubject:\nRE: Flock Cameras\nSensitivity:Normal\nWe put one of our vehicles into a hit list and drove through each camera. We did receive an alert on each one of the\ncameras. We have not gotten a hit since then but I am assuming that no vehicles have come through with any reason\nfor notifications.\n\nFrom: Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Wednesday, March 19, 2025 9:23 AM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock Cameras\n\nGood Morning,\n\nChecking in here - have you still not received any alerts from those newly installed cameras?\n\nBest,\nGeorgia\n\nOn Fri, Mar 14, 2025 at 9:17 AM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nOk I was able to view 12 17 and 8 and it is recording plates. I went into the alerts tab and they are all selected. When I\ndid a test search for a vehicle image from these cameras came up.  I guess no vehicle has come through there that\nwould cause an alert which is very odd.\n\nChief Joe Babkiewicz\n\nFrom: Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, March 13, 2025 9:43 AM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Flock Cameras\n\nGood Morning,\n\nOf course - I changed the camera name for #13.\n\nAs for, #12, #17 and #08, I can see that they are all active and working properly. Have everyone double check\nwhich devices they have selected to get alerted on from the Alerts page. Let me know if those cameras are\nalready selected.\n\nIf the user selected individual devices, when new ones get installed, they'll have to select those new cameras\nas well.\n\nAs an admin, you can also now create Zones for your department. The benefit of doing this is that you as an\nadmin can add new cameras to the zones and users who have that zone selected will automatically get alerts\noff those new cameras without having to adjust the devices they've selected from the Devices & Zones\nsection.\n\nFeel free to schedule a screenshare call with me if you want to go over this together.\n\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n\nOn Wed, Mar 12, 2025 at 4:49 PM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGod afternoon Georgia,\n\nI have a few questions regarding the recently installed flock cameras\n\nCamera #13 can we rename it to Buckwalter Parkway NB/Bluffton Parkway\n\nCameras\n12\n17\n08\n\nThe above listed cameras have been installed and it is showing that they are live, but we have yet to receive a hit\non it. I just want to make sure that these are up and running. Thanks\n\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nChief of Police\nOffice | 843-706-4537\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com\n\n--\n\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0176.pdf"},"e0988":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0988","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Project Update - 3_20_25","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-03-20","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nThursday, March 20, 2025 9:51:14 AM\nTo:\n'Babkiewicz, Joseph'\nSubject:\nRE: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Project Update - 3/20/25\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nThank you!\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nSr. Technical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com\n\nFrom: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Thursday, March 20, 2025 9:49 AM\nTo: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Project Update - 3/20/25\n\nYes we need to cancel. We are out at the special Olympics and will be here all day. We will help get these tasks\ncompleted. Thank you Kelly.\nSent from my iPhone\nOn Mar 20, 2025, at 9:41 AM, Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com> wrote:\n\nGood morning!\n\nWe have 2 pending integrations:\n\n<image002.png>\n\n<image003.png>\n\n<image004.png>\n\n<image005.png>\n\n1. SSO Setup: last update from Bob was 2/20, he was waiting for the certificate and would pass it along to Alex;\nwe have sent follow up emails and are awaiting a response\n2. VMS w/ Gateway: we have reached out to Bob to schedule a call to gather info and send the gateway; we\nhave sent follow up emails and are awaiting a response\n\nWe are behind schedule with these integrations and would appreciate the PD’s assistance to get these moving.\n\nI have no other updates for today, please let me know if you would like to cancel today’s call.\n\nThanks!\n\n<image001.png>\n\nKelly\nBaeza\nSr.\nTechnical\nProject\nManager\n<image006.png>\n flocksafety.com\n<image007.png>","pdf":null},"e0993":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0993","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Project Update - 4_3_25","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-04-03","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nThursday, April 3, 2025 9:42:56 AM\nTo:\n'Alex Menke'; 'Georgia Abdallah'; 'Joe Babkiewicz'; 'Ryan Fazekas'; 'Craig Karafa'; 'Edith Moody';\njdestasio@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nBluffton PD / FlockOS - Project Update - 4/3/25\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood morning,\n\nI wanted to check with the PD to see if we should keep today’s call. See below for updates outstanding integrations, and\nplease let me know if you’d like to keep or cancel today’s call.\n\nSSO setup\nWaiting on Bob to send the certificate\nVMS integration w/ Gateway\nAlex emailed Bob to confirm the 2nd half of April 23rd works to come onsite, and can be available 4/24 if needed\nAlex asked to schedule a call with Bob next week to “check out your SSO configurations, look into VMS setup and\npreplan static IP and port forwarding rules”\n\nThanks!\n\nKelly Baeza\nSr. Technical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0670":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0670","title":"Defending the Tools That Keep Communities Safe","frm":"Garrett at Flock Safety","date":"2025-04-03","text":"From:\nGarrett at Flock Safety\nSent:\nThursday, April 3, 2025 5:16:34 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nDefending the Tools That Keep Communities Safe\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nView in Browser  |  Forward to a Friend\nDear Flock Community,\nAt Flock, our mission has always been clear: to eliminate crime while protecting the\nprivacy and freedoms that make our communities thrive. That’s why I want to take a\nmoment to update you on a recent legal development in Virginia—and how we’re taking\naction to stand by our customers and the communities we serve.\nWhat’s Happening in Norfolk, Virginia\nLast October, a lawsuit was filed in Norfolk, Virginia, challenging the use of license plate\nreaders (LPRs) by Norfolk law enforcement.\nTo be clear, Flock has not been sued.\nHowever, we have requested the judge allow Flock to intervene in this case. Why? Two\nreasons. First, we know the technology and are best positioned to answer the questions\nasked by the judge. Second, the legal outcome could impact how our customers—cities,\nlaw enforcement agencies, businesses, and neighborhoods—use the tools we provide to\nprevent and solve crime.\nIntervention is a legal process that allows a third party to ask the Court’s permission to\njoin an existing case when they have a direct interest in the outcome. We believe it’s\nimportant that Flock’s voice, experience, and commitment to civil liberties are part of the\nconversation.\nThe Legal Landscape\nThere is strong legal precedent supporting the constitutionality of LPRs. Courts in at\nleast fourteen states, including this week in Illinois—and the U.S. Courts of Appeals for\nboth the 9th and 11th Circuits—have affirmed that license plate readers do not violate\nthe Fourth Amendment.\n\nWhy? Because:\nThere is no expectation of privacy in a license plate, which is publicly displayed and\nissued by the government\nLPRs aren’t designed to capture intimate or personal details about a person—they\ncollect still images of cars and license plates in public spaces\nThese tools do not allow for continuous or detailed tracking of the whole of an\nindividual’s movements\nThousands of public officials, elected by the communities they serve, have voted on\nand approved the use of LPRs and set local safeguards\nWhy Flock Is Getting Involved\nWe feel a strong sense of responsibility to contribute our expertise to the questions\nraised by this case. Flock’s technology is purpose-built with privacy protections like short\ndata retention windows, strong access controls, and transparency into how the tools are\nused.\nImportantly, we are asking the court to let us step in to stand behind our products and\nsupport our customers. You rely on Flock to help make your communities safer—and the\ndata shows it works. Whether it’s recovering stolen vehicles, identifying suspects in\nviolent crimes, recovering missing people, or deterring criminal activity altogether, LPRs\nare a critical part of modern public safety.\nWe’re Putting the Community First\nAt Flock, we are proud to build tools that strike the right balance between effectiveness\nand privacy. We will always stand up for what’s right—supporting the people and\nagencies who work every day to protect our neighborhoods, while staying grounded in\nthe rights guaranteed by the Constitution. We’re here for you. We’re committed to this\nmission. And we’re not backing down.\nIf you have questions, please just respond to this email and a member of Flock’s legal\nteam will reach out to you.\nSincerely,\nGarrett Langley\nCEO, Flock Safety\nFlock Safety\n1170 Howell Mill Rd NW, Suite 210\nAtlanta, Georgia 30318, United States","pdf":null},"e0705":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0705","title":"Flock Safety - Thank You Video_Notes","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2025-04-07","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nMonday, April 7, 2025 9:01:26 AM\nTo:\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nFlock Safety - Thank You Video/Notes\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Morning,\nI hope you had a great weekend. I’m reaching out with a small request. We’re preparing for our upcoming company event, and\nwe’d love to include appreciation messages from our customers to share with the Flock team.\nWe’re looking for brief, heartfelt contributions, either through a short video (about 30 seconds, recorded on your phone) or a\nwritten note. Something simple, such as a thank you for how Flock has supported you, impacted your community, or enhanced\nyour experience. It doesn’t need to be elaborate.\nThese messages will stay internal, shared only with our team, so there’s no need to worry about polish or production. If you’re\nwilling to participate, I’d greatly appreciate it if you could send your video or written note to me by April 15th. No pressure of\ncourse, and thank you for considering it.\nAs always, if you need anything from me, please don't hesitate to give me a call.\nBest,\nGeorgia\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com\n\n--","pdf":null},"e1070":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1070","title":"Flock Safety _ Monthly Product Update _ April 2025","frm":"Myron Maret","date":"2025-04-07","text":"From:\nMyron Maret\nSent:\nMonday, April 7, 2025 10:13:00 AM\nTo:\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nFlock Safety | Monthly Product Update | April 2025\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nHello,\nHere's our monthly snapshot of our latest updates and product releases. We've included videos and\narticles to help you make the most of your Flock Safety system. Click here to see what's new.\nTopics in this month’s newsletter include:\nScheduled Guardian Mode\nSaved Searches (coming soon)\nFlock Forward registration\nCovered Plates search filter\nFor a deeper dive, we'd encourage you to check out the Help Center to access knowledge articles, create\nand track the status of your cases, and take advantage of trainings and certifications. Access the\nupdated help center here.\nIf you have any questions about how any of our latest enhancements might help your agency solve crime\nor you want to learn more about any other feature, please always feel free to reach out to your Customer\nSuccess Manager or support@flocksafety.com\nThank you and be safe,\nMyron Maret\nFlock Safety\nCustomer Success\n myron.maret@flocksafety.com\n 404.631.6599\n flocksafety.com\nClick here to unsubscribe from this list or manage your preferences here.","pdf":null},"e0706":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0706","title":"New Feature Alert - Zones","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2025-04-08","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nTuesday, April 8, 2025 12:42:40 PM\nTo:\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nNew Feature Alert - Zones\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood afternoon,\nI'm reaching out to share a quick update with you on a feature called Zones that is available now for all admins. I included a\nquick tutorial here. The main benefits of zones are:\nIt gives admins a little more control over which devices users are getting alerts off of\nRemoves the need for users to update their alert camera preferences everytime new devices are installed or new cameras\nwithin your jurisdiction are shared with you.\nNewly installed cameras within a particular zone will automatically be added to that zone.\nPlease give me a call if you have any questions.\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com\n\n--","pdf":null},"e0998":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0998","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - SSO Setup","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-04-10","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nThursday, April 10, 2025 1:26:01 PM\nTo:\n'Alex Menke'; 'Georgia Abdallah'; 'Joe Babkiewicz'; 'Ryan Fazekas'; 'Craig Karafa'; 'Edith Moody';\njdestasio@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nBluffton PD / FlockOS - SSO Setup\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi Bob,\n\nI’m following up to see if you can send us the SSO cert so we can finish up the SSO integration.\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nSr. Technical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0666":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0666","title":"Chief Babkiewicz, Early Bird Pricing Ends April 30","frm":"Garrett Langley","date":"2025-04-16","text":"From:\nGarrett Langley\nSent:\nWednesday, April 16, 2025 10:04:44 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nChief Babkiewicz, Early Bird Pricing Ends April 30\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi Joseph,\nIt’s Garrett — the CEO of Flock Safety. I wanted to reach out with a discount code for Flock Forward, our conference for\nlaw enforcement leadership, which is taking place from August 4-6 in Atlanta.\nSimply use the code EARLYBIRD at checkout to receive 50% off your registration. But you'll need to act fast because this\ncode is only valid until April 30th.\nHope to see you in Atlanta!\nGarrett","pdf":null},"e0884":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0884","title":"Flock Safety Project Updates","frm":"Heather Phillips","date":"2025-04-17","text":"From:\nHeather Phillips\nSent:\nThursday, April 17, 2025 1:14:09 PM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nRe: Flock Safety Project Updates\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nThank you Chief!\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 412-512-0563\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com\nOn Thu, Apr 17, 2025 at 1:13 PM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nBoth cameras have been approved. Thank you\n\nFrom: Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, April 17, 2025 12:00 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>; Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>; Georgia\nAbdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Flock Safety Project Updates\n\nGood Afternoon Chief,\n\nReaching out to seek your approval on locations #03 and #16 in the updated Deployment Plan.\n\n@Taylor Ellison - following up on the request to remove locations #02 and #15.\n\nConstance - quick update that location #09 is installed. Our tech is returning on 4/21 to complete #13 and #14. Spreadsheet\nupdated.\n\nI hope everyone has a wonderful holiday weekend.\n\nThank you!\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 412-512-0563\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e1008":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1008","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - RESCHEDULE Project Call on 5_1_25","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-04-21","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nMonday, April 21, 2025 11:52:43 AM\nTo:\n'Babkiewicz, Joseph'; 'Alex Menke'; 'Georgia Abdallah'; 'Fazekas, Ryan'; 'Karafa, Craig'; 'Moody, Edith';\n'Destasio, John'\nSubject:\nRE: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - RESCHEDULE Project Call on 5/1/25\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nThanks! I just updated the invite.\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nSr. Technical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com\n\nFrom: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Monday, April 21, 2025 11:42 AM\nTo: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>; 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; 'Georgia Abdallah'\n<georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig\n<ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Moody, Edith <emoody@townofbluffton.com>; Destasio, John\n<jdestasio@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: RE: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - RESCHEDULE Project Call on 5/1/25\n\nYes that is fine. Thank you\n\nFrom: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, April 21, 2025 11:16 AM\nTo: 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; 'Georgia Abdallah' <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; Babkiewicz,\nJoseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig\n<ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Moody, Edith <emoody@townofbluffton.com>; Destasio, John\n<jdestasio@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - RESCHEDULE Project Call on 5/1/25\n\nGood morning!\n\nAlex and I will be unavailable for our project call on Thursday, May 1st at 11:30am; we will be in Atlanta for Flock Together.\nMay we please reschedule the call for Thursday, May 8th, at 11:30am?\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nSr. Technical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0707":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0707","title":"Live Video is Now Available in the Mobile App - Flock Safety","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2025-04-21","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nMonday, April 21, 2025 3:48:49 PM\nTo:\nJoe Babkieweicz\nSubject:\nLive Video is Now Available in the Mobile App - Flock Safety\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nI'm reaching out to share a quick update regarding our mobile app. Organizations with live video/VMS can now\nwatch live streams directly through the mobile app. Watch a quick tutorial here.\nStreams can be accessed by their location, alphabetically or by networks so users can quickly find the live\nstream they need.\nSpecific Streams can also be pinned for quick access. Easily switch streams within a network with a tap of a\nbutton.\nVideo can be watched in both Portrait, Landscape and Picture-in-Picture. PiP, allows for the individual to\nkeep eyes on the stream while navigation through Flock Safety Mobile app or other apps on their phone.\nNOTE: Today we do not support Recorded Video or PTZ control.\nYou need to be on iOS\n 1.33 and Android\n 1.39.\nPlease let me know if you have any questions.\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com\n\n--","pdf":null},"e0188":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0188","title":"Checking In - Flock Safety + Bluffton PD","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2025-04-29","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSent:\nTuesday, April 29, 2025 3:38:44 PM\nTo:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nCc:\nBurke, Helen; Karafa, Craig; Fazekas, Ryan\nSubject:\nRE: Checking In - Flock Safety + Bluffton PD\nSensitivity:Normal\nYes that will work.\n\nFrom: Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, April 29, 2025 1:59 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Burke, Helen <hburke@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig <ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas, Ryan\n<rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Checking In - Flock Safety + Bluffton PD\n\nHi Chief,\n\nI'm wide open next Tuesday. Should we shoot for 10 a.m.?\n\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n\nOn Tue, Apr 29, 2025 at 1:32 PM Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nThis week is filled up with events. How does next week look for you? I am open most of Monday, Tuesday, and\nWednesday (afternoon). Let me know what works for you.\n\nFrom: Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, April 29, 2025 12:58 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Burke, Helen <hburke@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig\n<ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Checking In - Flock Safety + Bluffton PD\n\nHi team,\n\nI hope your week is off to a great start. Following up to see if we can get a quick call scheduled over the next\nfew weeks so that we can go over your Flock account.\n\nLet me know if you have any questions in the meantime.\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n\nOn Wed, Apr 23, 2025 at 9:27 AM Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nGood Morning,\n\nI know you're still working with Kelly Baeza on finalizing your FlockOS implementation but I wanted to see if\nyou might have time for a quick call either this week or next to discuss your overall experience with Flock\nover the past six months. I'm hoping to gather some feedback on what features are working well for your\nagency, what could be improved, and how we can better support your agency going forward. Please click\nhere to schedule the call at your convenience.\n\nI also wanted to let you know that I did a quick check on your account and noticed that you don't yet have\naccess to Lowe's cameras. It looks like the template hasn't been submitted from your side. Is this something\nyou are still working on or do you want me to resend the template?\n\nI look forward to speaking with you soon.\n\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0720":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0720","title":"Early Bird Registration Ends Tomorrow - Flock Forward 2025","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2025-04-29","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nTuesday, April 29, 2025 6:13:28 PM\nTo:\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nEarly Bird Registration Ends Tomorrow - Flock Forward 2025\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nIf you haven't registered for Flock Forward yet and you plan to attend, I recommend signing up by tomorrow (April 30) to\nreceive 50% off the $350 registration cost with the code EARLYBIRD.߮\nEvent Date:\n August 4-6th, 2025\n߶\nLocation:\n Intercontinental Buckhead in Atlanta, GAͫ\nRegistration & Coupon Code:\nwww.flocksafety.com/flock-forward\n & EARLYBIRD\nThe FF25 conference is a unique opportunity to connect with industry experts, gain insights into the future of security\ntechnology, and engage with our leadership team.\nLet me know if you have any questions—I hope to see you there!\nBest,\nGeorgia\n\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com\n--\nUnsubscribe","pdf":null},"e1060":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1060","title":"Chief Babkiewicz, join me at Flock Forward","frm":"Mike Moulton, Retired Police Chief","date":"2025-04-30","text":"From:\nMike Moulton, Retired Police Chief\nSent:\nWednesday, April 30, 2025 10:10:49 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nChief Babkiewicz, join me at Flock Forward\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi There,\nI wanted to personally invite you to this year’s Flock Forward conference, happening August 4-6 in Atlanta, GA.\nLast year, I had the opportunity to attend the inaugural event, and I can say without hesitation—it proved to be one of the\nmore impactful public safety conferences I’ve participated in—offering real value through meaningful discussions, new\ntechnology insights, and powerful networking opportunities.\nThis year, I’m proud to be back—not just as an attendee, but as a presenter. I’ll be sharing and discussing with other public\nsafety leaders how Flock Safety’s advanced technologies helped enhance public safety and support officers in the\ncommunity I served in as a Police Chief in San Diego County.\nWhether you're already using Flock or are just exploring ways to make your community safer, Flock Forward is the place\nto connect with forward-thinking leaders, learn from real-world success stories, and get a firsthand look at what’s next\nin public safety technology.\nA sneak peek of the agenda is coming soon, and I can tell you...it’s shaping up to be even bigger and better than last year.\nI hope you’ll join me in Atlanta this August. It’s more than a conference - it’s a chance to move the mission forward\ntogether. You can register here.\nLet me know if you have any questions. Hope to see you there.\nAll the best,\nMike Moulton\nConsultant | Flock Safety\nRetired Police Chief, City of El Cajon","pdf":null},"e1149":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1149","title":"Flock Safety - Falcon Flex LPR Quote","frm":"Taylor Ellison","date":"2025-04-30","text":"From:\nTaylor Ellison\nSent:\nWednesday, April 30, 2025 10:17:06 AM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nFlock Safety - Falcon Flex LPR Quote\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:Quote_20250430_141500.pdf ;\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\nPlease see your quote attached - let me know if you have any questions!\nTaylor Ellison\n704-942-6362\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nAccount Executive\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e1016":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1016","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Project Call Agenda - 5_8_25","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-05-07","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nWednesday, May 7, 2025 5:13:08 PM\nTo:\n'Alex Menke'; 'Georgia Abdallah'; 'Joe Babkiewicz'; 'Ryan Fazekas'; 'Craig Karafa';\njdestasio@townofbluffton.com; 'Charles, Robert'\nSubject:\nBluffton PD / FlockOS - Project Call Agenda - 5/8/25\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood afternoon,\n\nBelow are the agenda items and project contacts for tomorrow’s call, please let me know if you have any questions!\n\nAgenda:\nSSO setup complete!\nVMS with Gateway\nAwaiting list of cameras from Bob\n\nMeeting\nAttendees\nAttendees - Flock Safety\n Kelly Baeza, Technical Project Manager\n Alex Menke, Integrations Manager\n Georgia Abdallah, Customer Success Manager\n\nAttendees - Bluffton PD - EST\n Chief Joe Babkiewicz\n Lieutenant Ryan Fazekas\n Captain Craig Karafa\n John Destasio\n Bob Charles\nProject\nMaterials\nProject Tasks: high level overview and status of the project tasks\nGoogle Drive: meeting notes and project documents saved here\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nSr. Technical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e1071":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1071","title":"Flock Safety _ Monthly Product Update _ May 2025","frm":"Myron Maret","date":"2025-05-08","text":"From:\nMyron Maret\nSent:\nThursday, May 8, 2025 2:24:06 PM\nTo:\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nFlock Safety | Monthly Product Update | May 2025\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nHello,\nHere's our monthly snapshot of our latest updates and product releases. We've included videos and\narticles to help you make the most of your Flock Safety system. Click here to see what's new.\nTopics in this month’s newsletter include:\nMobile App Live Video & Map Attachment updates\nSaved Searches\nFlock Forward registration\nCustom Hotlist update\nFor a deeper dive, we'd encourage you to check out the Help Center to access knowledge articles, create\nand track the status of your cases, and take advantage of trainings and certifications. Access the\nupdated help center here.\nIf you have any questions about how any of our latest enhancements might help your agency solve crime\nor you want to learn more about any other feature, please always feel free to reach out to your Customer\nSuccess Manager or support@flocksafety.com\nThank you and be safe,\nMyron Maret\nFlock Safety\nCustomer Success\n myron.maret@flocksafety.com\n 404.631.6599\n flocksafety.com\nClick here to unsubscribe from this list or manage your preferences here.","pdf":null},"e1021":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1021","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Need List of Cameras","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-05-12","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nMonday, May 12, 2025 10:31:55 AM\nTo:\n'Alex Menke'; 'Georgia Abdallah'; 'Joe Babkiewicz'; 'Ryan Fazekas'; 'Craig Karafa';\njdestasio@townofbluffton.com; 'Charles, Robert'\nSubject:\nBluffton PD / FlockOS - Need List of Cameras\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood morning, Bob,\n\nPlease send the list of cameras at your earliest convenience so we can add them to Flock.\n\nThanks!\n\nKelly Baeza\nSr. Technical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com\n\nFrom: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Wednesday, May 7, 2025 5:13 PM\nTo: 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; 'Georgia Abdallah' <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; 'Joe Babkiewicz'\n<jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; 'Ryan Fazekas' <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; 'Craig Karafa'\n<ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; jdestasio@townofbluffton.com; 'Charles, Robert' <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Project Call Agenda - 5/8/25\n\nGood afternoon,\n\nBelow are the agenda items and project contacts for tomorrow’s call, please let me know if you have any questions!\n\nAgenda:\nSSO setup complete!\nVMS with Gateway\nAwaiting list of cameras from Bob\n\nMeeting\nAttendees\nAttendees - Flock Safety\n Kelly Baeza, Technical Project Manager\n\n Alex Menke, Integrations Manager\n Georgia Abdallah, Customer Success Manager\n\nAttendees - Bluffton PD - EST\n Chief Joe Babkiewicz\n Lieutenant Ryan Fazekas\n Captain Craig Karafa\n John Destasio\n Bob Charles\nProject\nMaterials\nProject Tasks: high level overview and status of the project tasks\nGoogle Drive: meeting notes and project documents saved here\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nSr. Technical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e1030":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1030","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Awaiting List of Cameras","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-05-19","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nMonday, May 19, 2025 1:27:55 PM\nTo:\n'Charles, Robert'; 'Babkiewicz, Joseph'\nCc:\n'Alex Menke'; 'Georgia Abdallah'; 'Fazekas, Ryan'; 'Karafa, Craig'; 'Destasio, John'\nSubject:\nRE: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Awaiting List of Cameras\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi Bob!\n\nDid you sent the list of cameras to Alex?\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nSr. Technical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com\n\nFrom: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Thursday, May 15, 2025 12:18 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>; Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; Georgia Abdallah\n<georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig\n<ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Destasio, John <jdestasio@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Awaiting List of Cameras\n\nI’m working on getting through all of the cameras to link up now. Each one has to be reconfigured for Flock so as to\nprevent security issues.\n\nI will have this buttoned up tomorrow/Saturday and forward the list w/credentials.\n\nBob\n\nRobert Charles\nLaw Enforcement Technical Analyst\n\nOffice | 843-706-7814\n\n<image002.png>\n\n<image003.png>\n\n<image004.png>\n\n<image005.png>\n\nTown of Bluffton | Police Department\nPO Box 386\n101 Progressive Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nOn May 15, 2025, at 10:23 AM, Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nI do not see Bob on this email list, so I am adding him. Bob please send this list to Kelly as soon as possible.\nThank you.\n\nFrom: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, May 15, 2025 10:07 AM\nTo: 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; 'Georgia Abdallah' <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>;\nBabkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa,\nCraig <ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Destasio, John <jdestasio@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Awaiting List of Cameras\n\nGood morning,\n\nI pushed this morning’s call to next week, as the only outstanding item is the list of cameras we need to bring into\nFlock.\n\nBob,\n\nPlease send the list as soon as possible so we can wrap up this integration.\n\nThanks!\n\n<image001.png>\n\nKelly\nBaeza\nSr.\nTechnical\nProject\nManager\n<image006.png>\n flocksafety.com\n<image007.png>","pdf":null},"e0232":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0232","title":"ACTION REQUIRED_ Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Awaiting List of Cameras","frm":"Charles, Robert","date":"2025-05-22","text":"<image002.png> <image003.png> <image004.png> <image005.png>\nFrom:\nCharles, Robert\nSent:\nThursday, May 22, 2025 1:53:33 PM\nTo:\nKelly Baeza\nCc:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph; Alex Menke; Georgia Abdallah; Fazekas, Ryan; Karafa, Craig; Destasio, John\nSubject:\nRe: ACTION REQUIRED: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Awaiting List of Cameras\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:image001.png ;image002.png ;image003.png ;image004.png ;image005.png ;image006.png ;image007.png ;\nSounds great Kelly. Thanks again!\nRobert Charles\nLaw Enforcement Technical Analyst\n\nOffice | 843-706-7814\n\nTown of Bluffton | Police Department\nPO Box 386\n101 Progressive Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nOn May 22, 2025, at 12:42 PM, Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com> wrote:\n\nThanks, Bob!\n\nI got the task to Alex to add the cameras, we’ll reach out w/ any questions or once they’re available in Flock.\n\nThanks,\n\n<image001.png>\nKelly\nBaeza\nSr.\nTechnical\nProject\nManager\n<image006.png>\n flocksafety.com\n<image007.png>\n\n<image002.png> <image003.png> <image004.png> <image005.png>\n\nFrom: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Thursday, May 22, 2025 12:23 PM\nTo: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nCc: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; 'Georgia Abdallah'\n<georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig\n<ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Destasio, John <jdestasio@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: RE: ACTION REQUIRED: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Awaiting List of Cameras\n\nGood afternoon. Attached please find the list of cameras to set up on the Flock Gateway.\n\nI have included the secondary streaming address for each. Please use this to minimize the traffic impact on our\nside.\n\nA credential was added for viewing only for Flock. The UID is ‘flock’ and the PWD is ‘[REDACTED]’.\n\nPlease contact me if you have any issues. Note: the cameras with red IP address’ are currently down. You can set\nthese up but obviously you won’t be able to stream right now.\n\nThank you in advance!\n\nBob\n\nFrom: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, May 22, 2025 9:52 AM\nTo: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; 'Georgia Abdallah'\n<georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig\n<ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Destasio, John <jdestasio@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: RE: ACTION REQUIRED: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Awaiting List of Cameras\n\nThanks Bob, looking forward to getting these added.\n\nI will go ahead and cancel today’s call, and we will plan to meet next week.\n\nThanks,\n\n<image001.png>\nKelly\nBaeza\nSr.\nTechnical\nProject\nManager\n<image006.png>\n flocksafety.com\n<image007.png>\n\n<image002.png>\n\n<image003.png>\n\n<image004.png>\n\n<image005.png>\n\nFrom: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Wednesday, May 21, 2025 9:58 PM\nTo: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nCc: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; Georgia Abdallah\n<georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig\n<ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Destasio, John <jdestasio@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: ACTION REQUIRED: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Awaiting List of Cameras\n\nTomorrow we will be finished! Sending you the stream addresses to use too…\n\nBob\n\nRobert Charles\nLaw Enforcement Technical Analyst\n\nOffice | 843-706-7814\n\nTown of Bluffton | Police Department\nPO Box 386\n101 Progressive Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nOn May 21, 2025, at 7:16 PM, Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com> wrote:\n\nHi Bob,\n\nPlease send the list of cameras as soon as you can, as we are close to wrapping up the project.\n\nThanks,\n\n<image001.png>\n\nKelly\nBaeza\nSr.\nTechnical\nProject\nManager\n<image006.png>\n flocksafety.com\n<image007.png>\n\n<image002.png>\n\n<image003.png>\n\n<image004.png>\n\n<image005.png>\n\nFrom: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, May 19, 2025 1:28 PM\nTo: 'Charles, Robert' <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>; 'Babkiewicz, Joseph' <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; 'Georgia Abdallah' <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>;\n'Fazekas, Ryan' <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; 'Karafa, Craig' <ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; 'Destasio, John'\n<jdestasio@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: RE: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Awaiting List of Cameras\n\nHi Bob!\n\nDid you sent the list of cameras to Alex?\n\nThanks,\n\n<image001.png>\n\nKelly\nBaeza\nSr.\nTechnical\nProject\nManager\n<image006.png>\n flocksafety.com\n<image007.png>\n\nFrom: Charles, Robert <rcharles@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Thursday, May 15, 2025 12:18 PM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>; Alex Menke <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; Georgia Abdallah\n<georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig\n<ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>; Destasio, John <jdestasio@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Awaiting List of Cameras\n\nI’m working on getting through all of the cameras to link up now. Each one has to be reconfigured for\nFlock so as to prevent security issues.\n\nI will have this buttoned up tomorrow/Saturday and forward the list w/credentials.\n\nBob\n\nRobert Charles\nLaw Enforcement Technical Analyst\n\nOffice | 843-706-7814\n\nTown of Bluffton | Police Department\nPO Box 386\n101 Progressive Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\n<image002.png>\n\n<image003.png>\n\n<image004.png>\n\n<image005.png>\n\nOn May 15, 2025, at 10:23 AM, Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nwrote:\nI do not see Bob on this email list, so I am adding him. Bob please send this list to Kelly as soon\nas possible. Thank you.\n\nFrom: Kelly Baeza <kelly.baeza@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, May 15, 2025 10:07 AM\nTo: 'Alex Menke' <alex.menke@flocksafety.com>; 'Georgia Abdallah'\n<georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>;\nFazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Karafa, Craig <ckarafa@townofbluffton.com>;\nDestasio, John <jdestasio@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Bluffton PD / FlockOS - Awaiting List of Cameras\n\nGood morning,\n\nI pushed this morning’s call to next week, as the only outstanding item is the list of cameras we need\nto bring into Flock.\n\nBob,\n\nPlease send the list as soon as possible so we can wrap up this integration.\n\nThanks!\n\n<image001.png>\n\nKelly\nBaeza\nSr.\nTechnical\nProject\nManager\n<image006.png>\n flocksafety.com\n<image007.png>","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0232.pdf"},"e1150":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1150","title":"Join Us at Flock Forward 2025","frm":"Taylor Ellison","date":"2025-05-29","text":"From:\nTaylor Ellison\nSent:\nThursday, May 29, 2025 9:02:47 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nJoin Us at Flock Forward 2025\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi ChiefBabkiewicz\nI wanted to personally invite you to Flock Forward 2025, our big public safety conference happening this August\nin Atlanta. It’s a great chance to see what’s next in crime-fighting tech and connect with other law enforcement\nleaders from across the country.߮\n August 4–6, 2025\n߶ InterContinental Buckhead | Atlanta, GAͫ\n Regsiter here: www.flocksafety.com/flock-forward\nWHY ATTEND?\nGet direct access to Flock experts.\nWhether you're just getting started or scaling your impact, it’s your chance to ask the hard questions and get real-\ntime answers tailored to your agency.\nBring home what’s working.\nYou’ll leave with playbooks and real-world strategies you can immediately apply back in your community.\nConnect with your peers.\nThis isn’t just about content—it’s about conversations. You’ll meet other forward-thinking leaders facing the same\nchallenges you are and learn from each other.\nLet me know if you’re thinking about attending - happy to send more details your way.\nBest,\nTaylor Ellison\n704-942-6362\nTaylor Ellison\nAccount Executive\n flocksafety.com\n\nIf you'd like to stop receiving these emails, let me know.","pdf":null},"e1050":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1050","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Today's Project Call - 5_29_25","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-05-29","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nThursday, May 29, 2025 9:50:09 AM\nTo:\n'Alex Menke'; 'Georgia Abdallah'; 'Joe Babkiewicz'; 'Ryan Fazekas'; 'Craig Karafa';\njdestasio@townofbluffton.com; 'Charles, Robert'\nSubject:\nBluffton PD / FlockOS - Today's Project Call - 5/29/25\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood morning,\n\nWe’ve added the camera streams from the gateway, but we can’t get the cameras to connect. Alex reached out to Bob and\nClay to hopefully schedule a call today to get this resolved. I don’t have any updates for our project call, so I will go ahead and\ncancel, and hopefully our next call will be reviewing the FlockOS project closing document!\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nSr. Technical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e1151":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1151","title":"Flock Safety - Add live video to your LPR for $500_","frm":"Taylor Ellison","date":"2025-06-03","text":"From:\nTaylor Ellison\nSent:\nTuesday, June 3, 2025 2:42:16 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nFlock Safety - Add live video to your LPR for $500?\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHello Chief Babkiewicz,\nHope you're doing great!\nWe just announced some updates on Friday that I was hoping to get your feedback.\nHere’s the short version: We've been adding live video to existing LPRs as part of a bundled solution and are seeing strong\nresults.\nA few key benefits:\nSee more context around every LPR read. Get a better visual of what’s happening from a different angle—useful in\nparking lots, intersections, or high-traffic areas.\nSpeed up investigations by seeing what happened before and after a vehicle passes through the LPR field of view.\nImprove situational awareness in places where foot and vehicle traffic overlap or visibility is limited.\nYou might be thinking, “Isn't that already possible?” It is, but what's new is the pricing. You can now upgrade your existing LPRs\nfor just $500 a year and a one-time $150 install fee. We can also do this on all new LPR cameras moving forward.\nIt's an easy, low-cost way to increase the value and coverage of your current camera network.\nI'd love to set up a quick meeting to get your feedback on how your team would use this. Plus, if it makes sense, review your\nlocations and identify where we can bring the most value right away.\nWould early next week work for a 20-minute call?\nTaylor\nTaylor Ellison\nAccount Executive\n\n flocksafety.com\nIf you'd like to stop receiving these emails, let me know.","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item1151.pdf"},"e1055":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1055","title":"Bluffton PD _ FlockOS - Project Closing Document - 6_3_25","frm":"Kelly Baeza","date":"2025-06-03","text":"From:\nKelly Baeza\nSent:\nTuesday, June 3, 2025 6:29:37 PM\nTo:\n'Alex Menke'; 'Georgia Abdallah'; 'Joe Babkiewicz'; 'Ryan Fazekas'; 'Craig Karafa';\njdestasio@townofbluffton.com; 'Charles, Robert'\nSubject:\nBluffton PD / FlockOS - Project Closing Document - 6/3/25\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:Bluffton PD - FlockOS Advanced Project Closing - 6.3.25.pdf ;\n\nGood afternoon!\n\nAttached is the project closing document indicating the completion of your FlockOS integrations. For training on the\nintegrations, please reach out to Georgia.\n\nIt’s been a pleasure working with the PD!\n\nThanks,\n\nKelly Baeza\nSr. Technical Project Manager\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e1072":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1072","title":"Flock Safety _ Monthly Product Update _ June 2025","frm":"Myron Maret","date":"2025-06-12","text":"From:\nMyron Maret\nSent:\nThursday, June 12, 2025 7:11:35 PM\nTo:\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nFlock Safety | Monthly Product Update | June 2025\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nHello,\nHere's our monthly snapshot of our latest updates and product releases. We've included videos and\narticles to help you make the most of your Flock Safety system. Click here to see what's new.\nTopics in this month’s newsletter include:\nFreeForm Camera Selection\nOrganization Audit Review\nAudio Detection History Filtering\nAdmin Defined Reasons for Search & Custom Hotlist\nFor a deeper dive, we'd encourage you to check out the Help Center to access knowledge articles, create\nand track the status of your cases, and take advantage of trainings and certifications. Access the\nupdated help center here.\nIf you have any questions about how any of our latest enhancements might help your agency solve crime\nor you want to learn more about any other feature, please always feel free to reach out to your Customer\nSuccess Manager or support@flocksafety.com\nThank you and be safe,\nMyron Maret\nFlock Safety\nCustomer Success\n myron.maret@flocksafety.com\n 404.631.6599\n flocksafety.com\nClick here to unsubscribe from this list or manage your preferences here.","pdf":null},"e0648":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0648","title":"Outcomes issue","frm":"Flock Safety Support","date":"2025-06-27","text":"From:\nFlock Safety Support\nSent:\nFriday, June 27, 2025 4:25:49 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nOutcomes issue\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\n\nI was advised this should be resolved now!\n\nPlease let me know if this is still not working properly for you.\n\nStay safe,\nCorey\nthread::MEXDy7waIS66L-D9Sg-vCA4::","pdf":null},"e1073":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1073","title":"Flock Safety _ Upcoming Community Website Update","frm":"Myron Maret","date":"2025-07-07","text":"From:\nMyron Maret\nSent:\nMonday, July 7, 2025 6:53:32 AM\nTo:\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nFlock Safety | Upcoming Community Website Update\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nHello,\nThis email is to inform you that we're upgrading your Flock Safety Community Camera Program webpage\nto provide a more streamlined, efficient, and ADA-compliant experience for you and your community.\nYou can preview the upgraded page samples at this link. There are three options and we will implement\nthe option you currently have for your site (Register Only, Integrate Only, or Register & Integrate).\nYour current page will automatically be replaced with this new design and functionality on July 18th,\n2025.\nReasons for the Upgrade:\nAccessibility Compliance: Meeting essential standards to ensure your webpages are accessible\nfor everyone.\nImproved User Experience: Clearer, more intuitive navigation and content focused on delivering\nmore cameras into your network.\nClearer Communication: Enhancements to deliver clearer communication on registration or\nintegration status to your team and members of your community.\nWhat is Remaining Unchanged:\nYour existing URL structure remains consistent, meaning all current QR codes and marketing\nmaterials remain valid.\nEssential features like Register, Integrate, and Purchase remain fully intact.\nThe central goal of promoting community safety and collaboration stays at the forefront.\nKey Features of the Upgrade:\nImproved Communication & Notifications: Your team and community members will now\nreceive automatic notifications upon submission with clear next steps. This will enable us to add\ncameras to your network faster, and reduce confusion for registration and integration participants.\nEnhanced, User-Friendly Layout: Retaining the familiar flow of the current webpage, we've\noptimized your community webpages for improved clarity and user engagement, so you get more\nregistrations.\nProven Community Engagement: Provide concrete evidence of community safety\nimprovements, building greater trust and participation with the new Solved Stories Map.\nImplementation Timeline:\n\nHere’s how the upgrade process will work:\n1. Initial Notification: You'll receive a clear overview of the upcoming upgrade, what to expect, and\nwhen.\n2. Page Upgrade & Launch: We'll handle the technical implementation and your updated page will\ngo live on July 18th.\n3. Ongoing Support: After launch, your Customer Success Manager will remain available for any\nsupport or further adjustments.\nDedicated Support:\nOur Customer Success team is ready to assist you throughout this upgrade. Contact your Customer\nSuccess Manager (CSM) directly with any questions or for additional support.\nWe look forward to partnering with you to further enhance your community's safety and engagement.\nMyron Maret\nFlock Safety\nCustomer Success\n myron.maret@flocksafety.com\n 404.631.6599\n flocksafety.com\nClick here to unsubscribe from this list or manage your preferences here.","pdf":null},"e0724":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0724","title":"Flock Forward Conference \\(August 4-6\\)","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2025-07-11","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nFriday, July 11, 2025 3:37:36 PM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nCc:\nFazekas, Ryan; Burke, Helen; Karafa, Craig\nSubject:\nFlock Forward Conference (August 4-6)\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nI hope all is well. We would love to have someone from your department at our Flock Forward conference this\nyear. We have two free tickets reserved for your department so just let me know if anyone can attend and\nI'll send you the registration discount code.\nFlock Forward is a unique opportunity to connect with industry experts, speak directly with our Product\nManagers to gain insights into the future of law enforcement technology, and engage with our leadership team. If\ninterested, below are the details:\n Event Date: August 4-6th, 2025\n Location: Intercontinental Buckhead in Atlanta, GA (room block nightly rate is $182/night + taxes and fees)\n Registration: www.flocksafety.com/flock-forward\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0724.pdf"},"e0725":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0725","title":"National Night Out","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2025-07-22","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nTuesday, July 22, 2025 11:50:15 AM\nTo:\nBcc:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nNational Night Out\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nI'm passing along a message from our marketing department. If your agency is participating in National Night Out this year and\nyou would like some Flock swag to hand out, please let me know by tomorrow so that we can send you a free swag kit.\nThanks,\nGeorgia\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0726":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0726","title":"Please Join Us - Greater Charleston Area Flock Forum_ Collaborative Policing","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2025-07-31","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nThursday, July 31, 2025 10:32:20 AM\nTo:\nBcc:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nPlease Join Us - Greater Charleston Area Flock Forum: Collaborative Policing\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nI hope you can join our team on Wednesday, August 27, at the Colleton County Sheriff’s Office for a Flock\nForum.\nWe will have subject matter experts onsite to explore our Drone-as-First-Responder and Real-Time Policing\nproducts as well as our software platform. We’ll share invaluable insights into real-time policing strategies\napplicable to agencies of any size or stage of development.\nLunch will be provided and we'll have time to network with your peers.\nDate:\nWednesday, August 27th\nTime:\n11:00 am to 1:30 pm ET\nLocation:\nColleton County SO\n394 Mable T Willis Blvds Walterboro, South Carolina 29488\n\nRSVP:\n Click here\n to register\nThank you,\nGeorgia\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0727":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0727","title":"Reminder_ Please Join Us for a SC Regional Flock Forum","frm":"Georgia Abdallah","date":"2025-08-12","text":"From:\nGeorgia Abdallah\nSent:\nTuesday, August 12, 2025 10:47:25 AM\nTo:\nBcc:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nReminder: Please Join Us for a SC Regional Flock Forum\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Morning,\nI hope you can join our team on Wednesday, August 27, at the Colleton County Sheriff’s Office for a Flock\nForum.\nWe will have subject matter experts onsite to explore our Drone-as-First-Responder and Real-Time Policing\nproducts as well as our software platform. We’ll share invaluable insights into real-time policing strategies\napplicable to agencies of any size or stage of development.\nLunch and prizes will be provided and we'll have time to network with your peers.\nDate: Wednesday, August 27th\nTime: 11:00 am to 1:30 pm ET\nLocation:\nColleton County SO\n394 Mable T Willis Blvds Walterboro, South Carolina 29488\nRSVP: Click here to register\nThank you,\nGeorgia\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0076":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0076","title":"Quick Intro & Meeting Request","frm":"Anabel Pozzi","date":"2025-08-13","text":"From:\nAnabel Pozzi\nSent:\nWednesday, August 13, 2025 4:05:00 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nQuick Intro & Meeting Request\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi Chief Babkiewicz,\nI hope you’re doing well. I wanted to introduce myself — I’m Anabel Pozzi, your new Account Executive here at Flock Safety. I\nam taking over Taylor Ellison's role. I’m excited to work with the Town of Bluffton and see how we can support the great work\nyou're already doing.\nI'd love to set up a quick Zoom to connect. You can book time below with my calendar.\nBook Time With Me\nLooking forward to meeting you,\nAnabel Pozzi\nFlock Safety\nCall me at: 803-262-2019\nSouth Carolina Regional Account Executive\nBook Time With Me","pdf":null},"e1074":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1074","title":"Flock Safety _ Admin Feature Update Webinar","frm":"Myron Maret","date":"2025-08-14","text":"From:\nMyron Maret\nSent:\nThursday, August 14, 2025 6:58:01 PM\nTo:\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nFlock Safety | Admin Feature Update Webinar\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nHello,\nPlease see below for an upcoming Admin user training webinar covering new features and best practices\non 08/20/2025 at 1:00 PM EST.\nIn this Training Session, we’ll walk through new enhancements designed to give you more control and\nvisibility across your organization.\nWe’ll cover:\n1. How to update Custom Search Reasons and Custom Hot List Reasons, plus how to require Case\nNumbers for added accountability for your users.\n2. The latest updates in the VMS tab, including the ability to see live events while viewing recorded\nfootage, identify who else is viewing the same stream, and improvements to Guardian Mode.\n3. A quick tour of improvements to Sharing Tools, Network Permissions, and the Users List to help\nstreamline admin workflows.\nWhether you're a system admin or power user, this session will help you stay ahead of the curve.\nRegister now to make the most of Flock’s newest features! Registration link here.\nMyron Maret\nFlock Safety\nCustomer Success\n myron.maret@flocksafety.com\n 404.631.6599\n flocksafety.com\nClick here to unsubscribe from this list or manage your preferences here.","pdf":null},"e0249":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0249","title":"Flock Safety _ Understanding Sharing, Search, and Audits in the Flock LPR System","frm":"Chris Colwell","date":"2025-08-20","text":"From:\nChris Colwell\nSent:\nWednesday, August 20, 2025 3:07:13 PM\nTo:\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nFlock Safety | Understanding Sharing, Search, and Audits in the Flock LPR System\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nHello,\nWe have recently been asked how data sharing works with Flock License Plate Readers (LPRs). We\nhope you find this information helpful.\nEach LPR camera in your network captures vehicular evidence to help solve crime. That data belongs to\nyou as the customer. As the system administrator, you have full control over whether and how your\nagency shares this information with others.\nTime and again, data sharing has proven invaluable—helping agencies locate kidnapped children across\nstate lines, find missing seniors, and solve cross-jurisdictional narcotics and burglary cases. To make\nthis possible, the Flock platform provides flexible options for sharing:\n1. National sharing\nOpt into Flock’s national sharing network. Access via the national lookup tool is limited—\nusers can only see results if they perform a full plate search and a positive match exists\nwithin the network of participating, opt-in agencies. This ensures data privacy while enabling\nbroader collaboration when needed.\n2. Share with agencies in specific states only\nShare with agencies with similar laws (for example, regarding immigration enforcement and\ndata)\n3. Share within your state only or within a certain distance\nYou can share information with communities within a specified mile radius, with the entire\nstate, or a combination of both—for example, sharing with cities within 150 miles of Kansas\nCity (which would include cities in Missouri and neighboring states) and / or all communities\nstatewide simultaneously.\n4. Share 1:1\nShare only with specific agencies you have selected\n5. Don’t share at all\nIn some states, sharing is automatically restricted as required by law, and searches with search terms\nthat indicate a purpose prohibited by law have been disabled in our product. For example, in Virginia, out-\nof-state sharing is disabled and in Illinois, accessing data for certain purposes is not allowed.\nHowever, you are responsible for knowing your agency’s laws and policies, and ensuring that\nyou and your agency’s users are using the Flock system in compliance with these rules.\nImportantly, private customers never have access to law enforcement data.\nBy giving you control over how your data is shared, Flock Safety makes it easier to collaborate across\njurisdictions while maintaining compliance and protecting ownership. For more, see this recent statement\non our website.\nTo review and/or adjust your sharing settings, please follow the linked instructions here. If you’d like to\ndiscuss how your agency can get the most out of these options, I’d be happy to connect.\nBest regards,\nChris Colwell\nSVP of Customer Experience\n\nClick here to unsubscribe from this list or manage your preferences here.","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0249.pdf"},"e0887":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0887","title":"Flock Meeting and Spreadsheet","frm":"Heather Phillips","date":"2025-08-27","text":"From:\nHeather Phillips\nSent:\nWednesday, August 27, 2025 2:02:18 PM\nTo:\nClarkson, Constance\nCc:\nFazekas, Ryan; Babkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nRe: Flock Meeting and Spreadsheet\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nThank you, Constance, for the update.\nCaptain Fazekas, it's a pleasure to \"e-meet\" you. I have shared our external tracker with you, and I am very much looking\nforward to our meeting tomorrow to discuss the process and where we are in implementation.\nThank you,\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 412-512-0563\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com\nOn Mon, Aug 25, 2025 at 3:06 PM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\n\nGood morning Heather.\n\nPlease provide a link to the Google spreadsheet and Deployment Plan to Capt. Fazekas.  He is now overseeing the\nprocess from the BPD division.\n\nI would appreciate if you can provide him with a summary of the process and your role during our meeting this\nThursday.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov","pdf":null},"e0077":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0077","title":"Quick intro + time to connect_","frm":"Anabel Pozzi","date":"2025-08-26","text":"From:\nAnabel Pozzi\nSent:\nTuesday, August 26, 2025 9:00:19 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nQuick intro + time to connect?\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi Chief Babkiewicz,\nI’m Anabel Pozzi, your new Account Executive at Flock Safety supporting Bluffton. I’m excited to partner with you and make\nsure you’re getting maximum value from your current setup while exploring anything on your roadmap.\nCould we set up a quick 30-minute Zoom next week to align on priorities and next steps? You can grab a time that works for\nyou on the link in my signature.\nLooking forward to working together!\nAnabel Pozzi\nFlock Safety\nCall me at: 803-262-2019\nSouth Carolina Regional Account Executive\nBook Time With Me","pdf":null},"e0194":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0194","title":"Flock_Bluffton PD Map Review","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2025-08-27","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph on behalf of: Taylor Ellison\nSent:\nWednesday, August 27, 2025 12:38:37 PM\nTo:\nBurke, Helen; Fazekas, Ryan; DuBose, Amanda; Clarkson, Constance; Jones, Kim\nSubject:\nFW: Flock/Bluffton PD Map Review\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:attachment.ics ;invite.ics ;\n\n-----Original Appointment-----\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Wednesday, August 27, 2025 11:46 AM\nTo: Taylor Ellison; Babkiewicz, Joseph; Christine Spencer\nSubject: Flock/Bluffton PD Map Review\nWhen: Tuesday, September 2, 2025 3:00 PM-4:00 PM America/New_York.\nWhere:\n\n – 4 p m\n\nThis event has been updated\nChanged: conferencing\n\nJoin Zoom Meeting\nflocksafety.zoom.us/j/8134458332...\nID: 81344583321\nJoin by phone\n(US) +1 507-473-4847\nJoin using SIP\n81344583321@zoomcrc.com\nJoining instructions\nJoining notes\nWhen\nTuesday Sep 2, 2025 ⋅ 3pm – 4pm (Eastern Time - New York)\nGuests\nTaylor Ellison - organizer\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nChristine Spencer\nView all guest info\nReply for jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\n\nMeeting host:\ntaylor.ellison@flocksafety.com\nJoin Zoom Meeting:\nhttps://flocksafety.zoom.us/j/81344583321?\njst=2\nYes\nNo\nMaybe\nMore options\nInvitation from Google Calendar\nYou are receiving this email because you are an attendee on the event.\nForwarding this invitation could allow any recipient to send a response to the organizer, be added to the guest list, invite others regardless of their\nown invitation status, or modify your RSVP. Learn more","pdf":null},"e0890":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0890","title":"Flock Meeting for Phases 2 and 3, 9_2_25","frm":"Heather Phillips","date":"2025-08-27","text":"From:\nHeather Phillips\nSent:\nWednesday, August 27, 2025 2:59:21 PM\nTo:\nClarkson, Constance\nCc:\nFazekas, Ryan; Taylor Ellison; Babkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nRe: Flock Meeting for Phases 2 and 3, 9/2/25\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood afternoon,\nI appreciate you looping me in Constance! I will be available to join.\nThanks,\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 412-512-0563\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com\nOn Wed, Aug 27, 2025 at 2:35 PM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood afternoon Heather.\n\nThe Town is meeting with Taylor next Tuesday for Bluffton Flock phases 2 and 3.  I explained to the Chief how it\nwould be beneficial to have you at the meeting so we’re all on the same page from the beginning.\n\nWe can still meet with Ryan this Thursday to give him an overview of the process along with the progress of phase 1.\n\nPlease confirm you can attend next Tuesday, 9/2/25 at 3pm.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov","pdf":null},"e1153":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1153","title":"Flock Phase 2 Quote","frm":"Taylor Ellison","date":"2025-09-02","text":"From:\nTaylor Ellison\nSent:\nTuesday, September 2, 2025 3:13:04 PM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nFlock Phase 2 Quote\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:Quote_20250902_191158.pdf ;\n\nChief,\nPlease see attached!\nTaylor Ellison\n704-942-6362\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nAccount Executive\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e1156":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1156","title":"Bluffton Flock Phases 2 and 3","frm":"Taylor Ellison","date":"2025-09-03","text":"From:\nTaylor Ellison\nSent:\nWednesday, September 3, 2025 10:03:48 AM\nTo:\nClarkson, Constance\nCc:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph; DuBose, Amanda\nSubject:\nRe: Bluffton Flock Phases 2 and 3\nSensitivity:Normal\nWARNING!\nThis email originated from outside of the Town of Bluffton's email system. DO NOT click any links or open any attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content\nis safe.\nAll,\nPlease see the link below.  This shows Phase 1 and 2 together.  This is as close as I was able to get to your request.  Hope this helps, and don't hesitate to call me if you need\nanything else!\nhttps://planner.flocksafety.com/planning-portal/deployment-\ntracker/public/0e9440b0b04e3eddd28792717c8857c8e152a9e863741136144b724b4b83cf92c315af59596a983bd87a21c8c2228a067759376994a949e312d7ceeae6b08404\nTaylor\n704-942-6362\nOn Tue, Sep 2, 2025 at 5:19 PM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nChief and Taylor.\n\nPlease forward the map of locations at your earliest convenience.  We want to provide Amanda with as much time as possible for her due diligence prior to\nThursday’s meeting.  So that only leaves tomorrow morning as this is a short week and she leaves at 1pm.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nAccount Executive\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0196":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0196","title":"Flock_Bluffton PD Mapping Cont'd","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2025-09-03","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph on behalf of: Taylor Ellison\nSent:\nWednesday, September 3, 2025 7:25:05 AM\nTo:\nJones, Kim; Clarkson, Constance; DuBose, Amanda; Fazekas, Ryan; Burke, Helen\nSubject:\nFW: Flock/Bluffton PD Mapping Cont'd\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:attachment.ics ;invite.ics ;\n\n-----Original Appointment-----\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, September 2, 2025 3:46 PM\nTo: Taylor Ellison; Babkiewicz, Joseph; Christine Spencer\nSubject: Flock/Bluffton PD Mapping Cont'd\nWhen: Wednesday, September 10, 2025 3:00 PM-4:00 PM America/New_York.\nWhere:\n\n – 4 p m\n\nThis event has been updated\nChanged: conferencing\n\nJoin Zoom Meeting\nflocksafety.zoom.us/j/8320349220...\nID: 83203492209\nJoin by phone\n(US) +1 689-278-1000\nJoin using SIP\n83203492209@zoomcrc.com\nJoining instructions\nJoining notes\nWhen\nWednesday Sep 10, 2025 ⋅ 3pm – 4pm (Eastern Time - New\nYork)\nGuests\nTaylor Ellison - organizer\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nChristine Spencer\nView all guest info\n\nMeeting host:\ntaylor.ellison@flocksafety.com\nJoin Zoom Meeting:\nhttps://flocksafety.zoom.us/j/83203492209?\njst=2\nReply for jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nYes\nNo\nMaybe\nMore options\nInvitation from Google Calendar\nYou are receiving this email because you are an attendee on the event.\nForwarding this invitation could allow any recipient to send a response to the organizer, be added to the guest list, invite others regardless of their\nown invitation status, or modify your RSVP. Learn more","pdf":null},"e1075":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1075","title":"Flock Safety _ Monthly Product Update _ September 2025","frm":"Myron Maret","date":"2025-09-04","text":"From:\nMyron Maret\nSent:\nThursday, September 4, 2025 2:30:32 PM\nTo:\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nFlock Safety | Monthly Product Update | September 2025\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nHello,\nHere's our monthly snapshot of our latest updates and product releases. We've included videos and\narticles to help you make the most of your Flock Safety system. Click here to see what's new.\nTopics in this month’s newsletter include:\nScheduled Patrol for PTZ Live Video Cameras\nUser Filtering by Roles\nViewer List for Live Video Feeds\nFreeform Contact for moderation email\nFor a deeper dive, we'd encourage you to check out the Help Center to access knowledge articles, create\nand track the status of your cases, and take advantage of trainings and certifications. Access the\nupdated help center here.\nIf you have any questions about how any of our latest enhancements might help your agency solve crime\nor you want to learn more about any other feature, please always feel free to reach out to your Customer\nSuccess Manager or support@flocksafety.com\nThank you and be safe,\nMyron Maret\nFlock Safety | Customer Success\nClick here to unsubscribe from this list or manage your preferences here.","pdf":null},"e1158":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1158","title":"Flock - Tax Clarification","frm":"Taylor Ellison","date":"2025-09-11","text":"From:\nTaylor Ellison\nSent:\nThursday, September 11, 2025 8:43:59 AM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph; Roth, Felicia\nSubject:\nFlock - Tax Clarification\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nChief Babkiewicz and Felicia,\nSee below from my billing team regarding paying taxes for Flock in SC:\n\"The products purchased are categorized as computer software, non-educational, pre-written/canned, electronically downloaded\nsoftware or installation, not associated with the sale of tangible personal property (labor only).  At this time, both are exempt in\nSouth Carolina\"\nHope this helps, and let me know if you have any questions!\nTaylor Ellison\n704-942-6362\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nAccount Executive\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e1098":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1098","title":"Flock Safety Phase 2 - Additional Services Agreement","frm":"Smith, Dana","date":"2025-09-12","text":"From:\nSmith, Dana\nSent:\nFriday, September 12, 2025 9:33:02 AM\nTo:\nRoth, Felicia; Taylor Ellison; Babkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nRE: Flock Safety Phase 2 - Additional Services Agreement\nSensitivity:Normal\nGood morning Felicia,\n\nThe contract 2026-18 is not listed in the drop down when tyring to attach the contract.  The drop down only has the old\ncontract 2025-21.  Please advise so that I can complete the requisition and release.\n\nThank you.\n\nHave a Great Day,\n\nDana Smith\nExecutive Assistant to Command Staff\nCALEA Accreditation Manager\n(843)706-7804\n\nBluffton Police Department\n101 Progressive Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nPh.: 843-706-4550\nFax:843-757-2269\nwww.blufftonpolice.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Roth, Felicia <froth@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Thursday, September 11, 2025 4:04 PM\nTo: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Smith, Dana <dsmith@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: RE: Flock Safety Phase 2 - Additional Services Agreement\n\nThanks Taylor. Attached is the executed agreement.  Please email it back fully executed at your earliest\nconvenience.\n\nChief and Dana:  I am setting up Phase 2 as contract 2026-18 in MUNIS.  Just FYI for you Dana when you enter\nin your purchase order.\n\nFelicia L. Roth, J.D.\nDirector of Compliance and Contracts\n\nTown of Bluffton\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nOffice: 843-7 06-7 816\nNEW mobile: 843-540-57 12\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Thursday, September 11, 2025 9:39 AM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Roth, Felicia <froth@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Flock Safety Phase 2 - Additional Services Agreement\n\nChief Babkiewicz and Felicia,\n\nAttached you will find the additional services agreement for Phase 2.  The original MSA (T&C's) that we agreed\nto in Phase 1 still hold valid per the language at the top of the order form - we are simply adding products to your\nexisting account.\n\nPlease have signed and return to me at your earliest convenience.  I will send the final rendition of the map over\nonce Christine has finalized it.\n\nCall me with any questions!\n\nTaylor Ellison\n704-942-6362\n\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nAccount Executive\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item1098.pdf"},"e1164":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1164","title":"Flock Phase 2 Locations - NEEDS APPROVAL","frm":"Taylor Ellison","date":"2025-09-15","text":"From:\nTaylor Ellison\nSent:\nMonday, September 15, 2025 12:05:48 PM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nFlock Phase 2 Locations - NEEDS APPROVAL\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\nI hope you had a great weekend.  Phase 2 locations are ready for approval - I will need this completed in order to process your order.\nFollow the link below - once in you will log into Flock at the top right corner.  From there, you will go back to the top right corner where you will see \"Approvals\".  Please\ncheck the checkboxes to approve all locations.  Confirm with me once you have completed this, and I'll get everything finalized on my end.\nhttps://planner.flocksafety.com/planning-portal/deployment-\ntracker/public/0e9440b0b04e3eddd28792717c8857c8b39c802712efed723006a38b1e152fca30479a967904cb87f275bac076fd8d3e74171b38944d1179b53afbf3a16b2e07\nCall me with any questions.\nTaylor Ellison\n704-942-6362\n--\nTaylor Ellison\nAccount Executive\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0201":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0201","title":"Legal Spreadsheet - Flock Addition Request","frm":"Babkiewicz, Joseph","date":"2025-09-16","text":"From:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph\nSent:\nTuesday, September 16, 2025 8:59:41 AM\nTo:\nClarkson, Constance; Roth, Felicia; Taylor Ellison\nCc:\nJones, Kim; Rooney, Pat; Fazekas, Ryan; DuBose, Amanda\nSubject:\nRE: Legal Spreadsheet - Flock Addition Request\nSensitivity:Normal\nGood morning Taylor,\n\nI went to approve the locations for the Phase 2 Flock cameras. However, there were two on May River Road that may\nbe a problem. It appears that Dominion Energy does not have third party permission to put cameras on their poles, and\nwe would have to get permission from SCDOT (which we know will not happen at this time). I will not approve the two\non May River unless they are powered by solar, not attached to a pole, and off SCDOT property. If that is the case, we\nwill have to find different locations for these two cameras.\n\nChief Joe Babkiewicz\n\nFrom: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Thursday, September 11, 2025 8:51 AM\nTo: Roth, Felicia <froth@townofbluffton.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Jones, Kim <kjones@townofbluffton.com>; Rooney, Pat <prooney@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas, Ryan\n<rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; DuBose, Amanda <adubose@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: RE: Legal Spreadsheet - Flock Addition Request\n\nFelicia, thanks so much for the quick response.\n\nChief, I’ll wait to get the list from Flock for Phases 2 and 3 where they plan to attach to a Dominion pole in the SCDOT\nROW.  I’ll then reach out to SCDOT to discuss their approval for all the locations before submitting the Pole Attachment\napplications because each pole request requires a separate application.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions in the meantime.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Roth, Felicia <froth@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Thursday, September 11, 2025 8:38 AM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Jones, Kim <kjones@townofbluffton.com>; Rooney, Pat <prooney@townofbluffton.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph\n<jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; DuBose, Amanda\n<adubose@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: RE: Legal Spreadsheet - Flock Addition Request\n\nI’ll put it on the list but my opinion is that if the easement that Dominion obtained does not say that the property\nowner also grants permission for third parties to access and use Dominion’s easement, then Dominion cannot\ngive us such authorization.  We may be able to use their poles but they cannot speak for land owners.\n\nSince the next legal meeting is not until 9/23, what I’d recommend is that we bundle all of the desired mount\nlocations within the SCDOT ROW and make one request for access in writing and see what SCDOT says.\n\nFelicia L. Roth, J.D.\nDirector of Compliance and Contracts\n\nTown of Bluffton\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC  29910\nOffice: 843-7 06-7 816\nNEW mobile: 843-540-57 12\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Wednesday, September 10, 2025 6:32 PM\nTo: Roth, Felicia <froth@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Jones, Kim <kjones@townofbluffton.com>; Rooney, Pat <prooney@townofbluffton.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph\n<jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; DuBose, Amanda\n<adubose@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Legal Spreadsheet - Flock Addition Request\n\nAfternoon Felicia.\n\nI couldn’t find the Legal spreadsheet to add the following:  Flock cameras on existing Dominion poles in SCDOT\nROW.  Please place this in the next legal meeting for discussion.\n\nDuring the Flock meeting today, I was advised by Flock that they have previously received permissions from Dominion\nto place a Flock camera on their existing poles even though it is within the SCDOT ROW.\n\nTown staff was told previously that SCDOT has paused all new Encroachment Permit approval for Flock cameras due to\nongoing litigation so we can’t place them in the SCDOT ROW.\n\nIn addition, the Dominion Pole Attachment Application has a disclosure stating:  The entity requesting attachment is\nresponsible for all city, county, and/or state permits and easements, including any associated fees. In all\nsituations, prior permission must be obtained from property owners and governmental entities for use of\nprivate property and public road rights-of-way. Dominion Energy South Carolina assumes no responsibility for\nsecuring such required permission, and the entity requesting attachment should assume that no such permission\nexists based solely on the presence of existing Dominion Energy facilities.\n\nConsidering the above and before I put forth a lot of work into this process, I’d like a legal opinion to determine if we\ncan use an existing Dominion pole in an SCDOT right of way for a Flock camera, with Dominion approving the pole\nattachment application.\n\nThanks so much for your help.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0201.pdf"},"e0302":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0302","title":"Flock Meeting 9_23 3-4pm","frm":"Clarkson, Constance","date":"2025-09-17","text":"From:\nClarkson, Constance\nSent:\nWednesday, September 17, 2025 9:20:24 AM\nTo:\nTaylor Ellison\nCc:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph; chistine.spencer@flocksafety.com; Fazekas, Ryan\nSubject:\nFlock Meeting 9/23 3-4pm\nSensitivity:Normal\nTaylor.\n\nAre we planning to go through the remaining cameras?  If so, is one hour really enough?\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov","pdf":null},"e1096":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1096","title":"BPD Flock Phase 2 Plan","frm":"Shani Patterson","date":"2025-09-18","text":"From:\nShani Patterson\nSent:\nThursday, September 18, 2025 4:27:28 PM\nTo:\nClarkson, Constance\nCc:\nchristine.spencer@flocksafety.com; Taylor Ellison; Heather Phillips; Fazekas, Ryan; Babkiewicz, Joseph; DuBose,\nAmanda; Burke, Helen\nSubject:\nRe: BPD Flock Phase 2 Plan\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon All,\nConstance, thank you again for taking my call today and walking me through your process. I’ve attached a copy of the proposed\nlocations for your reference and visibility.\nI’ll follow up with you next week to finalize everything before moving forward with installation. I’m looking forward to working\ntogether to help make your community a safer place. If you need anything in the meantime, please don’t hesitate to reach out. I’m\nhappy to help.\nAll the best,\nShani\n SC-Bluffton DP.pdf\nOn Thu, Sep 18, 2025 at 3:37 PM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nAfternoon Christine.\n\nI’m resending this email to copy you as I noted the spelling was incorrect in the below.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\n\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Clarkson, Constance\nSent: Thursday, September 18, 2025 3:35 PM\nTo: 'SHANI.PATTERSON@FLOCKSAFETY.COM' <SHANI.PATTERSON@FLOCKSAFETY.COM>\nCc: Taylor Ellison <taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>; Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>;\nchistine.spencer@flocksafety.com; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Babkiewicz, Joseph\n<jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; DuBose, Amanda <adubose@townofbluffton.com>; Burke, Helen\n<hburke@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: BPD Flock Phase 2 Plan\n\nGood afternoon Shani.\n\nThank you for your call this afternoon and offer to forward the phase 2 plans.  Please ensure to copy the team on your\nemail.\n\nI understood your role is to obtain the encroachment permits for the Town of Bluffton and Beaufort County.  Once the\nChief and Capt. Fazekas decide on the phase 2 locations during the meeting next week, that will serve as Bluffton’s\ndirection and permission to place the equipment on any selected property owned by the Town of Bluffton.  You won’t\nneed any additional paperwork for Bluffton.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any other questions.  Thank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\n--\nShani Patterson\n\nPermitting Associate\n 4047841347\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item1096.pdf"},"e0897":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0897","title":"Ready for Halloween_","frm":"Jamie at Flock Safety","date":"2025-09-19","text":"From:\nJamie at Flock Safety\nSent:\nFriday, September 19, 2025 10:11:19 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nReady for Halloween?\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi Chief Babkiewicz,\nHalloween draws crowds, traffic, and oftentimes, the unexpected. Mobile security trailers help communities prepare with\nreal-time security in high-risk areas, no existing infrastructure required.\nWith instant alerts and live footage, you’ll have the backup you need to respond before incidents escalate.\nTalk to an expert now about securing your mobile security trailer, before Halloween arrives.\n- Jamie","pdf":null},"e0308":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0308","title":"Fwd_ Flock Safety -SC - Bluffton PD - #1238221","frm":"Clarkson, Constance","date":"2025-09-23","text":"From:\nClarkson, Constance\nSent:\nTuesday, September 23, 2025 1:52:27 PM\nTo:\nShani Patterson\nCc:\nFazekas, Ryan; Babkiewicz, Joseph; Heather Phillips; Burke, Helen\nSubject:\nRE: Fwd: Flock Safety -SC - Bluffton PD - #1238221\nSensitivity:Normal\nGood afternoon Shani.\n\nThe Chief and Capt. are meeting today to decide on the final camera locations.  Afterward, the list will be reviewed for\nthe number of Dominion pole locations which will require electrical engineer plans, an electrician and in some cases\nan easement in addition to the pole attachment application.  Everything will then be compared to the budget. Powered\ncameras or a Flock poles and solar cameras will be determined based on the collected information.\n\nI expect to have the above completed within the next few weeks and will follow up with you then.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions in the meantime.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Shani Patterson <shani.patterson@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, September 23, 2025 12:44 PM\nTo: LYNDA ORANGE <lynda.orange@dominionenergy.com>\nCc: WILLEM VAN ZYL <jaco.van.zyl@dominionenergy.com>; Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>; LINDA\nMATHEWS <linda.mathews@dominionenergy.com>\nSubject: Re: Fwd: Flock Safety -SC - Bluffton PD - #1238221\n\nSubject: Clarification on Proposed Camera Locations\nGood Afternoon,\nThank you for your response. Yes, we are working with Constance Clarkson to finalize the proposed locations for\napproval. I just wanted to confirm—since solar-powered attachments are not authorized on DESC utility poles—\nwould the proposed locations need to be placed on Flock-owned poles instead, or is there a difference given\nthat Constance previously applied through Powerclerk?\nPhase 2 was broken up between city and county permitting jurisdictions, and I just want to make sure there isn’t\nanything additional needed from us to move forward.\nPlease let me know if my understanding is correct.\nBest regards,\n\nOn Tue, Sep 23, 2025 at 12:11 PM LYNDA ORANGE <lynda.orange@dominionenergy.com> wrote:\nGood afternoon, Shani,\n\nSolar-powered attachments are not authorized to attach to DESC utility poles. Please let me know who you\nare working with from the Bluffton Police Dept. I’ve copied Constance Clarkson who’s previously applied\nthrough our application system; Powerclerk.\n\nThank you,\nLynda Orange\nDESC Joint Use Attachments\nO: (803)217-4567\nM: (803)315-9787\n\nFrom: Shani Patterson <shani.patterson@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, September 23, 2025 10:08 AM\nTo: Lynda Orange (DESC Trans Distribution - 7) <lynda.orange@dominionenergy.com>\nSubject: [EXTERNAL] Fwd: Flock Safety -SC - Bluffton PD - #1238221\n\nCAUTION! This message was NOT SENT from DOMINION ENERGY\nAre you expecting this message to your DE email? Suspicious? Use PhishAlarm to report the message. Open a\nbrowser and type in the name of the trusted website instead of clicking on links. DO NOT click links or open\nattachments until you verify with the sender using a known-good phone number. Never provide your DE password.\n\nSubject: Request for Approval to Attach License Plate Readers to Utility Poles\nGood Afternoon,\nWe are partnering with the Bluffton Police Department to install ( 3 ) automatic license plate reader (ALPR)\ncameras within the jurisdiction. For this deployment, we are requesting permission to attach the equipment to\nexisting utility poles owned by your company.\n\n[linkedin.com] [instagram.com] [facebook.com] [youtube.com]\nThe ALPR units are compact, solar-powered, and fully self-contained. Installation does not require a bucket\ntruck, road closure, or any disruption to traffic. Our team will coordinate to ensure all safety and compliance\nstandards are met during installation.\nFor your review, I’ve attached the following documents:\nSite List (with proposed pole locations)\nDeployment Plan (including site-specific installation details)\nPlease let me know if additional information, drawings, or applications are required to proceed with this\nrequest. I’d be happy to provide any further documentation needed.\nThank you for your time and assistance.\nBest regards,\n\n[ f lo c k s a f e t y . c o m\n]\nShani\nPatterson\nPermitting\nAssociate\n 4047841347\n flocksafety.com [flocksafety.com]\n[flocksafety.com]\n\nCONFIDENTIALITY NOTICE: This electronic message contains information which may be legally confidential\nand or privileged and does not in any case represent a firm ENERGY COMMODITY bid or offer relating\nthereto which binds the sender without an additional express written confirmation to that effect. The information\nis intended solely for the individual or entity named above and access by anyone else is unauthorized. If you\nare not the intended recipient, any disclosure, copying, distribution, or use of the contents of this information is\nprohibited and may be unlawful. If you have received this electronic transmission in error, please reply\nimmediately to the sender that you have received the message in error, and delete it. Thank you.\n\n--\nShani Patterson\nPermitting Associate\n 4047841347\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0338":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0338","title":"Flock Camera Project - Follow Up","frm":"Fazekas, Ryan","date":"2025-09-25","text":"From:\nFazekas, Ryan\nSent:\nThursday, September 25, 2025 12:11:48 PM\nTo:\nClarkson, Constance\nCc:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph; Heather Phillips\nSubject:\nRE: Flock Camera Project - Follow Up\nSensitivity:Normal\nConstance,\n\nWe did meet and finalize the final two locations yesterday. We decided to place one camera on the West side of New\nRiverside Rd, near the New Riverside Park entrance to catch Southbound traffic. The other camera will be placed on\nthe East side of New Riverside Rd, near New Riverside Village Way to catch Northbound traffic. Hopefully, that makes\nsense!!!! If not, please let me know and I will clarify the best I can!!!!\n\nThanks,\n\nCaptain Ryan Fazekas\nOffice of Professional Standards\n843-706-4513\nBluffton Police Department\n101 Progressive Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nPh.: 843-706-4550\nFax:843-757-2269\nwww.blufftonpolice.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nSent: Thursday, September 25, 2025 11:51 AM\nTo: Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Heather Phillips <heather.phillips@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Flock Camera Project - Follow Up\n\nGood morning Ryan.\n\nThis is just a follow up regarding the Flock project.\n\nPlease advise if you met and finalized the phase 2 locations. I would like Flock to get these in a spreadsheet form\nsimilar to how we are tracking phase 1 progress.\n\nI had our biweekly meeting with Heather Phillips, Flock project manager for phase 1.   Once the locations are finalized\n\nfor phase 2, I have requested that the Flock site surveys be completed before any other work is done.  The Flock site\nsurveys determine if there is adequate solar, if the location is close enough to the road, exact placement of the\npole/camera, direction, etc.  I’ve accompanied the Flock technician on a few phase 1 site surveys.  From this\nexperience, I highly recommend that someone in BPD who is familiar with this project, go on the site surveys for each\nphase 2 location.\n\nAs a follow up for phase 1, please test camera #2 at the BPD substation for images.  The Chief checked it when it was\nfirst set up but we didn’t get any images at that time.  I confirmed with Heather there is a heartbeat and they show the\nlocation is 100% capable.\n\nThank you, sir.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov","pdf":null},"e0078":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0078","title":"Flock named to Forbes Cloud 100 \\204 Building Safer Communities Together","frm":"Anabel Pozzi","date":"2025-10-01","text":"From:\nAnabel Pozzi\nSent:\nWednesday, October 1, 2025 4:21:05 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nFlock named to Forbes Cloud 100 — Building Safer Communities Together\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHello Babkiewicz,\nI’m excited to share some big news — Flock Safety has been named to the Forbes Cloud 100 list, recognizing the top\nprivate cloud companies shaping the future.\nIn the feature, our CEO Garrett Langley outlines his vision for Safe Cities and safer communities nationwide. Here are a few\nkey highlights:\n80,000+ AI-powered cameras already deployed across the U.S.\nExpansion beyond fixed cameras with U.S.-made drones to extend visibility and support ground operations\nLaunch of Flock Nova, a public safety data platform integrating camera feeds, records, and critical datasets\nAcquisition of Lucidum, advancing data integration and real-time intelligence\nThese advancements strengthen Flock’s mission: to provide your team with more connections, broader coverage, and\nenhanced capabilities to prevent and solve crime.\n.\n\nҥ [Read the Full Forbes Article Here]\nThank you for your continued partnership in building safer communities.\nBest regards,\nAnabel Pozzi\nFlock Safety\nCall me at: 803-262-2019\nSouth Carolina Regional Account Executive\nBook Time With Me","pdf":null},"e0079":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0079","title":"Scheduling a Visit","frm":"Anabel Pozzi","date":"2025-10-15","text":"From:\nAnabel Pozzi\nSent:\nWednesday, October 15, 2025 11:26:26 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nScheduling a Visit\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi Cheif Babkiewicz,\nIt was great meeting you at the recent chief conference. I wanted to let you know that I will be in Hilton Head on Wednesday\nafternoon.\nI was hoping to see if you might be available for a visit either Tuesday afternoon or Wednesday morning. Please let me\nknow if either of those times works for you.\nLooking forward to connecting again.\nAnabel\nAnabel Pozzi\nFlock Safety\nCall me at: 803-262-2019\nSouth Carolina Regional Account Executive\nBook Time With Me","pdf":null},"e0836":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0836","title":"Webinar access issue \\204 here\\220s the new link","frm":"Hayden at Flock Safety","date":"2025-10-21","text":"From:\nHayden at Flock Safety\nSent:\nTuesday, October 21, 2025 10:10:25 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nWebinar access issue — here’s the new link\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nWe apologize for the difficulties you experienced when trying to access the link to our upcoming webinar, 'Prepared for\nAnything: How Cities Prepare for Planned and Unplanned Events'.\nThe problem has been resolved, and you can now sign up below to join us on November 5th, at 2 p.m. EST / 11 a.m. PST.\nLearn how cities are transforming emergency management by integrating Real-Time Crime Centers to create faster,\nsmarter, and more connected responses to any event or crisis.\n✅ Register Here\nSee you soon,\nThe Flock Safety Team\n\nP.S. If you can’t attend live, we’ll send a full recording afterward.","pdf":null},"e0841":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0841","title":"New Flock Safety Customer Success Manager - Buffton PD","frm":"Heather Ouellette","date":"2025-10-23","text":"From:\nHeather Ouellette\nSent:\nThursday, October 23, 2025 3:04:32 PM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph; Fazekas, Ryan; Burke, Helen; Karafa, Craig\nSubject:\nRe: New Flock Safety Customer Success Manager - Buffton PD\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon!\nAs Georgia mentioned, I will be your new Customer Success Manager (CSM). Prior to working at Flock, I was a Detective\nassigned to the Intelligence Center at the Raleigh Police Department and used Flock daily.\nMoving forward, the CSM focus will be on partnering more closely and strategically with agencies, like yours, that are leveraging\nFlock to drive measurable results. I'm excited to work with you to build on the progress and successes you have already made.\nI'd love to get an introductory meeting scheduled, where we can overview the new CSM role, discuss ROI and agency metrics,\nreview training needs, and cover any other general inquiries. Please let me know a day/time that works best for your team,\nor use this link to schedule with me.\nThank you,\nHeather\nOn Thu, Oct 23, 2025 at 1:31 PM Georgia Abdallah <georgia.abdallah@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nGood Afternoon Team,\nI wanted to let you know that Flock recently restructured our team's territories to further improve the level of service and\nattention each customer receives. As a result, Heather Ouellette will be your new Customer Success Manager at Flock. I have\nCC'd her on this email thread so that she can set up an introductory call with you.\nIt has been a privilege working with your agency, and I wish you all the best.\nPlease don't hesitate to contact me if you have any questions.\nBest,\nGeorgia\n--\nGeorgia Abdallah\n\nRegional Customer Success Manager II\n 470-820-1996\n flocksafety.com\n--\nHeather Ouellette\nCustomer Success Manager\n 470-852-3342\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0250":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0250","title":"Introducing Flock Academy \\204 Your New Training Hub for Flock Safety","frm":"Chris Colwell","date":"2025-10-24","text":"From:\nChris Colwell\nSent:\nFriday, October 24, 2025 12:26:38 PM\nTo:\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nIntroducing Flock Academy — Your New Training Hub for Flock Safety\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nHello Joseph,\n\nWe’re thrilled to introduce Flock Academy, our new Learning Management System designed to make learning Flock easier,\nfaster, and more accessible for everyone.\n\nExplore self-paced courses, live webinars, and certifications for you and your team — all accessible directly within the Flock platform.\n\nWhether you’re onboarding new team members or looking to build deeper expertise, Flock Academy offers a consistent, on-demand\nlearning experience that grows with you. New courses and features are added regularly to support your ongoing success.\n\nSee Flock Academy in Action!\n\nTo get started, click on the question mark icon in the navigation bar, and select Flock Academy. You’ll also receive a welcome email\nconfirming your profile — no further action needed.\n\nWe encourage you and your team to explore, complete courses, and earn certifications that help you get the most from\nFlock. As you learn, we’d love your feedback — it helps ensure Flock Academy continues to meet your needs and evolve with you.\nYou can share your thoughts anytime through our feedback form.\n\nThank you for being part of the Flock community,\n\nChris Colwell\nSVP, Customer Experience\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e1076":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1076","title":"Flock Safety _ Monthly Product Update _ October 2025","frm":"Myron Maret","date":"2025-10-27","text":"From:\nMyron Maret\nSent:\nMonday, October 27, 2025 8:57:12 PM\nTo:\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nFlock Safety | Monthly Product Update | October 2025\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nHello,\nHere's our monthly snapshot of our latest updates and product releases. We've included videos and\narticles to help you make the most of your Flock Safety system. Click here to see what's new.\nTopics in this month’s newsletter include:\nEvidence File Validator\nAdmins can now reset user Multi-factor Authentication\nAlert Sources by Zones (coming soon)\nNetwork Audit Update\nWe'd also like to invite you to an upcoming training webinar in November!\nThis webinar, on November 13th at 2:00p EST, will cover a complete review of the new Search\nexperience. This will include tips and best practices, as well as improvements based on your feedback so\nfar. All users are invited to attend. Register here.\nFor a deeper dive on all of the Flock Safety features, we'd encourage you to check out the Help Center to\naccess knowledge articles, create and track the status of your cases, and take advantage of trainings\nand certifications. Access the updated help center here.\nIf you have any questions about how any of our latest enhancements might help your agency solve crime\nor you want to learn more about any other feature, please always feel free to reach out to your Customer\nSuccess Manager or support@flocksafety.com\nThank you and be safe,\nMyron Maret\nFlock Safety | Customer Success\nClick here to unsubscribe from this list or manage your preferences here.","pdf":null},"e0854":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0854","title":"Meeting Follow Up","frm":"Heather Ouellette","date":"2026-02-12","text":"From:\nHeather Ouellette\nSent:\nThursday, February 12, 2026 11:45:11 AM\nTo:\nBurke, Helen; Fazekas, Ryan; Babkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nMeeting Follow Up\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:Transparency Portal One-Pager (5).PDF ;\n\nGood Morning,\nThank you again for taking the time to meet with me yesterday. I really appreciate the update on how your agency is using Flock,\nespecially the recent vehicle theft pattern around Westbury Park. I'd love to hear if you're able to recover those vehicles and/or\nmake any arrests.\nAs a quick recap:\nInvestigator Training: Once your Operations Captain connects with the Detectives, let me know a few dates/times that\nwork for a virtual session (about an hour, can be shorter if needed).\nWebinars: Below are the dates & times of our upcoming live webinars. The hyperlinks will bring you to the registration\npage. These are always great to attend! The New Search on March 4th is great for Patrol, specifically those on night shift.\nPlease forward the links to other members of your agency that could benefit from attending.\nFeb 25th, 1pm - Solving Cases with Live Video and LPR\nMarch 3rd, 2pm - Sharing and Filters\nMarch 4th, 6am - New Search - After Dark + Enhancements\nMarch 11th, 1pm - FlockOS: Deep Dive of the Real Time Features\nMarch 24th, 2pm - Role Management\nMultifactor Authentication (MFA): Since you’re already using Duo, you can enable MFA in the Organization settings\nwhenever you’re ready. I can resend the email template you can use to notify staff if that’s helpful.\nTransparency Portal: If you’d like to move forward, we can schedule a short 15‑minute call to configure a public-facing\nportal, including any success stories you’d like to highlight. I'm attaching an overview to this email to help you better\nunderstand what can be shared.\nHere is a live example: Gastonia PD's Transparency Portal\nSuccess Stories: Please send over any additional success stories you can think of!\nZones: I'm happy to jump on a call to design these with you, or if you'd like to create them on your own, you can do so\nfrom: Admin > Zones\nLowe’s Network Access: Below is the email template to gain access to Lowe's devices. I highly recommend doing so.\nAs always, please reach out if you need anything at all.\nBest,\n\nHeather\n--\nLowe's Camera Sharing Next Steps\nEmail Template to be completed by the head of the agency BELOW\n—\nEmail Subject Line- Lowe’s Camera Share; Name of the Agency\nEmail Template sent to: todd.a.isenhour@lowes.com and\nCC emma.jensen@flocksafety.com and christopher.cater@flocksafety.com\nAs TITLE for CITY/ COUNTY, I would like to formally request regional access to Lowe’s owned Flock safety\nsystems and/ or LiveView. This technology will assist in preventing or investigating criminal activity in the local\ncommunity we both serve. Lowe’s technology and my department’s access to such will only be used for bona fide\ninvestigations, which are documented within our department and via audit trail within the Flock Safety platform.\nThese investigative tools and technology will not be permitted for personal use, for use on unauthorized devices\nor by unauthorized users within our department.  I understand if the technology is not used\ncorrectly, Lowe's reserves the right to terminate the department’s access to Lowe's owned Flock safety systems\nand/or LiveView.\n\nName\nSignature of Head of Agency, Chief of Police or Sheriff\nTitle\n--\nHeather Ouellette\nCustomer Success Manager\n 470-852-3342\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e1056":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1056","title":"We read every word_ Your Flock survey is coming next week","frm":"Lisa Krolikowski","date":"2025-11-03","text":"From:\nLisa Krolikowski\nSent:\nMonday, November 3, 2025 3:08:05 PM\nTo:\nJoseph Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nWe read every word. Your Flock survey is coming next week\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nHi Joseph,\n\nI hope you’re doing well. Next week, you’ll get a short 2-minute survey from Flock.  We send these surveys every 90 days, and I’m\nreaching out personally because your feedback truly matters to us.\n\nWhen you share what’s working and what isn’t, we take it to heart. We read every response word-for-word, review it that week, and\nassign it to the right owner.\n\nBecause of what you’ve told us, we’re building and improving:\n\nDevice Health Dashboard (in development): clearer, near-real-time visibility into camera health and fix status - what’s down,\nwhy, and when it’ll be resolved.\n\nInstall Timeline Transparency: more accurate milestones and status updates so you don’t need to chase dates.\n\nSearch Experience Clarity: On November 13th at 2:00p EST, we will cover a complete review of the new Search experience.\nThis will include tips and best practices, as well as improvements based on your feedback so far. All users are invited to\nattend. Register here.\n\nContinued Learning: we know it’s difficult to keep your users updated and new hires trained.  We have developed a new learning\nmanagement system with learning tracks and certifications that you can send to users and track progress to ensure everyone is\nup to date on the latest from Flock.\n\nWhen your survey arrives next week, I’d be grateful if you could take a minute to respond. All feedback is welcome - positive and\nconstructive. If something’s off, we want to fix it. If something helps your team, we want to do more of it. If you’d rather talk directly, my\npersonal email is lisa.krolikowski@flocksafety.com. Please reach out anytime if you want to discuss feedback, concerns, or ideas.\nWe’re here to help.\n\nThank you,\n\nLisa Krolikowski\nVP, Customer Success\n\nClick here to unsubscribe from this list or manage your preferences here.","pdf":null},"e0080":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0080","title":"Join Us_ How Cities Prepare for Planned & Unplanned Events","frm":"Anabel Pozzi","date":"2025-11-04","text":"From:\nAnabel Pozzi\nSent:\nTuesday, November 4, 2025 4:43:25 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nJoin Us: How Cities Prepare for Planned & Unplanned Events\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi Joseph,\nWe’re hosting a webinar, “Prepared for Anything: How Cities Prepare for Planned and Unplanned Events,” on Wed, Nov 5, at 2:00 pm ET.\nJoin public safety leaders from the City of New Orleans and Elk Grove PD to see how pairing real‑time strategies with emergency\nmanagement creates faster, smarter, more connected operations.\nWhat you’ll learn:\nIntegrate RTCCs into emergency management to connect intelligence, communications, and field response in real time.\nApply after‑action insights from major events to improve coordination and readiness.\nFuture‑proof city response with technology and processes that scale to any event or emergency.\nEnhance jurisdictional collaboration by connecting multiple city stakeholders within a single workflow.\nRegister here: Click Here\nCan’t make it live? Register to receive the on‑demand recording.\nAnabel Pozzi\nFlock Safety\nCall me at: 803-262-2019\nSouth Carolina Regional Account Executive\nBook Time With Me\nIf you'd like to stop receiving these emails, let me know.","pdf":null},"e1078":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1078","title":"Flock Safety _ Upcoming Training Webinars","frm":"Myron Maret","date":"2026-01-22","text":"From:\nMyron Maret\nSent:\nThursday, January 22, 2026 9:36:58 PM\nTo:\nJoe Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nFlock Safety | Upcoming Training Webinars\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nHello,\nWe want to invite you to join two upcoming training webinars focused on enhancing your use of the Flock\nSafety system.\n1. New Search Experience Overview - Thursday, January 29th at 2:00 PM EST\nThis session will provide an overview of the new Search interface, including best practices and recent\nupdates implemented based on agency feedback.\nRegister below:\nNew Search Registration\n2. New Search Experience Overview - Thursday, February 5th at 2:00 AM EST\nThis session will provide an overview of the new Search interface, including best practices and recent\nupdates implemented based on agency feedback. This session will be conducted overnight\nspecifically for overnight users / morning watch.\nRegister below:\nNew Search After Dark Registration\nAll agency users are encouraged to attend these webinars. Please feel free to share this invitation with\nother members of your department.\nWe look forward to seeing you there!\nBe safe,\nFlock Safety | Customer Success\nsupport@flocksafety.com\nClick here to unsubscribe from this list or manage your preferences here.","pdf":null},"e0252":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0252","title":"Introducing 24_7 Chat Support \\204 Now Available in the Flock Safety Platform","frm":"Chris Vetrano at Flock Safety","date":"2025-11-10","text":"From:\nChris Vetrano at Flock Safety\nSent:\nMonday, November 10, 2025 10:08:55 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nIntroducing 24/7 Chat Support — Now Available in the Flock Safety Platform\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi Joseph,\nWe’re excited to announce that starting today, all Flock Safety customers now have access to Chat Support directly within the Flock Safety Platform.\nThis new in-product experience gives you:\nInstant answers to common questions, 24/7\nSeamless access to our Support team when you need human assistance\nSmarter, faster help — right inside your Flock Safety Platform workspace\nYou’ll now see the new Chat icon on your Flock Safety Platform navigation bar. Simply click it to launch Chat and start typing your question.\nNo more searching for forms or waiting on hold. Just quick, clear support when and where you need it. This enhancement was made possible thanks to the\nfeedback from our early pilot participants, who helped us refine and perfect the experience.\nWe’re excited to bring this to your entire organization and look forward to hearing how Chat Support helps your team save time and stay focused on your\nmission.\nThank you for partnering with us – and for your patience – as we continue to build a smarter, faster, and more connected Support experience.\nChris Vetrano & the Flock Safety Team\nDirector, Customer Support","pdf":null},"e0667":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0667","title":"Fact Check_ No Hack_ We will never stop fighting for you_","frm":"Garrett Langley","date":"2025-12-08","text":"From:\nGarrett Langley\nSent:\nMonday, December 8, 2025 4:00:00 PM\nTo:\nJoe Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nFact Check: No Hack. We will never stop fighting for you.\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nHi SC - Bluffton PD Team,\n\nI’m writing to you directly because I want there to be zero confusion about what’s happening.\n\nFlock has never been hacked. Ever.\nFlock is CJIS compliant.\nFlock does not share, or resell your data. Nor have we ever.\nFlock adheres to the highest security standards, including:\nNDAA\nSOC2 (Type II)\nSOC3\nISO 27001\nHigher Education Community Vendor Assessment Tool (HECVAT)\nFERPA\nWe are also aligned with the security protocols established by NIST Cybersecurity as well as the Cloud Security\nAlliance CAIQ framework.\n\nFlock is building tools to help you fight the real crime affecting communities across the country.\n\nMany activists don’t like that.\n\nLet’s call this what it is: Flock, and the law enforcement agencies we partner with, are under coordinated attack.\n\nThe attacks aren’t new. You’ve been dealing with this for forever, and we’ve been dealing with this since our founding, from the same\nactivist groups who want to defund the police, weaken public safety, and normalize lawlessness. Now, they’re producing YouTube\nvideos with misleading headlines. They’re also trying to turn a public records process into a weapon against you and against us.\n\nMake no mistake, we’re fighting this fight for you, and, I hope, with you. I remain committed to building world-class technology\nto help you keep your communities safe. And doing so in a transparent, secure, and privacy centric way.\n\nPlease be on the lookout for more information from our Customer Success and Product teams.\n\nGarrett\n\nGarrett Langley\nChief Executive Officer\n\n flocksafety.com\n\n    (714) 333-0236","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0667.pdf"},"e1057":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1057","title":"What you Need to Know About Recent Online Disclosures","frm":"Lisa Krolikowski","date":"2025-12-08","text":"From:\nLisa Krolikowski\nSent:\nMonday, December 8, 2025 4:12:38 PM\nTo:\nJoe Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nWhat you Need to Know About Recent Online Disclosures\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nHi SC - Bluffton PD Team,\n\nWe are aware that agencies across the country, particularly in states with broad public-records laws, are seeing increased PRA/FOIA\nactivity seeking, among other things, LPR search logs.\n\nRecently, a third-party website began aggregating search information that appears to have been released through these public-records\nprocesses. We recognize that seeing investigative search activity displayed publicly can raise understandable concerns about officer\nsafety, investigative integrity, community perception, and compliance with state law.\n\nTo be clear: Flock has not been breached or compromised.\n\nThe Intent of this note is to provide factual context about what is happening and how Flock is supporting you.\n\nWhat’s happening\nA number of agencies have received public-records requests seeking detailed audit logs, and some have disclosed those logs\npursuant to their state’s legal requirements. Based on what we have seen, websites like the one circulating online are using agency-\nreleased public-records data.\n\nTo be clear:\nFlock does not publish or distribute agency search logs.\nFlock does not provide search histories or lookup activity to public websites or third parties.\nAll Flock data is owned and controlled by the agency that collected it.\n\nWe understand how concerning this situation is, and we know many of you are fielding questions from leadership, legal teams, and\ncommunity members.\n\nWhat Flock is doing\nWe are actively developing product and policy improvements, focusing on redaction capabilities and additional safeguards, to help\nagencies limit what is included in audit exports and to support more precise responses to PRA/FOIA requests. These enhancements\nare planned for early 2026 and are designed to reduce the risk of broad disclosures like those currently circulating.\n\nWhat you can do now\nUntil these new tools are available, we recommend:\nReviewing your sharing settings and considering a temporary shift from Nationwide Lookup to Statewide Lookup, if that better\naligns with your agency’s legal guidance and operational risk posture.\nAgencies that choose to temporarily narrow sharing can revisit and reopen those settings in Q1 2026 once our new\nsafeguards are released.\nConnect with your CSM or contact support@flocksafety.com if you’d like assistance reviewing your current audit logs and\nsharing settings.\n\nWe know this environment is challenging. We are committed to supporting you with clear communication, better tools, and improved\nsafeguards moving forward. If your agency would like a deeper discussion, we’re more than happy to set that up.\n\nLisa Krolikowski\nVP, Customer Success - Law Enforcement\n\nHow We Protect Privacy While Advancing\nPublic Safety\n\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item1057.pdf"},"e0651":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0651","title":"Assistance needed with Flock Safety camera","frm":"Flock Safety Support","date":"2025-12-10","text":"From:\nFlock Safety Support\nSent:\nWednesday, December 10, 2025 10:13:33 AM\nTo:\ndchandler@townofbluffton.com; jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com; cgonzales@townofbluffton.com;\ninvoice@townofbluffton.com; ssteese@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nAssistance needed with Flock Safety camera\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi there,\nWe received an alert regarding power connectivity from Flock Safety camera P#11 May River Rd EB @\nBPD Substation at SC - Bluffton PD Phase 1. At your earliest convenience, could you please help\nensure that power is flowing normally to the AC box?\nPlease follow the below steps to check your power source and prevent prolonged camera downtime.\nConfirm the red light is glowing on the rectangular box that feeds a wire to the camera:\nIf the Red light is not lit (Off), please have a professional check your incoming power for\npotential issues such as a tripped circuit breaker or damaged power line. Please look carefully\nas the light can be faint in daylight.\nIf the Red light is lit (On), please reply to this message or email Flock Safety via\nsupport@flocksafety.com and let our team know so that we can send a technician out to\ntroubleshoot.\nNote: Some models have a Green light; if this is the case, please report whether it is On or Off.\nThank you for your assistance, and stay safe,\nFlock Safety Support\nRef: 01419329 P#11 May River Rd EB @ BPD Substation\n\nHave questions? Check out the FAQs on our website! - FAQs\nOr you can always email us at support@flocksafety.com and we'll get back to you as soon as possible.","pdf":null},"e0837":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0837","title":"Last Call_ Bridge the Dispatch and Real-Time Center Gap","frm":"Hayden at Flock Safety","date":"2025-12-10","text":"From:\nHayden at Flock Safety\nSent:\nWednesday, December 10, 2025 10:25:21 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nLast Call: Bridge the Dispatch and Real-Time Center Gap\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi Joe,\nQuick reminder that tomorrow at 1 pm ET / 10 am PT, leaders from Elk Grove and Vacaville are sharing how they\nimproved communication between dispatch and Real-Time Centers.\nIf your teams deal with mismatched updates, repeated calls, or slow information flow, this webinar will be useful.\n→ Register here\nHope you can join us,\nHayden","pdf":null},"e0262":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0262","title":"Important Update to Flock Audit Logs to Protect Officer Safety & Active Investigations","frm":"Chris at Flock Safety","date":"2025-12-11","text":"From:\nChris at Flock Safety\nSent:\nThursday, December 11, 2025 2:49:01 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nImportant Update to Flock Audit Logs to Protect Officer Safety & Active Investigations\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\nFlock was founded on the principle of promoting public safety, while\npartnering closely with law enforcement agencies across the country to bring\nclarity and allow accountability, which helps to maintain public trust.\nThat commitment to transparency remains unchanged, but the environment\naround us has changed dramatically. We cannot let those abusing our\ntransparency compromise officer safety and the safety of our community.\nTo that end, we are making an important update to how Flock’s Network\nAudit Logs display information. As a reminder, Network Audit logs are the\nbreadcrumbs for reciprocal sharing on Flock’s National Lookup tool:\nEffective this week, Network Audit Logs will now only include:\nA unique alphanumeric search identifier\nSearching agency name\nDate of search\nTimeframe\nNumber of networks searched\nOffense Type or free text search reasons\nTo protect officer safety and active investigations, Network Audit Logs\nwill no longer include:\nOfficer names\nSpecific plates searched\nVehicle fingerprint information\n\nThese changes ensure agencies retain visibility and accountability while\npreventing the misuse of sensitive operational data. And all the details will be\npreserved with and visible to the originating agency. If agency B wants to\nunderstand more details in a Network Audit, they can simply contact the\noriginating agency A and reference the unique alphanumeric search identifier\nto cross-reference the specific information they require.\nYour Organization Audit Logs, the audit trail for your agency’s own users,\nwill remain unchanged. You will continue to have full access to all details you\npreviously relied on.\nAdditionally, our new required Offense Type field, which is rolling out to all\ncustomers this month, will bring unprecedented consistency and clarity to\nsearch reporting. By standardizing intent across all Flock searches, we\neliminate subjective or inconsistent entries while strengthening compliance\nand public accountability.\nOnce the required Offense Type drop-down is live for a customer, we will\nreplace the Free Text search reason in the Network Audit with the Offense\nType.\nWe remain deeply committed to transparency and democratic oversight. But\nwhen transparency is weaponized to harm officers, derail investigations, and\nembolden criminal networks, we have a responsibility to act. These updates\nhelp us strike the right balance: maintaining clear, consistent auditability while\nensuring no sensitive information can be exploited to jeopardize your work or\nyour people.\nIf you have questions or want to discuss these changes further, my team and\nI are here to support you. Thank you for your continued partnership and for\nthe work you do every day to keep communities safe.\nRespectfully,\nChris Colwell\nSVP, Customer Experience\nFlock Safety\n\nFlock Safety\n1170 Howell Mill Rd NW, Suite 210\nAtlanta, Georgia 30318, United States","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0262.pdf"},"e0263":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0263","title":"Standing With You \\204 Momentum, Progress, and What\\220s Ahead","frm":"Chris at Flock Safety","date":"2025-12-19","text":"From:\nChris at Flock Safety\nSent:\nFriday, December 19, 2025 10:07:39 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nStanding With You — Momentum, Progress, and What’s Ahead\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\nOver the last several weeks, Flock has faced one of the most challenging\nperiods in our history - and one of the most important. In that time, agencies\nlike yours have helped us demonstrate something that matters deeply: when\nfacts, transparency, and public safety lead the conversation, communities\nrespond.\nWhen major crimes capture national attention, Flock often operates quietly\nbehind the scenes, helping agencies connect the dots and bring suspects into\ncustody; just yesterday, the public learned that the Brown / MIT shooter\ninvestigation was aided by Flock as Rhode Island and New Hampshire\nseamlessly shared data across a multi-state network, demonstrating exactly\nwhy secure, cross-jurisdictional sharing matters and how a connected Flock\nnetwork can turn fragmented information into fast, coordinated action when it\ncounts most.\nIn just the past two weeks, Flock partner agencies succeeded before city\ncouncil in San Diego and Oakland - among the most complex and scrutinized\njurisdictions in the country. Despite organized opposition and widespread\nmisinformation, the outcomes were clear: communities listened, leaders\nengaged, and law enforcement prevailed.\nThat success is not accidental. Over the past three weeks, our executive\nleadership team has met directly with more than 300 Chiefs through small,\ncandid roundtables across the country. We’ve heard your concerns: the\nfrustration, the pressure, and the responsibility you carry. The consistent\ntheme is that you want partners who are honest, responsive, and committed\nto standing alongside you when the work gets difficult.\n\nProduct Progress Focused on Clarity and Safety\nIn recent weeks, our Product and Engineering teams moved quickly to deliver\nnew system updates designed to support compliance, protect sensitive\ninformation, and provide meaningful clarity, without putting officers or\ninvestigations at risk.\nThese include:\nExpanded privacy protections in your Network Audit by redacting user\nnames, license plates, filters, and case numbers to better safeguard your\nactivity data.\nContinued rollout of offense-type categorization drop-down field for\nclearer reporting and oversight\nNew controls that balance transparency with officer and public safety\nThe feedback from agencies and elected officials has been overwhelmingly\npositive. Leaders are asking for clarity - not raw data that can be\nmisinterpreted or misused - and these updates deliver exactly that.\nBefore year-end, we will also be releasing a Federal Opt-In capability,\ngiving agencies additional control and flexibility when working with federal\npartners.\nLegal Momentum\nLast week, a Washington State judge ruled that license plate reader data is\nexempt from the state’s public records law. While this ruling differs from a\nprior opinion and the broader debate continues, it represents meaningful\nmomentum as we head into a challenging legislative cycle. It reinforces a\nprinciple many Chiefs already know firsthand: public safety data requires\ncareful stewardship, not weaponization.\nLooking Ahead\nThis is a demanding season for law enforcement. The issues are complex, the\nscrutiny is real, and the stakes are high. But Flock is entering this next phase\nstronger than ever, with expanded legal resources, a fast-moving product and\nengineering organization, a deeply engaged community team, and an\nexecutive group fully aligned behind our customers.\nMost importantly, we remain committed to operating like a first responder:\nmoving quickly, telling the truth, and standing shoulder-to-shoulder with the\nagencies we serve.\nThank you for your leadership, your partnership, and your trust. We are\nconfident that the work ahead will make all of us stronger.\n\nRespectfully,\nChris Colwell\nSVP, Customer Experience | Flock Safety\n\nFlock Safety\n1170 Howell Mill Rd NW, Suite 210\nAtlanta, Georgia 30318, United States","pdf":null},"e0264":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0264","title":"Update on Limited Condor Misconfiguration","frm":"Chris at Flock Safety","date":"2025-12-23","text":"From:\nChris at Flock Safety\nSent:\nTuesday, December 23, 2025 12:31:51 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nUpdate on Limited Condor Misconfiguration\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\nWe recognize that you may have noticed a few recent communications from\nus. This increased frequency is intentional and directly reflects the feedback\nwe’ve received from our law enforcement partners, who have emphasized\nthe importance of staying well-informed about any updates or issues. Our\ngoal is to provide the transparency and timely information you’ve asked for,\nso you can remain confident in the reliability and security of your Flock\nSafety devices.\nWith that commitment in mind, we are writing to share an update regarding a\nlimited configuration issue identified on a very small number of Condor video\ndevices. No LPR devices, audio devices, or trailers were impacted.\nYesterday, we reached out directly to the small group of customers whose\nvideo devices were affected. We are now sharing this broader update to\nmaintain transparency with our entire customer community.\nWhat Happened\nThe debug interface on a small number of Condor units was temporarily\naccessible on the internet without password protection. These units were part\nof a standard testing process used to validate compatibility and reliability with\ncellular carriers such as Verizon, AT&T, and T-Mobile.\nThis debug interface is used solely for troubleshooting. It does not allow for\nany manipulation of the camera, does not provide access to the Flock cloud,\nand does not enable access to customer accounts, search functionality, or\nanalytics. The only content visible was live or recorded video comparable to\nwhat could be observed from a public roadway.\n\nA website and a sensationalized YouTube channel inaccurately portrayed the\nextent of this access. Although we do not wish to draw further attention to the\nvideo, it is important that you have the facts needed to address potential\nquestions from council members and the public. To be clear: no sensitive or\nconfidential information was accessed or available.\nOnce identified, the issue was promptly corrected, and security updates were\ndeployed across the affected devices. This was a limited, isolated\nconfiguration issue and is not indicative of a broader or ongoing concern.\nFor a more detailed explanation of this event, please refer to our recent blog\npost: Update on Limited Condor Device Configuration Issue\nWe take security seriously at every stage of development and are committed\nto maintaining the trust you place in us. If you have any questions or would\nlike additional detail, please don’t hesitate to reach out. We also encourage\nyou to forward this information to others in your department or to\ncouncilmembers so they can be prepared for any potential questions.\nBest regards,\nChris Colwell\nSVP, Customer Experience | Flock Safety\nPS - want to opt out of communications like this? Update your preferences\nhere.\n\nFlock Safety\n1170 Howell Mill Rd NW, Suite 210\nAtlanta, Georgia 30318, United States","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0264.pdf"},"e0093":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0093","title":"Strengthening Transparency in Every Search","frm":"Ashley at Flock Safety","date":"2025-12-29","text":"From:\nAshley at Flock Safety\nSent:\nMonday, December 29, 2025 12:56:54 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nStrengthening Transparency in Every Search\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\nAt Flock Safety, we believe that public safety technology only works when it\nearns the trust of the communities it serves. That’s why we’re continually\nimproving how agencies can use and audit Flock data, building transparency\nand accountability right into the product.\nStarting today, you’ll see a new step in every Flock LPR Search:\nOffense Type Dropdown: Before running a search, users will be required to\nselect an offense type from a NIBRS-based list (expanded through customer\nfeedback and data analysis).\nThe “Search Reason” field will remain as an optional way to add additional\ncontext.\nWhy It Matters:\n\u0000 Greater Transparency: clearer insight into the purpose behind\nevery search.\n\u0000\nCleaner Audits: consistent, standardized data across your agency\nand the agencies you share with.\n\u0000 Improved Filter Confidence: stronger assurance that searches\nalign with investigative needs and policy.\nWhat’s Ahead:\nWe’re also building offense type reporting and search-usage analytics by\nagency to provide deeper visibility and support data-driven accountability.\n\nFor more information, you can learn more in this doc.\n- Ashley at Flock Safety\nLearn More About the Enhancements\n\nFlock Safety\n1170 Howell Mill Rd NW, Suite 210\nAtlanta, Georgia 30318, United States","pdf":null},"e0893":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0893","title":"Flock Camera - Bluffton #04 S Okatie Hwy @ New River Boat Landing","frm":"Heather Phillips","date":"2025-12-30","text":"From:\nHeather Phillips\nSent:\nTuesday, December 30, 2025 11:00:12 AM\nTo:\nClarkson, Constance\nCc:\nFazekas, Ryan; Babkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nRe: Flock Camera - Bluffton #04 S Okatie Hwy @ New River Boat Landing\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Morning,\nThank you for confirming. I requested that our Engineering team review.\nThank you,\nHeather Phillips\nProject Manager\n 412-512-0563\n 470-762-4276\n flocksafety.com\n UPCOMING OOO: 12/30-1/2\nOn Tue, Dec 30, 2025 at 10:53 AM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nGood morning all.\n\nThe Flock camera at the above location was connected to power this morning.  Please complete any necessary tests\nand reply to this email with confirmation that it is fully operational.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\n\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov","pdf":null},"e0847":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0847","title":"Flock Usage Audit","frm":"Heather Ouellette","date":"2026-01-08","text":"From:\nHeather Ouellette\nSent:\nThursday, January 8, 2026 4:12:03 PM\nTo:\nFazekas, Ryan; Babkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nFlock Usage Audit\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nHappy New Year! I hope you both had wonderful (and relaxing) holidays!\nIn one of our prior meetings, we briefly touched on some of the information that is collected and/or presented at your council\nmeetings. I understand you have a committee meeting tonight to discuss your Flock usage/audit. Are you willing to share a copy\nof the data that will be presented at the meeting? Do you also cover successes/metrics in these meetings or strictly present agency\nusage?\nThank you for your dedication to our partnership.\nBest,\nHeather\n--\nHeather Ouellette\nCustomer Success Manager\n 470-852-3342\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0847.pdf"},"e0267":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0267","title":"Upcoming Change to Accessing Flock Academy","frm":"Chris at Flock Safety","date":"2026-01-23","text":"From:\nChris at Flock Safety\nSent:\nFriday, January 23, 2026 10:07:34 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nUpcoming Change to Accessing Flock Academy\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHello Chief Babkiewicz,\nAt Flock Safety, we are committed to ensuring that you have seamless\naccess to all learning resources, including our Help Center, which offers\nstep-by-step articles, and Flock Academy, which provides a variety of\ncourses to help you navigate Flock effectively.\nAs part of our ongoing evaluation of these tools, we have received requests\nfor the ability to assign Flock Academy courses to team members. Currently,\nthis functionality is limited due to the way users log in. To address this\nrequest, we will be changing the login method for Flock Academy.\nThis update will also:\nMinimize issues with certificate generation,\nEnable internal admins to be promoted to Manager roles in Flock\nAcademy (instructions to follow later this year), and\nEnsure that user profiles display complete name information.\n\nImportant Details:\nEffective January 30th, 2026, Single Sign-On (SSO) will no longer be\nused to access Flock Academy.\nWhen you click on Flock Academy, you will be directed to a login page.\nClick on “Forgot my password”.\n\nPlease use the email address associated with your Flock account;\ndo not use any other personal email.\nYou’ll receive an email to “Activate Account” with Flock Academy.\n\nOnce you click on “Activate Account”, you’ll be prompted to update\nyour password. Take this time to also update your profile information\nsuch as your First Name and Last Name. This is an important step to\nensure your certificates print out correctly.\nFor all new users moving forward, they will receive an email being\nwelcomed to Flock Academy and will follow the instructions on setting\nup their profile. This will take approximately 2-3 hours to receive.\nQuestions and Support\ni\ni i\ni\ni\ni\n\nIf you experience any difficulties or have questions, our Support team is\navailable at support@flocksafety.com.\nWe appreciate your cooperation and look forward to continuing to enhance\nyour learning experience at Flock Safety.\nBest,\nCustomer Education Team @ Flock Safety\n\nFlock Safety\n1170 Howell Mill Rd NW, Suite 210\nAtlanta, Georgia 30318, United States","pdf":null},"e0850":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0850","title":"Flock - Quarterly Review Meeting","frm":"Heather Ouellette","date":"2026-01-16","text":"From:\nHeather Ouellette\nSent:\nFriday, January 16, 2026 1:32:40 PM\nTo:\nBabkiewicz, Joseph; Fazekas, Ryan; Burke, Helen\nSubject:\nFlock - Quarterly Review Meeting\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nI hope things have been going well with you and the team!\nIt's that time again for our quarterly review, and I’d love to get some time on the calendar to re-align on:\nGoals you have for your agency over the next ~3 months\nYour current product deployment, upcoming renewals, invoices, any budgetary needs, and your current processes for\ntracking ROI\nTraining needs for your agency, which could include a deep dive for investigators, admin refresher, new feature overviews,\nor any other training specific to your department\nDo any of these times work for a 30 minute meeting next week?\nTuesday 1/20 at 1p, 2p, or 3p\nWednesday 1/21 at 11a, 1p or 2p\nThursday 1/22 at 1p or 2p\nIf none of those are ideal, feel free to send over a couple of options, or you can grab a time that works best for you here:\nhttps://www.getclockwise.com/c/heather-ouellette-flocksafety-com/qbr-q1-2026\nFor this meeting in particular, I recommend inviting command staff, finance personnel, and any others that would benefit from\nsetting agency goals and aligning on budgetary items.\nI'm looking forward to catching up and planning out the next quarter with you!\nBest,\nHeather\n--\n\nHeather Ouellette\nCustomer Success Manager\n 470-852-3342\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0268":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0268","title":"Federal Court Upholds Constitutionality of LPR Technology","frm":"Chris at Flock Safety","date":"2026-01-27","text":"From:\nChris at Flock Safety\nSent:\nTuesday, January 27, 2026 1:18:21 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nFederal Court Upholds Constitutionality of LPR Technology\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\nI’m writing to share an important legal update regarding license plate\nrecognition (LPR) technology following a federal court decision issued today\nin Schmidt v. City of Norfolk, a Fourth Amendment challenge involving the\nCity of Norfolk’s use of LPRs.\nThe court upheld the constitutionality of license plate reader\ntechnology as used by the City of Norfolk, dismissing the plaintiffs’ claims.\nThis is a significant ruling. As the judge said,\n“Despite Plaintiff’s counsel’s effective advocacy, the Court must conclude\nthat that the limited number of photographs available on a 21-day rolling\nbasis from 75 camera track clusters in Norfolk does not ‘track’ the whole\nof a person's movements nor does it provide an ‘intimate’ window into\nwhere citizens drive, park, visit, linger, sleep, or patronize.”\nImportantly, the court’s decision aligns with strong national precedent. It\nrecognizes key distinctions between license plate reader technology and\nother systems that require a warrant, affirming what courts across the\ncountry have consistently found: when used responsibly and lawfully, LPR\ntechnology does not constitute continuous surveillance and is constitutional.\nThe court also left open the door to future suits on future facts, so we all must\nremain diligent to operate LPRs with good policy and within the confines of\nthe law.\nFor your department, the practical impact is continuity. Law enforcement\nagencies may continue to use LPRs - and the associated functionality within\nFlock’s system - without a warrant, consistent with existing law and policy.\nThere is no change to service, operations, or partnership as a result of this\n\nruling.\nWe recognize the gravity of cases like this and remain deeply committed to\nthoughtful, lawful use of LPR technology. Our focus continues to be\nsupporting public safety agencies with tools that respect constitutional\nboundaries, reflect best practices, and stand up to legal scrutiny.\nAt the same time, we expect the plaintiffs to appeal. And we are prepared to\ndefend this ruling as the process continues and will keep you informed of any\nmaterial developments. As always, we value your leadership and partnership,\nand we appreciate the responsibility that comes with deploying these tools in\nservice of your communities.\nIf you have questions or would like to discuss the decision in more detail,\nplease don’t hesitate to reach out.\nRespectfully,\nChris Colwell\nSVP, Customer Experience\n\nFlock Safety\n1170 Howell Mill Rd NW, Suite 210\nAtlanta, Georgia 30318, United States","pdf":null},"e0851":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0851","title":"Upcoming Webinar _ 2_5_2026 _ Overnight Users","frm":"Heather Ouellette","date":"2026-02-02","text":"From:\nHeather Ouellette\nSent:\nMonday, February 2, 2026 11:15:04 AM\nTo:\nBcc:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nUpcoming Webinar / 2/5/2026 / Overnight Users\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:Flock Safety Webinar After Dark.pdf ;\n\nGood Morning!\nYou may have already seen an email from my colleague about this, but I wanted to get it to you directly as well.\n\nTHIS THURSDAY from 0200-0300 we will be hosting a live webinar on New Search. As the legacy version\ncontinues to sunset, it is critical that all users understand how to use the New Search UI and this webinar can\ndirectly help with that. To target those specifically on night shift, we will be hosting this webinar at a time that\nworks best for them. The burden cannot land solely on you to get the entire agency up to speed -- this is how we\nhelp.\n\nPlease send this email to your entire agency (or at least those on night shift) so that every user has the\nopportunity to learn and participate. This one hour session will be beneficial for every user, no matter their tenure\nusing Flock.\n\nWhen: This Thursday 02/05/2026 , 2am - 3am\nRegistration Link\nFlyer Attached with QR code\nBest,\nHeather\n--\nHeather Ouellette\nCustomer Success Manager\n 470-852-3342\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e1079":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1079","title":"Flock Safety Webinars_ Enhance Your Proficiency with Flock Safety","frm":"Myron Maret","date":"2026-02-05","text":"From:\nMyron Maret\nSent:\nThursday, February 5, 2026 5:06:57 PM\nTo:\nJoe Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nFlock Safety Webinars| Enhance Your Proficiency with Flock Safety\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nHello,\nWe are pleased to announce our schedule of webinars throughout February and March, designed to\nmaximize your utilization of the Flock Safety platform.\nPlease review the schedule below and register for the sessions most pertinent to your role and needs:\nFebruary Webinars\nRole Management (Administrator Focus)\nThis session provides an in-depth examination of role management, specifically tailored for\nthe Administrator user. Attendees will gain a comprehensive understanding of creating\nroles, common role classifications, features frequently enabled at the role level, the process\nof adding networks to roles, and how to initiate share requests.\nDate & Time: February 10, 2026, at 2:00 PM EST\nRegistration Link: Register Here\nSharing and Filters (Administrator Focus)\nThis webinar will offer a high-level overview of Flock’s sharing framework and introduce the\nnewest enhancements to our sharing and filtering security protocols.\nDate & Time: February 19, 2026, at 2:00 PM EST\nRegistration Link: Register Here\nFlock Safety Solving Cases with Live Video and LPR (All Users)\nEncourage investigative use of Live Video in conjunction with LPR. Users will gain an\nunderstanding of how to use the features of the VMS tab and hear about success stories\ninvolving live video and LPR.\nDate & Time: February 25, 2026\nRegistration Link: Register Here\nMarch Webinars\nSharing and Filters (Administrator Focus)\nThis session will provide a comprehensive overview of Flock’s sharing framework and\nintroduce the latest updates to our sharing and filtering security protections.\nDate & Time: March 3, 2026, at 2:00 PM EST\n\nClick here to unsubscribe from this list or manage your preferences here.\nRegistration Link: Register Here\nFlockOS: An In-Depth Analysis of Real-Time Features (FlockOS, All Users)\nThis webinar will overview the new features and functionality enhancements implemented\nwithin FlockOS, including the selection tool, the response planner, and the utilization of\nzones.\nDate & Time: March 11, 2026\nRegistration Link: Register Here\nRole Management (Administrator Focus)\nThis deep-dive session on role management is specifically structured for the Administrator\nuser. Attendees will depart with a solid comprehension of role creation, common role\nprofiles, features typically enabled at the role level, methods for adding networks to roles,\nand procedures for submitting share requests.\nDate & Time: March 24, 2026, at 2:00 PM EST\nRegistration Link: Register Here\nIt remains our commitment to continuously provide webinar-based training on diverse topics, ensuring that\nall users, regardless of their specific role, have the opportunity to participate and enhance their skills\nThank you,\nFlock Safety | Customer Success\nsupport@flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0270":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0270","title":"Welcome to the Flock Newsletter_ What's In Flight _ Feb 2026","frm":"Chris at Flock Safety","date":"2026-02-10","text":"From:\nChris at Flock Safety\nSent:\nTuesday, February 10, 2026 10:37:50 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nWelcome to the Flock Newsletter: What's In Flight | Feb 2026\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nFlock Newsletter:\nWhat's In Flight\nEDITOR’S NOTE | FEBRUARY 2026\nYou’re reading the very first edition of our monthly Flock Safety\nnewsletter — a brand new resource created to empower you and your\ncommunity. We’re launching this newsletter with a clear purpose: to\nput the latest solved stories, breakthrough product updates, and\nactionable insights right at your fingertips, so you can lead with\nconfidence and make a real impact on public safety.\n\nWATCH THE PRESS CONFERENCE\nBut don’t let these updates stop with you! The more we spread\nthese stories and tools, the greater our collective impact.\nForward this email to your city council, include highlights in your\ncommunity newsletters, and share it with anyone who cares about\nbuilding safer, stronger neighborhoods.\nLet’s set the standard for transparency, action, and community\npartnership — together.\n— Chris Colwell, SVP, Customer Experience\nSOLVED STORIES\nFinding the Brown University Shooter\nIn a high-profile case connected to Brown University and MIT,\ninvestigators used Flock LPR and Freeform (an AI-powered feature that\nlets you search across LPR images and integrated video using plain\nlanguage) to rapidly identify a suspect vehicle, trace it to a rental\nagency, and confirm the individual’s identity.\n\u0000 RELATED: Cambridge cut ties with Flock Safety. Days later, an MIT\n\nprofessor was killed — and the suspect was found using Flock's tech.\nFlock, and the LPR was able to provide us with this\ndescription of this vehicle. Through that, the agents\nand their work were able to get us footage of this\nindividual as well as a copy of the agreement, which\nprovided his real name.\"\nOscar Perez, Police Chief, Providence PD\nSOLVED STORIES\nReducing Response Times to Gun Violence\nOur gunshot detection technology can be used to reduce response\ntimes to calls of gun violence. Read more here how Greenville,\nMississippi, our first Safe City in Mississippi, used it to apprehend their\nsuspect.\nFor more information on how gunshot detection technology can be\nused in your community, reach out to us here.\nSolving a Double Homicide in Michigan\nShelby Township Police Department used automated license plate\nrecognition to help solve a double homicide at a local car dealership.\nThe outcome reinforced how timely, objective data supports\naccountability and confidence in investigative decisions.\nRead more here about how our ALPR cameras played a pivotal role in\nsolving a double homicide at a car dealership in Shelby Township,\nMichigan.\n\nGarrett hosts office hours with Chiefs to\nhear what’s working and where agencies\nwant to go next, keeping leadership\nvoices central to how we support\nagencies. Register for his Q&A sessions\nby clicking here. New times will be added\nas they become available.\nREGISTER FOR OFFICE HOURS\nOur External Affairs team partners with\nagencies on public records, legislation,\nand community concerns. Chiefs and\ncommand staff can email\ncommunity@flocksafety.com for support\non upcoming votes, media, and\ni\nMAKING A DIFFERENCE\nLEADERSHIP & COMMUNITY MOMENTS\nGarrett’s Direct Conversations with Chiefs\nExternal Affairs Support and Direct Access\n\ntransparency planning.\nOffense Type Selection for Searches\nWe now require an Offense Type from a prefilled dropdown for\nevery search. Before running a search, users are required to\nselect an offense type from a NIBRS-based list. For more\ninformation on this change, please visit our blog post here.\nClearer Explanations for Audit Records\nWe’ve added clear disclaimer text to explain what information\nmeans when customers or the public see records with ***. This\nmessage clarifies that the information does exist, but is\nintentionally only visible to the searching agency.\nSelf-Serve MFA Reset for Administrators\nAgency administrators can now reset multi-factor\nauthentication for users without contacting support. Click here\nto learn more about how you can do this.\nAgency-Level Control for Federal Data\nSharing\nAgencies can now decide, at the agency level, whether they\nreceive data-sharing requests from federal partners. To see\nhow, watch a quick video here.\nPRODUCT UPDATES\nLOG IN TO YOUR ACCOUNT TO VIEW CHANGES\n\nNEWS & EVENTS\nWashington State Update\nA win for agencies using Flock everywhere.\nA recent decision from the Pierce County Superior Court (Rodriguez v.\nCity of Lakewood) brings welcome clarity for agencies using license\nplate recognition (LPR) technology.\nIn its ruling, the court found that LPR data stored in the cloud is not\nsubject to disclosure under Washington’s Public Records Act (PRA). This\nrepresents an important and positive step forward for agencies relying\non LPR to support public safety.\nOakland & San Diego City Council Support\n\nOakland and San Diego City Councils overwhelmingly renew Flock\ncontracts with a 6-3 vote in San Diego and a 7-1 vote in Oakland. If you\nwould like a Flock representative to engage with your elected leaders\nahead of a vote, reach out here.\n\u0000\nREAD: Oakland NAACP endorses Flock as a tool to reduce both bias and\ncrime\nCLOSING NOTE\nWe recognize the critical role you play and the trust your community\nplaces in you. Our commitment is to equip you with the tools,\ntransparency, and support that help drive real outcomes and strengthen\npublic confidence. We’re proud to partner with agencies leading the way\nin modern public safety.\nIf you have ideas on how we can make this newsletter even more\nimpactful, share your feedback here.\nRESOURCES\nGet Hands-On Platform Training in Flock Academy\nKeep Your Transparency Portal Up to Date\n\nKeep Your Transparency Portal Up to Date\nShare a Solved Story from Your Community\nConnect with Flock’s External Affairs Team\nUse Your Community Engagement Toolkit\n\nFlock Safety\n1170 Howell Mill Rd NW, Suite 210\nAtlanta, Georgia 30318, United States","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0270.pdf"},"e0656":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0656","title":"P#11 May River Rd EB @ BPD Substation","frm":"Flock Safety Support","date":"2026-02-27","text":"From:\nFlock Safety Support\nSent:\nFriday, February 27, 2026 9:46:58 AM\nTo:\ncclarkson@townofbluffton.com\nCc:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com; rfazekas@townofbluffton.com; michael.holub@flocksafety.com\nSubject:\nRE: P#11 May River Rd EB @ BPD Substation\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi there,\n\nThank you for letting us know. I will inform the Camera Engineers so it is notated.\n\nI have also deactivated Christian Gonzalez from our internal database for your organization. I apologize for any inconvenience.\n\nStay safe,\nDani\n\n--------------- Original Message ---------------\nFrom: Clarkson, Constance [cclarkson@townofbluffton.com]\nSent: 2/24/2026, 11:06 AM\nTo: support@flocksafety.com\nCc: jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com; michael.holub@flocksafety.com; rfazekas@townofbluffton.com\nSubject: RE: P#11 May River Rd EB @ BPD Substation\nGood morning Dani.  P#11 is not currently powered.  An engineered electrical plan is being designed to provide power\nto the device. It will be powered by May 2026.\n\nRyan, as a side note, you may want to update the Town’s contact information with Flock Support.  They had C Gonzales\nstill as a contact and they didn’t have you.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\n\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Flock Safety Support <support@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Tuesday, February 24, 2026 10:39 AM\nTo: Babkiewicz, Joseph <jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com>; Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>;\ncgonzales@townofbluffton.com\nSubject: P#11 May River Rd EB @ BPD Substation\n\nHi there,\nWe are reaching out regarding P#11 May River Rd EB @ BPD Substation. During a recent review of device performance, our\nteam identified that the equipment has not been receiving consistent power.\nTo ensure we have an action plan, we’ll need you to confirm power is flowing by checking the power box. Could you please\ncheck the equipment and confirm once this has been completed?\nThank you very much for your assistance, and we apologize for any inconvenience this may cause. I hope to hear from you soon.\n\nStay safe,\nDani\nthread::n58l_2NxKm-zDencTRfthQ4::\n\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to support+unsubscribe@flocksafety.com.","pdf":null},"e0271":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0271","title":"Welcome to the Flock Newsletter_ What's In Flight _ March 2026","frm":"Chris at Flock Safety","date":"2026-03-10","text":"From:\nChris at Flock Safety\nSent:\nTuesday, March 10, 2026 10:22:22 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nWelcome to the Flock Newsletter: What's In Flight | March 2026\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nTo view this email as a web page, click here\nFlock Newsletter:\nWhat's In Flight\nEDITOR’S NOTE | MARCH 2026\nOur goal with this newsletter is simple: to provide a consistent,\ntransparent line of communication between Flock and the agencies we\nserve.\n\nEach edition brings together real-world solved stories, meaningful\nproduct updates, and important policy developments, all in one place!\nWe want you to have clear visibility into how the technology is truly\nbeing used, how it’s evolving based on your feedback, and how\nagencies across the country are seeing measurable impact in their\ncommunities. We also aim to demonstrate accountability and ethical\nuse of the technology.\nThis is designed to be a valuable resource—please share it freely\nwith your entire team, your city council members, and your\ncommunity.\nTransparency builds trust. Shared knowledge strengthens public safety.\n— Chris Colwell, SVP, Customer Experience\nNEW BUNDLES\nExpansion, Built Around Your Priorities\nAgencies face different challenges. That’s why we created three\npurpose-built solutions designed around how you operate and scale.\nWhether you’re focused on response speed, investigative efficiency, or\nmaximizing the tools you already use, we’ve built each solution with that\nin mind.\n\nLEARN MORE\nSAFE CITY SPOTLIGHT\nGreenville, MS, Sees 60% Drop in Violent\nCrime Following Safe City Deployment\nGreenville, MS became the first Safe City in the state with full\ndeployment in just 90 days — including 262 live audio detection\ndevices and 100% user certification (which can be completed through\nFlock Academy). Within that same window, the department cleared its\nfirst homicide, locating the suspect while still on scene thanks to rapid\nalerts. In less than a year, violent crime is down 60%.\n\u0000 WANT TO TURN YOUR CITY INTO A SAFE CITY?\nLEARN MORE\nWith effective training, prosecutions will actually\nhappen — and that’s what will make a difference\nErrick Simmons, Mayor, City of Greenville\nin response to Flock's training experience\nSOLVED STORIES\nFlock Safety Network Helps Stop Multi-State\nMurder Suspect Within 24 Hours\nWithin 24 hours of a triple homicide in rural Utah, a stolen Subaru was\n\nREAD MORE SOLVED STORIES\nExtend LPR Coverage Without New\nHardware\nFlock’s Vehicle Detection Ingest API pulls detections from\nthird-party cameras into Flock—expanding coverage, lowering\nhardware costs, and speeding up alerts and investigations in\ntracked across four states and the armed suspect captured —\nbecause every agency was connected through the Flock Safety license\nplate reader network. Flock turned scattered leads into a single,\nlife\u0000saving trail.\nMulti\u0000County Coordination Leads to Swift\nArrest and Child Rescue\nAfter a homicide in Fulton County, Warner Robins PD used Flock\ncameras to locate the suspect vehicle in Houston County. A pursuit\nbegan when the driver failed to stop and ended in a crash near Hwy 96.\nOfficers discovered an uninjured child inside the vehicle. The case was\nthen turned over to Houston County authorities.\nMAKING A DIFFERENCE\nPRODUCT UPDATES\n\none platform. Learn how to get started.\nEnhance Transparency with Greater\nControl\nUpdates to the Transparency Portal allow agencies to display\nLPR-only camera counts, align public records with accurate\nNetwork Counts, and publish or unpublish their portal to keep\ninformation clear, consistent, and up to date.\nClearer Standards, Seamless Access\nA new login disclaimer reinforces CJIS compliance and clearly\noutlines authorized use requirements, including immigration and\nreproductive care laws in certain states. It replaces existing\npop-ups and one-offs without adding friction or changing login\nprotocols.\nGarrett's Office Hours are open for\nregistration, offering space for candid\ndialogue on public safety outcomes,\naccountability, and trust—ensuring\nleadership perspectives continue to shape\nhow we support agencies. Check back as\nnew times will be added soon.\nREGISTER FOR GARRETT'S Q&A\nIn early February, Chris hosted virtual\ndt bl\nith l\nf\nt\nLOG IN TO YOUR ACCOUNT TO VIEW CHANGES\nLEADERSHIP & COMMUNITY MOMENTS\nGarrett’s Direct Conversations with Chiefs\nChris Colwell, SVP of Customer Experience\n\nroundtables with law enforcement\nleaders to discuss what’s working and\nwhere we can improve. Key themes\nincluded clearer inter-agency data\nsharing, better visibility into policy\ncompliance, and appreciation for open\ndialogue. We also highlighted the\nTransparency Portal and shared solved\nstories. Leaders asked to continue the\nforum regularly.\nREAD MORE ABOUT FLOCK GUARDRAILS\nNEWS & EVENTS\nEast Palo Alto Mayor Clarifies Flock\nGuardrails\nWe know transparency and trust are essential for public safety\ntechnology. East Palo Alto Vice Mayor Mark Dinan recently shared how\nFlock is used in his community, including confirming ICE does not use\nFlock for immigration enforcement. Read his full perspective here.\nNew Mexico Senate Passes Driver Privacy &\nSafety Act (SB 40)\n\nLast month, the New Mexico House of Representatives approved the\nDriver Privacy and Safety Act (SB 40), sending the landmark ALPR bill to\nthe governor for signature. The bill represents extensive negotiations\nbetween law enforcement, Flock, and the ACLU, and provides a\nframework that establishes guardrails for ALPR data sharing while\npreserving the efficacy of this critical public safety tool.\nWEBINARS\nUpcoming Success Webinars:\nFlockOS: Deep Dive of the Real-Time Features | March 11th\nRole Management | March 24th\nWeekly Training Webinars:\nLaw Enforcement User Training | Mondays at 11am ET\nLaw Enforcement Admin Training | Tuesdays at 11am ET\nCLOSING NOTE\nWe recognize the critical role you play and the trust your community\nplaces in you. Our commitment is to equip you with the tools,\ntransparency, and support that help drive real outcomes and strengthen\npublic confidence. We’re proud to partner with agencies leading the way\nin modern public safety.\nIf you have ideas on how we can make this newsletter even more\nimpactful, share your feedback here.\nRESOURCES\nGet Hands-On Platform Training in Flock Academy\nKeep Your Transparency Portal Up to Date\nShare a Solved Story from Your Community\n\nShare a Solved Story from Your Community\nConnect with Flock’s External Affairs Team\nUse Your Community Engagement Toolkit\n\nFlock Safety\n1170 Howell Mill Rd NW, Suite 210\nAtlanta, Georgia 30318, United States","pdf":null},"e0272":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0272","title":"Update on Federal Law Enforcement Collaboration and Local Control","frm":"Chris at Flock Safety","date":"2026-03-23","text":"From:\nChris at Flock Safety\nSent:\nMonday, March 23, 2026 9:04:17 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nUpdate on Federal Law Enforcement Collaboration and Local Control\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nDear Chief Babkiewicz,\nWe are writing to share an important update regarding Flock Safety’s work\nwith federal law enforcement agencies, a necessary extension of our mission\nto help communities stay safe while earning and keeping public trust.\nWe understand that you face a daily reality where violent offenders do not\nrespect jurisdictional boundaries. Recent high-stakes incidents underscore\nthat in cases involving active fugitives, missing persons, or serious violent\ncrime, coordination across city, county, and state lines is critical, and time is\nof the essence.\nWe have published a detailed blog post (which you can read here) that\nexplains the principles guiding our work with federal agencies.\nIf you do not currently share with federal agencies, the default setting is that\nyou are undiscoverable to any federal agencies. If you would like to change\nthat, you must proactively log into Flock and adjust your settings.\nPlease be aware that clients who are currently sharing with federal law\nenforcement agencies, or who enable federal sharing in response to this\nmessage, may receive a data sharing request from the FBI in the coming\ndays. If you receive one, please review and approve or deny the request at\nyour earliest convenience. You can reach out to me with any questions.\nBelow are the key takeaways from this update:\nOur Mission Remains the Same: Safety and Civil Liberties\n\nFrom day one, Flock was designed to balance public safety needs with civil\nliberties. This principle guides our entire system:\nPurpose-Built: Focused on public safety, not generalized monitoring.\nLocal Ownership: Data is owned and controlled exclusively by local\nagencies, not a centralized database.\nAccountability: Built-in audit logs, access controls, and default limited\ndata retention ensure transparency and responsible use.\nPrincipled Collaboration with Federal Law Enforcement\nTo address how crime moves faster than jurisdictions, while acknowledging\nthe reality of state and local sharing restrictions, we are reiterating our\ncompliance features, built on the same foundation of transparency and\naccountability we’ve committed to you.\nWe never compromise on local control:\nPrinciple\nDetail\nLocal Control\nReigns\nSupreme\nFlock data belongs solely to the agency that owns the\ncameras. There is no backdoor access. Any sharing\nmust be explicitly permission-based and opt-in by\nthe local agency.\nDefault:\nUndiscoverable\nOur default setting is to make ALL local police\nagencies undiscoverable by federal law\nenforcement within the Flock system.\nThe \"Three\nGates\" for\nSharing\nFor a local agency to establish a sharing relationship\nwith federal law enforcement, three steps must be\ntaken:\n1. Local agency explicitly allows federal law\nenforcement to discover their presence (Off by\ndefault).\n2. Federal law enforcement must then request\naccess.\n3. The local agency must then accept the request.\n\nNote: This process is specifically for initiating new\ndata-sharing relationships with federal agencies. It\ndoes not alter or supersede any existing data-sharing\nagreements you already have with federal agencies.\nCustomers who already have a federal sharing\nrelationship in place are not affected by the 'default\noff' setting.\nLegitimate\nPublic-Safety\nUse\nUse is strictly tied to legitimate public-safety objectives\n(serious crimes, active threats, etc.). Every search is\nlogged with an associated NIBRS-based offense type.\nThis principled integration is the responsible path forward. It ensures that\nessential tools are available when coordination saves lives, while maintaining\nthe strictest guardrails and upholding your full control over your data.\nWe remain committed to our guiding principles: Safety with limits, human\njudgment always, auditable by design, transparency earns trust, and Local\ncontrol, without qualification or condition. We encourage you to read the\nfull blog post for a deeper understanding of our commitments. Thank you for\nyour partnership in keeping our communities safe.\nSincerely,\nChris Colwell\nSVP, Customer Experience\n\nFlock Safety\n1170 Howell Mill Rd NW, Suite 210\nAtlanta, Georgia 30318, United States","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0272.pdf"},"e0855":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0855","title":"Flock Impact Census","frm":"Heather Ouellette","date":"2026-03-26","text":"From:\nHeather Ouellette\nSent:\nThursday, March 26, 2026 2:55:25 PM\nTo:\nBcc:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nFlock Impact Census\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nApologies if you have been receiving more emails than normal from me and my team lately. I wanted to bump one in particular, in\ncase it got buried: the Flock Impact Census survey. You should have received an email over the last few weeks titled \"Invitation:\n2025 Flock Impact Census.\"\nIn short, we're asking agencies to participate in the survey so we can quantify outcomes like arrests, recoveries, and case\nsupport. We use this data to support your success reporting, council conversations, and renewals.\nI'm reaching out to quickly note that 1. the email is legitimate and from a member of the Flock team and 2. notify you that if you\ndo not see it in your inbox, the emails will be resent on Monday with the survey link. Keep in mind the survey closes on April 7th.\nThanks for all you do!\nHeather\n--\nHeather Ouellette\nCustomer Success Manager\n 470-852-3342\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0855.pdf"},"e0273":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0273","title":"How to Answer Council & Community Questions on Sharing, Access, and Audits","frm":"Chris at Flock Safety","date":"2026-03-30","text":"From:\nChris at Flock Safety\nSent:\nMonday, March 30, 2026 4:32:46 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nHow to Answer Council & Community Questions on Sharing, Access, and Audits\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\nAcross the country, many of you are getting questions from council\nmembers, city attorneys, and community stakeholders about how Flock\nhandles federal access, data sharing, and audit logs. None of this is new\npolicy, but we know having simple, ready-to-share language is often just\nas important as the underlying controls.\nBelow is a short Q&A you can share directly with your council or other\noversight bodies. You can forward this email as-is, or copy/paste the section\nbelow into your own memo, packet, or slide deck.\nCouncil Members,\nWe’ve heard questions about how our Flock system handles data sharing and\naudit logs. We want to share a clear, concise summary you can rely on and\nreuse in conversations with constituents.\nQ&A: How Our Flock Sharing and Audit Logs Work\n1. Can federal agencies see our Flock data by default? (If you are in\nCalifornia or Virginia, due to state law, this question does not apply\nto your agency. All Federal sharing is disabled by default in CA and\nVA).\nNo. Federal agencies and other outside organizations cannot see our\ndata by default. Our agency is unable to receive Sharing Requests from\nfederal agencies unless we choose to allow it. We control if, when,\nand with whom we share, and we can turn sharing off or revoke it at\nany time.\n\n2. Can other law enforcement agencies or organizations access our\nFlock cameras or data without our knowledge?\nNo. Other law enforcement agencies or organizations cannot access\nour Flock cameras or data without our knowledge. By default, our\nagency is defaulted to only be discoverable for sharing at the 50-mile\nand Statewide radius and no one outside our organization can see our\ncameras or data unless we accept a sharing request from them. This\ndiscoverability only means we can receive requests from them and then\nchoose how to respond.\nAccess is only possible if either of the following things are true:\n1. We choose to allow auto-approvals for local and state\nagencies for certain access.\n2. We explicitly review and approve a specific sharing request\nfrom another agency or organization.\nWe decide if, when, and with whom we share. We can turn sharing off\nat any time or revoke sharing with any agency or organization we\npreviously approved.\n3. How does a new federal sharing relationship get created, and does\nthis change existing agreements?\nBecause of the extra sensitivity around federal sharing, there are extra\ncontrols. To start any new federal sharing relationship, three things must\nhappen:\n1. We turn on the ability for a federal agency to send us a\nsharing request (off by default).\n2. They request access.\n3. We approve the request.\nIf we don’t approve it, they don’t get access. These defaults do not\nchange or cancel any existing federal MOUs or agreements we\nhave already put in place; they mainly govern new relationships\ngoing forward.\n4. Does Flock work with DHS or ICE/CBP, or sell them our data?\nNo. Flock does not contract with DHS agencies, does not sell or\nshare data with DHS, and has no relationship with ICE or CBP. More\ndetail:\nhttps://www.flocksafety.com/blog/does-flock-share-data-with-\nice\nhttps://www.flocksafety.com/privacy-ethics\n5. Is there a “backdoor,” or can Flock quietly change the logs?\n\nNo. There is no backdoor access for any agency. Audit logs are\ndesigned to be complete, transparent, and reviewable. Entries are\nwritten automatically, retained for oversight, and cannot be quietly\nedited or overwritten; changes to sharing or settings appear as\nseparate events, not hidden modifications.\n6. What do our Flock audit logs capture, and are searches justified?\nOur audit tools capture who searched, when, what they searched,\nwhich agency they’re from, and the associated offense type,\ncreating a record we can review and, if needed, share with appropriate\noversight bodies. Searches are tied to a standardized NIBRS-based\noffense type, so there is a clear public-safety justification documented\nfor every search. In Network Audits, certain sensitive fields from\noutside agencies (such as officer names, specific plates, case numbers,\nand some search filters) are masked for safety, while full details for our\nown users remain visible in our Organization Audit logs.\n7. How is accidental or unauthorized federal access being prevented\ngoing forward?\nFlock has implemented stricter sharing settings, permanent logging\nof sharing changes, NIBRS-based justifications, and state-specific\nguardrails (for example, in certain states, such as CA and VA, sharing\nwith federal agencies is completely disabled and cannot be turned on or\nconfigured otherwise). Details:\nhttps://www.flocksafety.com/blog/flock-implements-enhanced-\nguardrails-across-california-to-ensure-lawful-and-responsible-\nuse-of-lprs\nhttps://www.flocksafety.com/blog/does-flock-share-data-with-\nice\n8. Has Flock been “breached,” and why do I keep hearing that it has?\nNo. The recent concerns agencies are hearing are not the result of a\nsuccessful hack or compromise of Flock’s platform or cloud\nenvironment. The “breach” narrative you may see in YouTube videos,\nblogs, or on social media usually collapses several different things\ntogether, like FOIA releases of audit logs, historical\nsharing/configuration issues, how Network Audits appear when\nexported, and policy debates about federal access, and then labels all of\nthat as a “breach,” even though it is not a successful cyberattack. In at\nleast one widely circulated video, a camera was illegally removed from\nservice and taken off the network before it was probed, which is very\ndifferent from an attacker breaking into an active, in-service device.\nWhen issues are identified, Flock addresses them through product\nchanges, guardrails, and direct communication with affected agencies,\nnot because attackers gained unauthorized access to your data.\n\nIn addition, we’ve put together a few short videos that walk through common\nquestions we hear from council members and community stakeholders.\nThese can be helpful to share directly or to use as a quick reference ahead of\nmeetings:\nWhat Flock License Plate Readers Actually Do (and What They\nDon’t)\nA clear overview of what LPR technology captures, how it works, and\nthe boundaries of the system.\nInside a Flock LPR Search: How Investigators Actually Use the Tool\nA step-by-step look into how Flock LPR searches as conducted and\nhow results are interpreted.\nWho Can See Flock Data? How Sharing Controls and Audits Really\nWork\nAn explanation of access controls, approval workflows, and how audit\nlogs create transparency and accountability.\nOur goal is to ensure the technology we use is both effective for public safety\nand consistent with the expectations of our community and its elected\nleaders. If there are additional questions you are hearing, we’re glad to\naddress them and, where appropriate, add them to this Q&A.\nRespectfully,\n<Chief / Sheriff / Department Name>\nBest,\nChris Colwell,\nSVP, Customer Experience\n\nFlock Safety\n1170 Howell Mill Rd NW, Suite 210\nAtlanta, Georgia 30318, United States","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0273.pdf"},"e0253":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0253","title":"Attention_ NCIC Alert Issue on April 3, 2026","frm":"Chris at Flock","date":"2026-04-03","text":"From:\nChris at Flock\nSent:\nFriday, April 3, 2026 8:35:40 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nAttention: NCIC Alert Issue on April 3, 2026\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\nWe are writing to inform you of an issue that affected NCIC list alerts on\nApril 3, 2026.\nBetween 11:00 AM EDT and 12:09 PM EDT, a configuration error in our plate\nparsing system impacted how NCIC list matches were processed. As a result:\nSome alerts were generated for plates that were not actually on the\nNCIC list.\nDuring the same period, some valid NCIC hot plate alerts were not sent\nas expected.\nAt 12:09 PM EDT, we temporarily disabled NCIC list alerts while we\ninvestigated. At 1:12 PM EDT, we corrected the configuration issue and\nre\u0000enabled the NCIC source for all eligible users. We have also removed\ninvalid matches from alert history so they no longer appear as active NCIC\nhits in the Flock system.\nPlease note: email and SMS notifications that were sent before the issue\nwas resolved cannot be rescinded. If your agency took action based on\nNCIC alerts during this window, we recommend reviewing those incidents in\nline with your internal procedures and confirming status directly in NCIC\nwhere appropriate.\nThis issue is fully resolved, and NCIC list alerts are now functioning as\nexpected. We are reviewing our validation and monitoring processes to\neliminate the risk of similar issues in the future.\n\nIf you have questions about specific alerts or need assistance reviewing\nactivity from this timeframe, please contact support@flocksafety.com.\nThank you for your partnership and for all you do to keep your communities\nsafe.\nSincerely,\nChris Colwell\nSVP, Customer Experience\n\nFlock\n1170 Howell Mill Rd NW, Suite 210\nAtlanta, Georgia 30318, United States","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0253.pdf"},"e0254":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0254","title":"Welcome to the Flock Newsletter_ What's In Flight _ April 2026","frm":"Chris at Flock","date":"2026-04-07","text":"From:\nChris at Flock\nSent:\nTuesday, April 7, 2026 10:07:51 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nWelcome to the Flock Newsletter: What's In Flight | April 2026\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nTo view this email as a web page, click here\nFlock Newsletter:\nWhat's In Flight\nEDITOR’S NOTE | APRIL 2026\nWe’re excited to share April’s Newsletter with you! Engagement\ncontinues to grow and its clear these updates are reaching the right\nteams. Each edition highlights real-world solved stories, product\nupdates, and key policy developments— showing how the technology\n\nis evolving based on your feedback and making an impact in your\ncommunities.\nPlease continue sharing with your teams, leadership, and community.\nTransparency builds trust, and shared knowledge strengthens public\nsafety. We’d also love your feedback on what you’d like to see next\nby filling out this form.\n— Chris Colwell\nSVP, Customer Experience\n\u0000\nKnow someone who is interested in seeing these updates? Share this form so\nthey can subscribe to receive this newsletter.\nEVENTS\nGet Ready for Flock Forward 2026!\nYou’re invited to join us in Atlanta, GA from August 18–20, 2026, for\nthree days of cutting-edge innovation, exclusive insights, and essential\nconnections. Don't wait! Registration is live. Use code EARLYBIRD for a\n50% discount!\nStay tuned for the full agenda and exciting updates as we get closer to\nthe event.\n\nSAVE YOUR SPOT\nWATCH NOW\nDFR IN ACTION\nHow Corona PD Gets Immediate Eyes on\nScene\nThe Corona Police Department’s Drone as First Responder (DFR)\nprogram is reshaping how officers respond to calls for service.\nTwo\u0000thirds of the time, their Flock DFR drones beat patrol units to the\nscene, giving RTIC operators and pilots a real\u0000time view before officers\narrive.\nIn this new video, see how live aerial video, thermal imaging, and\nprecise location data help locate a baby locked in a hot car, guide fire\nand police responses, and capture critical evidence that leads to faster\nresponse times and better outcomes for the community.\nSOLVED STORIES\nFlock Technology, Dispatcher Skill Lead to\n\nSUBMIT YOUR CASES THROUGH THIS SHORT FORM\nStay on Top of Your Device Health\ni\ni\ni\nStolen Truck Recovery in an Hour\nLake County Sheriff’s 911 dispatchers played a critical role in the rapid\nrecovery of a stolen vehicle, using Flock LPR technology to locate a\ngrey Ford pickup without a license plate. Their real-time coordination\nhelped track the vehicle across multiple cameras, leading to its\nrecovery and the suspect’s apprehension within just one hour.\nFlock LPR and Inter-agency Takedown End\nWeeks-Long Crime Spree\nA joint operation between Pinecrest Police and the Miami-Dade Sheriff’s\nOffice led to the arrest of three suspects tied to a series of luxury auto\nthefts and residential burglaries. Using Flock LPR alerts, air support, and\ncoordinated ground units, agencies tracked and intercepted the vehicle.\nThe multi-jurisdiction crime spree was brought to an end in a single\nmorning, watch the video to see how.\nFLOCK ON-RECORD\nReal Stories, Real Impact: Help Us Tell Your\nCommunity’s Story\nWe’re working to elevate real stories of safety from your community. If\nyour agency has used Flock technology to help solve a crime, we’d\nlove to hear about it. Selected stories may be featured in a short,\ndocumentary-style piece (example) that includes perspectives from\nboth law enforcement and a community member directly impacted by\nthe case, helping to tell the full story of the outcome.\nPRODUCT UPDATES\n\nFlock admins can now check the status of LPR, video, and audio\ndevices in one place using the new device health page. Quickly\nidentify issues, track performance, and know your system is\nworking when you need it.\nEasily Spot Out-of-State Searches in Your\nAudits\nUse the new Network Audit filter to see only out-of-state\nsearches for any date range. Quickly confirm there’s no out-of-\nstate activity, or review the searches that did happen, across\nyour full audit history.\nYour VMS Called. You Might Want to\nAnswer.\nRahul got a midnight wake-up call from an old friend… Flock\nVMS. Turns out, it’s been busy. New alerts on the timeline,\nsmarter search, drone feeds, and more.  Watch the video to see\nwhat’s new and why your VMS just got a lot more useful\novernight.\nLOG IN TO YOUR ACCOUNT\nREGISTER FOR GARRETT's Q&A\nLEADERSHIP SERIES\nGarrett’s Office Hours with Chiefs\nA space for candid dialogue with law enforcement leaders on safety\noutcomes, accountability, and trust. Open for registration — check back\nas new times are added.\nSOCIAL\n\nTikTok\nFollow us\nInstagram\nFollow us\nStay Connected With Us - @flocksafety\nKeep updated on all things Flock and how we are shaping the future of\nsafety with communities across the U.S.\nNEWS & EVENTS\nMore Court Cases in Favor of LPR\nCourts across the country continue to affirmatively rule that LPRs can\nbe used without a warrant. Most recently, last week the 5th Circuit Court\nof Appeals held that individuals have no reasonable expectation of\nprivacy in their vehicle's location on public streets, and that use of ALPR\ndoes not violate any citizen's privacy ( US v. Porter, No 25-60163). Read\nmore here.\nMiami Dade Electronic Crimes Task Force\nPressure Tests Flock's Security\nThere's a lot of noise about Flock's security posture — but communities\ndeserve clarity not rumors Flock CISO Chris Castaldo traveled to\n\nREAD MORE\ndeserve clarity, not rumors. Flock CISO, Chris Castaldo, traveled to\nMiami to meet with the Miami Dade Sheriff's Electronic Crimes Task\nForce to discuss their independent findings about the security controls\non Flock's platform.\nCLOSING NOTE\nWe recognize the critical role you play and the trust your community\nplaces in you. Our commitment is to equip you with the tools,\ntransparency, and support that help drive real outcomes and strengthen\npublic confidence. We’re proud to partner with agencies leading the way\nin modern public safety.\nIf you have ideas on how we can make this newsletter even more\nimpactful, share your feedback here.\nRESOURCES\nGet Hands-On Platform Training in Flock Academy\nKeep Your Transparency Portal Up to Date\nShare a Solved Story from Your Community\nConnect with Flock’s External Affairs Team\nUse Your Community Engagement Toolkit\n\nFlock\n1170 Howell Mill Rd NW, Suite 210\nAtlanta, Georgia 30318, United States","pdf":null},"e0856":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0856","title":"Admin Webinar [Please Register] + Check In Meeting","frm":"Heather Ouellette","date":"2026-04-09","text":"From:\nHeather Ouellette\nSent:\nThursday, April 9, 2026 1:31:39 PM\nTo:\nBcc:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nAdmin Webinar [Please Register] + Check In Meeting\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nI hope you’ve had a good week! I'm thankful the pollen has gotten better and the weather is warming up.\nI have two quick requests:\nPlease register for 1 of the Admin Webinars listed below\nSchedule a separate check-in meeting with me (or send your availability)\nFor the Admin Webinar, pick whichever time works best with your schedule. You only need to sign up for one.\nI am co-hosting these webinars with one of my fellow CSMs (Jess -- who is great!) and multiple agencies will attend. This will be\nthe best and most efficient way for me to communicate recent admin updates, exciting platform changes, and best practices to\neveryone simultaneously. We will still meet for our regular check-in meetings to focus on your agency's specific needs, but please\ntry your best to attend one of these as well.\nPlease register for one of the following:\nWebinar Option 1: Thursday, April 16th, 11:30 AM — Registration Link\nWebinar Option 2: Wednesday, April 22nd, 1:30 PM — Registration Link\nIf you’re unable to attend either session live, you can still register to receive the recording afterward.\nWith the start of the new quarter, it's also a great time to schedule that check-in meeting. We will discuss agency-specific items,\ncover admin questions, align on any outstanding items from prior meetings, review account health, and focus on success metric\ntracking. You can use my scheduling link here to grab a time that works best for you, or let me know what day/time\nworks best and I will send an invite.\nBest,\nHeather\n\n--\nHeather Ouellette\nCustomer Success Manager\n 470-852-3342\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0857":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0857","title":"Free Audit Assistance Tool Now Available","frm":"Heather Ouellette","date":"2026-04-13","text":"From:\nHeather Ouellette\nSent:\nMonday, April 13, 2026 10:27:31 AM\nTo:\nJoe Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nNew: Free Audit Assistance Tool Now Available\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nClick here to unsubscribe from this list or manage your preferences here.\nHi there,\nI’m excited to reach out about a Flock feature we're rolling out to your organization: Audit Assistance.\nWe built this because we know how manual and time-consuming audit reviews can be today. With large volumes of data to sift\nthrough, it's easy for important details to get lost. Audit Assistance is an analytics tool that aggregates data already captured in your\nOrganization Audit, surfacing it in a more actionable, streamlined view - making compliance reviews faster and easier for your team.\nNo new data is collected; it is a new interface for seeing the same data already logged in your Organization Audit. For a description of\nwhat insights are available through Audit Assistance, our Auditing Best Practice Guide has additional information.\nIf your agency is in a state with broad public records laws, we'd recommend evaluating how a data-aggregation view like Audit\nAssistance is treated under those laws.\nThe tool is designed to help administrators understand organizational activity without being accusatory – think of it as an intelligent\nassistant that helps you stay on top of your oversight duties. To activate this new feature, those with admin privileges can navigate to\nyour organization settings in Flock and enable Audit Assistance, or reply to this email for assistance.\nHere are some resources to help you get started;\nAudit Assistance Help Article\n[Video] How Audit Assistance is helping improve transparency and accountability\nAs always, please feel free to reach out with any questions or concerns.\nBest regards,\nHeather Ouellette\nCustomer Success Manager\n\n flocksafety.com","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0857.pdf"},"e0858":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0858","title":"Admin Webinar Reminder [Registration Needed]","frm":"Heather Ouellette","date":"2026-04-17","text":"From:\nHeather Ouellette\nSent:\nFriday, April 17, 2026 12:32:26 PM\nTo:\nBcc:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nAdmin Webinar Reminder [Registration Needed]\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nI hope you've had a good week! I wanted to send a reminder about the Admin webinar coming up next Wednesday (4/22) at\n1:30pm. We hosted the first of these yesterday and have already received significant feedback on its value.\nHere is the link to register. I highly recommend signing up even if you can't join live because we'll send out the recording to all\nregistrants afterward for you to review on your own time. As a reminder, this will contain great information about new admin-\nspecific features, overall platform features, early access programs, and more. Let me know if there's anything I can do for you in\nthe meantime!\nBest,\nHeather\n--\nHeather Ouellette\nCustomer Success Manager\n 470-852-3342\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0255":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0255","title":"Join Flock CEO Garrett's Office Hours - Your Questions Answered","frm":"Chris at Flock","date":"2026-04-21","text":"From:\nChris at Flock\nSent:\nTuesday, April 21, 2026 10:03:48 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nJoin Flock CEO Garrett's Office Hours - Your Questions Answered\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\nWe’re excited to highlight an ongoing initiative that fosters open communication and provides an exclusive opportunity for\nour Chiefs and Sheriffs to connect directly with our CEO, Garrett.\nGarrett will be hosting monthly \"CEO Office Hours\" sessions, designed as an informal forum for you to ask any questions\nyou may have, share feedback, and hear insights from Garrett and other Chiefs and Sheriffs.\nWe currently have a few spots open in May.\nOffice Hours Details:\nHost: Garrett, CEO\nPurpose: An open Q&A and discussion forum for Chiefs and Sheriffs.\nFrequency: Monthly (at minimum)\nHow to Join: Please use this link going forward to see when we have available slots (Register Here)\nWe believe this direct line of communication will be invaluable, and we encourage you to sign up quickly as spots are\nlimited. In addition, our new Trust Hub is now live, giving you on-demand access to detailed information about our privacy,\nsecurity, and compliance practices here: Flock Trust Hub. We are committed to hosting a session every month going\nforward to ensure all Chiefs and Sheriffs have an opportunity to participate.\nWe look forward to your participation.\nBest regards,\nChris Colwell\nSVP, Customer Experience","pdf":null},"e0859":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0859","title":"Admin Webinar Today - Please Register","frm":"Heather Ouellette","date":"2026-04-22","text":"From:\nHeather Ouellette\nSent:\nWednesday, April 22, 2026 12:07:52 PM\nTo:\nBcc:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nAdmin Webinar Today - Please Register\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nThis is just a last minute reminder to register for the Admin Webinar today (4/22) at 1:30pm. We hosted the first of these last\nweek and received significant feedback on its value.  I highly recommend signing up even if you can't join live because\nwe'll send the recording to all registrants afterward for you to review at your convenience.\nHere is the link to register.  As a reminder, this will contain great information about new admin-specific features, overall\nplatform features, early access programs, and more.\nThank you,\nHeather\n--\nHeather Ouellette\nCustomer Success Manager\n 470-852-3342\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0860":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0860","title":"How to save hours auditing with Audit Assistance","frm":"Heather Ouellette","date":"2026-04-23","text":"From:\nHeather Ouellette\nSent:\nThursday, April 23, 2026 7:38:59 PM\nTo:\nJoe Babkiewicz\nSubject:\nHow to save hours auditing with Audit Assistance\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nClick here to unsubscribe from this list or manage your preferences here.\nHi there,\nReady to cut auditing time by hours? You’re invited to join our Audit Assistance Tool Webinar on Tuesday, April 28th, 2026 at 11\nAM EST to learn exactly how to take full advantage of our newest safety & compliance feature.\nIn this short session we’ll cover:\nWhat Audit Assistance is and how it works\nWhy we built it and the benefits for agencies and admins\nHow to explain the tool to city councils, community members, and internal stakeholders\nOperational and legal notes (data source and public-records considerations)\nLive Q&A\nThis free tool is designed to help surface atypical search patterns so that you can quickly review, mark, and escalate what actually\nmatters, while always assuming best intent.\nRegister here\nCan’t make it? Register anyways and we’ll send the recording.\nThanks,\nHeather Ouellette\nCustomer Success Manager\n\n flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e1165":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 1165","title":"Flock Safety Payment & Remittance Details - Please Review","frm":"dunning-noreply=flocksafety.com@sfmail.flocksafety.com","date":"2026-04-28","text":"From:\ndunning-noreply=flocksafety.com@sfmail.flocksafety.com on behalf of: Flock Safety\nSent:\nTuesday, April 28, 2026 11:49:00 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nFlock Safety Payment & Remittance Details - Please Review\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nThis is a friendly reminder of our payment remittance information. Please ensure\nthat all payments are sent to the appropriate address, depending on the payment\nmethod.\nACH / Electronic Payments\nBank Name:\nSilicon Valley Bank\nAccount Name:\nFlock Group Inc.\nAccount Number: 3302113966\nRouting Number: 121140399 / SVBKUS6S\nCheck Payments (Lockbox Address)\nFlock Group Inc.\nPO Box 121923\nDallas, TX 75312-1923\nAny payments received at an address other than the lockbox address listed\nabove may be returned to the sender.\nKindly include your invoice number or account number with all payments to\nensure they are applied correctly.\nIf you have any questions or need additional remittance information, please\ncontact us at Billing@flocksafety.com .","pdf":null},"e0256":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0256","title":"Meeting the Moment_ A Special Edition on Trust & Compliance","frm":"Chris at Flock","date":"2026-05-05","text":"From:\nChris at Flock\nSent:\nTuesday, May 5, 2026 10:06:11 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nMeeting the Moment: A Special Edition on Trust & Compliance\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nTo view this email as a web page, click here\nMay Newsletter:\nMeeting the\nMoment\nEDITOR’S NOTE | MAY 2026\n\nWelcome to this special edition focused on Trust & Compliance. Public\nsafety technology is under more scrutiny than ever and we’re meeting\nthat moment with transparency, accountability, and clear standards for\nresponsible use.\nInside, you’ll find how agencies are strengthening compliance,\nimproving auditability, and reinforcing confidence in their communities,\nalongside product updates that support secure, policy-aligned use.\nTo go deeper on the communication side, join me for an upcoming\nwebinar on how to effectively speak with city councils about\ntransparency, policy, and the role of technology in your community: \u0000\nRegister Here\n— Chris Colwell, SVP, Customer Experience\n      Sign Up for Garrett’s Office Hours\nwith Chiefs\nREGISTER FOR GARRETT's Q&A\nTRUST HUB\nCompliance Tool Center & Myths Vs. Facts\nHub\n\nLEARN MORE\nBuild trust with Flock’s Trust Hub. Explore our Compliance Tools center\nfor built-in guardrails, agency-controlled sharing, transparency\nportals, audit assistance, and 30-day data retention that keep every\nsearch accountable.\nThen visit Myths vs. Facts to see common concerns about ALPR,\nsurveillance, and data access answered in plain language.\nPRODUCT UPDATES\nAudit Assistance That Makes LPR Oversight\nManageable\nFlock’s new Audit Assistance Tool helps admins save time by flagging\nsearch activity that might be outside typical agency usage so it can be\nreviewed, making routine oversight faster, more consistent, and easier\nto explain, all at no extra cost.\nTRUST HUB\n\nProtecting civil liberties is foundational to\nhow Flock technology is designed and\nused, with built-in safeguards that limit\naccess to authorized users and make\nevery interaction accountable and\nreviewable.\nLearn more about our rights and\nsafeguards.\nData privacy is central to maintaining\npublic trust, so Flock systems are\ndesigned to minimize data collection,\nlimit retention, and restrict access to\nlegitimate investigative purposes.\nRead more about how we build privacy.\nSee the crime and usage trends that\nmatter most with Offense Type Analytics\n(early access), which helps you quickly\npull key stats, spot patterns, and monitor\nhow Flock is used.\nView the full article here: Offense Type\nReporting and Analytics Dashboard.\nTransparency and Oversight at the Core of\nPublic Safety\nPrivacy by Design Builds Public Trust\nSee the Trends That Matter Most\nSEE HOW WE PRACTICE TRUST\n\nControl Searches with Built-In Policy\nFilters\nOur Sharing Certification helps agencies build trust through\nsecure, compliant information sharing; giving teams the\nconfidence to collaborate responsibly while protecting access\nand accountability. \u0000\nEnroll Here\nSEE HOW WE PRACTICE TRUST\nSOLVED STORIES\nHistoric Drug Bust: TPD Seizes Nearly $1.8\nMillion in Narcotics, Arrests Large-Scale\nTrafficker\nWhat happened: Tallahassee PD seized nearly $1.8M in illegal\ndrugs, 6 firearms, and $30,000+ in cash during a months-long\nnarcotics investigation.\nHow they used Flock: Investigators combined historical hits,\nforecast analysis, and custom hot list alerts to pinpoint the right\ntime to act and safely serve a search warrant.\nImpact: Disrupted major trafficking activity, removed deadly drugs\nf\nth\nit\nd t\nth\nd\nbli\nt\nt th\nh\n\nCourt-Ready Image Exports from\nS\nh\nfrom the community, and strengthened public trust through\nfocused, accountable enforcement.\nLPR Hot List Alert Triggers Incident, Flock\nDFR Drone Locates and Captures Second\nFleeing Suspect\nWhat happened: A Flock hot list alert flagged a vehicle entering\nCastle Rock with a stolen plate, leading officers to two suspects\nwith felony warrants.\nHow they used Flock: Instead of a high-speed pursuit, officers\nused controlled tactics—including a tire deflation device and a\nFlock DFR—to safely locate and arrest the suspects.\nImpact: Enabled compliant, safety-first policing decisions,\nreduced risk to the public, and strengthened community trust in a\nfast-moving situation.\nPRODUCT UPDATES\n\nSearch\nDownloaded images from Flock Search now include a self-\nauthenticating certification, making evidence court-ready\nwithout extra steps. No need to return later for documentation.\nTransparency Portal Enhancements\nComing Soon\nThe Transparency Portal gives communities visibility into\npolicies, usage, and access rules. Explore the tool today to get\nfamiliar ahead of upcoming enhancements that will make it\neven easier to share information and strengthen public trust.\nControl Searches with Built-In Policy\nFilters\nDid you know you can block certain searches based on your\npolicy? Built-in filters prevent restricted searches from running\nat all, helping ensure compliance with local laws and sensitive\nuse case protections.\nLOG IN TO YOUR ACCOUNT\nCLOSING NOTE\nWe recognize the critical role you play and the trust your community\nplaces in you. Our commitment is to equip you with the tools,\ntransparency, and support that help drive real outcomes and strengthen\npublic confidence. We’re proud to partner with agencies leading the way\nin modern public safety.\nIf you have ideas on how we can make this newsletter even more\nimpactful, share your feedback here.\n\u0000\nKnow someone who is interested in seeing these updates? Share this form so\nthey can subscribe to receive this newsletter.\n\nRESOURCES\nFlock Academy Course Highlight: Sharing Certification\nGet Hands-On Platform Training in Flock Academy\nKeep Your Transparency Portal Up to Date\nShare a Solved Story from Your Community\nConnect with Flock’s External Affairs Team\nUse Your Community Engagement Toolkit\n\nFlock\n1170 Howell Mill Rd NW, Suite 210\nAtlanta, Georgia 30318, United States","pdf":null},"e0313":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0313","title":"Solar PTZ Request","frm":"Clarkson, Constance","date":"2026-06-03","text":"From:\nClarkson, Constance\nSent:\nWednesday, June 3, 2026 10:58:12 AM\nTo:\nAnabel Pozzi\nCc:\nFazekas, Ryan; Mike Holub; Taylor Ellison; Heather Ouellette; Babkiewicz, Joseph\nSubject:\nRe: Solar PTZ Request\nSensitivity:Normal\nThank you Anabel.\nChief and Capt. Please let me know if you need anything from me on this.\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\nFrom: Anabel Pozzi <anabel.pozzi@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Wednesday, June 3, 2026 10:55 AM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>; Heather Ouellette <heather.ouellette@flocksafety.com>\nCc: Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Mike Holub <michael.holub@flocksafety.com>; Taylor Ellison\n<taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: Solar PTZ Request\n\nHi Constance,\nI reviewed the camera counts by phase, and the confusion is likely coming from the rejected location in Phase 1.\nHere is the breakdown:\nPhase 1 shows 16 LPRs and 4 PTZs installed, with 1 rejected location. The opportunity called for 17 LPRs in this phase,\nso it appears that one LPR did not move forward.\nPhase 2 shows 13 LPRs and 19 PTZs installed. The opportunity called for 12 LPRs and 18 PTZs in this phase, so one\n\nadditional LPR and one additional PTZ were added here.\nNetting that out, the LPR count appears to wash overall, but the PTZ count ends up one over. Based on that, it appears an\nadditional PTZ was added that was not included in the original contracts.\nMy director, Taylor, has been in contact with the Chief, and we can bring this up, as you have identified an additional\nlocation that needs a solar PTZ.\nLet me know if you have any other questions.\nAnabel\nOn Tue, Jun 2, 2026 at 4:16 PM Anabel Pozzi <anabel.pozzi@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHi Constance,\nI am working with Heather about the unused camera slots. I will let you know once we complete our review.\nThank you!\nOn Tue, Jun 2, 2026 at 4:14 PM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nAnabel,\n\nWe won’t be meeting tomorrow, so please advise on the below as soon as possible this week so we can determine a\ndirection for the new pier location.\n\nWith the project so close to completion and a 6/30/26 deadline, feel free to email between the scheduled meetings\nso we can stay on target.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Mike Holub <michael.holub@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, June 1, 2026 3:06 PM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Anabel Pozzi <anabel.pozzi@flocksafety.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Solar PTZ Request\n\nFor full transparency, I'm unsure which items are on hold and which ones are not.  @Anabel Pozzi can you advise?\n\nMichael Holub\nProject Manager\nflocksafety.com\nmichael.holub@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Mon, Jun 1, 2026 at 1:36 PM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nAfternoon Mike.\n\nWe have a new location where we need a solar PTZ, New River Linear Trail pier.  Please advise of the unused\ncamera slots where we can allocate a solar PTZ to this location. In the alternative, please advise how else we can\nachieve a camera at the new location.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\n--\nAnabel Pozzi\nRegional Account Executive\nCall: 803-262-2019\nFlock Safety\nBook Time With Me\n--\nAnabel Pozzi\nRegional Account Executive\nCall: 803-262-2019\nFlock Safety\nBook Time With Me","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0313.pdf"},"e0350":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0350","title":"Flock _ Upcoming User Virtual Trainings in June","frm":"Flock Customer Success","date":"2026-06-04","text":"From:\nFlock Customer Success\nSent:\nThursday, June 4, 2026 9:16:16 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nFlock | Upcoming User Virtual Trainings in June\nSensitivity: Normal\n\nClick here to unsubscribe from this list or manage your preferences here.\nHello,\nWe would like to invite you to the upcoming user training webinars that are scheduled for June.\nYou are receiving this email as an administrator for your Flock system. Please feel free to\nforward to any of your users that you feel would also benefit from this training.\nWe look forward to seeing you there! If you’d like to see trainings on additional topics in the\nfuture, please reach out to myron@flocksafety.com\nSchedule:\nEnhanced LPR & Freeform Overview (Register Here)\nJune 10th, 3:00pm EST\nFlockOS for Real Time Users (Register Here)\nJune 18th, 1:00pm EST\nNew Search Overview and Updates (Register Here)\nJune 23rd, 2:30pm EST\nHotlist & Alerting Best Practices (Register Here)\nJune 25th, 1:00pm EST\n—\nFlock Safety | Customer Success\nsupport@flocksafety.com","pdf":null},"e0260":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0260","title":"Flock Monthly Newsletter_ Shaping Safety Together","frm":"Chris at Flock","date":"2026-07-07","text":"From:\nChris at Flock\nSent:\nTuesday, July 7, 2026 10:04:16 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nFlock Monthly Newsletter: Shaping Safety Together\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nTo view this email as a web page, click here\nJuly Newsletter:\nShaping Safety\nTogether\nEDITOR’S NOTE | JULY 2026\nWelcome to July’s Newsletter! Visibility and trust are at the heart of\neffective public safety. In this edition, you’ll get a first look at Flock\n\nAlpha, built to deliver clearer visibility when every second counts, and\nhear from Chief Information Security Officer Chris Castaldo as he\nanswers a critical question: What makes a public safety platform\nsecure?  From transparency and safeguards to accountability and trust,\nChris shares what agencies should expect from the technology they rely\non every day.\nPlease continue sharing with your teams, leadership, and community.\nTransparency builds trust, and shared knowledge strengthens public\nsafety. Have a solved story or feedback on what you'd like to see next?\nWe'd love to hear from you — share it here.\n— Chris Colwell, SVP, Customer Experience\n Sign Up for Garrett’s Office Hours with Chiefs &\nSheriffs\nREGISTER FOR GARRETT'S Q&A\nPLATFORM SECURITY\nMisinformation: Did Flock Get Hacked?\n\nLEARN MORE\nWATCH THE VIDEO + JOIN EARLY ACCESS\nFlock’s Chief Information Security Officer, Chris Castaldo, addresses\nrecent claims that Flock cameras were \"hacked\" and explains what\nactually happened. He also explores a broader challenge facing\npublic safety leaders: how do you know whether a technology\nprovider is actually secure? Learn what to look for beyond\nassurances, from independent audits and compliance standards to\naccess controls and incident response. Strong security programs make\nit clear how systems work, how data is protected, and what safeguards\nare in place.\nFLOCK ALPHA\nSee What Others Can’t with Flock Alpha\nIs that a weapon or a phone? Is that the suspect? What's the plate\nnumber? Get answers fast across your city, at any time of day, with\nFlock Alpha. With 800x zoom, 1080p thermal, and color night vision,\nAlpha turns uncertainty into clarity. Alpha sees what others can't and\ndelivers answers faster. Designed, assembled, and supported in the\nUSA. NDAA-compliant.\n\nTRUST & COMPLIANCE\nDeleted Means Deleted: How Flock Handles\nLicense Plate Data Retention\n“How do we know license plate data is actually deleted?” It is a fair\nquestion. Flock deletes data automatically based on each agency’s\nretention policy, with 30 days as the default. Automated lifecycle\ncontrols, independent audits, and audit logs help ensure policies are\nfollowed and data stays under local control.\n>> LEARN MORE\nWhen the Debate Ends: Why Cities Continue to\nChoose Safety and Privacy\nPublic scrutiny around safety technology is growing, and so are\nexpectations for privacy, transparency, and accountability. Across the\ncountry, cities are finding that effective public safety tools need clear\nsafeguards, including independent audits, access controls, data\nretention policies, and local oversight. Read how agencies are balancing\ninvestigative value with community trust.\n>> LEARN MORE\nEXPLORE THE TRUST HUB\nFLOCK FORWARD\nGet Ready for Flock Forward 2026!\nJoin us in Atlanta, GA from August 18–20th for three days of bold\nideas, practical insights and meaningful connections. Lock in your spot\n\ntoday!\nRegistration is live! Check out the agenda, breakout sessions, and more\nexciting updates as we get closer to the event. Take advantage of\nthe limited-time discount code SUMMERSPECIAL for 50% off.\nSee the Bigger Picture, Faster\nPRODUCT UPDATES\nThe new Sharing experience gives agencies a clearer view of who they\nshare with, what access exists today, and what additional opportunities\nmay be available to request. With organization-level visibility, improved\nfiltering, and streamlined management workflows, agencies can spend\nless time navigating sharing relationships and more time supporting\ninvestigations.\n>> EXPLORE NEW SHARING\nWhen crimes share the same MO, investigators may not have a suspect\nvehicle to start from. Multi-Geo Search (available with LPR Pro) now\nmakes it easier to connect related incidents to potential suspect\nvehicles, with grouped plate results, saved searches, and faster\nreview. Soon, an improved Convoy Search will add more case context\nwhen reviewing vehicles that may be tied to the same investigation.\n>> LEARN MORE ABOUT MULTI-GEO SEARCH\n>> LEARN MORE ABOUT CONVOY SEARCH\nFlockOS has a new look designed to help you stay focused on what matters\nmost. With a unified alerts rail, streamlined map controls, improved\nselection tools, and more map visibility, it's now easier to monitor\nactivity, investigate incidents, and maintain situational awareness.\n>> EXPLORE THE NEW FLOCKOS\nSOLVED STORIES\n\nSOLVED STORIES\nTerre Haute PD Utilizes Flock Technology to\nQuickly Apprehend Suspect in Sexual Battery\nCase\nAfter a report of sexual battery involving a juvenile, Terre Haute\ndetectives used Flock LPR to identify a vehicle tied to the case and\nlocate its last known area. Officers quickly converged and arrested the\nsuspect near a public playground.\n>> READ MORE\nPearland PD Arrests Serial Offender Targeting\nLocal Fitness Centers\nPearland PD connected locker thefts at local fitness centers to a larger\ntheft and fraud scheme across multiple Texas communities. Using Flock\nLPR alongside traditional investigative work, detectives identified\nkey evidence that helped stop the operation.\n>> READ MORE\nHow Effective is Flock?\n\n>> LEARN MORE\nLooking for New Training Content? Flock\nAcademy Has It!\nWe’ve recently added a few more courses to our training catalog to help\nyou and your agency feel equipped with Flock knowledge.\nTransparency Portal: Learn how to set up and customize your\nagency’s public-facing Transparency Portal, including policy and\nusage fields, public search audit options, branding, success stories,\nand publishing controls.\nAudit Assistance Webinar: This webinar walks through what\nAudit Assistance is, why Flock built it, how admins can enable and\nuse it, and best practices for reviewing atypical search patterns\nproactively.\nAudio Detection Certification: This certification covers what\nAudio Detection is, the incidents it can detect, how alerts work in\nFlock, key privacy safeguards, and how users can configure and\nreview Audio Detection alerts.\nCLOSING NOTE\nWe recognize the critical role you play and the trust your community\nplaces in you. Our commitment is to equip you with the tools,\ntransparency, and support that help drive real outcomes and strengthen\npublic confidence We’re proud to partner with agencies leading the way\n\npublic confidence. We re proud to partner with agencies leading the way\nin modern public safety.\nIf you have ideas on how we can make this newsletter even more\nimpactful, share your feedback here.\n\u0000\nKnow someone who is interested in seeing these updates? Share this form so they can\nsubscribe to receive this newsletter.\nRESOURCES\nGet Hands-On Platform Training in Flock Academy\nShare a Solved Story from Your Community\nConnect with Flock’s External Affairs Team\nCommunity Outreach & Engagement Tool Kit\n\nFlock\n3284 Northside Parkway NW, Suite 150\nAtlanta, Georgia 30327, United States","pdf":null},"e0088":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0088","title":"Scheduling an onsite visit","frm":"Anabel Pozzi","date":"2026-06-12","text":"From:\nAnabel Pozzi\nSent:\nFriday, June 12, 2026 9:44:32 AM\nTo:\nFazekas, Ryan\nCc:\nTaylor Ellison; jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nRe: Scheduling an onsite visit\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nCaptain Fazekas,\nI got some dates back and will see what works best for you and the team.\nWe are flexible between the dates of July 14-16. Can you check on your end if any of these dates work for you?\nAnabel\nOn Tue, Jun 9, 2026 at 5:18 PM Anabel Pozzi <anabel.pozzi@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHi Captain,\nMy apologies, some of my days got mixed up. Please hold, and I'll send an update on the dates.\nThank you,\nAnabel\nOn Tue, Jun 9, 2026 at 4:16 PM Anabel Pozzi <anabel.pozzi@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHi Captain Fazekas,\nThank you for the call today. As I mentioned, Taylor Ellison and I would love to get time on your calendar for an on-site in the\nnext two weeks. I checked both of our schedules, and the following options should work on our end:\nWednesday, June 10 at 11:00 a.m.\nThursday, June 11 at 11:00 a.m.\nWednesday, June 17 at 1:00 p.m.\nThursday, June 18 at 9:30 a.m.\nIf none of those work, I’m happy to find another time that better fits your schedule.\nBest,\n\nAnabel\n--\nAnabel Pozzi\nAccount Executive\nflocksafety.com\nanabel.pozzi@flocksafety.com\n  803-262-2019\n--\nAnabel Pozzi\nRegional Account Executive\nCall: 803-262-2019\nFlock Safety\nBook Time With Me\n--\nAnabel Pozzi\nRegional Account Executive\nCall: 803-262-2019\nFlock Safety\nBook Time With Me","pdf":null},"e0258":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0258","title":"Ingredients of a Trusted LPR Program","frm":"Chris at Flock","date":"2026-06-16","text":"From:\nChris at Flock\nSent:\nTuesday, June 16, 2026 10:05:31 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nIngredients of a Trusted LPR Program\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\nPublic safety technology is under more scrutiny than ever, and that's healthy.\nYour residents, councils, and boards are asking harder questions about how\nlicense plate reader (LPR) data is owned, shared, stored, and deleted. You\nshould expect clear, documented answers from every vendor, including\nFlock.\nHere's what we believe makes an LPR program worth trusting. Not every\nprovider can say these things in writing:\nYou own 100% of your data, and you're never locked in. What Flock\ncameras capture is yours, never sold and never trapped in a proprietary\nplatform. Be wary of vendors who are cheap to get into and\nexpensive to get out of. (Who really has access to your Flock data)\nChoose LPR that’s built as a core mission, not an add\u0000on. The most\nreliable systems are refined over dozens of iterations and thousands of\nreal investigations—not in a lab or bolted onto a bigger contract.\nA camera alone is not a safety network. Investigations shouldn't stop\nat city limits. Flock opt-in LPR network helps agencies cross-\njurisdictional leads while maintaining local control and accountability.\nDetermine if a vendor offers a connected network or isolated cameras.\nSharing is your decision, and prohibited use is blocked, not just\nlogged. With Flock, nothing is shared on your behalf, no agency can be\nadded without your approval, and there is no \"backdoor\" for anyone.\nBuilt-in filters block prohibited searches before they happen. Proactive\nreviews flag anomalies, on top of a full audit log. Ask whether your\n\nvendor prevents unacceptable use, or only records it after the damage\nis done. (Does Flock share data with ICE?)\nNetwork value and privacy should not be a tradeoff. Some vendors\ntreat limited data sharing as a privacy feature. You should expect both:\ninvestigative reach when you choose to collaborate, and strong local\ncontrols. With Flock, there is no sharing without your approval and no\n\"backdoor\" for anyone. Built-in filters block prohibited searches before\nthey happen, and proactive reviews flag anomalous usage. (Does Flock\nshare data with ICE?)\nStrong security starts at the login. Flock makes multi-factor\nauthentication (MFA) the default for every user and supports Single\nSign-On (SSO). We strongly recommend keeping MFA turned on for\nyour agency—it's the simplest, most effective way to keep\nunauthorized users out.\nAccountability must be clear from day one. A trusted LPR program\ndepends on more than hardware—it requires strong site selection,\npermitting, installation, maintenance, training, support, and continuous\nimprovement. If multiple vendors are involved, ask who owns the\noutcomes and who responds when something breaks.\nDeletion you can prove. With Flock, data is deleted automatically on\nyour schedule and validated yearly by our SOC 2 Type II audit. Ask\nwhether deletion is automated and audited, or simply a policy\npromise you take on faith. (How Flock handles license plate data\ndeletion)\nVehicles, not faces. Flock cameras capture vehicles in public view.\nThere is no facial recognition and no biometrics today, and these\nfeatures will not be quietly added to the roadmap later. We'll put\nthat in writing. (What Flock cameras actually capture)\nPredictable pricing. One subscription covers Flock hardware,\nsoftware, support, and compliance resources. No low-entry prices\nthat spike once you are locked in, and no requirement to buy a\nbroader bundle to preserve your program. (Explore the Flock Trust\nHub)\nThese aren't aspirations. This is how Flock was built, and we publish the\nproof. See our LPR Usage & Security Policy, request certifications through\nour security and trust portal, and separate fact from myth at our Trust Center.\nWhen you are evaluating any vendor, including us, these are the questions\nworth asking:\n1. How many crimes in your state has the LPR solution helped solve, and\nfor how many years has it operated fixed LPR at scale?\n2. Does the LPR program generate value beyond your own cameras\n\nthrough an opt-in, agency-controlled investigative network?\n3. Are you locked into the vendor's ecosystem, and is it prohibitively\nexpensive to switch to a best-of-breed solution later?\n4. Is LPR the vendor's core mission, or a loss leader product intended to\nfurther lock you into a larger bundle?\n5. If their public safety ecosystem relies on multiple third-party vendors,\nwho is accountable when something breaks?\n6. How does your platform proactively surface misuse—both today and on\nthe roadmap—while avoiding facial recognition and other biometric\ntechnologies? Can it block prohibited searches and review usage in real\ntime, or simply log misuse after the fact?\n7. What is the true cost of ownership over the life of the contract, including\nrenewal fee spikes, storage costs, upgrades, integrations & switching\ncosts?\nA vendor who hesitates, points to a roadmap, or hides behind a bundle\ninstead of proven outcomes is telling you something important. If your\ncouncil, board, or community is asking these questions, reach out to me\ndirectly or to your Flock account team anytime, and join the office hours\nGarrett is hosting for a more open conversation. I'm doing targeted\noutreach to get to as many of you as I can, as quickly as I can, to provide\ntransparency head-on. We'd rather over-explain than make you guess.\nSincerely,\nChris Colwell\nSVP, Customer Experience, Flock\n\nFlock\n1170 Howell Mill Rd NW, Suite 210\nAtlanta, Georgia 30318, United States","pdf":null},"e0315":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0315","title":"Solar PTZ Request - Follow Up","frm":"Clarkson, Constance","date":"2026-06-26","text":"From:\nClarkson, Constance\nSent:\nFriday, June 26, 2026 8:32:52 AM\nTo:\nAnabel Pozzi\nCc:\nFazekas, Ryan; Mike Holub; Taylor Ellison; Babkiewicz, Joseph; Heather Ouellette\nSubject:\nRE: Solar PTZ Request - Follow Up\nSensitivity:Normal\nGood morning Anabel.\n\nPlease advise the status of adding a PTZ at the New River Linear Trail pier.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Anabel Pozzi <anabel.pozzi@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Wednesday, June 3, 2026 10:55 AM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>; Heather Ouellette <heather.ouellette@flocksafety.com>\nCc: Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>; Mike Holub <michael.holub@flocksafety.com>; Taylor Ellison\n<taylor.ellison@flocksafety.com>\nSubject: Re: Solar PTZ Request\n\nHi Constance,\nI reviewed the camera counts by phase, and the confusion is likely coming from the rejected location in Phase 1.\nHere is the breakdown:\n\nPhase 1 shows 16 LPRs and 4 PTZs installed, with 1 rejected location. The opportunity called for 17 LPRs\nin this phase, so it appears that one LPR did not move forward.\nPhase 2 shows 13 LPRs and 19 PTZs installed. The opportunity called for 12 LPRs and 18 PTZs in this\nphase, so one additional LPR and one additional PTZ were added here.\nNetting that out, the LPR count appears to wash overall, but the PTZ count ends up one over. Based on that, it\nappears an additional PTZ was added that was not included in the original contracts.\nMy director, Taylor, has been in contact with the Chief, and we can bring this up, as you have identified an\nadditional location that needs a solar PTZ.\nLet me know if you have any other questions.\nAnabel\n\nOn Tue, Jun 2, 2026 at 4:16 PM Anabel Pozzi <anabel.pozzi@flocksafety.com> wrote:\nHi Constance,\n\nI am working with Heather about the unused camera slots. I will let you know once we complete our review.\n\nThank you!\n\nOn Tue, Jun 2, 2026 at 4:14 PM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nAnabel,\n\nWe won’t be meeting tomorrow, so please advise on the below as soon as possible this week so we can\ndetermine a direction for the new pier location.\n\nWith the project so close to completion and a 6/30/26 deadline, feel free to email between the scheduled\nmeetings so we can stay on target.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\nFrom: Mike Holub <michael.holub@flocksafety.com>\nSent: Monday, June 1, 2026 3:06 PM\nTo: Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com>\nCc: Anabel Pozzi <anabel.pozzi@flocksafety.com>; Fazekas, Ryan <rfazekas@townofbluffton.com>\nSubject: Re: Solar PTZ Request\n\nFor full transparency, I'm unsure which items are on hold and which ones are not.  @Anabel Pozzi can you\nadvise?\n\nMichael Holub\nProject Manager\nflocksafety.com\nmichael.holub@flocksafety.com\n\nOn Mon, Jun 1, 2026 at 1:36 PM Clarkson, Constance <cclarkson@townofbluffton.com> wrote:\nAfternoon Mike.\n\nWe have a new location where we need a solar PTZ, New River Linear Trail pier.  Please advise of the unused\ncamera slots where we can allocate a solar PTZ to this location. In the alternative, please advise how else we\ncan achieve a camera at the new location.\n\nThank you.\n\nConstance S. Clarkson, CEPSCI\nProject Manager\nProjects & Watershed Resilience\n843.540.3575\n\nTown of Bluffton\nPO Box 386\n20 Bridge Street\nBluffton, SC 29910\nwww.townofbluffton.sc.gov\n\n--\nAnabel Pozzi\nRegional Account Executive\nCall: 803-262-2019\nFlock Safety\nBook Time With Me\n\n--\nAnabel Pozzi\nRegional Account Executive\nCall: 803-262-2019\nFlock Safety\nBook Time With Me","pdf":null},"e0259":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0259","title":"Action Needed_ Multi-Factor Authentication Required by August 1","frm":"Chris at Flock","date":"2026-06-29","text":"From:\nChris at Flock\nSent:\nMonday, June 29, 2026 10:00:58 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nAction Needed: Multi-Factor Authentication Required by August 1\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\nI'm reaching out with an important update about how your team accesses\nFlock.\nProtecting the security of your data and your community starts at the login.\nMulti-Factor Authentication (MFA) has been the default for all Flock accounts\nsince 2024, and it remains the single most effective way to keep unauthorized\nusers out of your system. Our records show your organization does not yet\nhave MFA required for login.\nEffective August 1, 2026, MFA will be required for all Flock\norganizations. After that date, users will be prompted to verify their identity\nwith a second factor the next time they sign in, and access to the system will\nrequire that step to be completed.\nWhat You Need to Do:\nMFA will be automatically enforced for all users who have not already\nturned it on. If you’d like to control when your team transitions, please\ncontact our Support team in advance so we can help you enable it on your\npreferred timeline. We currently support:\nAuthenticator apps (recommended) — Available on both mobile and\ndesktop (for example Microsoft Authenticator, Google Authenticator,\nOkta Verify, and others). These apps generate a time-based code that\nyou enter in addition to your password.\nText message (SMS) — A one-time code sent to a mobile number at\neach login.\n\nWe are also planning to support physical security tokens (for example,\nYubiKey) in the future. If your organization requires physical security tokens\nin order to use MFA, please let us know and we will work closely with your\norganization to help address your need.\nWe’re Here to Help:\nIf you have questions or would like a hand getting set up, please reach out to\nsupport@flocksafety.com and we'll walk you through it. We can also help you\nconfirm the best method for officers and staff who don't have department-\nissued phones.\nIn the meantime, you can also visit our Multi-Factor Authentication Help\nCenter article for step-by-step instructions and FAQs on getting set up and\nmanaging your settings.\nThank you for partnering with us to keep your Flock system, and the data\nwithin it, secure.\nBest,\nChris Colwell\nSVP, Customer Experience\nFlock\n\nFlock\n3284 Northside Parkway NW, Suite 150\nAtlanta, Georgia 30327, United States","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0259.pdf"},"e0660":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0660","title":"Flock Safety - Recommending Tree Trimming at Location_ #08 Buckwalter Pkwy NB @ May River","frm":"Flock Safety Support","date":"2026-06-29","text":"From:\nFlock Safety Support\nSent:\nMonday, June 29, 2026 12:09:59 PM\nTo:\ndchandler@townofbluffton.com; jbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com; cgonzales@townofbluffton.com;\ninvoice@townofbluffton.com; ssteese@townofbluffton.com; rfazekas@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nFlock Safety - Recommending Tree Trimming at Location: #08 Buckwalter Pkwy NB @ May River\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nHi there,\nAn alert from one of your cameras indicated that trees/branches are in the immediate view of a Flock\nSafety camera. We recommend trimming the trees back from time to time so that the solar panel and/or\nthe camera has a clear line of sight towards the traffic lanes. If tree limbs are blocking the solar panel\nand/or the view of the camera, your camera may experience a declining charge (due to constant motion\ncapture) or register poor footage (due to trees in the way).\nHoping you can help by getting this taken care of.\nLocation Name: #08 Buckwalter Pkwy NB @ May River\nAddress: 866 May River Rd\nThanks so much, and stay safe,\nFlock Safety Support\nRef: 01889579 #08 Buckwalter Pkwy NB @ May River\n\nHave questions? Check out the FAQs on our website! - FAQs\nOr you can always email us at support@flocksafety.com and we'll get back to you as soon as possible.","pdf":null},"e0661":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0661","title":"Tampered LPR - #01 Buckwalter Pkwy @ Fording Island Rd SB","frm":"Flock Safety Support","date":"2026-07-09","text":"From:\nFlock Safety Support\nSent:\nThursday, July 9, 2026 2:32:20 PM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nTampered LPR - #01 Buckwalter Pkwy @ Fording Island Rd SB\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:#01 Buckwalter Pkwy @ Fording Island Rd SB - After.jpg ;#01 Buckwalter Pkwy @ Fording Island Rd SB -\nBefore.jpg ;\n\nHi Chief Babkiewicz,\nGeorge here with Flock Location Support. While responding to an alert for device #01 Buckwalter Pkwy @ Fording Island\nRd SB the technician discovered that the cable of the LPR device to the solar panel was ripped out (see attachment). The tech\nvisited the site on 6/11 and replaced the equipment during the visit. I've confirmed that at the moment, the equipment is\nfunctioning properly. There aren't any fees associated with this replacement. No further action is required on this ticket.\nThank you for your partnership, and we apologize for the inconvenience here. We look forward to your organization seeing\ncontinued success with your Flock technology.\nStay safe,\nGeorge\nFlock Location Support\nthread::Rlp_zjmbLMyi4DT-zQ6mtA4::","pdf":null},"e0261":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0261","title":"Open Door \\205 Office Hours for Chiefs & Sheriffs","frm":"Chris at Flock","date":"2026-07-14","text":"From:\nChris at Flock\nSent:\nTuesday, July 14, 2026 10:19:28 AM\nTo:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nOpen Door – Office Hours for Chiefs & Sheriffs\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nChief Babkiewicz,\nOnce a month, Flock CEO Garrett holds open office hours for chiefs and sheriffs. No agenda, no pitch – just a\nconversation.\nIf you have questions about where Flock is headed, want to share feedback, or just want to talk through something, we'd\nlike to hear it.\n→ Reserve your spot\nHope to talk soon,\nChris Colwell\nSVP, Customer Experience","pdf":null},"e0861":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0861","title":"Upcoming Meetings - CSM","frm":"Heather Ouellette","date":"2026-07-16","text":"From:\nHeather Ouellette\nSent:\nThursday, July 16, 2026 1:00:27 PM\nTo:\nBcc:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nUpcoming Meetings - CSM\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon!\nIf you don't have time to read this whole email, here are my (color-coded) requests:\nRegister for one of the upcoming Admin Webinars (Register 7/22 or Register 8/4)\nSchedule your Quarterly Meeting with me (Schedule by link or reply to this email)\nSubmit a Success Story (through this form or email me)\nAdmin Webinars-----\nBelow are the links to register for one of the two upcoming admin webinars. Please sign up for whichever session works best\nwith your schedule (both will cover the same topics).\nAs a reminder, I am co-hosting these webinars with Jess (CSM in Georgia). She co-hosted with me last quarter and you guys\nloved her so much that I recruited her back. We will cover the following topics:\nAuditing best practices\nThe upcoming MFA requirement\nWhat's new in Flock\nFAQs\nI highly encourage you to attend live, but if you cannot make either session, registering now will send you a copy of the recording\nafterward. You can also send these links (or the whole email) to anyone else you think should attend.\nPlease register for one of the following:\nWebinar Option 1: Wed. July 22 at 2:00pm\nWebinar Option 2: Tues. August 4 at 11:00am\nThis quarter, we are including an FAQ section that lists recent questions submitted by other CSMs or LE Agencies. We will then\ncover the answers live. If you have a question you'd like answered or a topic that you think would benefit the other agencies in\nattendance, you can submit them through this link: Submit a Question\n\nQuarterly Meeting-----\nWe will catch up on any outstanding tasks/needs, review account health, discuss agency goals, and if necessary, address any\nrenewal or contract needs. Schedule using my link below or let me know a date/time that works for you. Keep in mind, I will\nbe out of the office tomorrow, 7/17 and the week after next 7/25-8/3.\nSchedule directly using my scheduling link.\nLet me know your availability (email/text/call).\nSuccess Story-----\nAs a reminder, I recommend sharing at least one success story monthly (but the more, the better). You can share details via email\nor through this form -- whichever works best for you. If you haven't already shared your monthly/quarterly metrics, this is a\nreminder to send those over as well!\nThank you or all you do. I look forward to connecting soon!!\nBest,\nHeather\n--\nHeather Ouellette\nCustomer Success Manager\nflocksafety.com\nUPCOMING TIME OFF 7/25/26 - 8/03/26\nheather.ouellette@flocksafety.com\nࠇ  470-852-3342","pdf":null},"e0862":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0862","title":"Reminder - Upcoming Admin Webinar","frm":"Heather Ouellette","date":"2026-07-20","text":"From:\nHeather Ouellette\nSent:\nMonday, July 20, 2026 1:42:29 PM\nTo:\nBcc:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nReminder - Upcoming Admin Webinar\nSensitivity:Normal\n\nGood Afternoon,\nThis is a quick reminder to register for one of the two Admin Webinar options below if you have not already done so. You only\nneed to register for one, as both will cover the same topics. Jess (CSM in Georgia) and I are co-hosting again this quarter after\npositive feedback last quarter.\nRegistration Links:\nWebinar Option 1: Wed. July 22 at 2:00pm\nWebinar Option 2: Tues. August 4 at 11:00am\nWe encourage you to attend live, but if you cannot make either session, registering now will send you a copy of the recording\nafterward. You can also send the above links (or the whole email) to anyone else who should attend.\nThank you & I look forward to seeing you soon!\nBest,\nHeather\n--\nHeather Ouellette\nCustomer Success Manager\nflocksafety.com\nUPCOMING TIME OFF 7/25/26 - 8/03/26\nheather.ouellette@flocksafety.com\nࠇ  470-852-3342","pdf":null},"a2024-11-14":{"kind":"Agenda","src":"LECAC agenda","title":"LECAC meeting agenda, Nov 14, 2024","frm":"Town of Bluffton","date":"2024-11-14","text":"Law Enforcement Citizens Advisory Committee Meeting\nThursday, November 14, 2024 at 6:00 PM\nTheodore D. Washington Municipal Building, Henry “Emmett” McCracken Jr. Council Chambers,\n20 Bridge Street, Bluffton, SC\nAGENDA\nI.\nCALL TO ORDER\nII. ROLL CALL\nIII. APPROVAL OF MINUTES\na.\nOctober 10, 2024 Minutes\nIV. PUBLIC COMMENT\nV. OLD BUSINESS\na.\nReview of SOP 15 and recommended changes made by LECAC.  - Chief Babkiewicz\nb.\nReview of SOP 17 and recommended changes made by LECAC. - Chief Babkiewicz\nc.\nReview of SOP 18 and recommended changes made by LECAC. - Chief Babkiewicz\nVI. NEW BUSINESS\na.\nReview of New SOP for use of Flock Cameras.  - Chief Babkiewicz\nb.\nAdoption of 2025 Law Enforcement Citizens Advisory Commitee Meeting Dates. Chief\nBabkiewicz\nVII. DISCUSSION\na.\nUpcoming events\na.\nOperation Christmas Child\nb.\nFirst Responder Food Drive\nc.\nChristmas Tree lighting/Parade\nd.\nBPD Christmas Party\nVIII. ADJOURNMENT\nNEXT MEETING DATE: Thursday, December 12, 2024\n\n\n\nTown of Bluffton, SC\nLaw Enforcement Citizens Advisory Committee Meeting Agenda\nNovember 14, 2024\n\n\n\n“FOIA Compliance – Public notification of this meeting has been published and posted in compliance\nwith the Freedom of Information Act and the Town of Bluffton policies.”\nIn accordance with the requirements of Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990 (\"ADA\"), the\nTown of Bluffton will not discriminate against qualified individuals with disabilities on the basis of\ndisability in its services, programs, or activities. The Town of Bluffton Council Chambers are ADA\ncompatible. Auditory accommodations are available. Any person requiring further accommodation\nshould contact the Town of Bluffton ADA Coordinator at 843.706.4500 or\nadacoordinator@townofbluffton.com as soon as possible but no later than 48 hours before the\nscheduled event.\nExecutive Session – The public body may vote to go into executive session for any item identified for\naction on the agenda.\n*Please note that each member of the public may speak at one public comment session and a form must\nbe filled out and given to the Town Clerk. To submit a public comment online, please click here:\nhttps://www.townofbluffton.sc.gov/FormCenter/Town-15/Public-Comment-60\nPublic comment is limited to 3 minutes per speaker.","pdf":"docs/11-14-2024_LECAC_Agenda.pdf"},"a2025-01-09":{"kind":"Agenda","src":"LECAC agenda","title":"LECAC meeting agenda, Jan 9, 2025","frm":"Town of Bluffton","date":"2025-01-09","text":"Law Enforcement Citizens Advisory Committee Meeting\nThursday, January 09, 2025 at 6:00 PM\nTheodore D. Washington Municipal Building, Henry “Emmett” McCracken Jr. Council Chambers,\n20 Bridge Street, Bluffton, SC\nAGENDA\nI.\nCALL TO ORDER\nII. ROLL CALL\nIII. APPROVAL OF MINUTES\na.\nOctober 10, 2024 Minutes\nb.\nNovember 14, 2024 Minutes\nIV. PUBLIC COMMENT\nV. OLD BUSINESS\nVI. NEW BUSINESS\na.\nApproval of November 2025 Meeting Date Change. Chief Babkiewicz\nVII. DISCUSSION\na.\nChristmas Events- Updates\na.\nOperation Christmas Child- 150 boxes filled\nb.\nShop with a Cop Update\nc.\nBPD Christmas Party\nb.\nUpdate on Flock Cameras\na.\nPolicy has been posted\nb.\nWorking with CIP on abatement for locations of cameras\nc.\nProvide training to all staff\nd.\nHoping to have cameras in place by end of February\nVIII. ADJOURNMENT\nNEXT MEETING DATE: THURSDAY, FEBRUARY 13, 2025\n\n\n\nTown of Bluffton, SC\nLaw Enforcement Citizens Advisory Committee Meeting Agenda\nJanuary 09, 2025\n\n\n\n“FOIA Compliance – Public notification of this meeting has been published and posted in compliance\nwith the Freedom of Information Act and the Town of Bluffton policies.”\nIn accordance with the requirements of Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990 (\"ADA\"), the\nTown of Bluffton will not discriminate against qualified individuals with disabilities on the basis of\ndisability in its services, programs, or activities. The Town of Bluffton Council Chambers are ADA\ncompatible. Auditory accommodations are available. Any person requiring further accommodation\nshould contact the Town of Bluffton ADA Coordinator at 843.706.4500 or\nadacoordinator@townofbluffton.com as soon as possible but no later than 48 hours before the\nscheduled event.\nExecutive Session – The public body may vote to go into executive session for any item identified for\naction on the agenda.\n*Please note that each member of the public may speak at one public comment session and a form must\nbe filled out and given to the Town Clerk. To submit a public comment online, please click here:\nhttps://www.townofbluffton.sc.gov/FormCenter/Town-15/Public-Comment-60\nPublic comment is limited to 3 minutes per speaker.","pdf":"docs/01-09-2025_LECAC_Agenda.pdf"},"a2025-03-13":{"kind":"Agenda","src":"LECAC agenda","title":"LECAC meeting agenda, Mar 13, 2025","frm":"Town of Bluffton","date":"2025-03-13","text":"Law Enforcement Citizens Advisory Committee Meeting\nThursday, March 13, 2025 at 6:00 PM\nTheodore D. Washington Municipal Building, Henry “Emmett” McCracken Jr. Council Chambers,\n20 Bridge Street, Bluffton, SC\nAGENDA\nI.\nCALL TO ORDER\nII. ROLL CALL\nIII. PUBLIC COMMENT\nIV. OLD BUSINESS\nV. NEW BUSINESS\na.\nApproval of Flock Camera System Audit - Chief Babkiewicz\nVI. DISCUSSION\na.\nReview of Monthly Goals for February 2025 - Chief Babkiewicz\nb.\n2025 Bluffton Police Department Awards Ceremony - Chief Babkiewicz\nVII. ADJOURNMENT\nNEXT MEETING DATE: Thursday, April 10, 2025\n\n\n\nTown of Bluffton, SC\nLaw Enforcement Citizens Advisory Committee Meeting Agenda\nMarch 13, 2025\n\n\n\n“FOIA Compliance – Public notification of this meeting has been published and posted in compliance\nwith the Freedom of Information Act and the Town of Bluffton policies.”\nIn accordance with the requirements of Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990 (\"ADA\"), the\nTown of Bluffton will not discriminate against qualified individuals with disabilities on the basis of\ndisability in its services, programs, or activities. The Town of Bluffton Council Chambers are ADA\ncompatible. Auditory accommodations are available. Any person requiring further accommodation\nshould contact the Town of Bluffton ADA Coordinator at 843.706.4500 or\nadacoordinator@townofbluffton.com as soon as possible but no later than 48 hours before the\nscheduled event.\nExecutive Session – The public body may vote to go into executive session for any item identified for\naction on the agenda.\n*Please note that each member of the public may speak at one public comment session and a form must\nbe filled out and given to the Town Clerk. To submit a public comment online, please click here:\nhttps://www.townofbluffton.sc.gov/FormCenter/Town-15/Public-Comment-60\nPublic comment is limited to 3 minutes per speaker.","pdf":"docs/03-13-2025_LECAC_Agenda.pdf"},"f20363":{"kind":"FOIA response","src":"FOIA 20363","title":"Bluffton Flock camera locations (50 sites)","frm":"Town of Bluffton","date":"2026-07-06","text":"Bluffton Flock Camera Locations\nDisclaimer: This project is nearing completion; however, not all listed cameras are currently active\nor operational. Some planned camera locations may change prior to final installation due to\npermitting requirements, easement approvals, property owner permissions, or other project-related\nconsiderations.\n1. May River Road EB @ BPD Substation\n2. Buckwalter Parkway @ Fording Island Road (SB)\n3. Parkside Commons\n4. Route 46 @ Route 170\n5. South Okatie Highway @ New River Boat Landing\n6. Route 170 East @ May River Crossing\n7. Bluffton Parkway @ Buckwalter Parkway\n8. Bluffton Parkway EB @ Route 170\n9. Bluffton Parkway WB @ Route 170\n10. Route 170 WB @ Cypress Ridge\n11. Buckwalter Parkway NB @ May River\n12. Bluffton Parkway WB @ Goethe Road\n13. Bluffton Parkway WB @ Buckwalter Parkway\n14. Buckwalter Parkway NB @ Bluffton Parkway\n15. Buck Island Road SB @ Old Carolina\n16. Bluffton Road SB @ 184 Parking Lot\n17. Buck Island Road SB @ Bluffton Parkway\n18. Buck Island Road @ Grayco\n19. Buckwalter Parkway @ Cassidy Drive (NB)\n20. Buckwalter Parkway @ Shell Hall (SB)\n21. Okatie Highway @ Heritage West (SB)\n22. New Riverside Road @ Red Barn Drive (SB)\n23. Bluffton Road @ Village Commons (NB)\n24. Okatie Highway @ Seagrass (NB)\n25. Simmonsville Road NB @ Bluffton Parkway\n26. Fording Island Road @ Towne Drive\n27. Fording Island Road @ Toyota Drive\n28. Mill Creek Boulevard @ Okatie Highway\n29. Bridge Street & Wharf Street (SB)\n30. May River Road @ Buckwalter Parkway\n31. New Riverside Road @ New Riverside Village West\n32. Bluffton Parkway @ Buckwalter Parkway\n33. Buckwalter Parkway @ Farm Lake Drive (South)\n\n34. Simmonsville Road @ County Recycling Center\n35. Buckwalter Place Boulevard @ Buckwalter Parkway\n36. Innovation Drive @ Kroger\n37. Buck Island Road @ May River Road\n38. May River Road @ Bluffton Road\n39. Bruin Road @ Burnt Church Road\n40. Promenade Street @ State of Mind Street\n41. Heyward Street @ May River Road\n42. May River Road @ Calhoun Road\n43. Bridge Street @ Calhoun Street\n44. Buck Island Road @ Bluffton Parkway\n45. Red Cedar Street @ Bluffton Parkway\n46. Bluffton Parkway @ Simmonsville Road\n47. Buckwalter Parkway @ Pinellas Drive (South)\n48. Buckwalter Parkway @ Pinellas Drive (North)\n49. Bluffton Parkway @ Goethe Road\n50. 9th Avenue @ Pin Oak Street","pdf":"docs/FOIA.20363.Bluffton_Flock_Camera_Locations.fulfillment.7.6.2026.pdf"},"m2024-02-08":{"kind":"Minutes","src":"LECAC minutes","title":"LECAC meeting minutes, Feb 8, 2024","frm":"Town of Bluffton","date":"2024-02-08","text":"TOWN OF BLUFFTON LAW ENFORCEMENT CITIZENS ADVISORY COMMITTEE MEETING Thursday, February 8, 2024\n\nMembers present: Michael Frazier, George Baily, Mayra Rivera\n- Vazquez, Tabor Vaux\n\nMembers Not Present: Bill O’Toole, Jennifer Morrow, Reggie Howard\n\nStaff Present: Chief Joe Babkiewicz, Sergeant M. Ferrelli\n\nMichael Frazier called the meeting to order at 18:00 hrs. at the Henry “Emmett” McCracken Council Chambers located at 20 Bridge Street, followed by the Pledge of Allegiance. \n\nPublic Comment:Betty Black (address removed). Ms. Black stated that this was her first time attending and wanted to observe the goings on at the LECAC meetings. She also voiced her praises for the FLOCK cameras that are currently being used in her neighborhood (Pine Ridge). \n\nOld Business: - Mike Frazier made a motion to approve the prior meeting minutes, was seconded by Myra Rivera\n- Vazquez- Mike Frazier made a motion to approve the agenda for this meeting, was seconded by George Baily.- Mike Frazier made a motion to approve the 2024 LECAC meeting schedule, was seconded by Myra Rivera\n- Vazquez (Tabor Vaux also moved to approve with any future schedule modifications final approval by chairman Jennifer Morrow as see fit).\n\nNew Business:- Chief Babkiewicz presented 3 newly revised Bluffton Police Department Policies to the committee for their review, and discussed the changes made to each one.\n- BPD Pursuit Policy- George Baily motion to approve policy changes, seconded by Mike Frazier.\n- BPD Response to Resistance Policy- Mike Frazier motion to approve policy changes, seconded by George Baily.\n- BPD Discharging of Firearm Policy- George Baily motion to approve policy changes, seconded by Mike Frazier. \n\n\nDiscussion:\n- Chief Babkiewicz discussed the department stats in comparison to surrounding cities and towns of similar size within the state.\n- Chief Babkiewicz also discussed the department’s desire to obtain FLOCK camera systems, to be implemented and used throughout the town in hopes of increasing the probability of solving various crimes. \n\nA motion to adjourn was made at 1900 hrs. by Mike Frazier, and all members seconded the motion. \n\nThe next scheduled LECAC meeting is slated for March 14th, 2024, at 1800hrs. \n\nSergeant Matt Ferrelli Secretary","pdf":null},"e0348":{"kind":"Email","src":"FOIA 20394 · item 0348","title":"Invoice Delivery","frm":"Flock Billing","date":"2025-09-18","text":"From:\nFlock Billing\nSent:\nThursday, September 18, 2025 9:37:09 AM\nTo:\ninvoice@townofbluffton.com\nCc:\njbabkiewicz@townofbluffton.com\nSubject:\nInvoice Delivery\nSensitivity:\nNormal\nAttachments:Flock Safety_INV-74486_2025-09-18.pdf ;\n\nDear Felicia,\nPlease view the details of your recent invoice below.\nInvoice No: INV-74486\nInvoice Date: 9/18/2025\nInvoice Total: USD 109,500.00\nDue Date: 10/18/2025\nIf paying by check, please be sure to mail with a printed copy of your invoice\nto:\nFlock Group Inc\nPO Box 121923\nDallas, TX 75312-1923\nIf you have any questions about your service or installation, please contact\nsupport@flocksafety.com.\nIf you have any questions about your invoice, please reach out to\nbilling@flocksafety.com.\nNeed a copy of our W9 or COI? See below.\nFlock Group Inc. W9\nFlock Group Inc. COI\nWe appreciate your business!\nThank you,\nFlock Safety Billing","pdf":"docs/FOIA20394-item0348.pdf"}}};